window.AKK_THE_MARQUIS_MANSIONS_ELITE_CLASS_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_THE_MARQUIS_MANSIONS_ELITE_CLASS_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1: Married, Stepchild's Show of Force","paragraphs":["\"The young lady's life is over now. That young marquis has been missing for years. Marrying into that family is like marrying a dead man.\"","\"I heard she chose this marriage herself. Do you think she's been possessed?\"","\"She probably went mad after falling into that bathtub.\"","\"That makes sense.\"","\"...\"","Xu Wan sat at her dressing table in her red wedding dress, tapping the table with a vein popping on her forehead. \"Ladies, I'm still sitting right here.\"","Have people completely abandoned the courtesy of not gossiping about someone in their presence?","She had transmigrated into the body of a noble lady - couldn't they show her a little respect?","However, her protests were futile.","The room fell silent for a few seconds.","The maids rolled their eyes at her and left with the wedding trays.","Xu Wan: \"...\"","Fine, she admitted defeat.","In her previous life, Xu Wan died from overwork. When she first transmigrated and found herself as the legitimate daughter of a minister, she had crawled under her blanket and laughed hysterically for nearly an hour, rejoicing that she had finally escaped her miserable life as a corporate slave and was now on the path to prosperity.","Until the maids brought her a plate of sour fruits for dinner, and Xu Wan's hour-long dream shattered into pieces.","Although the original owner was the legitimate daughter of the Minister, her birth mother had passed away within two years. After the stepmother entered the household, she naturally had no good days ahead. While she held the title of the legitimate young lady on the surface, even the servants could bully her behind closed doors.","When she finally reached eighteen, her seemingly kind but cruel stepmother decided to marry her off, presenting her with three options:","First was a concubine's son from the Prime Minister's family - though prestigious, it would be laughable for a minister's legitimate daughter to marry a concubine's son;","Second was the legitimate second son of a duke's family - also prestigious, but he had countless concubines and mistresses, marrying him would mean endless humiliation;","The last option was the Yangyuan Marquis Manor, wealthy beyond measure. Their legitimate eldest son, Zong Zhao, had gone missing on the battlefield eight years ago. The old marquis recently claimed to have received a message from his son in a dream about wanting to arrange a marriage, so they were now seeking a bride.","Before his disappearance, Zong Zhao had no wife or concubines, only an eight-year-old son. Though without a legitimate mother, this boy was extremely favored and was immediately given the status of legitimate eldest grandson upon returning to the manor, becoming a unique case in the entire Capital City.","After a day's consideration, Xu Wan decisively chose the Marquis Manor.","Her husband was gone, she could spend money freely, and no servants would dare bully her. As for the stepson... he was just an eight-year-old brat, how much trouble could he cause?","\"Miss, it's the auspicious time. Please enter the bridal sedan.\"","The matchmaker's voice came from outside, accompanied by the snickering of other maids.","Xu Wan rolled her eyes, thinking to herself that she would endure it...","Once she reached the Marquis Manor, she would be free.","The sound of firecrackers filled the air.","The sedan chair from the Minister's Mansion slowly made its way to the Marquis Manor.","\"Step down from the sedan and cross the fire basin, bride.\"","Xu Wan was helped across the fire basin and followed the matchmaker's guidance into the manor.","Amidst all the ceremonial music and festivities, Xu Wan wondered who would perform the wedding ceremony with her since the groom was dead.","Would she be bowing to a memorial tablet?","Well, even a tablet would do - she couldn't see anything under her red veil anyway.","As long as she didn't feel embarrassed, the embarrassment would fall on the Marquis Manor.","However... reality slapped her in the face like a tornado.","\"Cluck... cluck...\"","\"Cluck... cluck...\"","Xu Wan thought she had misheard until the surrounding laughter grew louder and louder, becoming deafening!","\"They're making her bow to a chicken? What is the Marquis Manor thinking?\"","\"It looks like a hen.\"","\"Ah! Young Master Cheng switched the rooster for a hen!\"","\"Hahaha, has the Marquis Manor gone mad? Making the bride bow to a hen? This is unheard of!\"","\"This will be the talk of the town for a year!\"","\"Hahaha...\"","Xu Wan's head was pounding.","Young Master Cheng... that was her never-met eight-year-old stepson, Zong Jincheng, the little tyrant of the Yangyuan Marquis Manor.","As expected of him, his ability to cause trouble was unmatched.","Xu Wan tried hard to ignore the surrounding laughter, constantly brainwashing herself: \"It's okay, good days don't come easy, you have to give to receive, endure for a moment for peace, endure for a lifetime for happiness, even if uncle can't endure it, auntie must...\"","The Marquis Manor was still a prestigious household after all. After this incident, the matchmaker and steward quickly took control of the situation, urgently replacing the nearly-laying hen with a new rooster.","The other guests, considering the Marquis Manor's face, finally put away their amused expressions, though they were still struggling to hold back their laughter.","\"First bow to Heaven and Earth.\"","As the matchmaker's voice fell, Xu Wan quickly bowed her head in ceremony, while someone pressed down on the rooster's head on the other side...","\"BANG!\" An explosive sound.","\"Pop pop pop pop!\"","A string of firecrackers suddenly exploded above Xu Wan's head!","\"Oh heavens! There were firecrackers on the rooster!\"","\"It's Young Master Cheng again!\"","\"He's blown holes in the bride's veil!\"","Xu Wan angrily tore off her burned veil and looked out furiously. She immediately spotted a boy dressed in fine silk clothes, looking beautiful and delicate, appearing completely innocent - surely it couldn't be him.","But soon, Xu Wan saw the boy make a mischievous face at her...","Damn it!","It was this little devil!","The string in Xu Wan's mind that had been taut for a month finally snapped!","Forget about enduring for a better life, forget about finding freedom in the Marquis Manor, forget about eight-year-olds being little angels.","You little brat!","I'm going to beat you to death today!"]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2: The Bride Unsheathed Her Sword","paragraphs":["In her previous life, Xu Wan was a workaholic.","Although after her sudden death, she decided to change her ways and take life easy, her decisive and efficient way of doing things was still hard to change immediately, just like now—","She had already drawn swords from the guards on both sides and was charging towards Zong Jincheng with remarkably steady emotions!","\"Ah! Help! The lady is trying to kill the young master!\"","\"Quick, stop the bride!\"","\"Protect the young master!!\"","\"Slow down... ah... the wedding ribbons are ruined!\"","\"The wedding basin is broken too!\"","\"The wedding characters are gone too, ahhh...\"","...","The wedding at the Marquis Manor had descended into chaos, with guests fleeing the scene, afraid of getting caught in the crossfire.","What should have been a joyous occasion became the talk of the town, making the entire Sheng Capital City burst into laughter!","And when it came to gossip, the stories in the teahouses became more and more elaborate:","\"To have the wedding disrupted by the little devil on the very first day, even the gods would find it hard to swallow. My third aunt's cousin's nephew was there and said Miss Xu lifted her red veil, let out a mighty roar, and charged out with a sword!\"","\"Oh my! As expected of the Minister of Justice's daughter, she truly takes after her father!\"","\"Good! Well said! Keep going!\"","\"But young master Cheng of the Yangyuan Marquis Manor isn't someone to be trifled with either. After the young marquis disappeared, baby Cheng became his only bloodline. Who in the entire manor, or even the whole capital, wouldn't give him some face?\"","\"I heard the entire manor dotes on young master Cheng. I fear this Miss Xu will have a hard time...\"","\"Ah? Could she be divorced on her wedding day?\"","\"...\"","At the Yangyuan Marquis Manor.","Before the guards could apprehend her, Xu Wan had already grabbed the little devil... by his hair.","They say modern women like to pull hair when fighting, and now the advantage of ancient men became their weakness too.","\"Let go!\"","Zong Jincheng gritted his teeth, also pulling Xu Wan's hair with all his might, neither willing to yield.","\"No way, even if I have to sacrifice a thousand, I'll make sure you lose eight hundred today!\"","\"Ouch... let me go, I'm the young marquis's son!\"","\"Hah... and I'm the young marquis's new wife! You little brat, by rank, you should call me mother!\"","\"I won't call you that, you evil woman!\"","\"Still dare to insult me? Say goodbye to your hair!\"","\"Ah...\"","The maids watched anxiously as both their hairlines were in jeopardy.","One was the manor's lady, the other the manor's eldest grandson - they couldn't take sides!","\"The Old Marquis and Old Marchioness have arrived.\"","While still gripping the little devil's hair, Xu Wan turned to look at the elderly couple who had rushed over from the wedding hall.","The Old Marquis and Old Marchioness were both in their forties or fifties, dressed in fine silk robes, followed by countless maids and servants. Though their temples showed traces of gray, both elders appeared kind and gentle.","Especially the Old Marchioness, who was smiling so widely her eyes had almost disappeared.","\"What are you all standing around for? Quickly separate them!\" At the Old Marquis's command, others finally dared to step forward and break up the fight.","Though Zong Jincheng was usually mischievous, he greatly respected the Old Marquis and was the first to let go. After escaping Xu Wan's clutches, he stuck his tongue out at her triumphantly.","Xu Wan flexed her wrist and, not to be outdone, waved the few strands of hair she'd pulled from the little troublemaker.","The tension between them was palpable.","Finally, the Old Marchioness stepped in to mediate, taking Xu Wan's hands with a smile, saying, \"Wan'er, to have such a scene on your wedding day, you must feel wronged.\"","One shouldn't strike a smiling face, and Xu Wan's first instinct was to deny any grievance.","But thinking carefully, how could there be none? She was absolutely furious!","Although she wasn't favored at the Minister's Mansion, her stepmother was skilled at maintaining appearances and had always maintained a good reputation. Even when choosing a marriage partner for her, she insisted on a high-ranking family, afraid that marrying beneath their station would affect her own daughter's future marriage prospects.","However, due to her position, Xu Wan didn't dare express her dissatisfaction with the Marquis Manor, at most remaining a silent lamb.","The Old Marchioness exchanged a glance with the Old Marquis, then addressed the maids: \"You may all leave, I have something to discuss with Wan'er.\"","As the maids withdrew, Zong Jincheng tried to slip away too.","But the Old Marquis spoke up: \"Jincheng, stay.\"","Zong Jincheng blinked his big eyes, seemingly sensing something amiss. He slowly backed away, trying to laugh it off: \"Grandfather, Grandmother, I just remembered I haven't done my reading today, so I'll take my leave first. Please continue your discussion.\"","The little devil was blessed with striking good looks, with an adorable dimple on his left cheek. Whenever he smiled, people felt their hearts melt and were willing to indulge his every whim.","But this time, the Old Marquis seemed quite determined, giving him no chance to charm his way out: \"Stop right there. You haven't been to the study for a month, what reading could be so urgent now? Stay and listen.\"","Zong Jincheng quickly looked to the Old Marchioness, his eyes pleading: \"Grandmother...\"","However, even his usually doting grandmother didn't help him this time: \"Be good, Jincheng. Your grandfather has something to tell you.\"","\"Fine.\"","Having failed to escape, Zong Jincheng's entire demeanor screamed dejection.","Seeing the little troublemaker deflated, Xu Wan was absolutely delighted. If not for her excellent acting skills, she would have burst out laughing.","Zong Jincheng sensed her schadenfreude and shot her a fierce glare.","Xu Wan remained unfazed, even returning a smug look identical to his earlier provocation.","This made Zong Jincheng even angrier.","The Old Marchioness quietly observed their interaction and said to the Old Marquis, \"My lord, I think your dream might be right. Perhaps Wan'er is indeed the wife He'er would want.\"","The Old Marquis stroked his beard and smiled, \"I think so too. It's been a long time since anyone has put Jincheng in his place like this.\"","Xu Wan couldn't understand their cryptic exchange.","But her instincts told her it wasn't anything good.","However, before she could speak, the Old Marchioness had already removed a jade bracelet from her own wrist and smoothly slipped it onto hers.","The little devil beside them was stunned: \"Grandmother, that's your favorite bracelet!\"","He stared at Xu Wan in disbelief, then at his grandmother, remembering what someone had told him: \"Once your stepmother marries in, your good days will be over.\"","Zong Jincheng clenched his fists, his worries growing stronger.","It was true after all.","Xu Wan also realized the bracelet's value and was about to refuse when she saw the Old Marchioness pull out... the housekeeper's keys from her sleeve.","The housekeeper's keys...","The housekeeper's keys!!"]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3: Taking Over the Marquis Manor's Authority","paragraphs":["She had seen this thing in the Minister's Mansion before. Her stepmother had to wait a whole decade before finally receiving the household keys from her grandmother. After that, she ruled the mansion with absolute authority and lived a life of comfort.","And now, the keys before her represented complete control over the entire Yangyuan Marquis Manor!","Good heavens!","As a newly wedded bride who hadn't even changed out of her wedding dress, how could she possibly receive the household keys that everyone desperately coveted?","She must have woken up in the wrong position.","Xu Wan quickly pinched herself.","\"Ouch... that hurts.\"","So it wasn't a dream!","Zong Jincheng protested indignantly, \"Grandmother, how could you give them to her? Even if you were to give these household keys to Auntie Hong from the second branch, you shouldn't give them to her!\"","The Old Marquis had only a pair of twin sons. Eight years ago, during a great battle, his eldest son Zong Zhao went missing, while his second son Zong Yan died directly on the battlefield. The second son hadn't married before his death, but this year it was discovered that he had a mistress and an illegitimate son.","Having a mistress and an illegitimate child before marriage was scandalous, but since the person was already dead, the Old Marquis was overjoyed at the news that his second son had an heir. He immediately ordered people to bring the child back to the manor and registered him under the Zong Die family registry.","However, that mistress, Auntie Hong whom Zong Jincheng mentioned, had too humble an origin to be given the position of the official wife, let alone qualify for the household keys.","The Old Marchioness said, \"Jincheng, your grandfather is getting old, and this family will eventually rely on you and your father. With Zhao's fate unknown, you need a mother to take care of you. When you come of age, our marquis title will be passed to you, won't it?\"","Zong Jincheng complained, \"But I don't need a mother.\"","He had been used to living without parents since birth, and now at eight years old, he needed them even less.","Besides, she was just a stepmother, not his birth mother.","Xu Wan snorted inwardly, I don't want you as my son either!","Ungrateful child!","The Old Marchioness pushed the household keys into Xu Wan's hands and instructed, \"From now on, you are the properly married Marchioness of our manor. You will be in charge of everyone's daily necessities, food, clothing, and accommodation in this household.\"","Suddenly wielding such power, Xu Wan looked at the household keys in her hand and felt their weight. How did the responsibility for the entire marquis manor end up on her shoulders?","Wasn't she planning to just take it easy and live a peaceful life?","\"I have no experience in household management,\" Xu Wan admitted honestly.","Her stepmother, far from letting her manage the household, would have preferred not to give her even a bite of food.","Although in modern times when she was a top performer, she had risen to team leader position in just one year, that team only had a few people. Now she was being asked to manage an entire marquis manor with over a hundred people.","The Old Marchioness said, \"You'll learn as you go, it's easy to pick up.\"","\"Really? You're not deceiving me?\" Xu Wan asked seriously.","The Old Marchioness was amused by her question and laughed, \"Of course it's true.\"","Xu Wan pondered for a few seconds, thinking the job was acceptable. After all, this was a marquis manor, a wealthy and noble household. As the household manager, she would surely live a comfortable life.","\"Alright, I'll try... wait, are there any additional conditions?\" Xu Wan was about to agree when she noticed the Old Marquis grinning from ear to ear, and she instinctively felt there must be a catch!","The Old Marchioness shook her head, \"There are no additional conditions, just take good care of everyone in the manor, we have no other requirements.\"","\"Everyone in the manor...\" Xu Wan mulled over these words, then turned to see the defiant little boy glaring at her.","Xu Wan suddenly realized, \"Don't tell me that includes him?\"","Help! Such a little ancestor couldn't be beaten, who could possibly handle him?","The Old Marchioness smiled, \"Jincheng is a very well-behaved and intelligent child. As long as you guide him carefully, we believe he will surely achieve top honors in the imperial examinations.\"","\"???\"","Xu Wan nearly fainted.","Not only did she have to take care of this little demon king, but she also had to help him achieve top honors.","Top honors! That meant ranking among the top three!","In the imperial examinations held every three years!","This little devil Zong Jincheng probably couldn't even pass the entry-level scholar examination!","Xu Wan tactfully tried to return the household keys to the Old Marchioness, saying awkwardly, \"Old Marchioness, please be reasonable. You'd better keep these keys yourself. I lack both talent and ability to manage the entire manor, let alone bear the burden of educating a child to achieve top honors.\"","Just kidding, shouldn't the responsibility of this troublemaker's education fall on his tutors?","What did it have to do with her, a stepmother who just wanted to take it easy!","Seeing her backing down, Zong Jincheng quickly added, \"Yes, Grandmother, I also think we don't need her to manage. I'm very independent, I don't need her to teach me. She looks like someone who hasn't even studied herself.\"","Xu Wan almost blurted out that she had read more books than all the salt he had eaten in his life, this little illiterate who hadn't even completed nine years of compulsory education!","But saying that would mean she couldn't refuse this burden anymore.","Xu Wan held her tongue.","Unexpectedly, the Old Marchioness delivered another heavy blow: \"I've discussed with the Marquis, and we'll increase your monthly allowance from one hundred taels to three hundred taels.\"","Xu Wan's eyes immediately lit up.","Even without fully understanding the value of ancient silver currency, she knew how precious three hundred taels were. The original owner of this body hadn't managed to save even one tael of silver in over ten years of secret saving, let alone three hundred!","And this was three hundred taels every month!","The temptation was too great!","The Old Marchioness continued with her killer move: \"If Jincheng can achieve third place or better in the imperial examinations, we'll give you an additional fifty thousand taels.\"","Xu Wan: \"!!\"","Fifty thousand taels!!","She felt her mind being bombarded by gold ingots!","\"And if he can achieve first place, that will be changed to one hundred thousand taels.\"","After finishing, the Old Marchioness looked at her with a smile.","The hundred thousand taels that came from her mouth seemed as casual as ten taels.","Even Zong Jincheng was stunned.","He asked with a trembling voice, \"Grandmother, are you planning to give the entire manor to her?\"","He knew his grandmother's family was the wealthiest in Salt City, with enough family fortune to last for generations, but surely they hadn't reached the point of throwing silver around like dirt...","The Old Marchioness smiled, \"Jincheng, you should know that when you succeed, the entire marquis manor will benefit. Then, we can confidently hand over the entire manor to you, isn't that right?\"","Zong Jincheng: \"...\"","It made sense, but something still felt off.","Xu Wan immediately understood.","The Old Marchioness was painting a grand picture for both of them simultaneously.","No wonder she hadn't sent Zong Jincheng away.","The purpose was to give them both the same goal - she for money, he for power.","Once this brat realized this, he would probably start thinking about how to get rid of her!","But she wasn't going to be pushed around so easily.","Xu Wan quickly took back the household keys from the Old Marchioness's hand, deliberately waving them in front of the little demon king's face.","After receiving the angry glare from the little brat, she respectfully said:","\"Thank you, Mother-in-law, I accept the task.\""]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4: Fight Against the Little Demon King","paragraphs":["After the Old Marquis and Old Marchioness gave all instructions, they announced their plans to visit another estate for leisure, leaving the entire Marquis Manor under Xu Wan's management.","This announcement shocked the entire manor.","What leisure trip?","The trip was merely an excuse; delegating authority was the real purpose. If they remained in the manor, the young master would surely come crying to them constantly, and the new bride wouldn't be able to freely discipline the troublesome child.","Moreover, even those waiting outside to see Xu Wan make a fool of herself were all dumbfounded.","The storytellers in the teahouses, known for their eloquence, were caught off guard and could only manage to stammer: \"As expected of the Old Marquis, decisive in delegating authority.\"","Everyone: \"...\"","In the back courtyard of the Marquis Manor.","Xu Wan had already changed out of her wedding dress into new everyday clothes.","The Old Marchioness had prepared everything thoroughly for her; there were twenty sets of everyday clothes alone, more than the new clothes her stepsister received in an entire year.","The Lady of the Marquis Manor had six maids, all young and beautiful, efficient in their work. Usually, Xu Wan would have suspected these maids were meant to become concubines or bedchamber attendants for her husband, but now with her husband's fate unknown and likely deceased, having these pretty maids around was simply pleasing to the eye.","\"My Lady, these are the manor's accounts, recording all income and expenses for this year. If you wish to see previous years' records, I can have them brought from the accounting office,\" said Cui Zhi, whose mother was the Old Marchioness's dowry maid. Cui Zhi was the eldest among the maids at twenty-three, the same age as Xu Wan in modern years, and five years older than the original mistress.","However, women in ancient times managed households early, and Cui Zhi appeared reliable and steady.","Xu Wan flipped through the ledger; the accounts were clearly recorded. The surrounding maids were obedient and well-mannered, seeming even more docile than those in the Minister's Mansion. The entire atmosphere of the Marquis Manor impressed her.","\"Bring me Zong Jincheng's accounts to review.\"","The manor had a steward managing affairs, and the Old Marchioness had explained everything clearly before leaving. The keys were merely given to her to deal with the little devil, not because they actually wanted her to focus on household management.","She understood this clearly.","\"Yes,\" Cui Zhi responded and quickly brought the accounts.","\"First day of the first month, Young Master went boating on the lake with companions, spending three hundred taels, including fifty taels for food and entertainment, and finally bought the boat he fancied for two hundred and fifty taels.\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","This fool spent so much money on a boat; why didn't he just buy the entire lake while he was at it?","\"Second day of the first month, Young Master set off firecrackers with others, killing three thousand chickens in the neighboring farmhouse, compensating one hundred taels.\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","This is practically a living King of Hell! How could he face those three thousand wrongfully deceased chickens!","\"Third day of the first month, Young Master went out...\"","...","Xu Wan grew increasingly numb as she listened. That little troublemaker spent hundreds of taels every day, compared to her measly one tael of pocket money, he was truly a champion of wasteful spending.","The reading stopped after the seventh day—","She looked at Cui Zhi.","What's wrong? Afraid she couldn't handle more shocking news?","\"It's fine. Continue, I can take it,\" she had seen worse.","However, Cui Zhi said: \"Today is the eighth day of the first month, and the Young Master hasn't gone out...\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","Right, he hadn't gone out.","For the first seven days of the new year, he had been out making trouble and wasting money every day. The one day he finally stayed home, he terrorized his stepmother, causing her bridal veil to be blown up and humiliating her in front of the entire capital.","Just thinking about it made Xu Wan's anger surge!","\"Where is that brat now? Did the Old Marchioness punish him before leaving?\"","For such a major offense on such an important occasion, according to the rules of their Minister's Mansion, the severe punishment would have been a thorough beating, and the light punishment would have been kneeling in the ancestral hall for several days.","She couldn't believe Zong Jincheng could be fine!","However, Cui Zhi timidly said: \"The Old Marchioness never had the heart to punish the Young Master, so he's still comfortably staying in his courtyard...\"","Xu Wan's heart tightened as she sat down, constantly encouraging herself.","Stay calm, think about the astronomical salary...","A base salary of 300,000 per month with no liability, which would be considered super high-paying even in modern times, plus a one-time cash bonus of 100 million upon success.","100 million, 100 million.","Teaching a troublesome kid was nothing compared to that!!","When Xu Wan opened her eyes again, they were sharp. At this moment, she was no longer a passive stepmother but a competitive one, in full battle mode.","\"Go, call Zong Jincheng here. I need to have a word with him.\"","\"Yes.\"","Cui Zhi sent someone to fetch the Young Master.","Meanwhile, Xu Wan thought about how to educate the little devil.","The 100-million goal required him to achieve top ranks in the imperial examinations, which meant he needed to study in the study room first, but she remembered the Old Marquis saying this troublemaker hadn't entered the study room for a month.","Moreover, the little troublemaker currently harbored strong hostility towards her and wouldn't follow her arrangements.","Xu Wan wondered if she should use reverse psychology, but remembering that kid's cunning smile, she feared he wouldn't fall for her tricks so easily.","Perhaps she should try the opposite approach...","\"My Lady.\" A little maid ran in from outside, looking troubled, \"The Young Master refuses to come. He's preparing to go out and doesn't plan to return to the manor tonight. He also said... he said as long as you don't leave the Marquis Manor, he won't come to the main courtyard.\"","Xu Wan thought: Huh! Come or don't come, I'd rather not deal with your trouble!","Though this result was unexpected, it was also understandable. If the little devil would obediently come to listen to her lecture, he wouldn't be worth the 100 million reward.","Xu Wan had already adjusted her mindset and had a rough plan of action.","Beside her, Cui Zhi saw her silence and thought she was out of ideas, so she stepped forward to suggest: \"My Lady, shall we have the Young Master forcibly brought back?\"","Xu Wan raised an eyebrow: \"We can do that? Didn't the Old Marchioness leave instructions about not harming him?\"","Cui Zhi shook her head: \"The Old Marchioness said you could discipline him as you see fit.\"","\"The Old Marchioness is surprisingly open-minded.\" So open-minded that Xu Wan thought she must be a fake grandmother. Weren't grandparents supposed to be the most doting?","Cui Zhi explained: \"The Old Marchioness and Old Marquis have always doted on the Young Master. Since childhood, forget about beating or scolding, they haven't even reprimanded him. The Young Master was born with a likable smile that makes it hard for anyone to be harsh with him... But as he grew older, he became increasingly unruly. The Old Marchioness finally realized this problem, which is why she asked for your help in teaching him.\"","Xu Wan's mouth twitched as she thought, that makes sense.","If even his own grandparents couldn't bear to hit him, only a stepmother would have the heart to do so.","However, beating and scolding children was the worst approach, not suitable unless absolutely necessary.","\"Going out to play, is he...\" Xu Wan's lips curved slightly upward as she formulated her strategy.","Little troublemaker, you think you're tough?","I'll make you understand who provides the resources for your arrogance.","\"Cut off all his expenses, stop his source of money, leave him with nowhere to eat, nowhere to stay, nowhere to cause trouble, until he has no choice but to return to the manor.\""]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5: The Failed Door-Kicking Little Demon King","paragraphs":["At Qingbo Lake.","The little tyrant was confidently patting his chest, saying to his playmates with bravado, \"Eat and drink as you please! Young Master Zong will cover all expenses today!\"","\"How generous of Young Master Zong!\"","\"Jincheng is truly my best brother!\"","\"Jincheng is so magnanimous!\"","Everyone knew that the Yangyuan Marquis Manor was as wealthy as a nation, and its only legitimate grandson was treasured like a jewel, often spending money lavishly. Thus, many people gathered around to curry favor with him.","Zong Jincheng's mood improved as he listened to everyone's flattery; it was indeed more pleasant outside than in the manor.","When it came time to pay the bill, Zong Jincheng was about to leave with his group, as usually the servants would stay behind to settle the payment.","However, unexpectedly, the manor's steward suddenly appeared and said something to his servant, who hastily handed over all the money he was carrying.","Moreover, they hadn't even paid the bill yet, and the merchant was now looking at him with the eyes of a debt collector.","The smile on Zong Jincheng's face instantly froze: \"Steward Liu, what is the meaning of this?\"","The other young nobles gathered around, looking at Zong Jincheng in confusion.","Someone suddenly spoke up: \"Jincheng said he would pay for today's bill. What's Steward Liu playing at? Is this some good cop, bad cop routine to get out of paying?\"","Zong Jincheng was stung by the accusation of trying to dodge payment.","How could he, the legitimate grandson of the marquis and future young lord, possibly try to evade paying a bill?","The little tyrant suppressed his anger and ordered, \"Steward Liu, settle the bill.\"","Steward Liu apologetically replied, \"I'm sorry, young master, but the madam has ordered that all your expenses be suspended. Please return to the manor with me.\"","Upon hearing this, the others immediately understood: \"Oh, so you're being controlled by your stepmother.\"","\"Jincheng, you've met your match this time. Your stepmother is really putting you in your place.\"","\"Oh dear, oh dear, the young master of the marquis manor is trying to skip out on the bill.\"","The jeering voices grew louder, and Zong Jincheng rarely blushed. He angrily said, \"If she just wants me to go back to the manor to hear her lecture, fine, I'll go. Just pay the bill first.\"","Steward Liu kept his head lowered and apologetically said, \"I'm sorry, young master, but I cannot disobey the madam's orders. I cannot settle this bill for you.\"","Currently, Xu Wan was the lady of the house at the marquis manor, and he could only follow her orders.","This was also specifically instructed by the old madam before she left.","\"You...\" Zong Jincheng finally understood how it felt to be angered by someone.","But he knew Steward Liu's uncompromising nature; he definitely wouldn't pay the bill today.","The little tyrant anxiously removed the jade pendant from his waist and threw it to the merchant, then stormed off toward the manor in a huff.","The other young masters followed, gleefully discussing how Zong Jincheng would have no peace in the future, their laughter carrying far into the distance.","After everyone had left, Steward Liu rubbed his nose, thinking to himself that the madam had calculated correctly - without money to pay the bill, the young master could only settle it with his personal belongings.","The meal only cost a few dozen taels, but that jade pendant was worth three thousand taels. If pawned, it could cover quite a lot of expenses. But the young master had no concept of money's value and wouldn't think about whether it was worth it or not.","How could he possibly match up against the madam like this...","\"Ah...\"","At the marquis manor.","Zong Jincheng angrily ran inside, with servants chasing after him.","Xu Wan was leisurely drinking premium Biluochun tea, thinking to herself how wonderful the life of the wealthy was.","\"Cui Zhi, keep the courtyard gate open. We don't want the young master breaking it in his anger - that door looks expensive.\"","Cui Zhi responded with a light laugh: \"Yes, I'll go open it right away.\"","Zong Jincheng swore he had never been so humiliated in his life. Just thinking about how those people had mocked him made his blood boil.","It was all because of this woman.","Everything changed when she arrived.","Before she came to the manor, his life had been so carefree. Now that his grandparents weren't around, she was taking every opportunity to bully him.","Zong Jincheng gathered his strength, preparing to kick her door down and teach her a harsh lesson.","But when he kicked...","Damn it, why was the door already open?!","The little tyrant, having kicked at nothing, nearly fell face-first.","He stumbled, quickly looked around to make sure no one had seen, then straightened his clothes and walked in angrily as if nothing had happened.","Xu Wan was drinking tea when Cui Liu, the martial arts-trained maid, came over and whispered the situation at the door in her ear, nearly making her spray out her tea.","\"Pfft, how can this boy be so amusing?\"","He couldn't possibly think that just because he couldn't see others, they couldn't see him.","When Zong Jincheng entered, he saw Xu Wan laughing heartily, with five or six maids attending to her throughout the courtyard. The table was laden with delicacies and drinks, and this woman, wrapped in a snow-white fur coat, sat in a comfortable chair holding a large hand warmer, half-squinting her eyes as she basked in the sunlight, completely at ease.","Thinking back to his recent embarrassment made him even angrier by comparison.","\"Give me back my money.\" The little tyrant sat at the stone table, speaking to her furiously.","Xu Wan glanced at him and said amusingly, \"Why are you so angry? It's just one meal. Even if you couldn't pay at the moment, didn't your friends help? According to the accounts, you've treated them to plenty of meals and drinks. What's wrong with letting them treat you for once?\"","Zong Jincheng's face reddened at her words. He snorted, \"Stop playing innocent. Steward Liu must have told you everything. Yes, they didn't help me pay, but that's because I had promised to treat them today. If you hadn't sent Steward Liu to stop me, how could I have lost so much face?\"","The little fellow argued righteously: \"If word gets out, people will think our marquis manor is stingy and doesn't keep its promises. You almost ruined my grandparents' lifetime of good reputation.\"","\"Tsk, you're quite good at making serious accusations, aren't you?\" Xu Wan looked at him with new respect; this little tyrant wasn't just a pretty face after all.","Zong Jincheng thought he had intimidated her and immediately said sternly, \"Return the money, and we'll stay out of each other's way.\"","He had no interest in the manor's authority and thought his grandmother's agreement with her was pointless.","\"Too late.\" Xu Wan stood up from her chair and pointed to the setting sun, \"See that? The sun hasn't set yet, and my wedding day isn't over. You made me lose face, so you've already crossed the line. It can't be undone, and it's unforgivable.\"","\"You!\" The little tyrant clenched his fists, \"What exactly do you want?\"","\"What I want, you should know clearly. The old madam didn't hide it from you when she spoke to me.\" Because of the old madam's openness, Xu Wan had to be straightforward with him, \"You cooperate with me and study well. Once you achieve top honors in the imperial examinations, you can be the young marquis and manage the household, and I'll take my money and leave. We both get what we want.\"","This was a win-win arrangement, and it was also the old madam's intention, but they had all underestimated this rebellious child's determination.","Zong Jincheng decisively declared, \"I don't like studying, and I won't take any imperial examinations! Whatever agreement you have with grandmother is your business - I absolutely won't cooperate!\"","\"That's not up to you.\" Xu Wan had anticipated his resistance and wasn't surprised by his defiance.","\"Steward Liu, go collect all the valuable items from the young master's rooms and keep them safe. We can't have him pawning off more of the manor's precious things. A jade pendant worth three thousand taels, used to pay for just one meal - what a waste, what a waste.\"","\"Yes,\" Steward Liu acknowledged and led people to search Zong Jincheng's quarters.","Zong Jincheng: \"???\"","\"Hey! This is outright robbery!\"","\"Steward Liu! Have you gone mad? I'm the young master of this manor!\"","\"You dare listen to this woman and bully me? I'm writing to grandmother!\""]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6: The Little Demon's Counterattack","paragraphs":["The little fellow ran after them, shouting as he chased, causing the maids along the way to turn their heads.","But Steward Liu, who was following orders, remained as stubborn as iron.","From the small courtyard came the angry roars of the little tyrant:","\"You can't take this away, it's my favorite lounge chair!\"","\"Not this pillow, what am I supposed to rest my head on!\"","\"Shoes! Shoes! Am I really so poor that I need to sell my shoes?!\"","\"You all... are shameless!\"","The little tyrant tried frantically to stop them, but he couldn't jump as high as they could, and he didn't know any martial arts, so he could only hop around uselessly.","When Xu Wan came to call him for dinner, she found the little tyrant's voice had gone hoarse, and he was slumped against the doorframe, muttering non-stop: \"Bastards... fair-weather friends... ungrateful wretches... to think how well this young master treated you all before...\"","Looking inside, the entire room had been stripped bare, its emptiness shocking to behold.","Xu Wan blinked in surprise, not expecting Steward Liu to be so thorough, actually taking away everything valuable as she had instructed.","\"You're even taking my clothes, are you trying to force this young master to walk around naked?!\"","Zong Jincheng was tired of cursing. He was very hungry now and desperately wanted a feast.","Just then, an appetizing aroma wafted over. The little tyrant turned his head to see Cui Zhi carrying a tray with two fragrant chicken legs.","He swallowed hard, then glanced to the side to see Xu Wan's unsympathetic face.","Evil woman, what a waste of that pretty face.","\"Young Master Jincheng, tired from all that shouting? Have something to eat,\" Xu Wan gestured outside, reminding him, \"It's dark now, time for dinner.\"","Zong Jincheng gave her a cold look but held out his hand, and Cui Zhi quickly brought the tray over.","The little tyrant usually had impeccable table manners, but today he was so angry and exhausted that he didn't even wash his hands, grabbing the chicken legs and devouring them directly.","Cui Zhi, who had watched him grow up since he was little, had never seen the young master so defeated before, and couldn't help but smile.","That small smile was caught by the little tyrant, who shot her a fierce glare. He now saw everyone in the Marquis Manor as Xu Wan's people.","At least Xu Wan had some conscience, not forcing him to go without food unless he entered the study. She waited until the little fellow had finished both chicken legs before slowly speaking: \"The meals are served in the main hall. If you want anything else to eat, go there as you please. From now on, all three meals will be served there. Eat whatever the kitchen prepares, no being picky. Otherwise, you'll have to figure out your own meals.\"","Xu Wan spoke calmly, seemingly without threat, yet firmly establishing the rules.","Zong Jincheng was spoiled and difficult to please, of course picky with food, but now under Xu Wan's control, he was isolated and helpless. Being stubborn would only leave him hungry.","The little fellow's eyes darted around before he responded, \"I understand.\" Then he stood up and went to the main hall to eat.","The evening passed peacefully. After dinner, Xu Wan returned to her room to rest. The maids helped her bathe and lie down on the enormous luxury bed, where she could roll around comfortably in any direction.","Looking at the red canopy and the crimson decor throughout the room, Xu Wan remembered that today was supposed to be her wedding night with Zong Zhao, but he had been missing for years. She was probably history's first bride to spend her wedding night alone.","But this was fine too - it meant fewer people to deal with.","She was exhausted from the busy day. Although everyone in the manor had cooperated with her actions, from taking over the household keys to matching wits with the little tyrant, so many things had happened that she was mentally drained...","The next day.","Xu Wan rarely slept until the sun was high in the sky, with sunlight streaming through the windows onto her eyes.","\"Cui Zhi, what time is it?\"","\"My lady, it's the fourth quarter of the si hour.\" [Around 10 AM]","Xu Wan was still groggy, but upon hearing this, she shot up in bed.","Ten o'clock!","Ancient people, lacking rich nightlife activities, believed in early to bed and early to rise. Her father would go to court at four or five in the morning, and the women of the household would also rise early with him.","This was the first time she had woken up so late since arriving here.","\"Is there... nothing scheduled today? Why didn't you wake me?\" It was her first time sleeping in so late, and Xu Wan felt a bit embarrassed.","Cui Zhi smiled and said, \"Today should have been when the new bride serves tea to her in-laws, but since the Old Marquis and Old Marchioness aren't here, you didn't need to rise early.\"","Xu Wan thought about it and agreed.","So, she lay back down.","Cui Zhi asked, \"Are you hungry, my lady? Should I bring you some porridge?\"","Xu Wan waved her hand: \"No need, I'll rest a bit more... Oh right, what about Zong Jincheng? Did that boy properly go to the main hall for meals?\"","\"Yes, the young master was very obedient and went,\" Cui Zhi praised, \"Only you could manage this, my lady. Before, the Old Marchioness could never get the young master to go, but now he comes without reminder at mealtimes.\"","While the praise was satisfying to hear, Xu Wan felt something was off.","Especially remembering how the little tyrant had rolled his eyes before leaving yesterday... how could he become so obedient?","\"Something's not right. He's up to something.\"","Xu Wan threw off her covers and got up, efficiently dressing herself, leaving the waiting maids with no chance to help.","Only at the end, when it came to styling her hair, did she let them assist. But Xu Wan wasn't idle: \"Cui Liu, go investigate where Zong Jincheng went after waking up, who he met, what he did, and report back to me with every detail.\"","\"Yes, my lady.\" Cui Liu accepted the task and left to carry it out.","While doing her hair, Cui Zhi smiled: \"My lady, are you worried the young master is plotting something?\"","Xu Wan snorted: \"That boy is clever. Before, he only needed to cry and throw tantrums to deal with his grandparents, but now he faces me, a stranger as his stepmother. This might bring out a different kind of evil in him.\"","\"A different kind of evil?\" Cui Zhi frowned.","She felt the word was too harsh. Though their young master was mischievous, he was pure-hearted and wouldn't intentionally harm others.","Xu Wan looked at two hairpins on the dressing table - one simple and elegant jade pin, one luxurious gold pin.","Previously, she would have chosen the jade pin for its clean look.","But now...","The woman picked up the gold pin and handed it to Cui Zhi: \"Everyone has evil thoughts; the difference lies in their bottom line. Some have low standards and will do anything to achieve their goals; others have higher standards and lack the courage to act on their evil thoughts.\"","Little troublemaker, let's see where your bottom line is.","Fully dressed, Xu Wan walked out. She usually ate in her own courtyard, but information was harder to come by there, so she followed Cui Zhi to the main hall.","By this time, the hall was empty.","Xu Wan sat in her seat, casually sipping porridge while occasionally looking up to observe the maids coming and going outside. From the main seat, she could see everything clearly.","Cui Liu came in to report: \"The young master woke up at the chen hour [7-9 AM], came to eat after waking, then went to the stables. He didn't interact with anyone outside his courtyard during this time.\"","\"Not in the manor...\" Xu Wan rolled her neck, putting herself in Zong Jincheng's shoes, trying to figure out what the boy was thinking.","He must be thinking...","He's now penniless, and it would be difficult to get money from his stepmother. Only if the stepmother left the Marquis Manor could he return to his former position.","Or if the stepmother voluntarily gave up her household authority and begged the grandmother to return for support, then he might have a chance to persuade his grandmother to cancel this boring education plan.","Just as Xu Wan was considering the second possibility, several maids rushed in with urgent reports:","\"My lady, there's trouble in the back courtyard, two maids are fighting in the laundry room!\"","\"My lady, Auntie Hong from the second household has lost something, saying it was a gift from the Second Master when he was alive!\"","\"My lady, the newly hired maids were fooling around and set fire to the kitchen!\""]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7: You Should Call Me Mother","paragraphs":["Xu Wan clenched her fingers and raised her eyebrows with a smile. \"As expected, they've come.\"","\"Cui Liu, take some people to put out the fire in the kitchen first.\"","There were priorities to handle, and right now the most urgent matter was to protect the mansion. The disputes among maids were trivial in comparison.","\"Yes.\" Cui Liu led a group of people to the kitchen.","Behind them, Cui Zhi secretly marveled at the new mistress's reaction. To remain so calm in the face of multiple crises - such composure and steadiness was rare in such a young bride.","The new mistress was reportedly only eighteen years old.","It was unexpected that the Minister of Justice's second wife had raised such an excellent daughter. The old madam truly had good judgment.","The other two maids who had come to report news quickly said, \"Madam, our matters are urgent too. Why did you send everyone to deal with the fire?\"","Xu Wan smiled, \"Should we wait until the entire Marquis Manor burns down? Cui Zhi, detain these two and await punishment.\"","\"Yes.\"","The two maids were completely stunned, never expecting that just one comment would get them arrested like thieves.","But they quickly recovered and cried out, \"Why are you detaining us, Madam? We came to report news, what wrong have we done?\"","\"Don't touch me! I used to serve in the young master's quarters. If you dare lay hands on me, the old madam won't let you off when she returns!\"","Of the two maids, one took a soft approach while the other took a hard one. The softer one appeared foolish, but the aggressive one was more concerning. At her words, even Cui Zhi took a step back.","Cui Liu's brows also furrowed.","The young master was the manor's only taboo subject.","His belongings and servants were treated like treasures, as the old madam often used them to remember him.","Now that madam wanted to arrest a maid from the young master's quarters, this would be difficult to handle...","Seeing this, Xu Wan turned to ask Cui Zhi, \"I recall mother saying my husband had no concubines or personal maids. What was this maid's rank?\"","Cui Zhi lowered her head and replied, \"The young master had two maids serving him, both third-rank, lower than footmen and attendants. Hong Shao was only promoted to second-rank after the young master's disappearance, and was then assigned to work in the second household.\"","Hong Shao's face grew even more smug hearing this.","The young master had promised that as long as she served his interests well, he would transfer her from the second household and make her a first-rank maid in his own quarters.","What did it matter if the new mistress had household authority? The young master was the future heir, and she had served in his quarters - the new mistress wouldn't dare touch her!","\"The old madam misses the young master every day. If this servant is mistreated, the old madam will surely be heartbroken...\" Hong Shao deliberately left her sentence unfinished, clearly implying that the old madam would strip the new mistress of her authority over the household.","Cui Zhi frowned but was also intimidated, appearing completely different from her previously capable and efficient self, knowing how much the old madam valued anyone connected to the young master.","Xu Wan observed both Hong Shao's arrogance and Cui Zhi's hesitation, naturally understanding the underlying dynamics.","So, as everyone watched expectantly for drama, Xu Wan casually said, \"Then send her to the villa so she can be close to the old madam and let her 'remember through objects' up close.\"","Cui Zhi, who had been looking down, suddenly raised her head, feeling at this moment that madam's face seemed to be glowing.","Could... could they really handle it this way?","Hong Shao, who had been feeling smug, immediately changed expression.","She stared at Xu Wan in shock, never expecting the new mistress would come up with this solution to deal with her!","While the old madam wasn't in the manor, she could throw her weight around based on seniority, but if she went to the old madam's side, wouldn't she lose all standing?","Realizing something was wrong, Hong Shao finally understood she had underestimated Xu Wan.","She quickly knelt down and knocked her head three times, begging, \"Please retract your order, Madam! The old madam and old marquis are away relaxing - this servant wouldn't dare disturb them!\"","If she was sent to the villa over this matter, the old madam would surely learn she had been causing trouble for the new mistress, and might not spare her even for the young master's sake.","Xu Wan smiled faintly and retorted, \"Go on then, after all, the old madam misses the young master daily and surely can't do without you. Isn't that right, Cui Zhi?\"","Cui Zhi burst out laughing - the new mistress was truly clever and witty, using Hong Shao's own words to checkmate her.","She kept laughing as she replied, \"Madam speaks truly.\"","\"Someone come and escort Hong Shao to the villa.\"","Xu Wan remembered something else: \"Oh right, there was another maid in my husband's quarters, what was her name?\"","\"Lu Ru.\"","\"Ah yes, send her along too.\" This would prevent that little brat from inciting another servant to cause trouble for her.","Better to resolve it completely and cut off this avenue entirely.","Cui Zhi exchanged glances with the other maids, all giving Xu Wan thumbs up in approval.","As Hong Shao was dragged away crying and wailing, Lu Ru, who had suddenly been implicated, began cursing Hong Shao. The two hurled abuse at each other as they were taken away, each more vulgar than the last.","Xu Wan frowned at the sound.","How did Zong Zhao end up with such maids?","Cui Zhi called out instructions: \"Such shouting and cursing is unseemly. Gag them and put them in the carriage - don't shame the Yangyuan Marquis Manor.\"","\"Yes.\"","Xu Wan watched as the two maids were taken away. Just as she was about to turn back to the manor, Zong Jincheng came running in angrily, calling out to her: \"Hey!\"","Hey yourself, you little brat.","Xu Wan ignored him and continued walking inside.","Zong Jincheng chased after her in frustration, calling out again: \"Hey! Can't you hear me calling you? It's very rude to ignore people - stop walking!\"","The little troublemaker blocked her path, preventing her from leaving.","The boy before her was still dressed in fine silks, his round eyes filled with anger, beads of sweat on his forehead as if he'd run a long way.","Clearly he'd heard about the two maids being sent away and was upset.","Xu Wan looked at him and said seriously, \"By status, you should call me mother. Even if you dislike me, you should at least address me as madam, not shout 'hey.' Moreover, I am your elder - between us, you are clearly the more discourteous one.\"","\"More discourteous\" was typically praise, but the main clause was criticism.","The little demon lord didn't have much education to begin with. After being both praised and scolded in one breath, it took him several seconds to realize she was scolding rather than complimenting him, immediately making his face flush red with anger.","\"You... you've gone too far! Those were my father's favorite maids, and you sent them to the villa!\"","Zong Jincheng tried to pull rank again, never mentioning his own status directly while constantly reminding everyone that he was the legitimate grandson of this marquis family.","Unfortunately, Xu Wan saw right through it.","She seized on his choice of words and counterattacked in his own style: \"My husband only had those two maids - if they were really so favored, wouldn't they have been promoted to second rank long ago? Why wait for my mother-in-law to do it?\"","You little brat, don't take advantage of them all being your relatives to talk nonsense.","She was now part of this family too - Zong Zhao's wife, the old madam's daughter-in-law, Zong Jincheng's mother.","None of their statuses were that much higher than the others!","Zong Jincheng was left speechless by her retort. After a while, he finally managed to respond: \"My father was used to their service. What if father suddenly returns and isn't comfortable with different maids serving him?\""]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8: Damn it, I won't beg for mercy.","paragraphs":["Xu Wan: \"Are you suggesting that my husband couldn't survive these eight years without those two?\"","Little Demon King: \"...\"","What she said did make sense!","Though the little one admitted this in his heart, his mouth remained harder than freshly baked bricks.","\"Have you found the items missing from Concubine Hong's room? And the maids fighting—such things never happened in the Marquis Manor before. It's all because of your poor management since you arrived. If you can't handle these two matters properly, it proves you're incapable of managing the manor!\"","Xu Wan remained unmoved: \"So?\"","Zong Jincheng spoke with growing confidence, snorting haughtily: \"I heard you never managed household affairs at the Minister's Mansion, so it's no surprise you can't handle our grand Marquis Manor. Here's the deal: if you say 'I give up' a hundred times and sincerely repent your mistakes, I'll forgive your previous actions and ask Grandmother to return and help clean up your mess.\"","\"Oh...\" Xu Wan responded indifferently, even somewhat disappointedly, \"I thought you were going to say that since I can't manage this household, you would do it.\"","\"Ah, how disappointing.\"","Zong Jincheng: \"...\"","He truly hated this feeling of punching into cotton.","The other maids, seeing the young master at a loss, were desperately trying to hold back their laughter, though their attempts were rather obvious due to lack of practice.","Zong Jincheng grew angry with embarrassment from their laughter.","He raised his little paw and fiercely said to Xu Wan: \"You'd better quit while you're ahead! Otherwise, when this manor falls into chaos, how will we explain it to my grandmother!\"","The little one spoke with puffed cheeks, but to Xu Wan, he looked particularly amusing, like a silly little frog.","Xu Wan said with a smile: \"Kid, your mother is in a good mood right now, so I'll teach you a lesson today: never underestimate anyone.\"","\"Nagging woman, only a fool would listen to your lectures.\" Zong Jincheng quickly turned away, plugging his ears with his hands.","Not listening, not listening, like a turtle reciting sutras.","Xu Wan watched him unilaterally blocking everyone out and rolled her eyes heavenward.","Indeed, only children would plug their ears like this.","But in fact, it was useless—he could still hear everything.","Xu Wan completely ignored his 'do not disturb' state and deliberately leaned close to his ear, shouting: \"Cui Zhi, tell the young master how these two matters would be handled if the Old Marchioness were in the manor?\"","Zong Jincheng: \"???\"","How could you be so excessive!!","Cui Zhi had always felt helpless about these two's sparring. Though the lady was clever, she had a childish temperament, and her arguments with the young master were more like children's squabbles, making her want to smile fondly.","She smiled, curtsied, and cleared her throat before instructing the maids on both sides: \"You two go help search for Concubine Hong's belongings. Check everything inside and out, find out when the items went missing, who passed through during that time, and whether the maids in the courtyard are clean. If you find anyone with sticky fingers, send them straight to the authorities.\"","\"Yes.\"","\"You two, make a list of the fighting maids. No need for beatings or deducting their monthly allowance. Call the Human Trafficker and have them taken away to be sold. We can't afford to keep such brazen maids in our Marquis Manor.\"","\"Yes.\"","Cui Zhi dealt with both matters efficiently, resolving everything in just two brief sentences.","As expected of the head maid, truly impressive.","Xu Wan nodded with satisfaction and gave her a round of applause.","The Little Demon King watched in shock from the side. Although he had plugged his ears, he could still hear Cui Zhi's words clearly.","All those maids' actions had been at his instigation, yet now some were to be sent to the authorities and others to be sold—neither group would meet a good end!","Though Zong Jincheng was mischievous, he wasn't a heartless villain. How could he bear bringing such trouble to others?","He quickly unplugged his ears and ran after them, shouting: \"Stop! Don't go!\"","The departing maids only listened to Xu Wan and Cui Zhi, paying no attention to the Little Demon King's shouts. After taking a few futile steps in pursuit, the little one ran back to Xu Wan and Cui Zhi, crying out:","\"You're going too far! They just had a fight, why do you have to sell them?\"","Zong Jincheng couldn't understand at all.","Because in his view, fighting was as simple as eating and drinking. He wrestled and raced horses with others every day, having great fun.","Never, never had anyone punished him like this.","Xu Wan didn't evade his questioning, but looked down at the naive Little Demon King before her and replied: \"If you did these things, you could just walk away without any consequences, relying on the manor's indulgence. But they're different—they don't have your privileged birth or any backing. If they make mistakes, they'll be thrown out of the Marquis Manor or even sent to prison, with no one to protect them.\"","\"Zong Jincheng, the Old Marchioness entrusted you to me because she couldn't bear to discipline you herself, but she also couldn't bear to watch you continue learning bad habits. So I think it's time you understood from another perspective what kind of person your grandmother really is.\"","\"All household affairs in the Marquis Manor are managed by your grandmother. The rules of the house and Cui Zhi's solutions just now were all established by her. She manages both the household and its people effortlessly, and all the servants in the manor are well-trained. They simply don't hold you accountable, but that doesn't make them fools.\"","\"And neither am I.\"","Zong Jincheng stared at her blankly: \"You...\"","This woman was clearly telling him that she had the same capabilities as his grandmother but wouldn't spoil him like she did...","After delivering her harsh words, Xu Wan's expression instantly changed to a smile, like a crafty little fox.","She turned her head and instructed: \"Steward Liu, I think Jincheng has too many servants around him. Let's reduce them from six to one.\"","Between instigating fights among maids, stealing things, and setting fires, there was clearly an excess of manpower.","His wings needed to be clipped further.","\"Yes, my lady,\" Steward Liu responded.","\"You!\"","Zong Jincheng's momentary shame instantly vanished, replaced by anger at Xu Wan's words.","First she cut off his money, and now she'd leave him with just one servant—was she trying to raise him like a beggar?!","This evil woman.","She was clearly seeking revenge, taking the opportunity to bully him!","\"A tiger fallen to the plains is bullied by dogs... How despicable! Don't think I'll beg you for mercy!\"","\"Go ahead and keep doing this if you dare. When Grandmother sees how badly you've mistreated me, she'll definitely settle accounts with you, and neither of us will have a good time!\"","\"Hmph!\"","The Little Demon King delivered his threats and turned to leave.","Xu Wan casually fanned the flames from behind: \"Jincheng, why are you getting angry so easily? Weren't you planning to go to the horse grounds? Why are you going back to your room?\"","Then she added: \"Oh right, I remember the horse grounds are free to enter, so you can go play without worry.\"","The Little Demon King felt worse with every word he heard, plugging his ears as he ran away frantically.","How infuriating!","This woman just wanted to make a fool of him!","What nonsense about it being free—all the young masters at the horse grounds had two or three attendants with them. If he went there with just one servant now, he'd be laughed to death.","Vicious!","How utterly vicious!"]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9: Naughty Little Demon","paragraphs":["Xu Wan watched the little fellow's running silhouette, looking just like a monkey, and couldn't help but chuckle, \"Oh, was he always this funny before?\"","Cui Zhi shook her head in horror: \"The young master was never funny.\"","No joke - who would dare make fun of a child pampered by the entire Marquis Manor!","Only the madam was bold enough to throw off her bridal veil and get ready for a fight...","Xu Wan said softly, \"Then he'll have many more funny days ahead.\"","Cui Zhi: \"...\"","Somehow, she wished the old madam would come back to see this.","At lunchtime.","As soon as Xu Wan entered the dining hall, she saw the little tyrant's eyes blazing like fire. Having already exhausted his harsh words from the morning, he could only glare at her frantically.","Attempting to... kill her with his gaze.","Xu Wan: \"...\"","What a childish technique.","But she had seen even fiercer cold stares when she was young; this child's trick wasn't anything special.","She sat down calmly and teased lightly, \"You don't actually think you can kill someone with a look, do you?\"","\"...\" The little tyrant's face instantly reddened when exposed.","But he quickly became righteous again.","\"I'll still make life difficult for you!\"","Zong Jincheng took up a stance of absolute opposition to her, appearing as if his pride could never be broken, which drew a light snort from Xu Wan.","How childish, so childish...","The maids nearby bustled about serving the dishes, placing them one by one on the table, each perfect in appearance, aroma, and taste.","Xu Wan picked up her chopsticks and tried a piece of lotus leaf-smoked duck.","Hmm...","The food at the Marquis Manor was indeed delicious.","Zong Jincheng felt hungry looking at all the dishes on the table.","He couldn't even bother complaining about Xu Wan's lack of manners for eating before he sat down... now she was the highest authority in the Marquis Manor, and everyone listened to her, so complaining would be pointless.","Hmph, grandmother will definitely regret this decision!","After the little fellow figured this out, he angrily sat down to eat, grabbing a bowl of rice with one hand while competing with Xu Wan's chopsticks for food with the other.","Whatever meat she picked up, he would go for the same piece;","Whatever vegetable she ate, he would snatch;","If she wanted soup, he would have someone serve him first.","He was determined to outdo her in everything, only then could he ease the hatred in his heart.","Cui Zhi and Cui Liu watched in amazement!","Was this really their young master who was so picky about food?!","Although the table was full of sumptuous dishes, there were hardly any that he actually liked!","Now, just to spite the madam, he had already eaten two large bowls of rice!","Good heavens!","Old madam!","Please come back and see this!","The young master has changed!!","Xu Wan pretended not to notice the little tyrant's food-snatching; she didn't eat much anyway, so eating less wouldn't matter.","But seeing the boy's cheeks puffed up with food, the anger in his eyes diluted, those eyes became even more beautiful, like stars in the deep sky.","She stirred slightly and asked, \"Are you full?\"","Zong Jincheng looked at the mess on the table, then at her bowl with barely half the rice eaten, and felt satisfied.","Just wait until you're starved for a month, then see if you still have the strength to fight with young master!","Zong Jingcheng ignored her and left after eating.","Leaving behind only a deliberately cold demeanor.","Xu Wan: \"...\"","You're such a childish spirit reborn!","After he walked away, she heard Cui Zhi and Cui Liu laughing. Xu Wan turned to look at them.","Cui Liu immediately pretended nothing had happened.","Only Cui Zhi said with a smile, \"At this rate of madam's provocation, the young master will gain three jin in a month.\"","Cui Liu added, \"But it's a good thing, the old madam always said he was too thin.\"","\"Let's quickly write to inform the old madam, she'll surely be happy for days when she knows.\"","\"Then we can have madam continue her efforts to fatten up the young master some more.\"","\"Yes, yes, yes.\"","The two chatted enthusiastically, each adding their own comments.","Xu Wan suddenly interjected: \"Then tell me, if I fatten him up by thirty jin, will the old madam give me extra rewards?\"","The old madam's hopes for her grandson's success shouldn't just focus on academic achievements, physical health is also very important!","Cui Zhi and Cui Liu: \"...\"","Thirty jin might be too much, the image was too beautiful to imagine.","But Xu Wan thought this was a good idea: \"I think it's feasible. Cui Zhi, mention it when you write to the old madam, I bet she'll agree.\"","The old madam's generous manner from yesterday was still fresh in her mind, and the money-loving Xu Wan had complete confidence in her.","Cui Zhi responded with a mixture of amusement and helplessness: \"Yes, this servant will do so right away.\"","The new madam was quite strange.","She seemed to love money and worked hard to earn lots of it, taking on the difficult young master and trying every way to match wits with him.","Yet she showed no interest in the authority to manage the Marquis Manor, completely entrusting it to the steward. The Marquis Manor was vast and wealthy - if she really became the managing mistress, wouldn't she have endless money to spend?","Really incomprehensible...","While Cui Zhi went to write the letter, Cui Liu accompanied Xu Wan to the study to see what subjects Zong Jincheng should be learning at his age.","As soon as they entered, the fragrance of books wafted over them.","Xu Wan walked in and saw various books arranged on the shelves, organized by difficulty level.","She casually asked, \"How far has Zong Jincheng progressed?\"","Cui Liu replied, \"The young master dislikes reading, he hasn't even memorized the Three Character Classic yet.\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","She had guessed he might be illiterate, but didn't expect him to be so thoroughly illiterate.","She picked up a book at random, opening the pristine pages and said, \"Ordinary children begin their education at seven, while officials' children start even earlier, at three or four. Zong Jincheng has truly been spoiled completely.\"","Cui Liu agreed.","But regarding the masters' affairs, she dared not comment inappropriately.","\"By the way, what's the name of the child the second branch brought back? How is his studies progressing?\"","Cui Liu said, \"That young master is called Zong Wenxiu. He lived in the slums since childhood and only had the chance to begin his education after being brought back to the manor before the new year. However, Master Wenxiu is exceptionally intelligent and studies very diligently. In just half a year, he has caught up with the progress of other noble children.\"","Xu Wan sighed inwardly.","This was truly a stark contrast!","If only the little tyrant were this reassuring, she would have to burn three incense sticks for him every morning in gratitude!","Throughout the afternoon, Xu Wan familiarized herself with the ancient children's curriculum in the study. The differences from modern education were neither too great nor too small.","Still, she had to find a way to get Zong Jincheng into the study to read.","Meanwhile, Cui Zhi kept receiving updates outside and reporting Zong Jincheng's activities to her:","\"After returning to his room, the young master sat on the doorstep lost in thought. During this time, he punched the door eight times, kicked the doorstep twelve times, and kicked the pebbles at the door thirty-three times.\"","\"Where did he get so many pebbles by his door?\"","Although Xu Wan had taken the valuable items from his courtyard, she hadn't added anything else.","\"It was one stone from a flower bed.\"","\"One stone? Kicked thirty-three times?\"","\"The young master had servants pick it up thirty-three times.\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","He truly was an ancestor who knew how to exhaust people."]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10: The Living King of Hell is Online","paragraphs":["\"Finally, Young Master played on the swing in the courtyard.\"","\"He would play such a boring activity as swinging?\" Xu Wan doubted it might be a super-sized swing.","If the rope broke, it wouldn't kill him.","\"Young Master doesn't play on the swing,\" Cui Liu replied.","\"?\"","\"It's the birds and cats that are swinging. There are eight cages hanging on the rope, four with birds and four with cats. Each bird has a cat glaring at it, and when Young Master swings the swing, the birds shriek in terror for the entire afternoon.\"","Xu Wan: \"......\"","The scene was already vivid in her mind. What a living devil!","\"But Madam, don't worry. These birds have been raised in Young Master's courtyard since they were little, so they are very resilient. Not a single one fainted after shrieking for the entire afternoon.\"","Xu Wan: \"......\"","No wonder they are birds raised by Zong Jincheng.","Their resilience is top-notch.","Xu Wan asked again, \"So, does he have any other serious activities to do? Does he study or practice martial arts?\"","At this point, Cui Liu suddenly fell silent.","Xu Wan turned to look at her.","She heard, \"Young Master really likes martial arts. General Zhao says he has great talent. If properly cultivated, he will surely become an outstanding general in the future. But as soon as the Old Marchioness heard that, she changed her face and forbade Young Master from touching any martial arts.\"","The ancestors of Yangyuan Marquis Manor were all born from military backgrounds, and the marquis title was won on the battlefield. But eight years ago, in that battle, the second son of the manor died, and the eldest son, who was said to be missing, was more likely because his body was never found.","The truth is something everyone knows.","Fortunately, Zong Zhao brought back Zong Jincheng before going to war, otherwise, the entire Yangyuan Marquis Manor might have become extinct.","No matter how strong the Old Marchioness is, she is still a mother. Losing a son in middle age is already extremely painful. If her grandson were to die on the battlefield in the future, it would be devastating for her.","Xu Wan quickly understood this and empathized with the Old Marchioness's decision. If it were her, she would probably make the same choice.","\"Besides martial arts, does he like polo or horse racing?\"","She still needed to find his interests.","Cui Liu said, \"Steward Liu just reported that the son of the Minister of Rites came to visit Young Master, inviting him to play polo at the horse racing field, but Young Master refused.\"","\"Ah?\" Xu Wan was stunned, \"Why?\"","Cui Liu initially didn't find it funny, but seeing that Xu Wan hadn't realized she was the culprit, she couldn't help but laugh, \"Madam, you forgot. You just reduced Young Master's servants from six to one. Young Master is probably too embarrassed to go out and play now.\"","\"Pfft, childish thinking. Even if others laugh at him, he's still the only legitimate grandson of the marquis manor! What's there to be embarrassed about? If I had his treatment, I'd be confident enough to go out and play every day.\" Xu Wan rolled her eyes to the sky, never expecting the little devil to care about his reputation.","Cui Liu said, \"Children's thoughts are indeed different from adults, especially since Young Master has always had a smooth life, never experiencing hardship, and easily gets hurt by others' ridicule.\"","Xu Wan nodded, \"I understand, he's like a flower in a greenhouse.\"","Cui Liu: \"......\"","What she wanted to express wasn't exactly that.","While they were talking, Cui Zhi walked over with a tray holding a purple luxurious gown.","\"Madam, this is the outfit for tomorrow's return to your family's home. Please try it on to see if it fits.\"","Xu Wan remembered that as a new bride, she had to return to her family's home after three days, even without her husband accompanying her. She would be the first in the entire capital to do so, and she could imagine what she would face.","Cui Zhi, being a capable maid, naturally understood her mistress's situation, so she chose a deep purple outfit for Xu Wan's return. Unlike her usual light-colored casual clothes, deep purple symbolizes the absolute status of the marquis's wife, exuding a sense of authority just by its presence.","Xu Wan touched the fabric of the dress, smooth and soft, made of the finest mulberry silk.","\"Not bad, I'll try it on.\"","The next day.","The marquis's wife returned to her family's home on the third day of marriage, attracting many curious onlookers who wanted to see the new bride's joke.","\"I heard that this marquis's wife took over the management of the manor on the day of her wedding, showing her remarkable skills. She must have a fierce appearance.\"","\"Of course, after all, she is the eldest daughter of the Minister of Justice. She must have inherited some of her father's true essence. Maybe she even used some underhanded means.\"","\"I'm curious, since the young marquis had to marry a chicken on his wedding day, will the marquis's wife return alone?\"","\"I also heard that the Old Marchioness and the Old Marquis went to a villa. There really isn't anyone else in the manor who can accompany her. She will definitely return alone.\"","\"After all, she's still a new bride. It's like living as a widow...\"","\"Looks glamorous, but actually lonely and desolate.\"","\"Alas...\"","Xu Wan put on her hairpins in the manor, dressed in a dignified and elegant manner. Her eyebrows were slightly long, her red lips slightly pursed. Wearing the deep purple matron's attire, she looked like a powerful matron when she raised her eyes, her clear eyes exuding a strong presence.","\"Cui Zhi, let's go.\"","As Cui Zhi followed Xu Wan out, they heard a clear voice of a young boy behind them:","\"Wait, I'm coming too!\"","Cui Zhi turned around in surprise.","The little boy wrapped in a snow-white tiger fur cape was none other than their mischievous little devil.","At this moment, he came, wouldn't he cause trouble again?","Cui Liu, being straightforward, directly blocked him and refused without hesitation, \"Young Master, this is Madam's return to her family's home. It's always been with her husband, how could she take a child?\"","Moreover, he wasn't Xu Wan's biological son. If he went back, it would be showing off, and people would only find more ways to slander Madam.","Although they didn't have deep feelings for the new madam yet, after these two days of interaction, they found her to be a good person. Besides, she also had the Old Marchioness's favor, so they naturally did their best to protect Xu Wan.","Zong Jincheng was seeing Cui Liu being so impolite to him for the first time. He wanted to shout back angrily, but seeing Xu Wan's face, his eyes rolled, and he immediately changed his demeanor.","The little devil cleared his throat, shook his round head like a big white clumsy cat, and spoke in a pretentious manner, \"I'm just feeling sorry for you going home alone. I generously decided to accompany you! If you admit your mistake and return the people and things to me, I might consider giving you a step down.\"","His voice got smaller and smaller, almost inaudible, clearly lacking confidence.","Xu Wan watched him shake his head and sway, his nose slightly red from the cold, his small face white and pretty, with an almost invisible dimple near his mouth. If he smiled, it would be very noticeable.","In that moment, she understood again why the manor indulged him so much. With such a beautiful and cute appearance, it's easy to let your views be swayed by your looks.","Xu Wan turned around and walked out.","She just wouldn't look, and she wouldn't feel soft-hearted!"]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11: The Provocative Little Demon King","paragraphs":["After struggling to hold back his words for so long, Zong Jincheng was stunned when she didn't even respond, his face instantly changing through various colors.","Just as he was about to shout out loud,","he heard her say: \"If you want to come, then follow. It's just an extra pair of chopsticks - the Minister's Mansion won't miss feeding you one more mouth.\"","\"As for wanting anything else, impossible—\"","Xu Wan dragged out her words lazily, as if deliberately teasing him.","The little demon king was burning with rage, the threads of rationality in his mind snapping one by one.","How infuriating!","This woman who showed him no face at all!","One day he would definitely trample her under his feet!","Make her shout \"I was wrong!\" to the heavens a hundred times!!!","However, thoughts aside.","At present, Zong Jincheng took several deep breaths and still swallowed his pride to follow her.","Since he had nowhere else to play, he might as well go to the Minister's Mansion and see what trouble he could cause for Xu Wan.","If he couldn't be comfortable, he wouldn't let her be at ease either.","Better yet if he could find her weakness and defeat her in one stroke, making it impossible for her to return to the Marquis Manor!","\"They're coming out, they're coming out! Make way, make way, don't push me!\"","\"My goodness, worthy of being the eldest daughter of the Minister's Mansion - her beauty is no less than the Capital City's number one talented lady.\"","\"The Marquis Manor's eldest grandson came out too, actually following along with the Marquis's wife. Could it be he's accompanying the new bride on her home visit?\"","\"A stepson accompanying on a home visit, though unusual, seems somewhat reasonable. It seems the Marquis's wife isn't just beautiful but also capable, having trained this stepson to be so obedient.\"","Zong Jincheng was just about to get into the sedan chair when he heard these words. His barely contained dignity instantly crumbled under the weight of his anger.","He stepped back outside and, hands on his hips, shouted at the commoners: \"What nonsense are you spouting? If anyone's doing the training, it's this young master training her!\"","Steward Liu, who knew everything: \"???\"","The young master training the madam?","Was he just putting on a brave face?!","After throwing out such harsh words, the little demon king put away his puffed-up cheeks and dove straight into the carriage, showing no intention of arguing with them further.","He was, after all, the legitimate young master of the Marquis Manor - he wouldn't stoop to arguing with commoners!","The stunned commoners: \"???\"","\"What just flashed past us?\"","\"It... it seems to be the Marquis Manor's eldest grandson.\"","\"Wow! Big drama!\"","\"The Marquis's wife doesn't get along with her stepson, forcing him to accompany her home visit - a great battle in the Marquis household is about to break out—\"","\"The Marquis's grandson causes chaos at the Minister's Mansion's homecoming feast, the Minister of Justice's backyard catches fire, household in complete disarray!\"","\"The storytellers this month will certainly have something to work with...\"","\"...\"","The sedan chairs lifted off, and the procession headed toward the Minister's Mansion.","Sitting in her sedan chair, Xu Wan listened to the commoners' discussions outside and a smile curved her lips.","Cui Zhi whispered from outside: \"Madam, should this servant go explain things? At the rate they're spreading news, it might reach the Minister's Mansion before we arrive. It might not be good for your homecoming.\"","It would be embarrassing for any family if their newly married daughter gained a reputation for mistreating her stepson, especially when they still had an unmarried daughter at home.","Particularly since Xu Wan had a younger legitimate sister who was Madam Liu's only daughter - they would naturally be extra concerned.","Xu Wan said: \"It doesn't matter, let them spread it.\"","She reasoned that if she appeared to be doing well, she would only invite her stepmother's jealousy. If she appeared to be doing poorly and made those people happy, perhaps her stepmother would cause her fewer problems.","As for affecting her legitimate sister's marriage prospects, that wouldn't be an issue. After all, she had become the Marquis Manor's madam and now held authority over household affairs. When her stepmother arranged marriages for her sister, she would only highlight the positive aspects.","Cui Zhi was still worried: \"When we arrive at the Minister's Mansion, the young master will surely try to cause trouble for you. Should we give him some silver to go play elsewhere today?\"","It was obvious to everyone that Zong Jincheng was there just to create problems for Xu Wan.","Xu Wan smiled: \"No need, let him come.\"","She wanted to see what other tricks this little demon king had up his sleeve.","\"Lower the sedan.\"","\"Madam, we've arrived.\"","Cui Zhi and Cui Liu approached from both sides of the sedan chair, lifted the curtain, and Xu Wan stepped out, elegantly placing her hand on Cui Zhi's offered support.","\"Wan'er, you've finally returned. Mother has prepared a feast for you and has been waiting,\" said a woman in green clothing, appearing as kind as a Buddha.","It was her hypocritical stepmother, Madam Liu.","\"Greetings, Mother,\" Xu Wan responded.","With so many commoners gathered outside the Minister's Mansion waiting to see drama unfold, Xu Wan naturally wouldn't create conflict with Madam Liu right after her marriage - that would do her no good.","Madam Liu, having perfected the art of keeping up appearances over many years, smoothly pushed Cui Zhi aside and took Xu Wan's arm, speaking with affected warmth: \"Your father is still occupied at the Ministry of Justice and hasn't returned yet. Your sister has been waiting for you for ages, saying she would go to the Marquis Manor to fetch you if you didn't come soon.\"","\"I was delayed by some household matters, I hope Mother doesn't mind.\"","\"How could I? You're now the household manager of the Marquis Manor - I couldn't be happier for you, how could I blame you?\"","...","\"Ahem—\"","\"Ahem ahem—\"","While the two were chatting away, Zong Jincheng was left ignored on the side.","The little demon king coughed forcefully several times, startling even the nearby horses into raising their hooves, before the two women finally looked his way.","Madam Liu asked in surprise: \"And who might this be?\"","\"Zong Jincheng, my son,\" Xu Wan said naturally, as if he were truly her own flesh and blood.","Zong Jincheng had been holding his head high proudly, but upon hearing the words \"my son,\" he was momentarily stunned, feeling a warm current flow through his heart, both comforting and pleasant.","But then he quickly remembered who was speaking - it was Xu Wan - and the warmth that had just risen was instantly extinguished.","His face turned red, then purple, and after a long while, he finally managed to stammer out: \"Who's your son?\"","He had a mother!","Although he didn't know who she was, it certainly wasn't Xu Wan.","At her age, how could she possibly have a son as old as him!","Madam Liu suddenly understood: \"Oh, so it's Jincheng! Come in quickly, I'll have them prepare more pastries - children your age love such treats.\"","She reached out to pat the little demon king's head, but Zong Jincheng quickly dodged, automatically maintaining a meter's distance.","He had the complete appearance of \"don't touch me\" and being difficult to approach.","Xu Wan pretended not to notice, but was secretly laughing inside.","Letting the little demon king's face-giving-adverse nature interact with Madam Liu was indirectly avenging the mistreatment she had suffered before her marriage.","Having been rebuffed, Madam Liu was naturally unhappy, but for the sake of appearances, she still endured it and led them into the mansion.","At the feast.","\"Sister, try this dish, I had the kitchen prepare it especially for you,\" her legitimate sister Xu Lian'er served her food.","Xu Wan smiled in thanks.","Looking at the small mountain of food piled in her bowl, and thinking of the sour fruits she used to eat, she thought to herself that these mother and daughter were really trying to outdo each other in their act. Did they think she had forgotten everything?","\"Mm, I'll try it.\"","The three women's performance was in full swing.","Warmth masking hypocrisy, hypocrisy tinged with comedy.","Cui Zhi and Cui Liu stood to the side, keeping their eyes down, each trying harder than the other not to laugh, afraid that if they couldn't hold it in, they wouldn't be able to leave this place.","Although Madam had told them about her maiden family's situation before coming, they hadn't expected it to be so... so low-level.","Madam Liu and Xu Lian'er's intentions were written all over their faces, each trying to stuff their madam to death.","And their own madam was even more outrageous, saying \"good, good\" while not moving her chopsticks at all, as if watching to see who could put on the better act.","Finally, Zong Jincheng couldn't stand it anymore. His hand playing with the chopsticks slipped, and one chopstick shot up and landed right in the center of Xu Wan's bowl...","Standing straight up like an offering to the heavens.","Xu Wan: \"...\"","Was he trying to send her straight to heaven?"]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12: The Little Rascal Got Used as a Gun","paragraphs":["The Little Demon King's gaze was extremely provocative.","The boring conversation made you all ignore this young master. If you don't want to eat, then none of you should eat!","Anyway, he was already full, so he started causing trouble!","Madam Liu was the first to notice something was amiss and hurriedly called out, \"Quickly take it away and bring Wan another bowl.\"","\"Yes.\"","The maids, who had been arrogant before Xu Wan's marriage, now that Xu Wan had gained power, all put away their airs and diligently served her.","Xu Wan smiled, not caring.","Knowing there was a rift between her and her son, Madam Liu deliberately asked, \"Jincheng, have you been getting along well with your mother these past few days?\"","Xu Wan wanted to say that this question was as good as not asking. With Zong Jincheng's overbearing demeanor, it was obvious that things weren't going well. This rude boy didn't even give his own mother face, let alone Madam Liu, this stepmother he barely knew.","Zong Jincheng smirked, \"Of course it's pleasant. We never fight.\"","Xu Wan knew he wouldn't say anything good.","Who measures a pleasant relationship by whether they fight or not?","This was clearly an attempt to tattle on her to Madam Liu.","If Madam Liu cared for her, she might just let it go; if not, she would surely side with Zong Jincheng and gang up on her.","Obviously, Zong Jincheng knew a thing or two about the inner workings of the household.","He had preconceived notions: all stepmothers in the world were bad.","When Xu Lian'er heard this, she was naturally excited.","She feigned surprise and asked, \"No fighting...? Do you two have such a bad relationship that you have to resort to physical violence?\"","Looking at Zong Jincheng's aggressive demeanor, it seemed like he was bullying her right at her doorstep. Xu Lian'er couldn't help but gloat. What good was holding the Marquis Manor's household power if she was still bullied by a stepson?","Xu Wan smiled, \"Of course not. Jincheng is a well-behaved child. He's certainly not like those riffraffs who cause trouble and spout nonsense every day. When it comes to etiquette, the Old Marchioness is very skilled at raising children.\"","Xu Wan's words were polished, praising Zong Jincheng and flattering the Old Marchioness.","Such a well-crafted response even made Xu Lian'er's previous words seem out of place, as if she was implying Zong Jincheng had no upbringing.","Zong Jincheng's face immediately changed.","He glared fiercely at Xu Lian'er, hoping she would just shut up if she didn't have anything nice to say.","So what if she was the daughter of the Minister of Justice? There wasn't a single person in the entire Capital City who dared to offend him, the young master of the Zong family!","\"Wan is also fortunate, otherwise why would the Old Marchioness single her out?\" Madam Liu said with a forced smile.","She was even beginning to regret giving Xu Wan the option of marrying into the Marquis Manor. She had wanted Xu Wan to become a widow with a title but no real power. Who knew that the old lady of the Marquis Manor had gone blind and handed over the household power the same day? It was really strange!","Xu Wan smiled sweetly, \"I also have to thank Mother for your efforts. If it weren't for you strongly recommending the Yangyuan Marquis Manor to me and praising how intelligent Jincheng is, I wouldn't have been so set on marrying into the Marquis Manor. That's how I ended up getting such a great deal.\"","Zong Jincheng felt more and more uneasy with each word.","It felt more and more off.","So it was this old lady who pushed Xu Wan into his family?","Damn it, too wicked!","He'd remember this debt!","Zong Jincheng's gaze became even fiercer, glaring angrily at Madam Liu!","Suddenly caught in the crossfire, Madam Liu: \"???\"","When did she ever strongly recommend the Marquis Manor to Xu Wan?","When did she ever say Zong Jincheng was intelligent?","Wait, what was that kid's look?","It was like he was glaring at a ten-generation enemy!","Behind them, Cui Zhi's shoulders were shaking, almost bursting into laughter. Fortunately, Cui Liu gave her a hard pinch, forcing her to suppress her laughter and even squeeze out a tear.","Throughout the dining hall, Xu Wan praised Madam Liu and Xu Lian'er one sentence after another, while Zong Jincheng's expression grew increasingly grim.","The angry Little Demon King glared at one person, then another, his eyes turning red from the effort. In the end, he didn't know whether to sit or stand, just huffing and puffing in anger.","It was quite a comical sight.","\"Since Father is busy and can't return, I'll take Jincheng back to the manor first. I'll visit Mother another day.\"","After having sufficiently riled everyone up, Xu Wan began to take her leave.","Madam Liu breathed a sigh of relief and said with a forced smile, \"Alright, alright. I'll have Lian'er see you out.\"","Damn that girl. After getting married, she had become so sharp-tongued. If she didn't leave soon, the little firecracker next to her might just end up flipping the table in anger.","Yangyuan Marquis Manor.","Xu Wan returned home with a smile on her face. As soon as they arrived at the manor, Cui Zhi started laughing, so much so that Cui Liu had to hit her.","\"Hahaha, Madam, you're really too good with words. I think your stepmother tonight will be too angry to sleep.\"","\"And the young master, today he was really too amazing. He was like your assistant, specifically there to anger those two hypocritical women.\"","Xu Wan sipped her tea and said lightly, \"My stepmother may be bad, but she's simple-minded. It wouldn't work with someone more formidable.\"","Cui Zhi asked curiously, \"Madam, you're so intelligent. How did you ever get bullied by such a person before?\"","Xu Wan said indifferently, \"Before, I didn't want to compete. I thought it was nice to just lie down and rest.\"","\"And now?\"","\"Now I still don't want to compete.\"","\"Ah? Then what was today...?\"","Xu Wan exclaimed, \"I was just teasing Zong Jincheng. Isn't it obvious?\"","Cui Zhi: \"...\"","It was obvious, but she hadn't expected it to be so childish.","Playing with a child...","Xu Wan hummed, \"Isn't Zong Jincheng capable? He still wants to cause trouble for me. Let's see who ends up embarrassed. Little rascal...\"","In the courtyard.","The little rascal kicked the tree as he returned.","\"Damn it, damn it, damn it!\"","\"All surnamed Xu are no good, one more bullying than the other!\"","\"Just wait, when this young master regains his power, I'll settle accounts with each of them!\"","\"Kick you to death, kick you to death! You're the one with no manners! You're the one who's unruly! You're the one who's annoying!\"","Zong Jincheng jumped around the courtyard, pointing at the tree and cursing wildly, howling like a grasshopper.","A servant behind him trembled and said, \"Young master, weren't you going to cause trouble for Madam? Why did you get angry at the Xu family?\"","Zong Jincheng fumed, \"It's all Xu Wan's fault! It's all her family's fault...\"","No, wait!","Her family didn't mean that...","Zong Jincheng, as he cursed, suddenly realized something was off. He carefully recalled everyone's words, all of which were explained by Xu Wan, and then his anger was ignited.","He felt that the Xu family was provoking him, but in reality...","In reality, Xu Wan was using him as a pawn!","The little guy finally realized it!","No wonder Cui Zhi was trying so hard not to laugh. He thought Cui Zhi was also on Xu Wan's side, wanting to bully him. In fact, she was laughing at him like a fool being played.","And Xu Wan must have been watching him like a monkey!"]},{"number":13,"title":"Chapter 13: Or You Could Just Stab the Lady","paragraphs":["“Ahhhh! I'm going to fight her to the death!!!”","Zong Jincheng's patience was instantly depleted, and he stormed into the room, rummaging and tossing things around. The once barren courtyard, now emptied of its contents, gained a new sense of liveliness due to his chaotic mess. This, however, terrified Shunzi, the only remaining servant.","“Young Master, what are you looking for?” Shunzi asked tremblingly.","Originally, he had five companions to share the burden of serving this mischievous young master. But now, as the sole survivor, he could hardly withstand such torment!","Zong Jincheng angrily demanded, “Where’s my knife?”","Xu Wan had dared to wield a knife against him the moment she married in. Surely, a knife was not hard to find?","Where was it?","Shunzi, in panic, replied, “What does Young Master need a knife for? There have never been any sharp weapons in our courtyard!”","The young troublemaker’s eyes reddened with fury: “Find me a knife! Damn it, I’m going to end it all with her!”","It was too much!","He had lived for eight whole years without ever suffering such humiliation!","If we’re going down, we’re going down together!","Shunzi was about to faint.","He pinched his own philtrum, forcing himself to stay strong, and hurried over to advise, “Young Master, think carefully! You’ve already suffered once, you can get back at her later. But life is precious; if you lose it, you’ll be at an even greater disadvantage. A gentleman’s revenge can wait ten years!”","Shunzi had used all the knowledge he had acquired in his lifetime for this speech, just hoping his young master would stop causing trouble.","To his surprise, the young troublemaker actually heeded the advice.","He calmed down and shifted his focus: “You, think of a way to get back at her.”","Shunzi looked behind him.","There was no one.","He turned back, pointing at himself: “?”","Zong Jincheng stared at him and said, “Yes, you. Think fast!”","Shunzi: “......”","Maybe you should just go stab the mistress with a knife.","However.","Under Zong Jincheng’s deathly glare, Shunzi swallowed hard and finally came up with a brilliant plan:","“Why don’t you go to the academy to study?”","“Huh?” Zong Jincheng glared, signaling him to choose his words carefully.","Shunzi weakly suggested, \"Madam now has wealth and power; we can't confront her head-on. It's better to retreat and avoid her sharpness, waiting until the old lady returns to Marquis Manor before discussing your return.\"","There were many academies in the capital, some even offering free board and lodging. If his young master was determined to go to an academy, even without paying, the academy would likely accept him out of respect for the Marquis Manor.","“Then wouldn’t I be playing into her hands?” Zong Jincheng grumbled, “She just wants me to study hard. Going to the academy would only make her happy!”","“Young Master, you’re just going to the academy. Whether you study or not depends on you. Even if the tutor chants in your ear, it won’t matter if you don’t listen.”","Zong Jincheng was wary: “Will the tutor really chant in my ear?”","Shunzi: “......”","He’s a tutor, not a monk.","Who would chant to you for no reason!","Despite his thoughts, Shunzi, being a dutiful servant, explained kindly, “I just meant that as an example. The tutors at the academy teach dozens or even hundreds of students; they won’t single out Young Master.”","Zong Jincheng found this reasonable.","The plan could work.","“Let’s go find that woman and tell her I want to study hard!”","In the main courtyard.","Cui Zhi was introducing various academies to Xu Wan.","“There are many academies in the capital, but the most prestigious is the Hanlin Academy. Every year, the top scholars of Great Chu Dynasty come from here!”","“The Hanlin Academy is divided into north and south campuses. The south campus admits those with noble backgrounds and wealth, while the north campus admits those with outstanding academic achievements. With our Marquis Manor’s background, Young Master can easily enter the south campus.”","Xu Wan lay on the chaise lounge, listening with half-closed eyes.","Isn’t this just like modern times?","A key high school's student body is half selected from top junior high students and half from nearby school district housing zoning enrollment. The top students are taught by key teachers, while the teachers for the zoning students are not necessarily the best.","“How are the academic levels of the students in the south campus?”","Cui Zhi replied, “They’re quite good. After all, they are the dearly loved children of various officials, who have been taught by excellent tutors since childhood, naturally surpassing ordinary children.”","“Oh, how many of them get into the top three rankings?”","Cui Zhi was silent for a few seconds.","The top three rankings are always filled by students from the north campus; the south campus hardly ever gets a spot.","Xu Wan understood from her expression.","The south campus was good, already providing better educational resources than most, but to achieve her goals, she needed to go to the north campus.","As she thought this, Zong Jincheng burst in again, rashly.","Xu Wan was used to his lack of manners, so the doors in her courtyard were usually left open. Seeing the boy suddenly appear, she was already accustomed to it: “What’s up, Young Master Zong? Do you need something from me?”","Zong Jincheng: “......”","This woman was truly hateful.","Her casual words could easily ignite his anger.","What was even more infuriating was that she always guessed right!","The young troublemaker’s face turned crimson with rage. If Shunzi hadn’t been holding him back, he might have jumped up and engaged Xu Wan in another hair-pulling contest.","“No? Then I’m off to stroll in the garden.” Xu Wan said, about to stand up.","Zong Jincheng squeezed out his words from between clenched teeth: “I want to go to the academy to study.”","Xu Wan dug her ears lazily, “Didn’t catch that.”","Zong Jincheng clenched his fists.","I’ll endure!","“I said I want to study, to learn properly! Isn’t that what you’ve been hoping for!”","He hoped she would agree to send him to the academy quickly.","Otherwise, he might really grab a knife and cause a scene!","Xu Wan oh-ed, pretending not to know, and said to Cui Zhi, “Go ahead and sign Young Master up for the entrance exam at the Hanlin Academy.”","Cui Zhi widened her eyes.","The entrance exam for the Hanlin Academy...?","The south campus could be entered with just a background, but only the north campus required an exam. With her young master’s lack of academic prowess, sending him to the north campus exam...","Was she planning for him to just write his name?","If his friends found out, they’d laugh their teeth out!","“Madam, are you sure it’s the Hanlin Academy?” Cui Zhi asked, fearing she had made a mistake.","Xu Wan smiled sweetly, “Yes, the Hanlin Academy is the best academy in the capital. Only it is worthy of our Marquis Manor’s eldest grandson.”","Zong Jincheng, unfamiliar with the academies, only heard Xu Wan mention his status and immediately straightened his back.","She knows how great I am.","“Yes, I’ll have someone register Young Master for the exam...” Cui Zhi gave Zong Jincheng a look of self-preservation before leaving.","Zong Jincheng, a sharp-witted person, had already been wary of Xu Wan’s tricks after their recent battles. Seeing Cui Zhi’s expression, he immediately asked suspiciously, “Are you digging another trap for me? What’s this entrance exam?”"]},{"number":14,"title":"Chapter 14: The Concubine's Son from the Second Household","paragraphs":["Xu Wan smiled like a wicked queen: \"It's just a test of your knowledge to see if you meet the admission standards of the Hanlin Academy.\"","If she didn't knock some sense into this kid, he would never understand that his \"two taels of ink\" were only enough to get him through the entrance exam, and nothing more.","Zong Jincheng was usually quite confident.","But when it came to the unfamiliar term \"exam,\" his heart couldn't help but tremble.","What would the entrance exam at the Hanlin Academy cover?","Would it include things he was good at, like cricket fighting, horse racing, or cuju?","Surely they wouldn't start by making him recite poetry and prose...","No, that couldn't be.","According to his friends, many young masters his age couldn't even recite the Four Books and Five Classics.","After all, those academies were still in it for the money. They wouldn't set an excessively high threshold and turn away a direct grandson of a marquis's household, would they?","Zong Jincheng made up his mind.","Attending the Hanlin Academy was the quickest way for him to escape Xu Wan's clutches.","There was no mountain of swords or sea of fire waiting for him.","He would go!","\"Alright, I'll take the exam. I'll go tomorrow!\"","It was just a small exam; Zong the Young Master wasn't afraid at all!","Xu Wan nodded, feeling somewhat relieved, and said to Cui Zhi, \"Then go prepare.\"","Cui Zhi: \"Yes, the Hanlin Academy already has writing materials, so I'll just prepare some dry rations for the young master.\"","Zong Jincheng was about to leave.","But upon hearing this, he was suddenly confused: \"???\"","\"Dry rations? What dry rations??\"","Wasn't he just going to take an exam?","Why did he need to prepare dry rations?","He wasn't about to move out of the marquis's residence immediately!","Cui Zhi smiled and explained, \"Young master, you may not know, but the Hanlin Academy is the best academy in our capital. There's even a saying that 'entering the Hanlin Academy is like stepping into a career in government.' That's why scholars from all over Great Chu are desperate to study here. The entrance exam is naturally more difficult than usual, lasting from morning till evening. One needs to prepare dry rations in advance to avoid going hungry.\"","\"...\"","The little devil's face visibly turned from white to green, from green to black, and from black to purple.","An entrance exam that tested so much—was this something a human could handle?!","\"I'm not taking it! I'm not going!\" Zong Jincheng, facing the difficulty, decisively gave up.","Come on, with that amount of work, he'd lose all face and dignity if he went.","It was better to give up early!","Xu Wan was unexpectedly caught off guard by this turn of events.","She hadn't expected Cui Zhi to reveal the difficulty of the Hanlin Academy so candidly, scaring the little devil into giving up before she could even lure him there.","Xu Wan frowned and shot a cold glance at Cui Zhi, who quickly lowered her head.","Cui Zhi was, after all, a senior maidservant by the old lady's side. Although she was usually quite steady, she didn't regard Xu Wan on the same level as the old lady, which led to her casual tone and this slip of the tongue. She was now filled with regret.","But Xu Wan only glanced at her once.","Then, as if nothing had happened, she said to Zong Jincheng, \"If you want to go to an academy, you can only go to the Hanlin Academy. As for elsewhere, I don't permit it.\"","Her words were neither light nor heavy, yet they carried a forceful tone, as if declaring her dominance.","Xu Wan knew that she couldn't trick Zong Jincheng anymore, so she decided to lay her cards on the table and simply forbid it.","If he really had the ability, then he could try to pass the exam.","Zong Jincheng was both angry and frustrated.","But under Xu Wan's authority, there was nothing he could do except vent his impotent rage: \"You just want to force me to study! I've already seen through you!\"","Xu Wan admitted without flinching, \"Yes, so what?\"","Did seeing through her make any difference?","Could it knock her down to the ground?","Could it overthrow her authoritarian rule and let him become the master?","The answer was, of course, no.","Zong Jincheng clenched his fists in anger, then released them, and turned to run out.","Damn it!","Damn it!","This wicked woman!","Just how many lifetimes of bad luck had he accumulated to meet someone like her to torment him!","Zong Jincheng's anger and resentment grew stronger. He started to resent his grandparents for not caring about him, then his mother for being absent, and finally his cousin Zong Zhao for not coming home. Otherwise, how could he, the direct grandson of the marquis, be living such a miserable life!","The marquis's residence was supposed to be his home, yet now it felt like he was living under someone else's roof!","It started to rain, fine rain falling from the sky, wetting Zong Jincheng's eyes.","Behind him, Shunzi's anxious voice called out, \"Young master, please slow down. The road is slippery in the rain. Be careful not to fall. I have an umbrella...\"","Zong Jincheng ignored Shunzi's voice. He wiped the rain from his face and ran forward with his head down.","Wicked woman.","Don't think I'll beg for mercy.","You can forget it. I won't cry, and I won't admit defeat!!","The rain grew heavier, but the little figure running in the rain grew faster, as if silently competing with someone.","\"Ah——\"","Just as Zong Jincheng ran out of the courtyard, he didn't notice the person kneeling at the corner and crashed right into them!","\"Thud——\"","The little devil, being tough and resilient, got up from the ground as if nothing had happened. He wiped the rain from his forehead and only then recognized who was in front of him.","Zong Wenxiu.","The second branch's illegitimate son.","Zong Wenxiu was about the same age as him and had grown up in the slums. Even after being brought back to the marquis's residence, he still wore coarse cloth clothes every day. Although they were neat and clean, he still looked like a country bumpkin to outsiders.","Zong Jincheng didn't like talking to him.","Because his friends would laugh at him for having a country bumpkin brother, which was embarrassing.","\"Hey, are you okay?\"","Zong Wenxiu was knocked to the ground and couldn't get up for a while, nor did he respond.","Seeing that he didn't answer, Zong Jincheng knelt down to check and noticed that the rain on his body had turned red. He exclaimed in worry, \"You're bleeding?\"","Zong Jincheng immediately turned to call out, \"Shunzi, Shunzi, quickly call the government doctor to come and take a look.\"","\"Yes, yes, I'll go get them right away!\" Shunzi handed the umbrella to Zong Jincheng and ran out quickly.","Zong Jincheng wasn't afraid of getting wet in the rain, but with this person injured, it was better to have an umbrella.","Thinking this, the pampered young master of the marquis's household held the umbrella over both of them: \"Are you alright? The family doctor will be here soon.\"","With the umbrella blocking the rain, Zong Wenxiu finally got up from the ground. He said he was fine and knelt back in place.","The young boy's posture was as straight as a pillar, and even with blood streaming from his nose, his clear eyes remained unchanged, as if the blood wasn't his.","Zong Jincheng stared in amazement, finally noticing his posture, and asked in surprise, \"It's raining, and you're injured. Why are you kneeling here? Did that woman also torment you?\"","They say that the enemy of my enemy is my friend.","Thinking this might be Xu Wan's doing, Zong Jincheng immediately felt he was no longer alone.","He wanted to join forces with Zong Wenxiu to defeat that wicked woman who had taken over his home!","Little did he know, his imagination was all wrong.","Zong Wenxiu raised his head, the rain sliding down from above. His thin frame was now completely soaked, making him look like a homeless kitten.","After a while, he said, \"I came to beg an audience with the Lady.\""]},{"number":15,"title":"Chapter 15: The Difference Between Legitimate and Illegitimate Sons","paragraphs":["The young boy's voice was soft and low, making him sound like someone who could be easily taken advantage of.","\"Want to see Xu Wan?\" Zong Jincheng said with clear disdain, his hand holding the umbrella growing impatient. \"That woman has a heart of stone. Even I have been repeatedly rebuffed by her. You're just wasting your time.\"","After spending a few days with Xu Wan, Zong Jincheng had a better understanding of her. He felt that Zong Wenxiu might have better luck asking him for help than Xu Wan.","Although he wasn't particularly close to this cousin from a concubine, the thought of Zong Wenxiu seeking help from Xu Wan stirred a bit of sympathy in him. \"But go ahead and tell me what's wrong. Maybe I can help you.\"","In the inner courtyard.","After sending Zong Jincheng away, Xu Wan returned to her room, only to sit down when Cui Zhi suddenly knelt on the ground, her voice trembling with anxiety. \"Madam... I... I...\"","The look Xu Wan had given her earlier had struck fear into her heart.","Xu Wan didn't rush to speak. She slowly sat down, picked up a teacup, and sipped it leisurely. Hmm... this is how it's done in dramas. By staying silent and appearing calm, one can exude an aura of authority without even having to raise one's voice.","She had to learn this!","In truth, Xu Wan understood Cui Zhi's situation. After all, they had only been working together for a few days, so it was normal for them not to be in sync.","But she needed to establish her authority.","Otherwise, if Cui Zhi continued to undermine her, there would be no point in her trying to guide Zong Jincheng.","As expected, the silence from Xu Wan made Cui Zhi even more nervous. She didn't even dare to raise her head.","\"Please give me another chance, Madam. I promise I won't disappoint you again!\"","Xu Wan said, \"Cui Zhi, you're very clever.\"","Cui Zhi kept her head down, not daring to nod.","\"I know you must think I'm making a big deal out of nothing right now. You've watched Jincheng grow up, so you feel free to speak your mind with him. But I think you might not fully understand why the Old Marquis and Old Marchioness left Marquis Manor. It's not just because they were afraid of interfering with my guidance of Jincheng, but also because they were afraid their old habits would make Jincheng as unrestrained as before. The Old Marchioness left you here to assist me, not to hinder me. If you continue as you did before, then perhaps you'd be better suited to taking care of the Old Marchioness.\"","As soon as Xu Wan finished speaking, Cui Zhi panicked. \"Madam, please forgive me! I will never do it again!\"","Cui Zhi's position next to the Old Marchioness was second only to the Old Marchioness's personal maid, but it was a gap she could never cross.","The Young Marquis's wife had no close personal maids, so if Cui Zhi could establish herself by Xu Wan's side, her status would be completely different!","Realizing that Xu Wan might dismiss her, Cui Zhi finally understood how grave her mistake had been. She was filled with regret!","Xu Wan stood up and helped her to her feet. \"I've never had a close maid since I was young, and I didn't even have a close friend in my chamber. I was very happy to have you here. Now that you've acknowledged your mistake, just do your job well in the future, and I won't treat you unfairly.\"","Xu Wan's words were simple, but the promise of future benefits was clear.","Cui Zhi immediately understood.","She stood up, her eyes still a bit red. \"Yes, thank you, Madam.\"","If she had previously thought of herself as the Old Marchioness's senior maid, from this day forward, she would focus on how to become Xu Wan's trusted personal maid.","Xu Wan smiled. \"It's raining heavily today. Go check if the stove in Jincheng's courtyard is still burning. The early spring weather is still cold. Don't let that boy catch a chill.\"","\"Yes.\"","Cui Zhi took her leave.","Outside the door, Cui Liu came in to report, \"Madam, Master Wenxiu is requesting an audience.\"","\"Hmm? Wenxiu? Why didn't you let him in with such heavy rain?\"","Xu Wan hadn't quite gotten used to the reporting customs of Marquis Manor. After all, Zong Wenxiu was still a master of the house.","But then she realized.","In ancient times, distinctions between legitimate and concubine-born children were strict. As a legitimate son, Zong Jincheng could shout and argue with her, but as a concubine-born son, Zong Wenxiu couldn't even enter without permission.","The contrast made her even more eager to discipline Zong Jincheng, that rebellious child.","\"Quick, bring him in,\" Xu Wan said, gesturing as she spoke. \"Add another stove to the room to keep him warm.\"","\"Yes.\"","Outside, Zong Jincheng had been unusually considerate, asking Zong Wenxiu many questions, but his cold and aloof cousin didn't say a word, clearly thinking that Zong Jincheng couldn't solve the problem.","This infuriated Zong Jincheng.","His hand holding the umbrella—tired from the effort—dropped, and the two of them ended up standing in the rain together.","The little troublemaker was tough and thick-skinned, and getting wet in the rain was as common as breathing for him. He even found it refreshing and liberating.","But Zong Wenxiu was different. After just a short while in the rain, he was shivering all over, his cold eyes barely able to stay open under the pounding rain. He looked so weak that it seemed he might faint at any moment.","Zong Jincheng had sympathy, but not much.","He simply sat down on the ground right in front of Zong Wenxiu, who was kneeling, and stared at him with wide eyes in the rain, hoping he would realize his mistake soon.","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","Cui Zhi saw this scene.","One person kneeling, and another sitting in front of the kneeling person. To an outsider, it looked like they were getting married.","\"No... Young Master! Master Wenxiu! Why aren't you using an umbrella?\"","\"Hey, there's a perfectly good umbrella on the ground. Why aren't you using it?\"","\"Get up, get up! You'll get sick standing in the rain like this. Come with me inside!\"","As Cui Zhi shouted, Shunzi finally arrived with the family doctor. Seeing the situation, both of them were so frightened that their legs went weak.","The group hurriedly helped the two drenched young masters into the inner courtyard, holding umbrellas and supporting them.","Xu Wan was tending to the stove in the room, thinking that the heavy rain might have soaked the child outside, so she had someone bring dry towels to dry his hair.","But instead, two little drenched figures were brought in.","Xu Wan: \"???\"","The first one was Zong Wenxiu. He looked dazed, his eyes half-closed from the rain, and his face pale.","Following behind was the little troublemaker, completely soaked but with bright, wide eyes, looking a bit excited.","Of course, it was the little demon king!","Xu Wan exclaimed in a hurry, \"How did they get so wet? Quickly prepare hot water to wash them and warm them up!\"","The maids in the room sprang into action, some boiling water, others fetching clean clothes, all in a flurry.","Zong Wenxiu, breaking free from Cui Zhi's support, stumbled over and pleaded, \"Madam, please save my mother!\""]},{"number":16,"title":"Chapter 16: I Want My Mother to Live","paragraphs":["The young man was soaked through, his body shivering from the cold, his teeth chattering as he spoke.","But Xu Wan still understood him.","However...","\"Auntie Hong isn't in the west courtyard? What happened to her?\"","Auntie Hong, though the only widow of the second branch, had been found after the death of the second master, and her identity was somewhat questionable. The old madame had only arranged for them to be cared for in the west courtyard, though the monthly allowance given to her was more than that of an ordinary concubine.","Xu Wan had been married to the manor for a few days and had yet to meet Auntie Hong. According to the customs of the Great Chu Dynasty's official households, Auntie Hong should have come to pay her respects to Xu Wan, but since Cui Zhi mentioned that she had been weak all along, Xu Wan hadn't inquired further.","Now, looking at the situation, could there be some hidden truth?","Little Demon King, though also drenched, was fully absorbed in the situation, his big eyes fixed on the scene.","\"The manor doctor said my mother is critically ill and there's no hope of recovery, but I heard that if a royal physician from the palace is invited, there might... there might still be a chance,\" Zong Wenxiu pleaded. \"As long as you agree to save my mother, I am willing to repay you with my life!\"","The young man's promise was so firm, yet it lacked credibility.","Not to mention that he was only ten years old, and even when he grew up, he would still be a mere illegitimate son. The mistress of the Marquis Manor wouldn't need his repayment.","Little Demon King tilted his head and reminded, \"Royal physicians are for treating the emperor and empress. How could they be easily invited? I haven't even seen a royal physician when I grow up, let alone for just a concubine.\"","After saying that, he looked up.","Just in time to meet Xu Wan's face, which had been oppressing him for days.","This wicked woman would never agree, right?","He had said that Zong Wenxiu would be better off begging him instead.","Xu Wan was aware of the process of inviting a royal physician. Back when her step-sister was ill, her father had sent someone to the palace to request one.","— It required the name of a high-ranking official.","And the high-ranking official of the Marquis Manor was naturally the old marquis. They could only send someone to inform the old marquis to request a royal physician for Auntie Hong.","Xu Wan gave a signal.","Cui Zhi, eager to prove her loyalty, immediately understood and, despite the rain, went out to make arrangements.","The servants in the room were still busy, while Cui Liu had already brought thick clothes and was directing people to dry the two young masters.","Cui Liu herself was pulling Little Demon King to take a hot bath, not wanting the manor's eldest grandson to catch a cold.","Before leaving, Little Demon King kindly reached out to pull Zong Wenxiu.","The latter, however, remained unmoved, thinking that Xu Wan hadn't agreed, and continued kneeling on the ground: \"Please, madam!\"","Little Demon King rolled his eyes to the sky.","He crossed his arms and said coldly, \"Stop begging her. It's useless. Come with me to take a bath; otherwise, if you catch a cold and can't be cured, you'll die too.\"","Little Demon King's words were indifferent.","He had never had a mother since birth, and his father was never around. Even with his grandparents, his feelings for his parents were always cold.","Moreover, Auntie Hong had nothing to do with him.","Xu Wan, who had originally wanted to explain, stopped.","This opportunity, however, was perfect to deal with the little troublemaker.","\"I didn't say I can't help.\"","Zong Wenxiu looked up in surprise, his face regaining color: \"Thank you, madam!\"","Little Demon King was stunned.","What? This wicked woman was willing to help his half-brother?","What did she mean by that?","Being so kind to an illegitimate grandson but bullying him, the eldest legitimate grandson!","Unfair!","The string in Little Demon King's mind snapped, and he threw the newly draped clothes to the ground, shouting angrily, \"You have the kindness to help him, but you deliberately target me! Do you just pick on me?\"","It's outrageous!","Xu Wan glanced at the easily provoked little chick and teased with a smile, \"Kid, please get it straight. From the beginning, it's been you throwing a tantrum. Look at Wenxiu, and then look at you. If you were half as obedient as him, our stepmother-stepson relationship wouldn't be so strained.\"","Zong Jincheng's face was full of dissatisfaction.","He turned his head and continued to sulk.","Xu Wan turned to Zong Wenxiu and said, \"You just said you'd repay me with your life. Life is too long; you don't need to do that. I just need you to help me with a small task.\"","\"Madam, please instruct,\" Zong Wenxiu replied.","Xu Wan pointed a finger at Little Demon King, arranging in front of the stunned boy: \"I want him to study with you in the manor.\"","She had decided that she didn't trust Little Demon King in an external school.","Keeping him under her watchful eye was more reliable.","Plus, with Zong Wenxiu, who was a diligent student, as a classmate, it would not only have a positive influence but also prevent Zong Jincheng from learning bad habits from other young nobles.","\"I agree,\" Zong Wenxiu replied almost immediately, afraid she might change her mind.","This task was indeed minor for him. If merely accompanying someone in their studies could secure his mother's safety, he was willing to accompany Zong Jincheng in his studies for a lifetime.","Zong Jincheng: \"???\"","Excuse me!","Have you asked for my opinion?!","I didn't agree!","\"I won't study!\"","Little Demon King immediately refused, plugging his ears with his hands to avoid hearing their secret plotting, \"This has nothing to do with me. You need the consent of the person involved, you know? Anyway, I didn't hear anything. I won't go, I won't study, I just want to lie around at home.\"","Zong Jincheng tried his best to feign deafness and dumbness, refusing to be arranged.","But unfortunately, it didn't work.","Standing opposite was the cold-hearted, unyielding, and merciless stepmother, Xu Wan.","The mother and son were at a stalemate, neither willing to yield, but Zong Wenxiu made the first move. Seeing that Little Demon King didn't agree, and with his mother's life hanging by a thread, he had no time to waste.","So, he turned around, lifted his robe, and was about to kneel, this time facing Zong Jincheng.","Little Demon King was of noble birth and had been knelt to many times, but those were all servants. Zong Wenxiu, however, was not; he was, after all, his elder brother, even if an illegitimate one, and shouldn't kneel to him.","Zong Jincheng quickly dodged to the side, crashing into a warm embrace.","When he reacted and looked up, he saw the beautiful face he had been extremely annoyed with recently.","\"...\" Embarrassing, how did he end up hiding by her side.","Realizing this, he quickly jumped far away, distancing himself from both of them.","Zong Wenxiu, pulled by Xu Wan, didn't kneel down.","Xu Wan spoke softly, \"A man's knees are made of gold; how can they be bent so easily?\"","Tears welled up in Zong Wenxiu's eyes as he suddenly said, \"But I want my mother to live.\"","Unlike Zong Jincheng, who had never had a mother, Zong Wenxiu had lived with his mother since childhood, surviving together in the slums. The bond between them was closer than that of ordinary mother and son.","Although they had been living in luxury since returning to the Marquis Manor, he knew that the people here didn't like them much. If his mother were gone, he didn't know how he could go on.","Perhaps his words were too powerful, as Zong Jincheng paused, his usual arrogance fading.","Xu Wan quickly noticed his change.","So, she added another sentence to further provoke him: \"Think of another way. Zong Jincheng won't study for you. I think breaking his leg would be easier.\""]},{"number":17,"title":"Chapter 17: Make Sure to Help Your Brother Pass the First Rank","paragraphs":["Zong Jincheng shared the same thought, but hearing those words actually come from Xu Wan's mouth made his face burn as if he'd been slapped in public.","\"Hey!\" he protested indignantly.","What did she mean by that? Did she really see him as nothing but a selfish person who didn't care about others' lives? And breaking his legs... couldn't he have volunteered to help someone of his own accord?","This woman was judging a gentleman's heart with a petty person's mindset!","Hmph!","Xu Wan responded with an \"Oh\" and reminded him, \"Address me as Mother.\"","This impudent boy had no manners.","\"I won't,\" he refused.","Zong Jincheng glared at her with puffed cheeks, then looked at the pitiful Zong Wenxiu beside him. Truth be told, his heart was softening and he wanted to agree, but seeing Xu Wan's confident expression made him feel like he couldn't back down, so he remained stubborn in his childish tantrum.","Just then, a gust of wind rattled the windows of the room. Although all doors and windows were tightly shut, both children instinctively shivered.","\"Well then, Jincheng has agreed. I'll arrange for the imperial physician. Quickly, take them both to warm up and change clothes,\" Xu Wan declared decisively, making the decision for the little tyrant, though she had already sent Cui Zhi to deliver a message to the Old Marquis.","Zong Wenxiu's eyes lit up – Mother would be saved!","Cui Liu was the most efficient of the servants; when given a task by the mistress, she would complete it perfectly by any means necessary. So now she maintained a stern face as she grabbed both boys, one in each hand, and dragged them off for their baths.","Halfway there, a confused Zong Jincheng thought: \"???\"","I didn't agree, I didn't agree at all, so how did she say I agreed?","I didn't say anything out loud, did I?","When the little tyrant realized he'd been tricked by Xu Wan again, he tried to stand up from the bath barrel, but as he rose, he caught sight of Zong Wenxiu in the adjacent tub.","Zong Wenxiu was so thin he was practically just skin and bones, his skin rougher than a servant's. Looking closer, Jincheng noticed several chilblains on his hands and many calluses on his palms.","Zong Jincheng sat back down and asked in confusion, \"How do you get calluses and chilblains just from reading and writing?\"","Hadn't Grandmother said that studying was the easiest thing in the world? Just sitting in a room reading and writing – you couldn't get cold or tired from that.","Shunzi, who was attending to his bath, couldn't help but sigh inwardly: The young master could be truly innocent sometimes.","Young Master Wenxiu hadn't grown up in the Marquis Manor like you. He came from the slums, where the Capital City's poorest families lived. People died there every day from illness, hunger, or cold. It was remarkable that Young Master Wenxiu had survived nine and a half years there – of course his body would bear more and more wounds, not fewer.","Zong Wenxiu was startled by the question. He instinctively withdrew his exposed hands under the water, thinking Zong Jincheng was mocking him. At his sensitive age, he remained silent.","Zong Jincheng glared at Shunzi: \"Have the manor's servants been bullying him?\"","With Second Uncle dead and no proper wife in the second branch of the family, it wouldn't be surprising if servants bullied them for being born of concubines.","Shunzi raised his hands in frightened protest: \"Not at all! The Old Madam has been very good to that courtyard. Young Master Wenxiu gets up before dawn to study, and they've even given him an extra brazier. He's been taken care of exceptionally well.\"","Realizing that Zong Wenxiu might feel embarrassed, Shunzi leaned close to the little tyrant's ear and explained the situation in a low voice.","Only then did Zong Jincheng understand that hands with chronic chilblains would easily develop them again even with the best care, and that children in the slums, even at just a few years old, had to do a lot of hard physical labor.","No wonder his cousin, though only two years older than him, wasn't much taller or stronger.","The little tyrant lowered his eyes thoughtfully, his earlier desire to argue with Xu Wan forgotten as he absently splashed the bathwater back and forth.","Zong Wenxiu was actually very nervous beside him. He could sense Zong Jincheng's reluctance and feared he might change his mind at any moment, so despite being in a warm bath, he didn't dare move a muscle, afraid that any movement might upset Zong Jincheng.","Suddenly, the little tyrant spoke up: \"I heard you've been studying books since you returned to the manor these past few months. What's so interesting about those thick books?\"","A few months ago, when Auntie Hong was brought back to the manor, the Old Marquis had arranged for them to live in the west courtyard, publicly announcing Zong Wenxiu as merely the second branch's eldest son born of a concubine.","Everyone knew the difference between legitimate and illegitimate children.","Regardless of whether Zong Jincheng studied or succeeded academically, no one could challenge his position as the legitimate grandson, so he had never felt any sense of crisis, nor did he understand why Zong Wenxiu was so fond of reading.","Zong Wenxiu replied, \"Because reading teaches you to understand principles and shows you many things you've never seen before. If you can achieve a good rank in the imperial examinations, you can do many things you want to do.\"","\"What do you want to do?\" Zong Jincheng asked.","Children their age only thought about playing; how would they know what studying was for?","Zong Wenxiu paused, then answered honestly, \"Actually, I don't know what I want to do when I grow up, but my mother says that whatever I choose to do, I should first have sufficient knowledge. That way, I'll have more paths to choose from later. For example, if I want to become an official, I need to pass the examinations first; if I want to go into business, I need to know the ways and methods of making money.\"","Zong Jincheng understood but felt it didn't apply to him.","With his status, if he wanted to become an official, his grandfather would arrange it, and it would probably be a good position; if he wanted to do business, his grandmother would provide the capital, shops, and even the people to manage them.","There was no need to study at all.","Clearly this wasn't a topic suited for his contemplation.","Zong Jincheng finished his bath hurriedly and got out, with Zong Wenxiu quickly following suit.","Just as Wenxiu was worrying that his reportedly willful brother might cause a scene, he heard Zong Jincheng ask ahead of him, \"Where do you study? It's not in Auntie Hong's courtyard, is it? How many braziers are there?\"","In that instant, Zong Wenxiu's anxiety melted away.","His furrowed brow relaxed as he patiently explained, \"Not in my mother's courtyard. Grandmother said there was an empty study in the manor that wasn't being used, so she told me to study there. It has an excellent collection of books, and there are three braziers in the room – it's warm and comfortable.\"","Zong Wenxiu hurried to catch up and describe everything to him. This was completely unexpected – his brother was nothing like the rumors suggested, but rather... awkwardly kind-hearted.","Zong Wenxiu made a silent vow.","He would definitely help his brother study well. Even if he himself couldn't achieve top honors in the examinations, he would make sure his brother did!"]},{"number":18,"title":"Chapter 18: The Retribution of Master Bai Li","paragraphs":["If Zong Jincheng knew what Zong Wenxiu was thinking right now, he would probably run away as fast as he could, rolling and scrambling.","Although they were talking about going to the study, their steps were heading towards Auntie Hong's courtyard. The young man was full of energy, and by the time they arrived, he wasn't even out of breath. However, unexpectedly, Xu Wan was outside Auntie Hong's door, listening to the family doctor discussing her condition.","\"Auntie Hong has tuberculosis. In slums like the ones in the Capital City, where the environment is dirty and chaotic, many people contract tuberculosis. To cure this disease, one needs renowned doctors and a large amount of medicine. Obviously, people in the slums don't have these resources and can only wait for death.\"","As the family doctor spoke, his gaze fell on Zong Wenxiu. This young man, who had been living in the slums, must have seen countless people die from tuberculosis.","Zong Wenxiu's face turned pale. He remembered it all too well, which was why he had knelt in the rain to beg Xu Wan when his mother's condition worsened.","Xu Wan was puzzled: \"Why didn't you mention this when the Old Marchioness was still in the mansion?\"","Given the Old Marchioness's character, she wouldn't have refused to invite imperial physicians to treat them.","Everyone turned to look at Zong Wenxiu, including Zong Jincheng, who also felt something was amiss. Could there be some hidden secret?","Zong Wenxiu closed his eyes, feeling ashamed: \"Because my mother said her illness was incurable. Instead of wasting the Old Marchioness's energy, it would be better to let her feel guilty. That way, she would take me... take me into her courtyard to be raised properly.\"","Auntie Hong's plan was well thought out.","She was even willing to sacrifice her own life to secure a future for her son. Unfortunately, her son was extremely filial, disrupting her plans.","Zong Jincheng stood by, deep in thought.","He should have been unhappy, because if Auntie Hong's scheme had succeeded, Zong Wenxiu would have been by the Old Marchioness's side all the time, possibly stealing some of his own favor.","However, he found himself a bit envious of this kind of bond, envious that Zong Wenxiu had a mother who planned for him.","The little troublemaker became more and more frustrated, kicking stones around with his feet.","The family doctor suddenly called out: \"Young Master Jincheng...\"","\"What?\" The little troublemaker snapped.","Didn't he see that he was in a bad mood?","The family doctor timidly said: \"You're kicking my foot.\"","Zong Jincheng: \"...\"","The imperial physician arrived quickly, so fast that Zong Jincheng suspected he had flown over. He didn't even question how Xu Wan had already sent someone to fetch him.","After diagnosing Auntie Hong, the imperial physician, though surprised it had been a long time since he had treated such a case, quickly regained his composure and began writing a prescription.","\"Take this prescription three times a day as directed. After three months, you should see improvement, and then the family doctor can take over.\"","\"Thank you for your efforts,\" Xu Wan said with a smile, signaling Cui Zhi to hand over a bag of silver as she escorted the imperial physician out of the mansion.","The maids in the courtyard busied themselves with fetching and boiling the medicine.","Xu Wan then turned to Zong Wenxiu: \"Go ahead and study. I'll take care of things here, and I won't let your mother come to any harm.\"","Zong Wenxiu, his eyes red, thanked her: \"Thank you, Madam.\"","A young man is most grateful for kindness. Instead of going to the study as he should have, he turned to Zong Jincheng, looking determined to teach his younger brother well.","Zong Jincheng: \"...\"","My cousin's gaze is terrifying. I want to escape.","The little troublemaker unconsciously took half a step back.","Xu Wan raised an eyebrow and said coolly: \"Some people wouldn't be thinking of breaking their promise, would they? But then again, he's just an eight-year-old child. What does it matter if he doesn't keep his word? Even if I call him a little turtle who doesn't keep promises every day, he wouldn't feel embarrassed, right?\"","The little turtle who doesn't keep promises: \"???\"","Zong Jincheng shouted angrily: \"Who's not keeping their promise? Who's the little turtle?\"","Xu Wan casually replied: \"Whoever doesn't keep their promise is the little turtle, of course.\"","Zong Jincheng was provoked and glared at her: \"Fine, fine! I'll study, I'll study! But tell me, how long do you want me to study for?\"","He didn't believe Xu Wan could make him study until the end of time!","Xu Wan propped her chin with one hand and looked the little troublemaker up and down. The brat had an indignant yet extremely proud expression. Directly asking him to study for three years would probably not work.","Her gaze shifted to Zong Wenxiu, and an idea suddenly struck her.","Got it!","\"You don't have to say I'm making things difficult for you. I'll set a small goal for you: pass Wenxiu. He's only been studying for a few months and grew up in the slums, so he knows much less than you. With your cleverness, Young Master Jincheng, you should be able to surpass him in no time, right?\"","Xu Wan's words, both overtly and subtly, flattered Zong Jincheng, making him feel elated.","He arrogantly raised his chin, thinking that it made sense. In a few months, he would definitely surpass Zong Wenxiu.","Seeing that he was softening, Xu Wan added another strong point: \"If you can keep up with Wenxiu's progress, I'll return your money and servants to you. I promise that while you're working to surpass him, I won't interfere with your affairs.\"","At the mention of this, Zong Jincheng perked up.","He immediately agreed: \"Deal!\"","The two clapped their hands together in the air, sealing a momentous agreement.","In the years that followed, Xu Wan often looked back on this moment and found it incredibly meaningful.","The place where they would study was naturally set in the large study, which had originally been used by the young marquis, Zong Zhao. Now, it seemed spacious even with both children using it.","When the Old Marquis and Old Marchioness heard that the little troublemaker was willing to study, they immediately invited the renowned scholar Baili Xi from the Capital City to teach in the mansion. This old scholar had also been Zong Zhao's private tutor.","On the first day of class, the old scholar conducted a preliminary exam.","When testing Zong Wenxiu, the old man's eyes were smiling, and he praised the boy for his hard work and rapid progress.","When testing Zong Jincheng, the old man's brow furrowed so deeply that he could have trapped ten mosquitoes. The little troublemaker answered every question wrong, not only lacking knowledge but also pretending to know everything.","After just half a day of teaching, the old scholar wanted to sigh to the heavens. Back in the day, people envied him for teaching Zong Zhao, who was a well-rounded scholar and martial artist, making him famous in the Capital City.","But now, looking at the mischievous child in front of him, he truly felt that this was karma. There really were no consecutive great fortunes in this world.","\"Jincheng, your foundation is too weak. The first priority is to build a solid base. These are the introductory books I've chosen for you. Try to memorize them in the next few days.\"","Zong Jincheng sat in his seat, staring at the stack of books the old scholar left, as tall as a bowl. He suddenly realized something was off...","He immediately turned to ask Zong Wenxiu: \"Have you memorized all these?\"","Zong Wenxiu nodded: \"These books may look thick, but the content is straightforward and easy to memorize. You can finish them in five days.\"","The little troublemaker sneered: \"Do you think I'll believe that?\"","\"...\"","Realizing something was wrong, Zong Jincheng finally asked the crucial question: \"How many books have you memorized in these few months?\"","Zong Wenxiu reluctantly said: \"Over a hundred.\"","In fact, he had memorized over two hundred, but seeing his younger brother's expression grow increasingly grim, he decided not to tell the truth.","Sure enough, Zong Jincheng was stunned upon hearing this. He finally realized he had been tricked again by Xu Wan. He took a deep breath and forced a fake smile: \"So, how many pages can you memorize a day now?\"","\"Ten... or so.\"","\"Good.\" Zong Jincheng closed the book in front of him, signaling Shunzi to close the door and block it tightly, ensuring not even a fly could get in."]},{"number":19,"title":"Chapter 19: The Eerie Endorsement Method","paragraphs":["Zong Wenxiu instinctively gripped the table beside him, feeling an urge to flee in the tense atmosphere.","Was his younger brother about to attack him?","The young troublemaker leaned over, flexed his wrist, and in Zong Wenxiu's slightly panicked gaze, threatened with a cute yet fierce expression, \"From today onwards, you're not allowed to study. Wait until I catch up with your progress, and then you can start reading again!\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","Very well, as arbitrary and unreasonable as the rumors said.","But...","\"When will you be able to catch up with my progress?\" He had started studying later than most children, and if he had to wait for Zong Jincheng to catch up, he feared he would fall further behind.","Zong Jincheng glanced at the stack of books on the table and uncertainly replied, \"A month, I guess.\"","What took Zong Wenxiu, a concubine's son, months to learn, he, as the clever and bright legitimate son, could surely memorize in a month.","Zong Wenxiu hesitated for a few seconds, thinking of the favor he had done for his mother, and finally nodded, \"Alright, I'll wait for you for a month. During this month, besides studying what Baili Fuzi teaches, I'll only review old knowledge and not learn new things.\"","The young troublemaker had wanted him to stop listening to the tutor as well, but he was afraid that Xu Wan, the wicked woman, would notice if he was too obvious. Reluctantly, he agreed.","\"Alright, you're quite loyal. You're a brother I can count on.\"","Zong Wenxiu smiled, \"Take a look at these books first. There are some obscure characters that might be hard to understand, and I can explain them to you sentence by sentence.\"","Zong Jincheng felt overwhelmed at the first hearing.","He waved his hand to refuse, \"No need, I just need to memorize these things so I can pass Baili Fuzi's questioning.\"","The specific meanings? Whoever wants to understand them can, but he certainly didn't!","The young troublemaker's study session went quite smoothly.","Although he was mischievous, he had a sharp mind. He could read a sentence from the book, close his eyes, and recite it from memory perfectly, word for word.","Read a sentence, recite a sentence;","Open his eyes, close his eyes;","Remember, and remember again...","Zong Wenxiu was amazed!","He considered himself quite intelligent and exceptionally diligent in his studies, which was why he had managed to catch up with others' years of progress in just a few months.","But how could someone memorize a sentence instantly?","Could his younger brother be a genius?","Zong Jincheng was parched from reciting and felt tired after just a few pages.","Shunzi, being very observant, immediately poured him some tea.","While the young troublemaker drank, Zong Wenxiu finally regained his composure and praised him, \"You're amazing. I've never seen anyone memorize so quickly!\"","At this rate, he wouldn't need a month—with a bit more effort, Zong Jincheng could catch up with his progress in just two weeks.","Zong Wenxiu suddenly felt the pressure rise!","However, the young troublemaker didn't seem to take pride in his achievement. Instead, he slumped into the chair, closed his eyes, and announced like a lord, \"I don't want to look at them anymore. My eyes are tired.\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","If he remembered correctly, the young lord had only been studying for less than fifteen minutes.","Starting to feel tired already? How could someone who studied for six hours a day even begin to compare?","Shunzi, being very observant, stepped forward to massage the young troublemaker's shoulders and back, helping the little master who had tired himself out after just fifteen minutes of studying.","Zong Jincheng was so comfortable that he started humming. Thinking about the unmemorized books, an ingenious idea suddenly flashed through his mind!","\"Shunzi, you read the book, I'm not looking at it anymore.\"","After all, he could remember everything after hearing it once. Listening to someone else read was the same as reading it himself!","Shunzi: \"?!\"","Could it really be done like this??","Shunzi was the only literate servant Xu Wan had left for him, which happened to be useful for the young troublemaker's unconventional method.","Thus, Zong Wenxiu witnessed this strange way of studying between the master and servant.","Shunzi read a sentence, and the younger brother recited it.","And he...","Actually memorized it!","Zong Wenxiu felt he needed some time to think.","This went against his usual belief that hard work could make up for lack of talent, and he was deeply skeptical...","In the main courtyard.","Xu Wan, listening to Cui Liu's real-time report, spat out her tea in one go: \"That rascal thinks up all sorts of strange tricks every day. All he knows is memorizing by rote. When the imperial exams come, he'll be lucky if he can even write his own name!\"","Cui Liu said, \"But it's still a big improvement. Young Master never memorized anything before, and even Old Marquis didn't know his memory was this good.\"","Cui Zhi also covered her mouth and laughed, \"With Young Master's cleverness, if he could study properly, he would definitely bring honor to our Marquis Manor. And Baili Fuzi's face wouldn't look so bad either.\"","Both she and Cui Liu were houseborn slaves, having grown up watching Zong Zhao being praised by Baili Fuzi. Now, seeing the old tutor's attitude towards Young Master, they felt like it was a world of difference.","Xu Wan hummed in agreement and also acknowledged Zong Jincheng's talent, but his lazy approach to studying made it hard to believe he would put in much effort. She estimated he would give up after half an hour at most.","However, the people around the young troublemaker could be useful.","Xu Wan instructed Cui Zhi, \"Later, go and privately tell Shunzi that I see how hard he works accompanying Young Master in his studies, so I'll double his monthly allowance. If Young Master catches up with Zong Wenxiu's progress, I'll triple his allowance.\"","Cui Zhi was even a bit tempted by this.","Although Shunzi's tripled allowance still wouldn't be as high as theirs, the idea of getting a double or triple raise on the original amount was very appealing!","Cui Zhi asked, \"Madam, are you trying to win over Shunzi to our side?\"","If Shunzi could be successfully won over, then everyone around Young Master would be under Xu Wan's control. In the game of Go, this would be a dead end, making it even easier to control the little one.","However, Xu Wan frowned and said, \"No need to win him over. That little rascal may be a troublemaker, but Shunzi has grown up with him. And I am not his enemy. All my plans are for him to study hard, not to leave him with no one to rely on or trust. A child's world shouldn't be that dark.\"","Cui Zhi and Cui Liu exchanged glances, more respectful of their new mistress's approach.","She had both cunning and strategy, but also a moral bottom line.","That said, Xu Wan still needed to carefully consider the pros and cons of the young troublemaker's unconventional method.","Although he could only memorize without understanding the characters or their meanings, at least he could get the information into his head first and digest it later.","But Zong Wenxiu... couldn't just wait for the young troublemaker to catch up with his progress because of his unreasonable request.","\"Bring the new pastries the manor bought, and I'll go check on them.\""]},{"number":20,"title":"Chapter 20: Got Fish for Candy","paragraphs":["“The heavens are dark, the earth is yellow, the universe is vast and ancient, the sun and moon wax and wane, the stars are arrayed, the seasons change, autumn harvests and winter stores...”","It seemed that the little devil, Zong Jincheng, had found a tiny sense of accomplishment in his smooth recitation, as even after half an hour, his voice could still be heard chanting the \"Thousand Character Classic.\"","“Give up the throne and yield the kingdom, there was Yu and Tang... Ouch, 'Yu wants sugar'? Do fish like sweet things? How can they ask for it when they don’t even have hands?”","Zong Wenxiu: “......”","Good heavens, the meaning I learned wasn’t this.","Shunzi: “......”","Sometimes, teaching Master Jincheng is truly helpless.","“Pfft...” Xu Wan, who had just entered, heard this divine translation and slipped, banging her head against the doorframe with a loud thud.","Oh God! Spare her ears!","What on earth was this translation?!","Cui Zhi, who was holding a food box, was startled and quickly helped Xu Wan up: “Madam! Are you alright?”","Hearing the noise, the little devil finally opened his eyes, which had been closed the entire time. Seeing Xu Wan, he immediately became on full alert and quickly sat up from his half-reclined position on the long bench.","Seeing Xu Wan’s startled appearance, he instinctively felt that something wasn’t right.","Xu Wan, supported by Cui Zhi, walked in and weakly pointed at the little devil: “‘Yu wants sugar’... Only you could come up with that. Why not say the fish comes ashore to grab the sugar itself?”","The little devil crossed his arms and stood confidently, looking like the smartest person in the world: “Fish can’t come ashore to grab sugar, you’re the one who’s stupid, not me.”","Xu Wan: “......”","Fine, if you can’t realize you’re stupid, then at least don’t think everyone else is.","Truly, you are the little devil of chaos.","Xu Wan took a deep breath and silently repeated “one hundred million, one hundred million, one hundred million” three times to calm herself down.","She said: “Shunzi, when you teach Master Jincheng, remember to translate a sentence along with it, so he doesn’t come up with explanations like this in class and make Master Bai blow his beard for three days.”","Zong Jincheng glared at her.","He immediately caught the sarcasm in her words!","He questioned: “Are you afraid that I’m so talented I’m about to win, so you’re deliberately trying to hinder my studies?!”","This woman just wants to withhold my monthly allowance and servants, trapping me in Marquis Manor to slowly torment me. Hmph, I’ve long seen through her!","Xu Wan looked at the immature boy in front of her, who wore everything on his face, and couldn’t help but roll her eyes at the ceiling: “Do you know what it means to judge a gentleman by a petty man’s heart? That’s exactly what you look like right now.”","The little devil narrowed his eyes: “So you admit you’re the petty one.”","“Oh, I mean the gentleman is me.”","“???”","“The gentleman is me.” Xu Wan repeated, in case he hadn’t heard clearly.","The little devil: “!!!” Where’s my knife!","The two were about to start arguing again, but Cui Zhi, with her sharp eyes, quickly stepped in to mediate.","She hurriedly opened the food box and placed it on the table in front of the two young masters. It contained Dong's Seven-Flavor Cake, the most popular treat in the capital these days, which could only be bought by lining up before dawn.","Zong Wenxiu, who hadn’t tasted many delicacies, didn’t know the value of the Seven-Flavor Cake, but for the extravagant Zong Jincheng, it was different. This was something he had eaten daily in the past, but since Xu Wan had cut off his servants and money, no one had been there to queue for him, nor did he have the funds to buy it.","“Master Jincheng, Master Wenxiu, this is a Seven-Flavor Cake that Madam specially had someone buy for you. Madam may not be good with words, but she always keeps you two in her heart.”","Zong Wenxiu, who was already grateful to Xu Wan, quickly thanked her: “Thank you, Madam, for your care.”","Cui Zhi smiled and handed him a piece of the cake to taste.","The little devil was still locked in a battle of wills with Xu Wan.","His bright eyes, full of spirit, refused to back down, while Xu Wan’s gaze, though gentle and without aggression, showed no trace of fear. Instead, her calm demeanor gave her the upper hand.","Xu Wan raised an eyebrow: “Boy, aren’t you going to eat the Seven-Flavor Cake?”","She didn’t believe anyone could resist their favorite food and still claim they didn’t like it.","Zong Jincheng turned his head stubbornly: “A gentleman does not eat food handed out in pity.”","Zong Wenxiu, who had just stuffed a piece of Seven-Flavor Cake into his mouth: “......”","There was no pity, really, no pity at all.","Xu Wan snorted and didn’t continue arguing with him. She just glanced at the book on the table in front of Zong Wenxiu, as if casually asking: “Wenxiu, why are you also reading the Thousand Character Classic? Didn’t you just start learning the ‘Meng Qiu’?”","She couldn’t directly expose the private agreement between the two, or the little devil would become defensive. But she also couldn’t let him hold Zong Wenxiu back, or else this little rascal might slack off, dragging Zong Wenxiu down with him.","Zong Wenxiu’s heart skipped a beat when asked.","He instinctively looked at his brother...","What should he do? If he told the truth, his brother would be angry, but if he lied to Madam, how could he repay her for saving his mother?","The little devil, full of resentment, glared at Xu Wan, expecting her to continue provoking him. But perhaps because he had been provoked so much lately, he was too busy being angry to remember to coordinate his story with his half-brother.","Zong Wenxiu, not getting a response from his brother, could only stutter: “R-reviewing...”","The child, clearly not used to lying, was so nervous that his body trembled. He didn’t even dare to look at her, his head sinking lower and lower.","Xu Wan had expected his reaction. She smiled and replied: “Reviewing the old to understand the new—it’s indeed a good habit.”","“Mm-hmm...” Zong Wenxiu mumbled in response, hoping she would quickly move on from the topic.","But as luck would have it, Xu Wan continued: “I just looked at the ‘Meng Qiu’ book. Although it’s a bit thick, it’s a collection of historical anecdotes that are very helpful for building your knowledge. Knowing history allows you to understand the present. You should take it seriously and not just swallow it whole like an illiterate, or come up with something as ridiculous as ‘Yu wants sugar.’”","Suddenly called out, the illiterate Zong Jincheng: “???”","Does she think he can’t understand such obvious sarcasm?","The little devil was about to explode.","But Xu Wan turned to Zong Wenxiu: “I’ve looked into your learning abilities, and you should be able to finish reading ‘Meng Qiu’ within a month. Helping your brother study is hard work, but remember to focus on your own studies as well. Don’t fall behind. I’ll check on your progress in a month.”"]},{"number":21,"title":"Chapter 21: The Comeback Kid: Master of Counterattack","paragraphs":["Zong Wenxiu instinctively looked at his younger brother.","Oh no...","It seems I'm going to break my promise to my brother.","The \"Meng Qiu\" is a text of only 2,384 characters, yet it contains around six hundred historical anecdotes from the Spring and Autumn period to the Southern and Northern Dynasties, covering politics, military, culture, art, divination, customs, and more.","If he were to memorize it like Zong Jincheng, doing it in a month would be no problem. However, the issue is that Madam Xu said she would test him, and it certainly wouldn't be a simple quiz.","His mother once mentioned that Madam Xu is the eldest daughter of the Ministry of Justice's Minister, raised in a strict household, and well-read. If she intends to test him, he definitely can't try to bluff his way through like his brother.","\"Yes, Madam Xu, Wenxiu will study diligently,\" the young boy said humbly, looking very obedient.","Zong Jincheng immediately exploded.","He complained loudly, \"That's unfair! He's always learning new things; how can I ever catch up with his pace? This is simply unreasonable!\"","He was already behind by over a hundred books, and now there's another one he's never even heard of, \"Meng Qiu.\" He felt even more exhausted just thinking about it.","Xu Wan calmly said, \"It's only fair that he studies while you do. Do you think you're playing a game of 'carving a boat to find a lost sword'?\"","Zong Jincheng didn't understand what she meant by \"carving a boat to find a lost sword,\" but he guessed it wasn't a compliment. He glared at her with his round, flushed face.","Xu Wan: \"...\"","This little hothead's face is as red as a branding iron.","However, Xu Wan didn't want to push him too far. She turned around and said, \"Besides 'Meng Qiu,' as long as you can keep up with Wenxiu's progress, our agreement still stands.\"","She didn't want this little troublemaker to keep coming up with schemes every day.","After Xu Wan said this, the tense atmosphere eased, and the little troublemaker stopped his antics. As he watched her leaving back, he still felt a bit of anger lingering. He waved his hand at her back, as if trying to scratch her from afar.","He looked like he wanted to claw her to death from a distance.","Zong Wenxiu, who had been observing the exchange between the two, saw his brother flailing his arms at Madam Xu's back like a little lobster waving its claws. He found it both amusing and helpless.","He quickly stepped in to mediate, soothingly saying, \"Alright, alright, Madam Xu is actually very kind. Don't be angry. I'll read with you.\"","The little troublemaker, still full of resentment towards Xu Wan, looked at him suspiciously and asked, \"Do you like that woman?\"","\"Hmm?\"","Zong Wenxiu was stunned for a moment. He was about to nod, but seeing his brother's face filled with a threatening \"If you say yes, I'll kill you,\" he swallowed hard and said, \"Maybe it's because I haven't met many people, but Madam Xu is the kindest person to me besides my mother... Oh, and also besides you.\"","Luckily, Zong Wenxiu managed to add that last part in time, or the little troublemaker would have started another tantrum. He pouted and grumbled, \"She's not a good person. You should stay away from her.\"","Zong Wenxiu forced a smile and agreed half-heartedly, \"Mmm...\"","After saying that, Zong Jincheng lay down again, closed his eyes, and instructed Shunzi to read aloud, resuming his lazy memorization method.","Zong Wenxiu could only sigh silently and shake his head in helplessness.","Time passed quickly. Xu Wan knew the two were studying hard and wisely refrained from disturbing them. It was rare for the little troublemaker to stay home for a whole month, almost like a completely different person.","On the day of the examination, Xu Wan came to observe.","Seeing the little troublemaker seriously studying, even Baili Xi, the teacher, couldn't help but admire him: \"Jincheng, though a bit mischievous, is not entirely hopeless. Alright, today I'll test you with something simple. Write out the 'Thousand Character Classic' from memory.\"","Xu Wan swore she hadn't coordinated with Baili Xi. The teacher didn't know that the little troublemaker could only recite but not read or write.","She had thought that if the boy could obediently memorize the text, she could compromise and return his servants and money, ending the feud between them.","But now...","Baili Xi probably thought writing the \"Thousand Character Classic\" was an easy task, but for the little troublemaker, even memorizing the \"Strategies of the Warring States\" would be easier.","She glanced at the boy, wondering if she should step in to help, but then thought it might be better for him to suffer a setback under the teacher's hands, which could motivate him to study harder.","When Zong Jincheng heard the question, he looked at Xu Wan and saw her waiting to see his failure.","Hmph, bad woman.","Do you think you're so smart?","Today, I'm going to turn the tables!","Shunzi, following Baili Xi's instructions, placed the inkstone, brush, ink, and paper on the table. He opened the inkstone and was about to grind the ink as usual when he noticed a momentary reflection of light in the water. When he looked again, it seemed like he had just imagined it.","He rubbed his eyes and continued grinding the ink.","The little troublemaker sat calmly at his desk, while Zong Wenxiu, beside him, looked more anxious than the one being tested.","It felt like an eternity as the ink was being ground.","Even Baili Xi couldn't help but yawn: \"Is the ink ready?\"","\"Yes, it's ready,\" Shunzi replied and stepped aside.","The little troublemaker confidently picked up the brush, dipped it in the ink, and began writing on the paper. However, each stroke came out blurry, and some characters even seemed to disappear.","Shunzi was puzzled.","\"This... why are the characters like this?\" Could it be that he didn't grind the ink properly?","Baili Xi also came down and saw Zong Jincheng innocently lifting his brush, saying sincerely, \"Teacher, it seems we bought a fake inkstone.\"","The little troublemaker's face was always very convincing. When he wasn't angry, he looked innocent and charming, even when not smiling.","Baili Xi, who had witnessed his mischief during the first few days but now observed his obedient change, wouldn't hold a grudge.","The old man looked at him now and thought of his talented student, Zong Zhao. He just smiled kindly and said, \"Then recite it instead. We'll try writing again another day.\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","Teacher, you're so easily fooled. What blinded your eyes?","Was it the lingering teacher-student love from the previous generation?","Zong Jincheng stood up to thank him and then began to shake his head and sway his head while reciting the \"Thousand Character Classic.\" As Baili Xi's smile grew more satisfied, he even volunteered to recite a few pages of the \"Strategies of the Warring States\" to see if he had memorized them correctly.","Xu Wan: \"???\"","How did this kid's emotional intelligence suddenly spike?","He even knew how to turn passive into active, guiding Baili Xi to follow his train of thought. Anyone unaware of the situation would surely praise him for his hard work and progress!","Indeed, Baili Xi's admiration was impossible to hide.","That's right! This is it!","This is the son of Zong Zhao!","The next great scholar of the capital!"]},{"number":22,"title":"Chapter 22: Did You Win the Bet","paragraphs":["Xu Wan rolled her eyes to the sky.","She knew it.","Who would have thought that the wise and learned old scholar would be so easily deceived by the little devil? Truly, the little devil was worthy of his reputation. Full of clever schemes and tricks.","\"Fine, fine, fine. The pupil is indeed teachable. Zong Jincheng, your progress over the past month has truly impressed me. As the ancient saying goes, 'It's never too late to mend,' and since you are still young, there's plenty of time to catch up with your studies.\"","Baili Xi praised him while smiling, his eyebrows and eyes crinkling together, making him look just like the Laughing Buddha with his plump figure.","Zong Jincheng, finally feeling a sense of triumph, proudly raised his eyebrows at Xu Wan and placed his hands on his hips.","It was as if he was saying:","See? This round is a victory for this young master!","The mischievous and confident expression of the young boy was dazzling, making even Cui Zhi feel anxious for him.","The young master was getting carried away, truly carried away.","Xu Wan knew his true abilities, and yet here he was, boldly challenging her. If she were to reveal the truth—that he could only recite but not write—it would be easy to expose his shortcomings.","But after all, he was still a child.","Zong Jincheng's thoughts were simple, and his calculations were no bigger than a mung bean. He couldn't foresee the consequences of his actions and politely replied, \"It's all thanks to your excellent guidance, Master. You've gone to great lengths for your student.\"","Seeing him become so polite and well-mannered, Baili Xi felt even more gratified.","He stroked his beard and arranged, \"In that case, Zong Jincheng will join the others in studying 'Meng Qiu' from now on. I will come to teach you all tomorrow.\"","\"Thank you, Master,\" the two children replied in unison.","Xu Wan stood up to see Baili Xi off the premises, politely adding on the way, \"We are grateful for your efforts, Master. Zong Jincheng has indeed made significant progress, all thanks to your meticulous guidance.\"","\"Madam, you flatter me. It's thanks to you that this child has been brought back on the right path...\"","The two adults continued to praise each other, walking further away in the midst of their mutual admiration.","Left behind, Zong Wenxiu was genuinely happy for his brother. Over the past month, although Zong Jincheng hadn't been particularly diligent and hadn't spent much time memorizing texts, his talent was astonishing, and he had quickly caught up with his brother's progress. Zong Wenxiu felt a surge of pressure. Fortunately, Xu Wan had kept him from stopping his studies, or else he might have been surpassed by his brother.","As he turned to look, he saw his brother suddenly change expressions.","Zong Jincheng's smiling face instantly collapsed the moment the two adults left. He transformed into a fierce, intimidating child, carelessly tossing the book he was holding onto the ground, where it landed with a loud thud, its fresh pages now covered in dust.","He sprawled lazily in his chair, his feet propped up on the table, the dirty soles of his shoes knocking over the inkstone, spilling ink all over the floor. The culprit showed no remorse, acting like a carefree young master who didn't care about the consequences of his actions.","Zong Wenxiu, who had just been praising his brother, was stunned.","Wait, what just happened?","Didn't his brother just improve?","\"Jincheng?\" Zong Wenxiu tentatively called out.","The young master continued his relaxed pose, his tired eyes closed, as he wailed loudly, \"I'm exhausted! Finally, this tough time is over. I'll never want to be a good Samaritan again. Hurry up, Shunzi, keep the door well. Once that woman returns, we'll immediately reclaim my silver and men. I swear I'll never recite another word of text in my life!\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","Right, he had almost forgotten. His brother hadn't been studying willingly but for his own sake. Now that the agreement with Xu Wan had been fulfilled, would his brother leave the study?","Zong Wenxiu felt a tinge of disappointment. Although his brother had been late to rise, half-asleep during recitations, and often left early, he was still the only peer he could talk to in this grand mansion.","Shunzi, as Zong Jincheng's sole servant, diligently kept watch at the door, but after a cup of tea's time, Xu Wan still hadn't returned.","The young master, even with his eyes closed, was getting impatient. He looked outside and said, \"What's going on? Has she run off without fulfilling her promise? This time is enough for her to see the master off three times.\"","Upon opening his eyes, he saw the outside was empty, with no maids in sight, just like the usual end of class.","Xu Wan... had she forgotten about them?","Zong Jincheng put his legs down from the table and just as he stepped onto the ground, he saw his cousin crouching on the floor, holding a clean cloth, meticulously wiping the ink stains.","It was the inkstone he had just kicked over.","The young master had done such things more than once or twice, and no one had ever scolded him. Even in front of his grandparents, his grandmother would kindly arrange for the maids to clean up.","Zong Wenxiu...","He was, after all, his elder brother.","Zong Jincheng suddenly felt an odd sense of guilt, an inexplicable discomfort. He stepped forward and pulled the boy up, \"Let Shunzi handle it.\"","Zong Wenxiu smiled at him, \"It's alright, Shunzi is busy keeping watch. I can clean it; it's not a hard task.\"","Zong Jincheng frowned and let go of him.","Then he watched as Zong Wenxiu quickly wiped the floor, switching sides of the cloth to keep it clean, the ink stains disappearing in no time.","After cleaning the ink, Zong Wenxiu placed the inkstone back on the table and picked up the books his brother had thrown, dusting them off and placing them neatly on the desk.","The young master had expected Zong Wenxiu to at least say a few words about how books shouldn't be treated that way, how scholars should be more particular, but instead, he said, \"Did you put something in the inkstone to make the ink unable to write?\"","Zong Jincheng proudly replied, \"Hehe, I added some lard.\"","Zong Wenxiu couldn't help but laugh, of course.","\"Madam must have noticed.\"","The young master shrugged nonchalantly, showing no fear, \"If she noticed, so what? The master already let me pass. If she goes back on her word, she's a dog.\"","Zong Wenxiu shook his head.","It wouldn't be that simple.","He had heard about the agreement between Xu Wan and their grandmother. She wouldn't give up so easily on making his brother study.","But the person involved didn't seem to realize that.","Xu Wan had intended to settle accounts with the young master after seeing Baili Xi off. After all, she had worked hard to get him into the study; there was no way she would let him escape so easily.","As she was thinking about what to do, Baili Xi suddenly said to her with a cryptic tone, \"Madam, in all matters, one should proceed step by step. Do not rush, lest you go astray.\"","Xu Wan blinked, looking at the smiling old man in front of her, and smiled back, \"Thank you for your guidance, Master.\"","She had thought Zong Jincheng had truly deceived Baili Xi.","It turned out the old man was wise in his own way.","He hadn't bothered to argue with the little rascal.","After all, he was the one who had taught a champion scholar. His mind was as clear as a mirror.","Baili Xi nodded at her and returned home, confident that Zong Zhao's wife would handle the rest perfectly.","As Xu Wan returned to the inner courtyard, she thought through various plans, considering the possible reactions and constantly coming up with new strategies.","Suddenly, she thought of one thing.","Her steps came to a halt—","\"Cui Zhi, how much is Wenxiu's monthly allowance?\""]},{"number":23,"title":"Chapter 23: Caught Two More Accomplices","paragraphs":["“Twenty taels.”","Xu Wan was astonished: “So much?”","She had thought that the monthly allowance for a concubine's son would be less.","In the Minister's Mansion, the concubine's sons only received five taels each month; even Xu Lian'er, her beloved younger sister who was a legitimate daughter, only got fifteen taels; the original mistress, according to the rules, should have also received fifteen taels, but due to various deductions, she was left with almost nothing.","In comparison, Zong Wenxiu's life was actually quite good.","But... it didn't show at all...","Cui Zhi nodded: \"Yes, usually a concubine's son in an ordinary family wouldn't get more than ten taels a month, but since Master Wenxiu endured nine and a half years of hardship outside, the Old Madam is very fond of him, so after he returned to the mansion, she gave him a lot of gold, silver, silk, and expensive writing materials, and also raised his monthly allowance to twenty taels.\"","“Then why is his clothing still so... plain?” Xu Wan noticed that he always wore hemp clothes, which were clean and neat, but certainly not as comfortable as silk.","Xu Wan had only taken over the education plan for the little demon king and hadn't interfered with the household affairs, so she had always thought that this was the treatment he received from the mansion.","Cui Zhi said: “Master Wenxiu said he wasn't used to it, so the Old Madam didn't force him and let him be.”","Xu Wan nodded.","A child from the slums, who had been struggling on the edge of life and death every day, suddenly becoming a rich young master, generally had two outcomes:","One was the mentality of a nouveau riche, indulging in retaliatory eating, drinking, and enjoyment, even going to extremes, which was a result of being overwhelmed by material desires, quite common;","The other was someone with extremely high moral standards, feeling guilty for not sharing the suffering of the common people, feeling ashamed of living in luxury.","Zong Wenxiu was the second type.","Xu Wan suddenly thought of something and asked: “By the way, Cui Zhi, has Wenxiu returned to the slums since coming back to the mansion?”","After escaping from such a place, probably no one would want to go back, but...","“He has, Master Wenxiu goes there once a month,” Cui Zhi mentioned this with some confusion, “Every time he goes, he takes a huge carriage, and we don't know what’s inside.”","Cui Zhi was afraid her words might be misunderstood, so she quickly added: “But nothing has ever gone missing from the mansion, and Master Wenxiu has always been virtuous.”","\"Hmm?\" Xu Wan keenly noticed something unusual and turned towards the inner courtyard, heading to the accounting room instead, \"Let's go, check the ledgers.\"","“Ah? The ledgers?”","In the accounting room.","The carriage was carrying sorghum buns, the cheapest kind of steamed bread, which noble families never have because they taste bad,\" the accountant reported the findings truthfully.","Cui Zhi and Cui Liu looked at each other.","They seemed to understand what Master Wenxiu was doing every month.","It was such a... noble act.","“Let’s go.”","Xu Wan called out to the two of them, looking up: “Time to discipline the little brat.”","Cui Zhi and Cui Liu nodded in unison and quickly followed.","After waiting for another teapot’s time, Zong Jincheng’s patience was running out. He was about to storm out to demand an explanation from Xu Wan, but before he could even step out, he saw Xu Wan and her entourage approaching.","Zong Jincheng looked up and said: “If you didn’t come back soon, I would’ve thought you ran away. Listen, this time I won, and if you don’t keep your promise, that’s... hey, why are you looking at me like that? What are you going to do?”","The little demon king’s light footsteps faltered when he met Xu Wan’s long, stern face, and he immediately took a step back.","It turned out that this notoriously infamous eldest grandson actually responded better to tough love. Having been pampered with gentle words since childhood, he had become oblivious to the realities of the world. Only when he encountered a tough challenge did he begin to reflect on himself.","What was this woman’s expression? It looked like she was ready to settle accounts with him.","Just knowing Zong Wenxiu’s secret, Xu Wan found Zong Jincheng particularly irritating. Both were surnamed Zong, so why did this one turn out to be such a mischievous troublemaker?","With such a contrast, it was hard to stay calm.","She took a deep breath, closed her eyes, and when she opened them again, her beautiful face had returned to its usual calm and composed state, as if the woman with intense pressure moments ago wasn’t her.","The little demon king was sharp and sensed the change in her aura, immediately starting to act up: “Return my people and money to me right now.”","Xu Wan nodded to the side.","Cui Zhi ordered two servants to be brought forward, both of whom had served in Zong Jincheng’s room before.","“Madam, we’ve caught everyone.”","“San De provided the lard, and Chang swapped the ink. It was the young master who asked them to do it.”","Zong Jincheng: “???”","How did they know!!!","The little demon king turned to glare at Shunzi, the only one who knew the truth!","“It wasn’t me!” Shunzi quickly waved his hands, panicking so much that he almost shouted “I’m innocent!”","Zong Wenxiu, who was watching from the side, was stunned. Although his brother’s trick with the lard was clumsy, Madam Xu had managed to interrogate everyone so quickly...","Too terrifying!","Xu Wan stood at the door, her figure silhouetted by the light, half of her face slowly emerging from the darkness: “Jincheng, you are clever, but don’t think everyone else is stupid. Our agreement was for you to keep up with Wenxiu’s progress. What you’ve done so far is merely surpassing in memorization.”","“Although there’s still a significant gap to our goal, it’s worth encouraging, so I agree to return your monthly allowance to you, at the standard for a noble family member, twenty taels a month.”","“Twenty taels?” Zong Jincheng had probably never heard of such a small amount. He spent more than that on a single meal with his friends!","“Grandmother never restricted my allowance before, and now you’re cutting it to twenty taels, and you have the nerve to call it returning my money? How can you even say that!” The little chick was clearly flustered, starting to wail.","Xu Wan’s head was pounding from the noise, and she covered her ears with her hands, trying to block out the sound: “If you want to spend money freely, you need to meet our agreement, otherwise, forget it.”","Xu Wan’s stance was firm.","Zong Jincheng was so angry that his face turned red, his body heaving violently. If he knew martial arts, he might have jumped up to scratch her by now.","“Tell me! What exactly do I need to do to catch up with his progress!” Zong Jincheng’s face was dark, his fists clenched, his usual cuteness gone, replaced by ferocity.","It’s just writing, what’s so hard about that!","He had the ability to memorize anything after reading it once, so naturally, he could write anything after reading it once!","And what’s this nonsense about understanding the meaning? He’ll just keep memorizing!","It’s just a matter of spending another month on it, he’s not short on time!","The little demon king’s inner thoughts were written all over his face. Xu Wan inwardly sighed, feeling that the heavens were indeed unfair. This mischievous child had an eidetic memory, and with rote memorization, he could soon be free.","With the goal of achieving the first rank still so far away, she certainly couldn’t let Zong Jincheng escape so easily. She needed to make him understand the importance of studying.","Xu Wan turned to ask: “Cui Liu, is the carriage ready?”","“It’s ready.”","“Alright, let’s go then.” Xu Wan signaled to the two boys to follow.","Zong Wenxiu obediently followed.","Zong Jincheng, however, wasn’t so obedient. He directly asked: “Where are we going? I still have to study at home, I don’t have time to wander around with you!”","Hmph, this woman had better say something nice, or else he might consider showing her around the luxurious and fun places in the capital!"]},{"number":24,"title":"Chapter 24: Kid, What Are You Running For","paragraphs":["Xu Wan lazily glanced at him and said, \"Fine, then I'll just take Zong Wenxiu out. Anyway, Young Master Zong Jincheng doesn't like meeting people, so he can stay home and guard the house.\"","As she spoke, she left with Cui Zhi, and Zong Wenxiu obediently followed behind her.","Seeing this, Zong Jincheng panicked.","This woman wasn't playing by the rules. Didn't she always stick to her word?","Why was she being so obedient now!","The little devil quickly found a way out for himself and hurried after them in two steps: \"No way, I'm coming too! Zong Wenxiu has no experience of the world, is obedient and easily fooled. If you have ill intentions and sell him off, where would I find another companion for reading?\"","Xu Wan walked while coolly adding, \"If we could sell people, you'd definitely be the first to go.\"","The little devil's tail immediately perked up: \"Of course, this young master is priceless, worth even more.\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","Xu Wan's mouth twitched, and finally, she turned to him with a smile, asking, \"You really know how to justify yourself. With your weak shoulders and hands that can't even lift a thing, if someone bought you to the countryside, you wouldn't even be able to raise a pig, a complete waste of food. I'm genuinely curious, where does this unfounded confidence of yours come from?\"","Zong Jincheng's happy face, upon hearing this blunt remark, immediately fell, and his beautiful black eyes began to burn with anger: \"Who would go to the countryside to raise pigs! Even if I went to the countryside, I'd be the young master!\"","Xu Wan concluded: \"Oh, blind confidence.\"","Zong Jincheng: \"...\"","The little devil, feeling humiliated and angry, continued to nag, clearly determined to persuade Xu Wan.","The three of them got into the carriage.","Xu Wan took out a prepared lunchbox from the carriage and handed it to Zong Wenxiu: \"It's a bit of a long journey, so if you get hungry, have some food to tide you over.\"","Zong Wenxiu, flattered, nodded: \"Thank you, Madam.\"","The completely ignored Zong Jincheng: \"?\"","What about me? What about me?","Am I not a person too!","He glared furiously at the two, trying to evoke some guilt, but Xu Wan completely ignored him, handing over the lunchbox and then closing her eyes to rest.","Zong Jincheng: \"!!!\"","Zong Wenxiu, keenly sensing that something was amiss, quickly pushed the lunchbox toward him: \"You eat first.\"","The little devil stared at the lunchbox for three seconds before turning his head haughtily to the side.","\"Hmph.\"","Not giving it to me, who cares.","Eating pastries will ruin my teeth anyway!","After some time, the road became rougher, and the carriage kept shaking.","The little devil was dizzy and disoriented, nearly falling onto Xu Wan several times, but he hated her, so he used Zong Wenxiu as a pillar to hold onto.","Every time the carriage shook, one brother tried to stay still while the other clung tightly to him.","\"Bang——\" A loud crash came from outside the carriage.","Xu Wan opened her eyes to see the two brothers hugging tightly, showing rare brotherly affection.","She teased, \"What are you two playing at?\"","\"We...\"","\"Bang——\"","\"Ah——\"","Before they could answer, the carriage suddenly shook violently, and the two brothers fell off their seats, with even Xu Wan hitting her head on the window, making a loud thud.","\"Madam!\" Zong Wenxiu was the first to crawl over, anxiously asking, \"Are you alright?\"","Xu Wan shook her slightly dizzy head and reassured, \"I'm fine, you two sit tight.\" Then she asked outside, \"Cui Zhi, what happened?\"","Cui Zhi reported the situation truthfully: \"Madam, our carriage hit a child.\"","\"What?\" Upon hearing they had hit someone, and a child at that, Xu Wan immediately panicked, \"Quick, see how he is, is he badly hurt?\"","Xu Wan lifted the carriage curtain and got out, with Zong Jincheng and Zong Wenxiu following closely.","In front of the carriage lay a six or seven-year-old boy, wearing dirty, ragged clothes, his face smeared with blood and mud, his frail body looking like it might break, yet he struggled to get up.","\"Quick, don't let him move!\"","Xu Wan knew that a severe impact could cause various fatal conditions, especially if the body moved, which could worsen the situation.","But the boy was desperate to get up, and upon hearing Xu Wan's words, he became even more frantic, using all his strength to crawl up and run into a nearby alley without looking back.","\"Kid, why are you running?\"","\"Come back, we'll take you to see a doctor.\"","\"Slow down, hey...\"","Two servants from Marquis Manor chased after the boy, causing the merchants on both sides to think a big official was causing trouble, and they all began preparing to pack up and go home, leading to chaos on the street.","Zong Jincheng completely failed to understand this situation. Puzzled, he thought, \"Why is this kid, covered in wounds, in such a hurry to run? Could he be a fugitive the authorities are after?\"","Xu Wan kindly reminded, \"Our laws state that children under seven, even if they commit murder, are not guilty.\"","Judging by the boy's age, he certainly wasn't over seven, so he couldn't be a fugitive.","Zong Jincheng frowned and honestly said, \"What about those implicated in a nine-family extermination?\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","She was actually speechless for a moment by the little devil.","She had overlooked that there was such a crime in ancient times.","Taking a deep breath, she said, \"In recent years, the current emperor hasn't exterminated anyone's nine clans. Can't you think of something positive?\"","Zong Jincheng defended, \"Is it my fault for not wanting to be positive? It's obvious he's acting suspiciously. Who runs away after being hit? It looks like he hit us.\"","\"The kid is covered in blood, how did you see he's acting suspicious? Judging others with petty thoughts.\" Xu Wan sharply evaluates.","Zong Jincheng, with an air of righteous indignation, said, \"I... I just saw it, anyway, he's not normal!\"","\"Slandering people without evidence, what if you wrong him?\"","\"Hmph, impossible! I've seen all kinds of people, if he's innocent, I'll write my name Zong Jincheng backwards!\"","\"Hehe, let's wait and see.\"","Xu Wan then had the two sit back in the carriage and headed in the direction the boy had disappeared.","Zong Jincheng and Xu Wan, having just argued, didn't speak to each other, but Zong Wenxiu, looking at the familiar uneven road outside, nervously tightened his fingers. He glanced at Xu Wan, seemingly understanding where she had brought them.","It was the slum where he had lived with his mother for nine and a half years...","A place no noble in the Capital City would ever want to visit."]},{"number":25,"title":"Chapter 25: Strange Power","paragraphs":["The worn-out road was uneven, and one could easily trip and fall if not careful. Little Demon King had never been to such a place before and stumbled and tripped along the way. However, his attention was entirely focused on catching the child, so he rarely complained about the poor environment.","The alley was so narrow that only two people could pass through at the same time, and the bloodstains on the ground were increasing, with each droplet of blood growing larger. Xu Wan mused, \"We need to find him quickly.\" The child was seriously injured.","The two boys quickened their pace upon hearing this, rushing into the depths of the alley. Children of that age were fast runners, but Xu Wan struggled to keep up. She turned to Cui Liu and instructed, \"Follow them and protect them from the shadows. Do not interfere with anything else.\"","\"Yes.\"","Zong Wenxiu knew the way, aware that the child was heading toward the slums. Even when the blood trail disappeared for a while, he could still figure out the direction. He had grown up here and knew every corner of this place.","Little Demon King, focused solely on running, followed Zong Wenxiu without hesitation, sweeping away countless spiderwebs and kicking aside broken windows and rotten wood along the way.","Finally, they found the child in a narrow corner. The young boy, losing too much blood, had collapsed on the ground. His tattered and thin clothes were soaked red, yet he still struggled to get up, like a snail making repeated efforts only to fall back weakly each time.","The boy's eyes were red, and he continued to struggle desperately.","Zong Wenxiu quickly ran over to help him.","The Little Demon King watched from a distance, disdainful of the child's dirty appearance, yet unable to tear his eyes away, filled with curiosity.","What a strange person, what a strange power.","What is he doing?","Zong Wenxiu, now covered in blood and mud, didn't care at all. Instead, he anxiously comforted: \"You're badly injured. You can't move anymore; it will hurt. The doctor will be here soon. Wait for him to check you before you try to get up.\"","The child in his hands was so frail that he felt like just a bundle of bones. He dared not apply too much pressure, fearing further injury.","Unexpectedly, the boy's struggle intensified upon hearing this, and this time, his strength was astonishing. He pushed Zong Wenxiu to the ground.","\"Ah...\"","Hearing Zong Wenxiu's shout, Little Demon King quickly came to help. With plenty of practical experience from fights, he directly pinned the child to the ground using both hands and feet: \"Don't move. I don't hold back when I strike.\"","Xu Wan arrived just in time to see this scene: \"Jin Cheng! Why are you fighting?\"","The boy was pinned down, tears streaming down his face, his sobs growing louder: \"Let me go, please let me go. I can't afford a doctor, I can't afford medicine. I really can't afford it... I have a younger sister to take care of at home. I really can't afford the medicine... Please, please let me go. I'll kowtow to you, I'll kowtow to you...\"","With only his head free, the boy repeatedly slammed it against the ground, the sound of kowtowing loud, his forehead bleeding profusely.","Zong Wenxiu was struck by realization and quickly pulled his brother off the child.","The boy, now free, tried to run again, but after such turmoil, he had no strength left and collapsed on the ground, silently weeping. Even speaking had become a luxury at this moment.","Little Demon King's eyes widened in shock, speechless.","What was he saying?","Because he couldn't afford medicine, he was so desperate to escape. Even though he was the victim, he refused to gamble on the possibility that they might take responsibility, fleeing with all his might.","What kind of despair had he experienced?","It was then that Little Demon King finally took a closer look at him. In the freezing cold, the boy wore only a thin garment, his face covered in frostbite, his hands and feet in a terrible state. Blood seeped from his head and body, yet he looked like an old man devoid of vitality, his eyes filled with sorrowful pleading. All he wanted was for them to let him go.","Cui Zhi, moved by the scene, wanted to speak up but saw Xu Wan shaking her head at her.","It was Zong Wenxiu who reacted first, unfastening his cloak and wrapping it around the child.","The boy, whose face was frozen purple and blue, felt his consciousness slowly returning as the warm clothes enveloped him.","Zong Wenxiu, however, sneezed heavily.","Little Demon King frowned, hesitating for a few seconds before grabbing his own fox-fur cloak and, in Cui Zhi's surprised gaze, wrapped it around both Zong Wenxiu and himself.","Cui Zhi: \"...\"","Disappointed. She had thought Jin Cheng would offer his cloak like Zong Wenxiu did.","But this was still progress. In the past, Jin Cheng wouldn't even have considered sharing.","Xu Wan arrived with the government physician, but the narrow alley was too small for the carriage, so the government physician had to walk in. The already cramped space became even more crowded.","\"It's just some superficial wounds. Apply some good medicine, and it will be fine.\"","Upon hearing this, the boy shuddered and struggled again, refusing to let the physician treat him.","Zong Wenxiu tried to reassure him, but the boy wouldn't listen. It was only when Little Demon King sternly shouted, \"Don't move. You're not paying for the medicine. We have it at our residence.\"","Perhaps the commanding tone frightened the boy, for he didn't resist for the first time and obediently let the physician treat his wounds.","Xu Wan: \"...\"","Even Little Demon King had a role to play here.","The government physician's skills were proficient, gently cleaning the wounds and applying medicine, slowly lowering the boy's guard.","Zong Wenxiu introduced themselves and asked, \"What's your name?\"","\"Jing Zhe.\" The boy replied.","\"Jing Zhe marks the time when the yang energy rises, temperatures warm up, thunder rumbles, and rain increases, bringing vitality to all living things,\" Zong Wenxiu said. \"It's a name full of hope.\"","Jing Zhe was stunned.","He had just learned the meaning of his name.","Seeing his stunned expression, Zong Wenxiu speculated, \"Did I misunderstand? Are those not the characters?\"","Jing Zhe's eyes reddened, his voice choked: \"A big brother gave me this name. I didn't know what it meant, only that it sounded nice. If I had known, I wouldn't have called myself this...\"","He lowered his head, feeling inferior, and said, \"Children born here don't live to see adulthood. I don't deserve such a good name.\"","Zong Wenxiu, having grown up in these conditions, could deeply empathize. Even before being brought back to the Marquis's residence, his thoughts had been the same as Jing Zhe's, unsure if he would see another day.","On the other hand, Little Demon King had no sense of immersion at all. He casually interjected, breaking Jing Zhe's melancholy: \"Names are meant to sound nice. There are plenty of people with the same name anyway. What's with this business of being worthy or not? Don't want to be called Jing Zhe? Would you rather be called Jing Xia (startle)?\""]},{"number":26,"title":"Chapter 26: What are you doing with his sister","paragraphs":["Zong Wenxiu's comforting words got stuck in his throat.","His brother had really outdone himself this time.","This way of offering comfort was truly unique!","Xu Wan couldn't help but roll her eyes at the sky again. Listening to the little demon's words was always a precarious balance between being infuriated and amused.","With such a bizarre thought process, why didn't it make people panic instead?","Jing Zhe: \"......\" He was furious but dared not speak out.","After all, he had accepted help and was now being treated with medicine. The child, covered in ointment, ultimately refrained from retorting.","With the assistance of the servant, Jing Zhe was helped onto the carriage. Xu Wan accompanied him all the way home, which also happened to be their destination for the day.","The slums.","This was a desolate, abandoned city, dark, dirty, and noisy, filled with the poorest residents of the Capital City. The constant coughing of the inhabitants revealed a heavy atmosphere of illness and death.","The little demon had never been to such a place before. He instinctively clutched Zong Wenxiu's sleeve, trembling with fear as he asked, \"What kind of place is this? Is this wicked woman planning to abandon us here? Abandoning children is against the law!\"","Before Zong Wenxiu could explain, Jing Zhe looked up earnestly and said, \"No child traffickers would come here to pick kids.\"","\"Why?\" the little demon asked instinctively.","\"Because... it's dirty,\" Jing Zhe hesitated to be more specific. Many of the children here were sick, and even those who weren't were filthy. The noble families would surely disdain them even more.","\"Oh,\" Zong Jincheng assumed he meant the traffickers found the place too dirty and quickly understood, thinking it was too filthy for anyone to want to come. Initially, he had tiptoed through the area, but upon realizing there was no clean spot, he decided to just give up and treat it like wading through mud.","After all, he didn't have to wash his clothes or shoes himself.","However, as they ventured deeper, the little demon gripped Zong Wenxiu's arm even tighter. In addition to many sickly old people and women, there were also numerous children of his age, living like countless other Jing Zhe's.","They endured the coldest winters with only a few tattered rags to cover themselves; their faces were sallow and emaciated due to hunger, their bones protruding frighteningly.","Zong Jincheng felt a bit uncomfortable.","He had never seen such a place, so many impoverished people.","In the glamorous and prosperous Capital City, he had only known himself and those around him to be either rich or noble. When Zong Wenxiu had first returned to the manor, he had been the most modest among them.","Suddenly being exposed to this other world made him feel a sense of unreality.","Jing Zhe led them to the entrance of his home's alley. What was called an alley was merely a few tattered cloths stretched over a makeshift shelter, and the houses inside were likely no better.","\"I'm home. Thank you for helping me treat my injuries today,\" Jing Zhe said.","The little demon's mouth twitched, feeling a bit awkward.","This was the first time he had ever been thanked after making a mistake, almost making him forget that this child had been the one he had knocked over.","As they were talking, a girl's cries suddenly echoed from the alley. A middle-aged man dressed in a steward's uniform was forcefully dragging a three-year-old girl.","Jing Zhe hurriedly rushed over and shouted, \"Bad man! Let go of my sister!\"","Although a child's strength couldn't compare to an adult's, the unexpected push caused the middle-aged man to stagger.","As he turned around, the little demon was stunned. It was someone he recognized, \"Steward Zhai? Is that you?\"","Steward Zhai was from the Weiyuan Earl Manor. His master's eldest son, Zhai Yao, was his good friend, often going out together to fight, play, and roam around, so he recognized him.","Steward Zhai was surprised, \"Master Jincheng? Why are you in a place like this?\" He then released the little girl and ordered the other servants, \"You, take her away. Be careful not to hurt her.\"","\"Yes,\" several servants rushed forward, pushing Jing Zhe aside and grabbing the little girl.","The entire action took less than two seconds.","Zong Jincheng watched as the bandages applied by the manor doctor to Jing Zhe began to unravel one by one. The feeling of all their hard work going to waste was truly terrible.","He stepped forward and blocked their path, asking, \"I'm here to send Jing Zhe home. What are you doing, taking his sister?\"","Steward Zhai didn't immediately answer the question. Instead, he cautiously glanced at the red-clad woman behind him, recognizing Xu Wan, the current head of the Marquis Manor.","Only then did he step forward and bow, answering insincerely, \"Madam, Master Jincheng, you may not know, but our young master wants a few foot-washing maids. I thought I'd pick some from the slums to bring back to the manor for a better life. Who would have thought they'd be so ungrateful and unwilling to let go? It's a waste of my good intentions.\"","Zong Jincheng: \"???\"","What was this old man talking about??","\"You want a three-year-old girl to be a foot-washing maid for Zhai Yao? Who exactly do you expect to serve whom?\"","Zong Jincheng almost wanted to ask if the man's brain was malfunctioning.","Steward Zhai calmly replied, \"It was our young master's specific request to choose younger ones. Starting to cultivate affection from a young age is more intimate. For our manor, it's just an extra pair of chopsticks. They'll grow up in a few years.\"","Xu Wan listened silently, her gaze scrutinizing him.","His voice was weak, his eyes shifty, his smile obsequious.","A slippery old fox.","Xu Wan asked, \"Why did Steward Zhai come here to pick children? I heard that even child traffickers don't want to come here.\"","Steward Zhai smiled, \"The children sold by traffickers are too old. Our young master wants to raise a few little playthings, and only here can you find them. Look, their family is so poor they can't even eat or wear warm clothes. If they come back with us to the manor, they certainly won't be mistreated.\"","What he said was true.","Even if they were just foot-washing maids in the Marquis Manor, their lives would undoubtedly be more comfortable than here.","However, something just felt off.","Xu Wan asked, \"Steward Zhai, does the Weiyuan Earl Manor have the proper documentation to take this child?\"","Even if children from the slums were to be sold, they needed to sign a contract to ensure the rights and interests of both parties.","Otherwise, that would be considered kidnapping.","Unexpectedly, as soon as the topic of the contract came up, Steward Zhai's expression changed immediately.","In less than a second, Xu Wan noticed a flash of ferocity in his eyes, but it quickly returned to his usual smooth and cunning smile.","\"Since this child is a friend of Master Jincheng, then I naturally cannot force the matter. Come, release her,\" Steward Zhai said, then apologized to Zong Jincheng, \"I'm sorry for disturbing Master Jincheng. We have urgent matters at the manor, so we'll talk another day.\"","The fierce servants all let go, and Steward Zhai quickly left with them.","Jing Zhe hurriedly went to take his sister.","Zong Wenxiu was seeing his brother's influence in action for the first time and couldn't help but exclaim in amazement, \"Jincheng, your face is really big. He let go without a word!\"","If he had been alone here, he certainly wouldn't have been able to do anything about the people from the Weiyuan Earl Manor.","Zong Jincheng, feeling flattered, proudly said, \"Of course, who would dare not give face to this young master? Unlike some people, who didn't even get a farewell greeting when they left!\""]},{"number":27,"title":"Chapter 27: The Little Demon's Face-to-Face Attack","paragraphs":["Xu Wan found the little prince's habit of 'taking every opportunity to boast about himself and put her down' incredibly childish.","Steward Zhai wasn't giving Zong Jincheng face at all; there must be some secret he didn't want to be deeply investigated, which was why he left in such a hurry.","However, Xu Wan wasn't interested in any of that. The first rule of the workplace is not to meddle in matters that don't concern you. Her current priority was to educate the little prince.","Xu Wan ordered, \"Cui Zhi, go and bring the food and drinks from our carriage, along with the clothes and fabrics. Oh, and take down the carriage curtain as well. I see this shed is so broken it doesn't even block the wind.\"","\"Yes.\"","Cui Zhi quickly brought everything over and handed it to the two young masters.","The brothers were busy changing the bedding and finding a ladder to replace the carriage curtain on the shed, all without relying on others.","— The servants, under Xu Wan's indication, had retreated far away.","Zong Wenxiu, having endured hardships since childhood, took the dirty and tiring tasks ahead of Zong Jincheng.","Zong Jincheng, on the other hand, rolled up his sleeves and worked up a sweat. For the moment, he didn't care about the dirt and was even more enthusiastic than Zong Wenxiu, grunting as he carried the ladder.","Xu Wan raised an eyebrow, thinking: Could it be that Wenxiu's praise earlier injected some kind of adrenaline into this kid?","The shed was quickly repaired, and boys always had a knack for such things.","However, the carriage curtain was a luxurious green drape, which looked extremely out of place on the shabby roof.","Cui Zhi's mouth twitched as she reminded, \"Madam, perhaps we should send someone tomorrow to replace it with something else for them. You and the two young masters will be taking the carriage back to the manor later, and without the curtain, it will be very cold.\"","Xu Wan was indeed someone who felt the cold easily. She was bundled up thickly for the outing, while the two young boys, being full of youthful energy, were much more resistant to the cold.","She smiled, \"It's fine, I'll just wrap myself tighter in my fur cloak.\"","Xu Wan had a tough childhood in an orphanage, often going hungry and cold, but fortunately, there were many warm siblings around her, which gave her solace.","Zong Jincheng came down from the ladder, took a step back, and admired his work, very satisfied with himself and giving it a perfect score: \"A! Top-notch A!\"","Xu Wan: \"......\"","This kid is way too narcissistic!","He's acting out the whole show by himself!","Jing Zhe, seeing his own house repaired, repeatedly thanked them.","His sister also helped pour a few bowls of water, inviting them in to drink. Seeing this, Jing Zhe quickly stopped her, \"Take it inside, they won't drink water from here.\"","His sister was scolded and took a step back, tears about to fall.","People in the slums often fell ill due to unclean water sources, but as they were of low birth, they couldn't find decent work outside and were trapped here generation after generation.","Zong Wenxiu knew this and wasn't too bothered, but his younger brother had been pampered since birth and might fall ill if he drank from here, so he also stepped up to stop it.","The little prince was about to say it was fine, but after glancing at the dirty rim of the bowl, he swallowed his words.","Forget it!","He'd better stick to being his precious young master!","While they were talking at the house door, Xu Wan was outside the street, arranging to return to the manor.","At that moment, the sound of horse hooves suddenly echoed through the street.","\"Get out of the way! Move!\"","\"This street has fewer people! We can make as much mess as we want!\"","\"Whoosh! This Akhal-Teke horse sure runs fast!\"","\"Brothers, charge! Today, I must win first place!\"","Several young masters in luxurious clothing recklessly galloped through the street, knocking over countless shabby stalls.","Debris flew everywhere, making the already impoverished street even worse, with cries of despair filling the air.","\"They're back again! They're back again!\"","\"These noble sons are trying to drive us to death!\"","\"Heavenly Father! Are you not going to let us live?\"","The cries of the poor went unanswered, only met with even more arrogant laughter from the young masters:","\"Zhai Yao, why are you pulling that flagpole? It's so dirty!\"","\"It's fun, I'll throw it away right away, watch this!\"","\"Pfft—\"","The thrown dirty flagpole flew from the sky and landed squarely on Jing Zhe's roof, piercing through—","The little prince's freshly placed carriage curtain...","It was ruined.","Zong Wenxiu's eyes widened.","Oh no!","His brother is definitely going to explode!","Xu Wan also doubted her eyes. In this entire capital, was there anyone who dared to confront the little prince like this?","The little prince: \"?????\"","What just flew by?","Who stuck a flagpole through his roof??","Who did it? Who did it???","Who the hell did it!","\"Shunzi, draw your sword! I'm going to fight them today!\" Zong Jincheng's eyes blazed with fury, his reason gone, as he struggled to break free and charge out.","\"Young master, please slow down...\" Shunzi hurriedly chased after him.","However, the other group was on horseback and had already disappeared, leaving only the shattered remains of the street.","Shunzi held back the furious Zong Jincheng, trembling as he reminded, \"M-master, it seemed to be Zhai Yao and the other young masters... If you want an explanation, you can go back and ask...\"","\"Zhai Yao again?\" Hearing the name for the second time that day, the enraged Zong Jincheng suddenly froze, almost doubting his ears, and asked uncertainly, \"Are you sure it was them?\"","In this vast capital, when it came to the most troublesome young masters that elders found headache-inducing, there were four.","Ranking first was Zong Jincheng of Yangyuan Marquis Manor, known for spending money like water and being the undisputed king of mischief and extravagance; second was Zhai Yao, the eldest son of Weiyuan Earl Manor, who was always involved in fights and frequently defied his elders.","\"Is he the Zhai Yao who Steward Zhai mentioned, the one who wanted a three-year-old foot-washing maid and is listed alongside you as one of the four young playboys in the capital?\" Xu Wan finally recalled the name.","The little prince clenched his fists and reiterated through gritted teeth, \"Who wants to be listed alongside him as one of the four young playboys!\"","This woman always gives him ridiculous nicknames!","Xu Wan raised an eyebrow and said, \"I remember now, the ledger mentioned you once spent two thousand taels to buy four Akhal-Teke horses and gave them to the three of them. Were those the horses we just saw? No wonder they ran so fast. What a fine horse!\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"......\"","Those horses were actually a gift from his brother, and Akhal-Teke horses were known to be very expensive.","Scary, how extravagant.","The little prince was once again mocked by Xu Wan, his clenched fists itching to smash her head.","But he was too short to reach her.","Damn it!","He must eat more and grow taller!"]},{"number":28,"title":"Chapter 28: Zong Jincheng Has Withdrawn into Himself","paragraphs":["Xu Wan kicked Zong Jincheng's leg again, not caring at all about his anger, and even deliberately provoking him, \"Hey, does this count as using your bowl to smash your pot?\"","\"Bang——\"","The anger meter was full.","Even though no sound was made, everyone could feel Zong Jincheng's fury, which was even greater than the anger he had shown every previous time Xu Wan teased him!","Zong Wenxiu quickly pulled him aside to calm him down, \"Don't be angry, don't be angry. It's just a small crack, much better than before. If you think it's not good enough, we can rebuild it tomorrow.\"","Jing Zhe also hurriedly added, \"It's already very good now. At least we won't be so cold anymore, and it's spring now, the weather will get warmer and warmer!\"","His younger sister, not very good at speaking, just tugged at his clothes, signaling him not to be angry.","Zong Jincheng strode forward.","Like a pufferfish, he sat angrily in the carriage heading home, his arms crossed.","The carriage had no curtain, and the cold wind blew in. The people on both sides of the road looked into the luxurious yet simple carriage, only to see—","A pufferfish-like Zong Jincheng, pouting all the way.","Although the wind was cold, at least the heart was warm. Xu Wan was about to laugh to death at this kid, but luckily, she still had a shred of conscience and didn't laugh out loud in the carriage.","Zong Wenxiu glanced at her face, which was trying hard not to laugh, completely puzzled about what the joke was.","The sulking Zong Jincheng got off the carriage and walked straight to his courtyard, ignoring anyone who called out to him, clearly not planning to eat dinner.","Xu Wan watched his back and said, \"Forget him, Wenxiu, let's go eat.\"","Zong Wenxiu hesitated, \"Isn't that a bit unkind? He's been running around all day and is now so angry... I think I should go persuade him.\"","Xu Wan smiled and called him to follow.","As they walked, the maids and servants passing by greeted them, and Zong Wenxiu, not yet accustomed to the rules of the marquis's residence, always instinctively nodded back, causing the maids to giggle.","Unaware of what was so funny, Zong Wenxiu's cheeks turned slightly red.","Xu Wan explained with a smile, \"Jincheng often hangs out with Zhai Yao and the others. Recently, after I had the housekeeper cut off his allowance, those guys still forced him to pay the bill, making Jincheng pawn his jade pendant worth thousands of taels of silver for that meal. But after that, Jincheng didn't cut ties with Zhai Yao and the others, not realizing at all that in their eyes, he's just a walking bank.\"","\"Thousands of taels...\" Zong Wenxiu was hearing about such a large sum of money for the first time. If it were him, he'd probably lose sleep, afraid of losing even a single tael.","Xu Wan continued, \"This incident just let him experience firsthand what it feels like to have something you worked hard on trampled on by others. Otherwise, who knows if one day, among those young scoundrels riding recklessly in the streets, there might be Zong Jincheng?\"","Zong Wenxiu was shocked.","He couldn't think too deeply about it. His younger brother, though not as notorious as rumored, rarely cared about others' feelings.","If today, it was his brother on the horse...","When he rode, he would indeed only care about his own pleasure, not noticing how a casual action of his could cause serious consequences for others.","A change in perspective brings a world of thoughts.","Xu Wan, walking ahead, had already pulled some distance from him. The noble and elegant figure in red was bold and beautiful. From afar, they heard her say loudly, \"Then today, let's teach him this lesson.\"","\"Do not do to others what you do not want done to yourself.\"","...","The swing in the small courtyard was flying again.","\"Meow! Meow!\"","\"Chirp! Chirp!\"","The birdcage hanging on the swing was filled with screams. The cat lurking behind was firmly gripping the gaps in the cage, and the swing was swinging wildly, scaring the little birds into flapping and screeching.","The instigator, Zong Jincheng, was still vigorously pushing the swing. His delicate little face was twisted, his eyebrows furrowed, his eyes sharp and irritable. The usually clear and clean black eyes now didn't bother to move much.","\"Young Master, the madam has had the food brought over. She said you can eat in the courtyard tonight.\"","Shunzi, carrying the food, didn't dare to enter, only poking his head out, afraid of being caught in that person's anger.","Sure enough, Zong Jincheng was unappreciative, like a lit firecracker, shouting, \"I'm not eating! Take it out! If you dare come in again, I'll break your leg!\"","Shunzi: \"...\" Alright, sir.","The sensible servant quickly retracted his head, pretending he had never spoken.","After the person left, Zong Jincheng kicked the swing in frustration, ignoring the screaming cats and birds behind him, and sat down on the steps in front of the house.","The steps were cold, but it woke him up.","Eight-year-old Zong Jincheng sat with his legs spread, watching the ants marching in formation on the ground, carrying white things, one team after another, with some leading small squads forward.","If it were before, seeing the ants moving, he would either step on them or pour a bucket of water, easily wiping out these weak creatures.","But now, he thought of today's flag.","The flag that ruined the result of his hard work.","To them, an insignificant carriage curtain could shield someone from the cold wind all night, even something that could save a life.","He remembered Xu Wan's reminder: the Hanxue Baoma (a legendary horse) was a gift from him to Zhai Yao, but Zhai Yao used it to smash the roof he had given to Jing Zhe and his sister!","He even thought, if it weren't for the sudden arrival of a stepmother in the house, if he hadn't been confined at home, if he had continued hanging out with Zhai Yao as usual, would he have been one of those throwing the flag today?","\"Damn it...\"","Zong Jincheng wanted to find an excuse to go settle accounts with Zhai Yao, but in the end, he realized he wasn't much better himself.","Zong Jincheng was in self-imposed isolation.","He leaned back and lay down on the eaves, wrapped in a fox fur cloak.","The cold wind blew, making him shiver, and he realized how cold the early spring evening was.","Zong Jincheng thought, what about Jing Zhe and his sister tonight?","The little devil quickly got up and ran out, heading straight for the dining hall.","Xu Wan and Zong Wenxiu had already finished eating. Seeing Zong Jincheng panting as he ran in, with fine sweat on his head, one would think he had just participated in a 1000-meter sprint.","Before she could speak, they heard the usually arrogant young dandy utter two sentences in quick succession:","\"Those three blood-sweating horses, I never said I was giving them away, just letting them play with them. The horse contract is still in the mansion!\"","\"We need to fix Jing Zhe's roof quickly, or they'll be cold tonight and might get sick!\""]},{"number":29,"title":"Chapter 29: What Can Be Bought for Twenty Taels","paragraphs":["Zong Wenxiu's chopsticks, which were halfway through picking up some food, dropped onto the table with a plop.","The six or seven maids serving in the dining hall all widened their eyes, each seeing the surprise in the others' eyes!","This...","Was this still their young master?","Could the things he gave away actually be taken back?","Could he actually be concerned about whether someone would freeze at night?","Old Marquis! Old Madam!","Look quickly!!!","The ancestors must be working their magic!!!","Cui Zhi, who had a keen sense, had already signaled someone, and a maid happily went to report the good news to the villa.","Zong Jincheng, the main character, didn't notice anything unusual.","Xu Wan, sitting opposite the main seat, was looking at him with a half-smile, her starry eyes shining brightly. In that moment, he seemed to realize that this woman was a bit attractive.","\"Ahem.\" Zong Jincheng, feeling everyone's eyes on him, awkwardly reminded them, \"Did you hear me? I don't want to say it a second time.\"","If she dared to say she didn't hear, he would throw a tantrum!","Zong Wenxiu blinked his eyes and was the first to respond, \"Madam has already sent someone to fix Jing Zhe's roof. It's just... it turns out you didn't give away those horses after all. No wonder you weren't so heartbroken. Madam said they cost over a thousand taels of silver.\"","Zong Jincheng snorted and sat down, muttering, \"Over a thousand taels of silver? What's that compared to the wealth in our mansion? Small-minded peasant, never seen the world.\"","Small-minded peasant...","Zong Wenxiu had heard this term before, but previously, it was always accompanied by disdain and ridicule. However, coming from his brother's mouth, it seemed to carry no such meaning, but rather a sense of indulgence.","Thinking this, a slight smile crept onto his lips.","The little devil, without even washing his hands, reached out to grab a bun. A pair of chopsticks suddenly appeared, blocking his hand, as Xu Wan gestured for him to go wash his hands first.","Zong Jincheng was dissatisfied, but the maids had already brought water to his side, so he didn't even need to stand up. He simply extended his hand, and they washed and dried it for him.","The young master grabbed a meat bun and started gnawing.","Xu Wan, rarely refraining from teasing him at this moment, patiently waited until he finished his third bun before addressing Cui Zhi, \"Tomorrow, have Shunzi go with Steward Liu to retrieve those three Akhal-Teke horses, and bring the horse contracts.\"","\"Yes,\" Cui Zhi replied, a bit surprised. She had thought Madam would make the young master go himself to retrieve them.","Only by witnessing the faces of those people himself could he truly empathize. She had thought Xu Wan wouldn't miss this great opportunity to educate Zong Jincheng.","Xu Wan had indeed considered this.","But even if it succeeded, it would only result in the disbandment of the Four Playboys. It wouldn't do much to encourage the little devil to study hard. He could still continue kicking stones and scaring birds at home every day.","They needed to wait for the right opportunity.","Zong Jincheng tilted his head to look at her, puzzled about what this woman was plotting, but too lazy to guess. He had run around all day, was tired and hungry, and reached out for a fourth meat bun...","A growing boy can eat his father out of house and home.","The next day, before lunch, in the back courtyard study.","Zong Wenxiu was quietly copying an essay. Studying wasn't just about memorizing, but also understanding its meaning and being able to write it down. No matter the weather, he had to complete each learning task every day.","His younger brother, the young master, was a different story. Although he had been kicked into the study by Xu Wan early in the morning, his mind was elsewhere. He was sprawled on the desk, a thick book covering his face, with a corner of the book slightly wet, clearly deep in conversation with the Zhougong.","\"Master, Steward Liu has retrieved the three horses,\" Shunzi excitedly burst in.","\"Ah! That's great!\" Zong Wenxiu stopped writing and smiled.","Zong Jincheng was startled by the shout, flusteredly sitting up from the desk, only for the book on his face to drop with a thud, and he tumbled off the table.","Shunzi: \"...\"","As a competent servant, he immediately closed his eyes, covered his head, and plugged his ears, pretending not to have seen it!","\"Shunzi!! What are you shouting about!!!\" The little devil's roar was still so vigorous.","\"I'm sorry, Master! I didn't see you sleeping, thought you were studying, and couldn't wait to share this good news with you!\"","Zong Jincheng took a deep breath, dissatisfied, \"When is Buyan coming back?\"","Buyan was one of the five servants Xu Wan had removed from his room. He was quiet, skilled in martial arts, and Zong Jincheng's favorite. But because he couldn't read, he was sent away along with the others.","The remaining Shunzi was only good at accompanying him in his studies!","Studying, studying, studying... it was so annoying. Who invented studying, anyway?","The little devil's head was steaming with anger, ready to cause trouble.","Shunzi quickly said, \"Soon, soon! Madam said that once you understand the meaning of those books, you can have Buyan come back first, and our monthly allowance can be raised to fifty taels!\"","As he spoke, he held up the twenty taels of silver he had just received, showing it to the irritable young master.","Zong Jincheng stared at the silver ingot for a full three seconds.","Although he hadn't had any money for a month, the mansion provided food and drink, so he could just stay home. But now that he had money, he still couldn't go out because...","\"What can this little money do? I can't even afford a meal!\" The young master's outings always cost hundreds of taels.","Shunzi's hands trembled, unsure of how to respond, but then he saw Zong Wenxiu's astonished gaze behind him and quickly seized the opportunity to say, \"Master Wenxiu's monthly allowance is the same as yours!\"","Zong Jincheng found a kindred spirit in misfortune.","He turned to ask, \"You're also this miserable?\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","He shook his head, \"Not miserable. I think I'm quite fortunate. Twenty taels is a large sum of money.\"","Zong Jincheng questioned, \"How is that possible? You can't even buy a boat with it, let alone beautiful jade pendants or good horses!\"","Zong Wenxiu was hesitant to tell the truth, as his brother's spending habits were far beyond the norm, even compared to other noble sons.","But remembering Madam's goal of teaching his brother a lesson... he thought he should broaden his brother's perspective, showing him how the world really was.","Then, under Shunzi's admiring gaze, Zong Wenxiu's calm voice gently spoke:","\"One tael of silver is a thousand coins, twenty taels is twenty thousand coins. Grain costs five coins per pound, so that's four thousand pounds. Four thousand pounds of grain can feed a family of four for four years. For Jing Zhe's family, it would be enough for them to eat for eight years, raising him to fourteen and his sister to eleven.","\"Jing Zhe said that in the slums, children rarely grow up, either starving to death or dying of illness, most of which is due to poor resistance from malnutrition. The money you call 'this little bit,' with just two months' allowance, could raise them both to adulthood, making them the only two to survive in that place.\""]},{"number":30,"title":"Chapter 30: Break His Perception","paragraphs":["\"Plop... plop...\"","The sound of ink dripping onto the floor.","While the eldest young master lay bored on the table, he had casually pushed the writing brush, ink, paper, and inkstone to the edge of the table. When he was startled awake by Shunzi, the expensive inkstone worth hundreds of taels of silver was knocked over, and the ink inside dripped down drop by drop.","In the dead silence of the study, the sound was deafening.","Zong Wenxiu was the first to act. Calmly, he walked over, flipped the inkstone back, and skillfully found a cloth to wipe the ink stains off the floor.","This wasn't the first time his younger brother had knocked over the inkstone.","Zong Wenxiu always felt heartache for those precious items wasted for no reason. Sometimes, even in the middle of the night, he would wake up, crying and asking his mother why everyone here was like this. Those wasted items could have saved so many people.","His mother would tell him that this was another world, and he only needed to accept it as a great blessing. He must never make any reckless moves, or else they would lose everything and return to that dark, damp, hopeless place.","Zong Wenxiu didn't want to go back to such a life. He wanted to stay here and live well, study well. So, he began to learn how to hide his emotions, hiding them so well that no one could notice.","But just now, when talking to his younger brother, his emotions couldn't help but rise, affecting Jingzhe... He wanted to see how his spoiled younger brother would react to this.","Zong Jincheng stood frozen in place, unable to believe it.","\"You're lying to me!\" He was very certain that the twenty taels of silver in his understanding couldn't be so different from the normal price.","Zong Jincheng looked at Shunzi, who was also nodding, but he still felt it was impossible!","Zong Wenxiu said again, \"If everyone were as rich as the Marquis Manor, then why don't Zhai Yao and the others buy the five-hundred-tael blood-red horses themselves? Why can't any of the three of them afford one?\"","\"If even the direct sons of the noble family can't afford a blood-red horse, then what kind of life are ordinary people outside living? Have you ever understood that?\"","Zong Wenxiu tried to keep his voice emotionless. His younger brother wasn't a bad-hearted child; he was just a privileged young master born and raised in wealth. He didn't know he was enjoying a life of rare luxury in this world.","Zong Jincheng backed out of the room.","After just a few steps, he felt something bump into him. Turning back, he saw that woman, along with the familiar Cui Zhi and Cui Liu.","Xu Wan was about to come in and tell the little troublemaker that the three blood-red horses had been retrieved. But just as she reached the courtyard, she heard Zong Wenxiu's calculations and couldn't help but smile brightly.","This little helper was really not a bad choice.","Zong Jincheng saw her smile and felt even more incredulous. \"You must have bribed them to lie to me! I knew it! It must be fake!\"","Xu Wan looked at the little troublemaker, whose forehead was throbbing, and felt even more amused. Oh dear, she was becoming more and more fond of seeing this little devil get angry. This bad habit... she needed to control it.","She cleared her throat and restrained her smile, saying, \"If you don't believe me, then go out of the Marquis Manor and take a look. See what the world outside is like, and see if everyone in the Capital City has been bribed by me.\"","\"Of course, I will! I'll expose your lies! Liars! What four thousand catties of grain? If grain is so cheap, then why do I have to pay dozens of taels for a meal!\"","Zong Jincheng ran off while saying this, his little legs stomping on the corridor. The clean ground didn't raise a single speck of dust. It was made of Yushan stone, meticulously crafted by skilled artisans to be smooth and flat, and then cleaned three times a day by the servants, so there was no chance of dust.","Xu Wan watched his retreating figure and said to Zong Wenxiu, \"Look at this child, living a carefree life. The old lady dotes on him like a treasure. His life is more comfortable than even that of princes and nobles.\"","Zong Wenxiu nodded, \"Actually, this is pretty good. He can live a happy life all his life.\"","Xu Wan smiled, \"This might be the consideration of the old marquis and old lady for the past eight years. I wonder why they've changed their minds now.\"","At lunchtime, the little troublemaker still hadn't returned. Xu Wan called Zong Wenxiu to eat first.","He scratched his head a bit shyly, \"I'll wait a bit longer for my younger brother.\"","\"Don't wait. Look at that kid's defiant expression, he's bound to ask around every street. He won't be back until evening.\" Xu Wan had already sat down and started eating.","Zong Wenxiu also sat down and asked, \"Do we really not need someone to follow him?\"","Xu Wan raised an eyebrow, \"Are you worried about his mental resilience?\"","\"My younger brother is still two years younger than me...\"","Xu Wan laughed without restraint, teasing, \"You're overthinking it. He may be spoiled, but he's thick-skinned. Otherwise, how could he have always been thinking of causing trouble for others? Speaking of which, if it weren't for your grandparents' disapproval, that little devil would actually be quite suitable for martial arts. He'd definitely be tough and resilient.\"","Zong Wenxiu quietly kept silent.","In the evening, the little troublemaker indeed returned, fuming, his voice filled with disbelief:","\"How could grain really be so cheap? Five coins? I've never heard of such a small amount of money in my life!\"","\"And those coarse cloth clothes, how could they cost only a dozen coins? Then why do my clothes cost dozens or even hundreds of taels?\"","\"And Zuixiang House! Why do they charge me dozens of taels for every meal? Aren't their chickens hatched from eggs? Aren't their dishes cooked in pots?\"","\"What kind of location? Even the most prosperous area in the Capital City can't sell me a roasted goose for two taels! A live goose only costs a few dozen coins!!!\"","\"They're robbing me! I've been cheated by them!!!\"","\"...\"","Xu Wan sat leisurely in the courtyard, reading a book of stories. Hearing these complaints, she laughed so hard she couldn't focus on the content of the book.","She closed the book and looked at the little rascal coming through the gate, smiling brightly, \"How was it? Have all the people on the streets outside been bribed by me?\"","A direct hit.","The insult was strong, and the damage was even stronger.","Little troublemaker: \"!!!\"","This woman is too much!","She's actually mocking me in my own courtyard!!!","Believe it or not, I'm going to run away from home right now!!!","Zong Jincheng's face was puffed up with anger, his cheeks red, almost like a red-hot iron.","Xu Wan thought that if she continued to laugh, the kid might explode on the spot and try to take her down with him.","Feeling charitable, the stepmother spoke up, \"Steward Liu has already retrieved your three blood-red horses for you, but it seems your friends reacted quite strongly, saying you're going back on your word by taking back what you gave.","\"Especially that Zhai Yao. He said if you don't go to his place to apologize, then there's no more friendship between you.\""]},{"number":31,"title":"Chapter 31: Learn One More Thing","paragraphs":["Zong Jincheng was already in a rage, and upon hearing this, he completely lost his cool!","He stomped around in fury, yelling, \"Pfft! Fine, if he doesn't want to be friends, then so be it! Who even cares about being friends with him! My roof was beautifully repaired, and he just had to go and ruin it with a single slap! I haven't even settled that score with him yet!\"","\"And he even dared to ask me for my prized blood-sweating horse worth five hundred taels! Only someone with a donkey-kicked brain would give that away!\"","\"Steward Liu! Where's Steward Liu? Listen, if Zhai Yao ever shows up at Marquis Manor again, you're to beat him out with three sticks!\"","Steward Liu hurried over and immediately memorized his young master's instructions, saying, \"I assure you, from now on, not even a bird with the last name Zhai will be able to fly into our Marquis Manor!\"","Zong Jincheng: \"...\"","What kind of bird has a last name, you idiot!","\"Your dinner is placed in your room. You don't need to go to the front hall tonight. Get some rest.\" Xu Wan stood up, ready to leave.","\"Hey!\" The little troublemaker called out awkwardly, his tone stiff.","Xu Wan stopped behind him, the corner of her mouth slightly lifting.","\"What is it, young master?\"","Hearing this mocking title, Zong Jincheng glared angrily at her back, \"The monthly allowance of twenty taels is too little! I want fifty taels!\"","Xu Wan turned around, amused, \"You know the normal prices outside, so why do you still think it's too little?\"","Zong Jincheng struggled for a moment, then grumbled, \"It's still too little!\"","He added, \"It's not even enough to raise two people until adulthood!\"","Xu Wan immediately understood his hidden meaning.","The boy wanted to give all the money to Jing Zhe and his sister.","She agreed, \"Alright.\"","Zong Jincheng's eyes lit up, surprised that she agreed so easily.","He thought she would definitely use Zong Wenxiu's allowance to block him!","Apparently, she also knew the difference between legitimate and illegitimate children, and that this household ultimately was his to decide!","However, the little troublemaker's beautiful fantasy didn't last three seconds before he heard Xu Wan say, \"Equivalent exchange. If you can understand the meaning and write the essence of the books you've memorized, I'll give you fifty taels a month, considering your hard work.\"","Zong Jincheng: \"!!!\"","That's what I get for thinking there'd be an easy deal!","\"You...!\"","\"You...!\"","The little troublemaker pointed at her in anguish, feeling utterly deceived.","But he knew his options were all blocked, and to get money from her, he had to meet her demands!","He was furious!","Xu Wan smiled and slapped away his finger, educating, \"Pointing at someone is very rude. Young master, you should rest well tonight. Tomorrow, I'll have someone prepare the translated texts for you in the study. Shunzi will read them to you, sentence by sentence, according to your memorization habits. Good luck!\"","Zong Jincheng: \"...\"","If the cold wind could talk, it would be playing a mournful erhu right now.","Shunzi saw Xu Wan off and closed the courtyard gate, then hurried back.","He brought the dishes out and placed them on the small stone table in the courtyard, calling, \"Master, please eat first. No matter how big the problem is, you can't go hungry. Today, we have your favorite steamed jade duck.\"","Hearing this, Zong Jincheng channeled his anger into appetite, tearing off a duck leg and stuffing it into his mouth, muttering, \"Eat! I'll eat back all the suffering!\"","\"Oh, and,\" the little troublemaker suddenly remembered something, \"have someone buy some cotton quilts, clothes, and medicine for wounds, and whatever money is left, send it all to Jing Zhe.\"","\"Ah?\" Shunzi was puzzled, \"All... all of it? The twenty taels of monthly allowance?\"","The little troublemaker firmly said, \"Yes, all of it!\"","...","Xu Wan went back and immediately arranged for the preparation of translated texts for the little troublemaker.","There were over a hundred maids and servants in the manor, and many of them could read and write, but when it came to translating classical Chinese, it was better to leave it to professional tutors.","That night, Marquis Manor, under Xu Wan's orders, quickly invited over a dozen tutors who translated and transcribed all the over a hundred books Zong Jincheng had memorized onto paper.","The next morning, Zong Wenxiu saw the hundreds of translated texts and was completely stunned.","\"This... can actually be translated and compiled into books?\"","Didn't classical texts usually involve memorizing them and then listening to the tutor explain while taking notes on key points?","How did this turn into a full word-for-word translation, made so... so formal?!","Zong Wenxiu was amazed.","Not only did he admire Xu Wan's method for being considerate and efficient, but he also admired how such a massive copying task was completed overnight.","The mistress is so devoted to her brother.","Whether Zong Jincheng was touched or not, Zong Wenxiu was already moved on his behalf.","When Zong Jincheng yawned and arrived, seeing the scene, he was shocked. He took a big step back, horrified, \"Why so many? There were only over a hundred books, right?\"","\"Did Xu Wan sneak in other books without me knowing?","\"How despicable!!!\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","Brother, your imagination doesn't need to be that rich.","Shunzi, who knew the situation, explained, \"Young master, you're mistaken. The translated text naturally has more words than the original, so there are so many.\"","Although seeing the hundreds of books filled him with immense pressure...","But thinking that he only had to read them, while his master had to memorize them, Shunzi felt he could handle it.","Better the master than me.","Zong Jincheng pouted, \"That seems like it can't be finished in a month.\"","He was very confident in his memory, but there wasn't enough time.","\"It can be done,\" Zong Wenxiu said.","He was very familiar with his brother's abilities. If his brother tried hard, he really could finish.","\"Ah? How?\"","Zong Wenxiu took a deep breath and said, \"If you increase your study time from one hour to two hours a day, you'll definitely be able to finish.\"","Heaven knows how envious he was when saying this.","His brother only studied for one hour a day, yet remembered more than he did in six hours. It was an inhuman blow!","Zong Jincheng immediately bristled, his pride stung, and retorted, \"I spend several hours in the study every day!!!\"","\"You fall asleep at least eight times while memorizing,\" Zong Wenxiu made an eight gesture and then counted on his fingers, \"The rest of the time, you're either kicking the desk, throwing books, or tossing pens, fiddling with the inkstone, or picking at the desk corners...\"","With each thing Zong Wenxiu mentioned, Zong Jincheng's face darkened a bit, until it was as black as a pot.","The little troublemaker started throwing a tantrum, \"Aren't you supposed to be studying seriously? Why are you observing me so closely!!!\"","\"I didn't want to...\" Zong Wenxiu said helplessly, \"You kept interrupting my study thoughts, so I had to stop and look at you.\"","Zong Jincheng: \"...\"","How come it's always my fault when we count it all up?","So infuriating!"]},{"number":32,"title":"Chapter 32: Zhai Yao Comes to Pick a Fight","paragraphs":["Zong Jincheng grumbled for a while, and all his sleepiness was gone.","Shunzi brought over a translation book, ready to start with the simplest ones. He first read the original text aloud, then the translated version, which left Zong Jincheng speechless.","If he had known he would have to memorize everything, he would have done it all at once last time. Now he had to waste time listening to the original text again.","Frustrated.","\"When people are born, their natures are inherently good. Their innate qualities are quite similar, but it is the different environments and educations they receive that lead to significant differences in their habits and behaviors.\" Shunzi read the translation.","Since the goal was not only to memorize the translations but also to be able to write them from memory, Zong Jincheng decided not to listen to the original text a third time. Instead, he would write and memorize the translations while Shunzi read the original text for the second time.","He picked up a brush and, looking at the open book on the table, asked, \"At the beginning of humanity, nature is inherently good. Is it written like this?\"","He started writing on the rice paper, filling half a page with the character for \"human.\"","Shunzi glanced at it and twitched his mouth, saying, \"Young master, the characters need to be smaller. You can't take up half a sheet of paper.\"","Zong Wenxiu, who was about to read his own book, paused: \"...\"","He came over to check on his brother and heard Zong Jincheng's bold statement: \"What's wrong with half a sheet of paper? Just buy more paper. Does she really begrudge spending money on me?\"","Shunzi's temple twitched, but he still spoke politely: \"Madam Xu hasn't restricted the use of paper. Please continue...\"","Hearing this, Zong Jincheng continued writing the character for \"of\" on the other half of the paper. Although it looked ugly and the brush strokes were messy, at least he got it right.","\"Hmm... not bad, not bad. Very talented!\" The little troublemaker's self-praise mode activated.","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","He would have to get used to his brother's blind confidence.","Despite thinking this, Zong Wenxiu still dutifully taught him how to write smaller characters and explained the basic techniques of calligraphy.","Zong Jincheng was smart and caught on quickly, mastering the skill rapidly.","A sense of accomplishment was the fastest way to boost one's motivation. The little troublemaker became more and more confident, picking up the brush and writing away.","\"Change the paper, grind the ink. I can write a dozen more!\"","By the end of the morning, Cui Zhi came in to call the two young masters for lunch. Seeing the stack of rice papers, she was stunned.","\"Goodness! These... were all written by Master Jincheng?\"","Zong Jincheng was chewing on a brush, swinging his legs, with an arrogant yet proud expression, answering her, \"Of course, it's me. Isn't it cool?\"","\"Cool! Very cool!\" Cui Zhi praised without hesitation, \"It's so cool that it makes the heavens and earth tremble, the sun and moon dim, and even spirits and demons pale in comparison!\"","\"If you keep this up, the other young masters will be too ashamed to show their faces!\"","\"Master Jincheng is amazing!!\"","From that day on, the little troublemaker found joy in writing. He spent his days in the study, drawing away, not caring whether the characters were ugly or not, just enjoying the process!","Not content with just black ink, he had people buy red, green, and even multicolored inks, turning writing into a form of painting, exploring all the fun in it.","Zong Wenxiu was also witnessing for the first time that his brother could actually study with him for hours on end!","It will definitely succeed!","He would definitely meet Madam Xu's requirements within a month!","Meanwhile, Xu Wan began to feel anxious.","Although progress was smooth, this was still a one-time deal. Once the little troublemaker finished this phase of his studies, he would go back to his old ways.","A forward-thinking leader must plan ahead.","At this time, the Yangyuan Marquis Manor received an invitation.","Half a month later, the Crown Princess's birthday celebration would take place, inviting various noble families to the palace.","Both adults and children were invited, including Zhai Yao and others.","Xu Wan thought it was time to use him to set a trap for Zong Jincheng. But how should she plan it?","The little troublemaker, engrossed in writing, hadn't realized that his 'wicked' stepmother was plotting against him again. He was still in the study, happily switching brushes, using thick ones for simple characters and thin ones for complex ones, and changing paper whenever he made a mistake.","Days passed.","The stack of filled rice papers in the study grew taller, and the number of translations to memorize grew smaller. Zong Jincheng spent more and more time in the study.","The atmosphere in the Yangyuan Marquis Manor became increasingly harmonious.","On the day they were to enter the palace, the harmonious atmosphere in the carriage vanished instantly.","As soon as Zong Jincheng got into the carriage, he glared at her angrily: \"We're going to the palace all day, and I haven't finished drawing the 'Strategies of the Warring States' yet. Kids aren't supposed to go, so why do you insist on taking me?\"","Xu Wan calmly replied, \"Learning should be gradual and balanced with rest. Spending so much time in the study every day is harmful to your eyes and neck. I don't want you to end up with a hunchback at a young age. I wouldn't be able to explain that to your grandmother.\"","\"Hmph, you're afraid of grandma getting angry? If she knew how you've been bullying me these past two months, she would definitely skin you alive!\"","Xu Wan chuckled, \"Dream on, little brat.\"","Everything that happened in the manor, the old lady knew about it. She didn't want to burst the little troublemaker's bubble. His boundless optimism was almost laughable.","Zong Jincheng turned his head away, refusing to talk to her. But he was a chatterbox, and after a while, he couldn't help but start talking to Zong Wenxiu: \"Once we're in the palace, stick with me and don't wander off. With me guiding you, nothing will go wrong. Someone here is also visiting the palace for the first time, and making a mistake in the royal palace is a big deal. I wonder how she'll handle it.\"","Zong Wenxiu nodded, \"I'll follow you.\"","Xu Wan, with her eyes closed, ignored his veiled mockery.","Although she was the new mistress of the Yangyuan Marquis Manor, she had no faction, no enemies, and no husband in the capital. The manor was wealthy, but the noble ladies looked down on the merchant-born old lady, paying little attention to them.","Even if they did, it was mostly disdain. As long as she didn't draw attention to herself or cause trouble, most noblewomen would ignore her, treating her like air.","However, before they even reached the East Palace, they were stopped.","A boy about eight or nine years old stood in front of them, glaring angrily at Zong Jincheng, shouting, \"Zong Jincheng, I never expected you to be such a person!\"","\"Zhai Yao?\" Zong Jincheng recognized him and all the bad memories came flooding back. He retorted irritably, \"What's wrong with you? Why are you blocking me? Looking for trouble?\"","Zhai Yao sneered, \"I just didn't expect the future young marquis of the Yangyuan Marquis Manor to be so stingy. You give away things and then take them back. Is your family really so poor that you can't even afford to keep a pot on the stove?\"","Zong Jincheng finally understood. It was about the Han Xue Bao Ma (Blood-Sweating Horse). He immediately got furious and retorted loudly, \"The item is mine, I can give it to whoever I want and take it back if I want. The contract is in my hands. Do you want to steal it? And 'can't afford to keep a pot on the stove'... I wonder whose family can't afford it. If you're so rich, why don't you buy it yourself? Asking me for things all the time, aren't you ashamed?\"","Zong Jincheng stuck out his tongue at him, provoking him with full confidence."]},{"number":33,"title":"Chapter 33: Jincheng Challenges the Duchess of Jin","paragraphs":["Zhai Yao was scolded to the point of being drenched in humiliation, but he still angrily demanded, \"You took my things, fine, but then you turn around and give them to those filthy beggars in the slums? Are you implying that I, the young master, am not even worthy of those lowly scum? Zong Jincheng, you're insulting people way beyond the limit!\"","Zong Jincheng was a bit confused upon hearing this. Slums? Was he referring to Jingzhe? When did he ever give his prized horse to Jingzhe?","Could it be that Xu Wan sold his horse and converted the money into his monthly allowance?","Thinking of Xu Wan's calculating nature, it was quite possible she would do such a thing. But even if she did, why was Zhai Yao cursing people?","\"Who are you calling lowly scum? He has a name, his name is Jingzhe! Besides, my things, I can give them to whoever I want. Do I need your permission? You're not my father!\"","The two boys arguing at the door attracted the attention of many passersby. A noblewoman dressed in luxurious attire passed by and recognized the identities of the two children.","Her maidservant chuckled softly, \"One from the Marquis Manor, the other from the Earl's estate. Why do they both seem to be a level below when they argue? How dare the Zhai boy?\"","The noblewoman replied, \"Not quite. Although the Zhai family is just an Earl's estate, they are currently in the emperor's favor. What does the Marquis Manor have? A widow and her child. What kind of trouble can they cause?\"","This noblewoman seemed to hold a high status, which is why she dared to openly mock the two families with such disdain in her eyes.","Xu Wan frowned instinctively upon hearing the term \"widow and child.\" Although Zong Zhao had disappeared for eight years, he had not been declared dead. This woman was being far too harsh by saying such things to her face.","Just as she was about to retort, the fiery-tempered boy beside her was the first to shout, \"Who are you calling a widow and child? My father is still alive! Who gave you the right to curse him?!\"","\"Oh, look at this child, why are you so worked up? I was just speaking casually.\" The noblewoman laughed carelessly, not taking the matter seriously. She reached out to pull him, \"Come on, let's go in. Don't keep the Crown Prince and Crown Princess waiting.\"","Zong Jincheng forcefully pulled his hand away and snapped, \"Don't touch me, you wicked woman!\"","The noblewoman was caught off guard and pushed back, her face turning angry. \"What did you say?\"","Her maidservant immediately scolded, \"How bold! How dare you speak to the Duchess of Jin like that? Apologize at once!\"","The little imp, used to being unruly, didn't care about the status of the Duchess of Jin at all. He continued to confront her coldly, \"I called you a wicked woman, what about it?\"","The Duchess of Jin refused to argue with a child. Instead, she directed her anger at Xu Wan, \"So you are the wife of Zong Zhao, aren't you? Your child is so ill-mannered, as a mother, don't you think you should do something about it?\"","Zong Jincheng's face darkened further.","The Duchess of Jin had picked the right person to target. Xu Wan was not on good terms with him, so she would definitely side with her against him!","Xu Wan smiled, \"Indeed, it's quite challenging to discipline this child.\"","Zong Jincheng: \"!!!\"","He knew it!!","He knew this woman would never side with him!!!","However, before the little imp could erupt in anger, Xu Wan's tone suddenly shifted as she directly stated, \"But this matter is indeed your fault. With your broad-mindedness, I'm sure you won't take it personally with a child. Would you please apologize to the child here?\"","The Duchess of Jin's smiling face instantly froze.","\"What... did you just say?\"","Had she heard wrong? Xu Wan was actually asking her to apologize to a child?","She was the Duchess of Jin!!!","Did she even know who she was talking to?!","Zong Jincheng was even more bewildered. Why had Xu Wan suddenly changed her stance and decided to help him? He looked at Zong Wenxiu, who was trying his best to stay out of the spotlight but still firmly believed in Xu Wan.","The little imp's iron-clad heart suddenly softened a bit.","This woman... wasn't entirely dislikeable...","Xu Wan stood her ground without showing any weakness, \"The Yangyuan Marquis Manor has served the court faithfully for generations. My husband's brother died on the battlefield, and my husband has also gone missing in battle. All the generals mourn their loss, and even the current emperor often mentions them. If the emperor were to learn that his loyal subjects were being cursed, he would surely be very angry. Don't you think so?\"","In other words, insulting her husband was insulting all the generals. The anger wouldn't just come from Zong Zhao's son but from the emperor and the people.","The accusation was huge, and not apologizing would be hard to resolve. But how could the Duchess of Jin possibly apologize to a Marquis Manor she looked down upon? She was furious and frustrated, turning to leave.","Xu Wan took a step forward, but was stopped by the Duchess's maidservant, who said coldly, \"Madam Zong, please behave.\"","\"Is the Duchess of Jin planning to escape?\"","\"How dare you! You dare to insult me!\" The Duchess of Jin was incensed by the word \"escape.\" She turned around and strode over, raising her hand to slap Xu Wan.","The slap was fierce, and if it landed, it would surely disfigure her.","Everyone around was holding their breath for Xu Wan.","Unexpectedly, Xu Wan caught the slap firmly, gripping the Duchess of Jin's wrist tightly and smiling, \"Using force at the Crown Princess's birthday banquet, isn't that a bit inappropriate?\"","She wasn't skilled in martial arts, but back in the orphanage, whenever her younger brothers and sisters were bullied, she was the one who led the charge to get justice.","When it came to fighting, she was a seasoned veteran.","The Duchess of Jin was furious, and her maids all stepped forward. The maids from the Marquis Manor, Cui Zhi and Cui Liu, were no pushovers either. Both sides were about to clash.","At that moment, the announcement rang out:","\"His Royal Highness the Crown Prince has arrived.\"","Both sides immediately cowered like quails and stopped fighting to greet him.","\"Greetings to His Royal Highness the Crown Prince!\"","\"We pay our respects to His Royal Highness the Crown Prince!\"","Everyone bowed their heads in respect until they heard the warm, gentle voice above them say, \"Rise, everyone. Why are you all crowded at the door? What caused this dispute?\"","Xu Wan looked up and saw a man in a silver-moon-colored robe, his body slender and graceful. His eyes and brows were warm and gentle as he spoke, except for a slightly sickly pallor on his face. He looked as beautiful as a Buddha descended from heaven.","This was the legendary Crown Prince Chu Heng, known for his love for the people.","\"I'm sorry to have caused you trouble, Your Highness. I was just about to go in, but Madam Zong kept stopping us and wouldn't let us leave. I'm not sure what she wanted to say to us.\" The Duchess of Jin quickly accused first.","Xu Wan, seeing that the Crown Prince had come out, didn't want to drag him into the petty disputes between the ladies. After all, there was a difference in gender, and it was more appropriate to report it to the Crown Princess once they were inside the Eastern Palace.","She whispered, \"It's a misunderstanding, Your Grace. Please, go ahead.\"","Behind her, Zong Jincheng, seeing her suddenly back down, immediately protested, \"What misunderstanding? You can't leave! She hasn't apologized for cursing my father yet!\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","Oh no, she had almost forgotten about this little troublemaker.","This boy really had no fear at all. Earlier, before they entered the palace, hadn't he just told Wenxiu not to cause trouble...","The Crown Prince looked over and asked, \"Who is this child?\"","Xu Wan quickly bowed her head and replied, \"This child is the eldest grandson of the Yangyuan Marquis Manor, Zong Jincheng. He speaks without thinking, I hope Your Highness will forgive him.\"","He gently rolled the name in his mouth, murmuring, \"Zong Jincheng... so it's you.\"","Xu Wan looked up and saw the Crown Prince's expression, feeling a bit surprised. Could it be that he knew Jincheng?"]},{"number":34,"title":"Chapter 34: The Crown Prince Stands Up for Jincheng","paragraphs":["She turned her head to look at Zong Jincheng, who appeared utterly bewildered, as if he didn't recognize the situation.","The Duchess of Jin quickly chimed in, \"Your Highness, this is Zong Jincheng, Zong Zhao's son, and he just turned eight this year.\"","She emphasized the name \"Zong Zhao\" heavily, fearing that the Crown Prince might not recognize the child or realize he was the son of someone the Crown Prince detested.","Everyone knew that Zong Zhao and the Crown Prince had grown up together, close as brothers. But eight years ago, they had a massive falling out, and since then, they had become virtual strangers, not even speaking to each other. Whenever someone mentioned Zong Zhao's name in front of the Crown Prince, it would cause him to frown, clearly indicating the depth of their animosity.","Xu Wan was also aware of this.","Before entering the palace, to avoid making mistakes at the Eastern Palace, she had asked Cui Zhi about the social connections of Marquis Manor, inquiring if they had any close allies or enemies among the court officials.","Cui Zhi had replied that Marquis Manor didn't engage much with others, and the only person they might have offended was the Crown Prince. However, given the Crown Prince's good nature, it was unlikely he would make things difficult for a woman like her.","After meeting the Crown Prince in person, Xu Wan was even more convinced of this.","Once the Crown Prince confirmed Zong Jincheng's identity, his eyes fixed solely on the boy, examining him from head to toe. Suddenly, he remarked, \"You've grown so much.\"","Zong Jincheng returned his gaze, his dark, luminous eyes filled with confusion. \"Do you know me?\"","The Crown Prince smiled. \"When you were born, I held you in my arms.\"","Xu Wan, with her sharp eyes, noticed a hint of bitterness in his smile.","Could there be some deeper connection between the Crown Prince and Jincheng?","Xu Wan couldn't help but wonder. Everyone knew that Zong Jincheng was Zong Zhao's eldest son, but his mother's identity was unknown. Marquis Manor had firmly registered him as the legitimate son. Could his mother have had a connection with the Crown Prince?","\"Oh, I don't remember you,\" Zong Jincheng replied honestly.","\"That's alright,\" the Crown Prince said, patting his head. \"Tell me, what's going on here?\"","The Duchess of Jin grew anxious at this. \"Your Highness, why are you...?\"","Before she could finish, the Crown Prince shot her a warning glance.","The Duchess of Jin was stunned. How had the situation taken such an unexpected turn?","Didn't the Crown Prince cut ties with Zong Zhao?","Why was he now chatting with Zong Zhao's son?","The Crown Prince ignored the Duchess of Jin's displeasure and focused solely on listening to Zong Jincheng recount the events. Then, his gaze shifted to Zhai Yao, the one who had started the trouble.","The smile in his eyes faded, but his tone remained calm and gentle. \"All men are born equal, regardless of status. Since you consider those people to be beneath you, then you must not have any regard for them. Come, inform Weiyuan Earl Manor that I, the Crown Prince, will send Zhai Yao to live in the slums, to experience firsthand the life of those he deems 'lowborn.' No one is to provide him with any assistance.\"","Zhai Yao panicked. \"No, no! I don't want to go to the slums! Your Highness, I was wrong! Please, show mercy! Spare me, Your Highness... spare my life!\"","\"Take him away,\" the Crown Prince ordered, and the guards immediately dragged Zhai Yao away, his cries growing louder as he was pulled further.","Perhaps the commotion had grown too loud, as the guests who had already arrived at the Eastern Palace began to emerge from inside. Noblewomen and children gathered, and even the Crown Princess came out to inquire, \"Your Highness, what has happened?\"","The scene at the entrance was chaotic, with everyone crowding together, making for an unsightly spectacle. Even the eunuchs and palace maids passing by outside couldn't help but glance over, and it might even disturb the other concubines in the palace.","The Crown Princess, known for her gentle disposition, stepped forward to mediate. \"Your Highness, there are many people here, and it's a bit crowded. If there's something to discuss, perhaps we should let them all come inside first?\"","Xu Wan also felt that things were getting out of hand. All the attention was now focused on them, and before coming to the Eastern Palace, Marquis Manor had no enemies. But after this visit, they were likely to make many.","Yet, despite his gentle manner of speaking, the Crown Prince's actions were anything but mild.","He said calmly, \"It's nothing major. Just that the Duchess of Jin said something unpleasant, and the child, not understanding social etiquette, simply wanted an apology.\"","The Crown Princess looked at the Duchess of Jin in surprise. \"Then, Madam, just apologize to him. Why make a fuss over a child?\"","\"I...\" The Duchess of Jin, though furious, dared not speak out. How had the situation turned into her fault? As the Duchess of Jin, how could she apologize to a child?","And what about Xu Wan, who had dared to confront her earlier? If she apologized, it would be admitting defeat, and the entire Duke Jin's Manor would lose face.","After waiting for a while with no apology forthcoming, the Crown Prince remained unmoved, and the Crown Princess was astonished. She seemed to understand why he had insisted on not entering the Eastern Palace.","In moments like this, where the couple was usually gentle, the one to take on the role of the stern one was always the Crown Princess. She straightened her posture and spoke coldly, \"Duchess of Jin, do you intend to keep the Crown Prince and myself waiting here until nightfall?\"","The Duchess of Jin was startled by her sudden change in demeanor. \"I dare not! I will apologize, I will apologize right now...\"","\"I'm sorry. I shouldn't have cursed at Young Master Zong. Please forgive my careless words, Madam Zong and Young Master Zong!\"","Zong Jincheng huffed and turned his face away.","The Duchess of Jin's face turned pale with anger.","This little brat! Once she left the Eastern Palace, she would make him pay!","Xu Wan, noticing the fury in her eyes, quickly interjected, \"The Duchess of Jin is very gracious. Please don't take it to heart, considering he's just a child.\"","The Duchess of Jin clenched her teeth, forcing a smile. \"Of course not...\"","The Crown Princess, observing the tense atmosphere, quickly stepped in to smooth things over. \"Alright, now that the matter is resolved, everyone, please come inside. The palace has prepared fruits and pastries for all to enjoy.\"","\"The Crown Princess has gone to great lengths. I heard there are even green grapes, we must have a taste.\"","\"There's plenty. The Emperor has bestowed many on the various palaces. Please, help yourselves.\"","The Crown Princess led the crowd inside, and the Duchess of Jin followed them.","Xu Wan was about to call for Zong Jincheng and Zong Wenxiu to join her when the Crown Prince suddenly stood beside Zong Jincheng, patting his little head. \"Jincheng, come and sit with me.\"","Xu Wan: \"!!!\"","What kind of secret relationship do you two have?!","How can you be so clingy after just meeting?!","Zong Jincheng, having just been helped by the Crown Prince to teach Zhai Yao a lesson and to stand up to the Duchess of Jin, was already fond of him. He agreed immediately, \"Okay!\"","The two walked off together, chatting and laughing, leaving Xu Wan and Zong Wenxiu staring at each other.","Zong Wenxiu timidly said, \"The Crown Prince seems to really like my brother. I don't think anything bad will happen...\"","Xu Wan gave a dry laugh. \"He won't have any problems. We, on the other hand, will.\"","\"Huh? Why?\""]},{"number":35,"title":"Chapter 35: Jincheng Was Not Wrongfully Accused","paragraphs":["The moment they entered, they immediately understood why.","With the Crown Prince standing up for them, all the elegantly dressed noble ladies in the room turned their scrutinizing gazes towards Xu Wan and the other woman, making them feel like they were sitting on pins and needles.","And knowing that Zong Jincheng was with the Crown Prince, the Crown Princess's smile began to falter.","She had married into the East Palace but had not borne any children. Although the truth was that the Crown Prince was sickly, and they had not conceived after five years of marriage, there were always those who liked to blame the woman, saying it was her inability to conceive, especially since the Crown Prince, for her sake, refused to take any concubines.","Now that the Crown Prince showed a strong liking for children, the others' gazes towards the Crown Princess became even more complicated. It was easy to imagine that behind her back, they were surely mocking her for being unable to bear children.","\"Madam Zong, come sit by my side,\" the Crown Princess said with a warm smile, gesturing towards her, which finally put an end to Xu Wan's uneasy state of sitting.","—Only to transition into an uneasy state of standing.","Xu Wan was inwardly groaning. Whether intentional or not, the little demon was causing her trouble. This was the esteemed Crown Princess; how could she possibly afford to offend her!","Looking at the smirks on these people's faces, it was likely that the Crown Princess would soon make things difficult for her.","This is a disaster!","Xu Wan took a deep breath, stepped forward to pay her respects, and was seated beside the Crown Princess, who began to gently interrogate her.","The two women, both smiling tigers, exchanged pleasantries, and surprisingly, they hit it off.","The Crown Princess, after all, harbored no ill will towards Xu Wan. Xu Wan was newly married into the marquis's household, and even if the Crown Prince had some connection with Zong Jincheng, the new bride likely didn't know much about the inner workings.","\"I see that the Crown Prince quite likes your Zong Jincheng. If you have time, do bring him to the East Palace more often. Don't just keep him cooped up at home studying. Such a big child can easily get stifled.\"","Xu Wan smiled, \"Thank you, Your Highness, for your kindness. Zong Jincheng is quite mischievous and might disturb the Crown Prince and Your Highness. I'll need to discipline him a bit more before bringing him to the palace.\"","The Crown Princess covered her mouth and laughed, \"Alright, I'll leave it to you. I see you're a very responsible stepmother, even more so than many biological mothers.\"","Xu Wan inwardly muttered: Of course, biological mothers raise their children out of maternal love, while I raise my child because of that one-hundred-million-tael silver pie.","One hundred million taels!","Pure, white silver!","Even Confucius would have to force Zong Jincheng to study for eight hours a day!","\"It's all thanks to my mother-in-law's trust. I wouldn't dare to let her down.\"","The Crown Princess said, \"Your mother-in-law certainly knows how to pick people. Look how well you've raised Zong Jincheng. I only just learned that he bluntly criticized Zhai Yao, the dissolute son of the Zhai family, at the gate, leaving him speechless. He's quick-witted and has excellent moral character. You know, those kids—I've heard there's even a ranking of the four most dissolute, all of whom are ten-year-old children. They're more difficult to manage than adults, but none of them are as well-behaved as your Zong Jincheng.\"","Xu Wan: \"......\"","For the first time in her life, she felt utterly at a loss for words. The Crown Princess was kindly praising Zong Jincheng, but it seemed to have backfired.","Xu Wan timidly said, \"That... Zong Jincheng... seems to be on that list as well...\"","She didn't dare to hide this fact, as if it were exposed to the Crown Princess, it would only make things worse.","\"Ah?\" The Crown Princess's smile froze on her face. \"Is there something wrong with this list? Could the other three children also be wrongly accused?\"","Xu Wan coughed, then truthfully said, \"There's one more you've met.\"","\"?\"","\"It's Zhai Yao.\"","The Crown Princess: \"............\"","Her worldview was suddenly turned upside down.","The Crown Princess's birthday celebration wasn't too grand. Neither the Emperor nor the Empress attended, only the wives of various families were present in full force.","Xu Wan, at the banquet, was enjoying the food in silence when Cui Zhi nudged her, whispering in her ear, \"Madam, look over at the Duke of Jin's wife.\"","Xu Wan followed her cue and saw a familiar figure—her younger sister, Xu Lian'er, sitting beside the Duke of Jin's wife, laughing and chatting.","This really is... birds of a feather flock together.","However, the Duke of Jin's wife was about the same age as her own mother-in-law. Xu Lian'er was so eager to please her; could it be that she wanted to marry into the Duke of Jin's household?","She asked Cui Zhi, \"Does the Duke of Jin's household have an unmarried eldest son?\"","Cui Zhi nodded, \"Yes, the eldest son, who just turned twenty this year. He's already a fourth-rank official at a young age, with both character and ability. Many noble ladies want to marry into the Duke of Jin's household.\"","Xu Wan said, \"Sounds like an excellent young man. With my father being the Minister of Justice, our family is certainly a match for the Duke of Jin's household. My stepmother has made a good choice.\"","Much better than the list she had when she got married.","Cui Zhi couldn't tell if she was happy or unhappy, so she leaned in and whispered a bombshell piece of information: \"This eldest son has a mistress outside, who used to be the top courtesan at Yihong House.\"","Xu Wan: \"!\"","\"How do you know this?\" Xu Wan was shocked.","In the strictly hierarchical Great Chu Dynasty, a man having a concubine before marriage was already a huge scandal; if the concubine was a courtesan, it was even worse.","A wife being forced to acknowledge a courtesan as a sister was a great humiliation to the noble lady and her family.","Cui Zhi whispered, \"Cui Liu accidentally stumbled upon it while running an errand. The old madam told us not to spread it around; almost no one in the capital knows about it.\"","Xu Wan swallowed hard, thinking how complicated things were.","On the surface, he seemed like a promising young talent, but he could also be a massive pitfall.","Xu Lian'er and her mother had mistreated the original owner, and now their bad deeds were catching up to them.","Knowing this piece of information, Xu Lian'er's pretentious demeanor now just seemed pitiful.","Forget it, let her and the Duke of Jin's wife engage in their own domestic strife.","After the banquet, Zong Jincheng, holding the inkstone gifted by the Crown Prince, grinned all the way home.","Xu Wan rubbed her temples in frustration. No one knew that while it seemed like their family had climbed the ladder to the East Palace, in reality, the Crown Prince's sudden intervention had disrupted her plans.","Although Zhai Yao was mischievous, his studies were quite solid. Xu Wan had originally planned to use the deepening conflict between the two to motivate the little demon to continue studying, but instead, the boy was directly sent to the slums.","What a headache...","That night, Xu Wan tossed and turned, thinking of various ways to cultivate the little demon into a top scholar after he started studying, but she was stuck on how to get him to study in the first place. It felt like an insurmountable chasm.","The next morning, Baili Xi, seeing her listless appearance, chuckled and asked, \"Zong Jincheng's recent progress in his studies is so smooth, why does Madam look even more worried?\"","Xu Wan looked at this highly respected tutor, thinking how impressive it was that he could cultivate a child like Zong Zhao. But the little demon was unwilling to study; even if she forced him, it wouldn't work.","\"To be honest with you, Master, Zong Jincheng's current efforts are due to a promise I made with him. In a few days, this promise will be fulfilled, and I'm worried he'll go back to slacking off.\"","\"I see. No wonder he suddenly has such a strong drive to study,\" Baili Xi said. \"However, I've noticed that he quite likes writing. Although his handwriting isn't that great yet, with this enthusiasm, it won't be long before he's on the right path.\"","Hearing this, Xu Wan's heart skipped a beat, as if something clicked in her mind."]},{"number":36,"title":"Chapter 36: The Little Tyrant Takes the Monthly Exam","paragraphs":["Baili Xi continued, \"Zong Zhao was very fond of reading when he was young. He spent more time in the study than in the training grounds, but since the Zong family has always been known for martial prowess, the Old Marquis forced him to spend more time in the training grounds, which only made him resent it and he stopped going for a while. It wasn't until the Old Marquis stopped pressuring him that he started to take martial arts seriously.\"","Xu Wan, hearing about her husband's childhood for the first time, couldn't help but laugh. \"He was quite feisty as a child.\"","Baili Xi reminisced, \"Yes, children are all like that. They have strong rebellious tendencies, so it's best to handle them gently.\"","Baili Xi's advice was subtle, leaving Xu Wan to ponder alone about how to handle the little stubborn mule that was Zong Jincheng.","In the March breeze, the pavilion was filled with a refreshing coolness. In the distance, the sound of children reading could be heard—one voice was serious and steady, the other carefree and playful.","Xu Wan tapped her fingers on the stone table, one after another.","She turned to Cui Zhi and asked, \"Are there any places in the capital where students can compete in reciting texts?\"","\"Reciting texts?\" Cui Zhi thought for a moment and replied, \"There are such events in the monthly exams of each academy, but they are usually just among the students of the same academy.\"","\"There's also the Children's Examination, which tests deeper knowledge. It's used by the court to select prodigies, and only those under the age of twelve can participate. If they pass the Children's Examination, they can bypass the minimum age requirement for the imperial examinations and skip the steps of becoming a scholar and a licentiate.\"","Xu Wan was intrigued by this. The Children's Examination could solve the age issue for Zong Jincheng. If everything went smoothly, he could achieve great success in three years instead of waiting six.","But considering the current progress of the little devil... she decided not to get her hopes up too high.","Xu Wan asked, \"Can Jincheng and Wenxiu participate in the monthly exams of those academies? I can pay the tuition fees for them to enroll, and then withdraw them after the exam.\"","Cui Zhi chuckled, \"Of course, the academies would be more than happy to take the money without having to actually teach the children. However, the academies are divided by age, so the two young masters, one being eight and the other ten, would be in different classes with different levels of difficulty.\"","Xu Wan's eyes lit up. \"So if Jincheng catches up with Wenxiu's progress, he could score better than Wenxiu?\"","\"That's correct.\"","Xu Wan immediately made her decision. \"Sign them up!\"","Despite the two children having different learning styles—one being more analytical and the other relying on rote memorization—they both had solid knowledge. So Xu Wan had Cui Zhi find a middle-tier academy with some competitive but not overly talented students, perfect for building confidence.","The day of the exam was the second-to-last day of Zong Jincheng's study period.","Zong Jincheng was dragged unwillingly into the carriage, grumbling all the way, \"What's the point of this exam? I hate these things the most. You're dragging me out now just to slow down my memorization progress, aren't you? How malicious!\"","\"I'll give you your monthly allowance after the exam,\" Xu Wan said.","The little devil's incessant complaints suddenly stopped when he heard this. His dark eyes suspiciously looked at her. \"You'd be that kind?\"","Shouldn't she be trying every trick in the book to make him study longer?","Xu Wan raised an eyebrow. \"Of course, I've always been a kind person.\"","\"Pfft—\" Zong Jincheng rolled his eyes.","The carriage headed toward their destination and finally stopped at the entrance of Qingbo Academy.","Zong Jincheng was the first to jump out of the carriage, not waiting for Xu Wan or Zong Wenxiu, and walked into the academy on his own, curiously looking around the unfamiliar place.","It was early morning, the time when students arrived for class, and the path was filled with students of all ages.","Seeing Zong Jincheng and the others descend from the carriage, accompanied by many servants and maids, the onlookers realized that a wealthy young master had come to enroll. Many gathered to watch the spectacle.","\"Are those the new ones? They look like they're going to the children's class. Today is the monthly exam, why are they enrolling now?\"","\"Those two must be rich. As long as they throw enough money, the dean would personally welcome them even on the day of the imperial examinations!\"","\"Look, the dean really came out. Wow, they must have some serious connections!\"","\"Hmph, I despise these parasites who rely on their families. If not for their fortunate birth, they wouldn't even pass the entrance exam to the academy!\"","\"That's the way it is. Even if they're empty-headed, there are always exams for them to scribble on. Unlike us, we're afraid of even smudging the paper when we write.\"","\"Hahaha, stop it. That short kid is looking over here. Look at his angry face. Relying on his father and not letting anyone talk about it. What's so impressive about that?\"","Zong Jincheng, who was already unhappy about coming to the monthly exam, exploded when he heard a few people talking bad about him.","He quickly walked up to the two who were about his height, his face dark, and demanded, \"Who are you two talking about?\"","One of them bluntly said, \"We're talking about you, kid. This is a monthly exam. Do you even have the guts to go in and take it? Or will you come out crying saying you don't know the answers?\"","Zong Jincheng laughed angrily. \"I'm here for the monthly exam, of course. A mere test paper? Who wouldn't know how to answer it? I could beat you two easily!\"","\"Hmph, what's your name? Dressed so flashy, just full of hot air! I want to see what you can actually achieve!\"","\"Zong Jincheng,\" the little devil spat out, \"And you? Don't hide when I finish and beat you!\"","\"I'm Wu Shusen.\"","\"I'm Zhang Zhi.\" The most arrogant of the group said his name and added, \"Kid, you won't beat us, and definitely not our academy's genius, Qin Ye.\"","Zong Jincheng said, \"Alright, I've got your names. We'll see who ends up without a place on the rankings!\"","Zhang Zhi mocked, \"Hah, don't cry and want to drop out when you fail!\"","Zong Jincheng gave him the middle finger.","Zhang Zhi: \"...\"","This scoundrel, does he even have a shred of a scholar's dignity?","Behind them, Zong Wenxiu followed his brother into the exam hall, while Xu Wan was still talking to the dean.","The dean, who had wanted to intervene earlier, was stopped by Xu Wan. He felt a bit awkward and said, \"Madam, those two students, though a bit immature, have solid academic skills and always score a 'B'. Your young master might find it challenging to compete with them...\"","Hearing the mention of a 'B', Xu Wan felt more confident.","She smiled and said, \"It's fine. My son is quite capable academically as well.\"","The dean immediately smiled, praising, \"The children of the marquis's household are indeed outstanding. I was overly worried. Madam, you are truly a skilled educator. I admire you.\"","\"By the way, who is this Qin Ye that those kids mentioned?\" Xu Wan asked."]},{"number":37,"title":"Chapter 37: Please Secure the First Position","paragraphs":["The dean spoke with pride, his back straighter than usual: \"Qin Ye is a very famous student at our academy. Despite being young, he masters his studies and almost never makes mistakes. His test papers are always flawless...\"","This was akin to having a perfect score hanging as a benchmark.","If you made even a single mistake, you would fall short.","Xu Wan thought for a moment and found it quite satisfactory.","Having such a peer as a standard could not only give the mischievous young master a sense of achievement by outperforming the others but also keep him vigilant about his own shortcomings, maintaining his motivation to continue learning.","She smiled and said, \"Then let Qin Ye continue to excel and hold onto his top position.\"","The dean raised an eyebrow, not quite understanding her, but still courteously escorted her to a side room to rest.","The monthly exam at Qingbo Academy consisted of two sessions, with provisions of dry food prepared in the examination hall, and students were only released after completing both sessions.","In the afternoon, Zong Wenxiu was the first to emerge from the examination hall.","He was a child of exceptional talent, extremely diligent in his studies, which allowed him to catch up with his peers in just half a year. Consequently, he finished his test papers faster than most, with a high accuracy rate.","Xu Wan praised him without reservation: \"Wenxiu, you did very well. You were the first in the entire academy to finish your test papers!\"","Zong Wenxiu, feeling a bit embarrassed by the praise, scratched his head and replied, \"This was my first time taking a proper exam. I didn't know how long it should take, I just heard the proctor say that once you're done, you can leave.\"","The dean also looked at him with admiration, clapping his hands in approval: \"Well done, well done! No wonder you're from Yangyuan Marquis Manor. Today, I truly witnessed something remarkable. With this pace, you've outstripped the other students by half an hour.\"","Xu Wan corrected him: \"Wenxiu is now also a student of the academy.\"","The dean laughed heartily: \"Hahaha, yes, yes, of course.\"","Zong Wenxiu sat down and waited for another half-hour, as more students gradually exited the examination hall, but Zong Jincheng was still nowhere to be seen.","He felt a bit anxious but, with the dean present, he didn't dare to ask outright.","It was Xu Wan who saw through his thoughts and spoke up: \"Jincheng's handwriting isn't very fluent yet. This is his first time facing such a large volume of questions, so he needs more time.\"","Zong Wenxiu thought about it and realized it made sense.","When he first started learning to write, his speed was even slower than his brother's. It was only through daily practice and memorization that he gradually improved.","With this in mind, he felt a bit more at ease but still couldn't sit still.","Just as he was getting restless, Zhang Zhi and Wu Shusen, who were in the same examination room, came out first and started whistling towards Zong Wenxiu, looking rather mischievous.","The dean's forehead bulged with veins, and he stood up to intervene, fearing that these two boys might offend Yangyuan Marquis Manor. However, Xu Wan poured him a cup of tea and gently said, \"Dean, have some tea. Let the children handle their own affairs.\"","The dean was momentarily stunned. He was surprised that Xu Wan not only didn't ask him to intervene on behalf of her child but also advised him not to meddle. Was she that confident in her child?","The two boys, seeing that the dean didn't move, became even more brazen. They taunted Zong Wenxiu: \"The questions in this month's exam were insanely hard. Your brother, who loves to boast, is probably struggling inside, about to cry. You better get ready to comfort your little master, haha!\"","Zong Wenxiu was a very socially anxious person, afraid of meeting people, interacting with strangers, and even more afraid of offending anyone.","But these two boys insulting his brother really angered him. Somehow, he found the courage to retort: \"The exam isn't about speed, but about mastery of knowledge. I have full confidence in my brother, confident that he will perform better than you!\"","The two boys were taken aback, not expecting this seemingly timid young boy to stand up for himself.","Zhang Zhi sneered: \"Taking so long to write the test paper, isn't it because you can't solve the questions? Some people are just stubborn, refusing to admit defeat, but in reality, their knowledge is no deeper than their tears, huh?\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"You...\"","\"What's going on here? Picking on my brother in my absence?\" A voice suddenly came from behind, and everyone's eyes turned towards it.","The two boys, seeing him return, didn't have the energy to argue with him and snorted before walking away.","The mischievous young master raised his fist towards their backs: \"Just wait until the results come out, I'll make you two regret it!\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","With this kind of spirit, she felt the mischievous young master could probably take ten more test papers.","However, after showing off, Zong Jincheng trotted over to Zong Wenxiu, looking dejected and complaining: \"This stupid test paper never ends, I've written several pages and there are still more! My hand hurts so much!\"","Zong Wenxiu, hearing this, quickly asked: \"Is it the muscles that ache, or the veins?\"","When he first started practicing writing, he often felt like his arms weren't his own.","Zong Jincheng thought for a moment, his expression showing a hint of confusion, and finally said: \"Both!\"","Zong Wenxiu immediately began massaging his brother's arms, saying as he did: \"Let me press some acupoints for you. This is what the family doctor taught me, it helps relieve the soreness.\"","\"Okay.\"","Shunzi watched as his young master, who seemed on the verge of collapse, looked completely different from the little playboy of two months ago. But seeing the young master now enjoying the arm massage, he felt something was off.","Xu Wan knew what was off.","The mischievous young master's arms weren't actually sore; neither the muscles nor the veins were affected. The boy just wanted to be pampered, his acting skills were terrible.","Xu Wan gave him a sidelong glance: \"Let's go back to the manor, I'll have the family doctor massage your arms. Your brother has just finished a day of exams, do you have no conscience asking him to massage you?\"","\"Mind your own business,\" the mischievous young master, emboldened, hummed as he got on the carriage.","After two months of almost closed-door studying, Zong Jincheng had developed a close relationship with his only peer, his brother Zong Wenxiu.","Of course, in Xu Wan's eyes, this boy was just a little lazy brat who took advantage of his brother's kindness.","Zong Jincheng's charming face made it hard for people to resist his cute antics, but Xu Wan felt goosebumps rising just watching: \"Can you keep away from Wenxiu? Are you treating him like a pillar?\"","Zong Jincheng was leaning against Zong Wenxiu, eyes closed, looking like he had no bones in his body. He lazily said, \"I'm too tired, you can try to pick me up if you have the guts.\"","Xu Wan: \"!\" What a thick-skinned kid.","\"I'll throw you out of the carriage in a minute.\"","The carriage swayed, and the mischievous young master's eyelids fluttered a few times before he fell asleep, the carriage now as quiet as a pin drop.","Xu Wan, seeing that her threat went unanswered, soon heard the boy's even breathing.","\"...\" He could actually fall asleep like that.","\"You're too lenient with him,\" Xu Wan said to Zong Wenxiu, \"he'll take advantage of you like this.\"","Zong Wenxiu looked a bit confused, as if he didn't quite understand the phrase. He chuckled innocently: \"My brother is really tired, he's been studying very hard these past two months.\"","Xu Wan: \"...\" It seemed she was meddling in what was none of her business.","The one being taken advantage of was doing so willingly."]},{"number":38,"title":"Chapter 38: The Acting Madam Zhai","paragraphs":["Zong Wenxiu said, \"The results of the monthly exam will only be out the day after tomorrow. Should we let my brother rest tomorrow?\"","\"He's already received his monthly allowance, so I'm afraid he won't come to the study room again, just waiting for the exam results the day after tomorrow,\" Xu Wan replied. She then asked, \"How did you do? Was it smooth?\"","Zong Wenxiu responded, \"It was okay, it shouldn't be too bad.\"","Xu Wan nodded, \"For your first exam, any score is a starting point. You've been reading books for so many years less than them, so it's normal if there's a gap. Otherwise, they'd be so stimulated they'd cry.\"","Zong Wenxiu laughed at her joke and replied, \"I understand, thank you, Madam.\"","Xu Wan always felt this address was a bit distant, not like a family member. But thinking of Zong Zhao being the eldest, Zong Wenxiu should call her \"Aunt\" or \"Elder Sister-in-law.\" This title made her feel ten years older, so she decided against it...","That evening when they got home, Zong Jincheng started eating like crazy.","Due to a whole day of intense brain activity, even Zong Wenxiu's appetite increased.","But seeing the kids eat with gusto made the adults feel good.","Cui Zhi instructed the kitchen to prepare more easily digestible food to prevent them from overeating and having trouble sleeping at night.","The next morning, the little devil Zong Jincheng wanted to sleep until noon, but after two months of early rising, his body clock had been set, and he couldn't sleep past dawn.","He pounded the bed and muttered, \"This annoying bodily reaction!\"","Shunzi brought water in to serve him, beaming with joy, \"Young Master, Madam has already given us this month's allowance, and Buyan is back.\"","Zong Jincheng glanced outside and indeed saw Buyan's figure.","Excitedly, he jumped out of bed, forgetting to put on his shoes, and ran to Buyan, saying, \"This family is too tough without you!!\"","Buyan: \"...\" Young Master, you're overacting.","Zong Jincheng, finally done with this miserable studying period, quickly dressed after receiving the fifty taels of silver, and called Buyan and Shunzi to head to the slums to see Jingzhe and check out Zhai Yao's tough life.","Xu Wan hadn't expected the kid to be so energetic, sneaking out to play so early in the morning. With such abundant energy, he still had the nerve to ask Wenxiu to serve him?","This little rascal...","Thinking of this, Xu Wan remembered something: \"Cui Zhi, how's Buyan's martial arts?\"","Cui Zhi replied, \"Buyan used to accompany the young marquis in practicing martial arts. His skills are formidable, rarely matched in the capital.\"","\"Accompanying the young marquis in martial arts?\" Xu Wan knew Zong Zhao was the martial arts champion, so his sparring partner must be reliable.","But...","\"Are they just going with the three of them? What about the coachman?\"","\"Buyan can drive the carriage.\"","\"...\" Truly a jack of all trades. No wonder the little devil is always crying out for him.","Xu Wan pondered for a moment and still said, \"Have Cui Liu follow them secretly.\"","The slums are a complex place, and if someone harbors ill intentions towards the little devil, Buyan alone might not handle it.","Moreover, Zhai Yao is also there.","Last time, the butler of Zhai Manor snatched a child in the slums. Although she didn't understand the key points, her heart kept pounding.","\"Yes, I'll arrange it right away.\"","Xu Wan had just finished speaking when someone came in to report: \"Madam, Madam Zhai from Weiyuan Earl Manor requests an audience.\"","\"Hmm? She's here to see me?\" Xu Wan thought it was probably about Zhai Yao.","She stood up to greet the guest.","Before Madam Zhai even entered, Xu Wan heard her sobbing like pear blossoms bathed in rain, \"Madam Zong, please save my son!\"","Seeing Madam Zhai in plain clothes, looking haggard, Xu Wan felt uneasy. Just overnight, how did she become like this?","They say a mother's worry for her child makes her haggard, which is normal, but looking at Madam Zhai, she felt something was off.","Behind her, Cui Zhi tugged at her hem, whispering, \"She's wearing whitening powder on her face.\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","Without lipstick and with a lot of powder, she looked incredibly haggard.","No wonder she felt something was off.","It seems Madam Zhai came prepared.","Xu Wan showed concern, \"Madam Zhai, please sit. How did you end up like this?\"","Madam Zhai refused to sit and even tried to kneel, but Xu Wan stopped her.","She cried, \"It's all because my son Yao was foolish and said those unpleasant things, which angered the Crown Prince. But Yao is only nine years old, raised in luxury since birth. How can he endure the slums? Madam Zong, please speak to the Crown Prince on our behalf and let our son come back. I'll take any punishment for him.\"","Xu Wan was troubled, \"Madam Zhai, what are you saying? The order came from the Crown Prince. My husband and other male family members are not in the manor, how can I, a mere woman, speak to the Crown Prince? Why doesn't Madam Zhai ask Master Zhai to try?\"","Upon hearing this, Madam Zhai's face changed instantly. A trace of impatience flashed in her eyes, caught by Xu Wan.","Indeed, it was all an act.","The next moment, Madam Zhai continued her plea, \"My husband refuses to go and beg. I have no other choice but to come to you for help. After that banquet, everyone knows the Crown Prince favors your son Jincheng. If you let Jincheng plead on our behalf, the Crown Prince will surely agree to let Yao come back.\"","Xu Wan sighed, \"Madam Zhai, it's not that I don't want to help, but I'm powerless. I'm just a stepmother newly married in, how can I be as effective as a birth mother? You know Jincheng's reputation in the capital, he doesn't cause trouble for me, that's good enough. How could he listen to my requests?\"","She spoke these words against her will.","Although Zong Jincheng was not on good terms with her, if she used her wits, she had plenty of ways to make the little devil agree.","But why should she?","Zhai Yao being disciplined by the Crown Prince was what he deserved.","And this Madam Zhai in front of her, with her obvious acting, might turn hostile the next second.","Why should she waste her impression points with the little devil for such a pair of mother and son?","Seeing her refuse to help, Madam Zhai's displeasure became more apparent. She stopped her fake crying, stepped back, and said coldly, \"It seems Madam Zong is unwilling to help?\"","Xu Wan inwardly sighed, indeed, she changed her face.","She didn't even last a cup of tea's time.","Xu Wan replied calmly, \"I'm truly powerless.\"","Madam Zhai coldly said, \"My husband is the only son of the Pingyang Princess. Offending the Zhai family is not the same as offending an ordinary earl manor.\""]},{"number":39,"title":"Chapter 39: Offend Someone, Blame It on the Deadbeat Dad","paragraphs":["Xu Wan squinted her eyes and said, \"Madam Zhai, you're joking. How could I dare offend you? The Pingyang Princess was the most beloved by the late emperor. If she were to intervene and go to the Crown Prince's residence, I'm sure the Crown Prince wouldn't refuse to release him.\"","You're using the Pingyang Princess to pressure me, but why don't you dare pressure the Crown Prince?","Look at how capable you think you are.","Madam Zhai pointed angrily at her, \"You...\"","Xu Wan smiled, putting on an innocent and harmless expression.","Madam Zhai sneered, \"You're so unfeeling. I can only assume you're relying on your family's influence. Your father may be the Minister of the Ministry of Justice, but he comes from a humble background. If something unexpected happens in his work, it might force him to retire early!\"","Xu Wan's eyes lit up upon hearing this.","Is this good news?","Did she offend someone, and it's being blamed on her father?","This is great! The sooner that man retires, the better!","Xu Wan was secretly delighted but maintained a stubborn demeanor on the surface. \"My father is an honest and upright official. He has nothing to fear. If Madam Zhai thinks she can threaten us with such tactics, even if my father were here, he wouldn't yield!\"","\"Fine! Let's see just how incorruptible your father truly is!\" Madam Zhai stormed off in anger, her sleeves flailing.","Only when Madam Zhai's figure had completely disappeared did Xu Wan finally drop her pretense. She let out a series of uncontrollable giggles, her shoulders shaking until she burst into loud laughter.","\"Hahahahahahahaha...\"","Cui Zhi, seeing her tears almost falling, quickly handed her a handkerchief. \"Madam, laughing so loudly like this, if Madam Zhai were to hear it, she'd be furious.\"","\"Haha, you don't understand, it's really funny. My father probably doesn't even know he's considered so incorruptible,\" Xu Wan said, wiping her tears of laughter.","Cui Zhi couldn't help but laugh and worry at the same time. \"If they really find something, it wouldn't be good for your reputation...\"","Although the two heads of the Xu household aren't exactly model citizens, they're still part of the same family. The entire clan rises and falls together.","Xu Wan waved her hand dismissively. \"Don't worry. My father, though foolish, is extremely cautious in his official duties. That's how he rose from being a Number Two Scholar to the Minister of the Ministry of Justice. Madam Zhai investigating my father because of me will only annoy him for a few days. They won't find anything.\"","Cui Zhi breathed a sigh of relief. \"That's good...\"","Xu Wan watched Madam Zhai's retreating figure and thought of Zong Jincheng, who had gone to the slums. After a moment's consideration, she still felt uneasy.","\"Prepare the carriage. We're going to wait for Jincheng.\"","\"Wait? For him?\"","Yes, wait.","Xu Wan sat in the carriage and waited outside the slums, not interfering with Zong Jincheng's charitable efforts.","She was worried that the Zhai family might try to harm Zong Jincheng there, so she brought many people to wait. If Cui Liu sent back any bad news, she could rush in to save him.","Meanwhile, Zong Jincheng's side was bustling with activity. Buyan first took him to the market to buy clothes and shoes, then some food, filling half the carriage.","Since Buyan returned, Shunzi was even happier than Zong Jincheng.","He was the one protecting the young master, driving the carriage, shopping, and carrying the goods.","It was so relaxing that it felt like he was also a master. It was great!","\"Master, we're here,\" Shunzi said, helping Zong Jincheng out of the carriage. Using his silver tongue, he began to enthusiastically describe the changes in Jing Zhe's home over the past month.","\"The roof has been repaired, the door is new, the musty bedding and quilts have been replaced, and Jing Zhe's injuries have healed quickly.\"","Zong Jincheng stood at the doorway, hearing Shunzi shout loudly, \"Jing Zhe, our master has come to see you!\"","Hearing this, Jing Zhe rushed out of the house, seeing them and immediately wanting to kneel, but Buyan quickly stopped him.","Zong Jincheng laughed and patted his shoulder. \"It's been a month, and you look stronger!\"","Jing Zhe was overjoyed, his voice hoarse. \"Thanks to the life-saving silver you sent, my sister and I could survive here. From now on, my life belongs to you!\"","Zong Jincheng felt an unprecedented sense of accomplishment for the first time being thanked as a savior. He laughed throughout the conversation with Jing Zhe.","Buyan, watching from behind, was quite surprised.","In just two months, Master Jincheng has become so fond of laughing?","Shunzi nudged his shoulder and whispered, \"You don't get it, do you? It's all thanks to Madam's excellent parenting.\"","Buyan was astonished, staring at him as if he were a strange creature. \"Aren't you afraid of being beaten by the master for saying that?\"","From what he observed, Master Jincheng and Madam were at odds.","Shunzi replied, \"I'm just telling you this quietly. It's only because our master is a bit slow that he hasn't noticed his own changes. If the Old Marquis saw him, he might think Master Jincheng had been possessed.\"","Buyan: \"...\"","Upon careful thought, it really could be possible.","Scary.","Zong Jincheng and Jing Zhe chatted merrily for a long time before finally bringing up Zhai Yao.","Jing Zhe said, \"Recently, I did hear that a noble young master was punished and sent here, living in the next alley. There are two guards at his door, not allowing him to leave. I can even hear his crying from home.\"","\"He's crying??\" Zong Jincheng was shocked.","Was this still the fearless, reckless friend Zhai Yao he knew?","Recalling the day Zhai Yao insulted Jing Zhe as a \"lowborn\" in the Crown Prince's residence, Zong Jincheng thought that crying for a day was too light a punishment. He should cry for at least a month.","Thinking of this, he felt the urge to go see Zhai Yao.","He wondered if the guy had learned his lesson and if he would dare to insult him again.","Jing Zhe replied, \"He's crying very pitifully, with a loud voice. Especially at night, my sister is so scared that she can't sleep.\"","Zong Jincheng shook his head. \"That's too cruel. I'll go and tell him to cry more quietly at night.\"","Jing Zhe: \"...\"","It's thoughtful, but something feels off?","With Jing Zhe leading the way, Zong Jincheng easily found Zhai Yao's \"home,\" which was actually just a dilapidated thatched hut, with leaks everywhere and a muddy, filthy drainage ditch in front of the door.","Before Zong Jincheng could enter, a steamed bun was suddenly thrown out of the house. Zhai Yao's furious voice echoed, \"Get out! I, Zhai Yao, would rather starve to death than eat this pig food!\"","Seeing the good steamed bun thrown on the ground, Jing Zhe immediately felt heartbroken and picked it up. Then, suddenly remembering Zong Jincheng was beside him, he hesitated whether to throw it away: \"This food... throwing it away is too wasteful. Eating this at least can keep you from being hungry for a day.\"","The contrast between Zhai Yao and Jing Zhe was so stark that Zong Jincheng was instantly angered without needing any explanation: \"Zhai Yao isn't hungry enough.\"","The Crown Prince's punishment was right; he should be here to temper his character.","Just as Zong Jincheng was about to leave after watching the spectacle, an elderly man, trembling and haggard, walked out of the house. His face was filled with sorrow.","\"Who is this? Isn't Zhai Yao living here alone?\""]},{"number":40,"title":"Chapter 40: Xu Wan Saves Jin Cheng","paragraphs":["Jing Zhe said, \"After they sent Zhai Yao here, he stayed at Grandpa Zhao's house. They probably worried that he wouldn't have enough to eat, so they gave some grain to Grandpa Zhao to take care of him. But... Zhai Yao doesn't eat the food here and often abuses Grandpa Zhao, hitting and cursing at him.\"","“He dares to hit people?” Even the most rebellious little devil knows to respect the elderly and care for the young. How could Zhai Yao dare to lay hands on an old man?","Before Jing Zhe could nod, a stool was thrown out of the house, hitting Grandpa Zhao's bent back. The old man, caught off guard, fell to the ground.","\"Grandpa Zhao!\" Jing Zhe was shocked and hurriedly stepped forward to help him up!","Zong Jincheng also rushed over, helping Jing Zhe to support Grandpa Zhao from both sides.","The little devil was completely enraged. He rolled up his sleeves and charged into the house, grabbing Zhai Yao and throwing a punch, muttering, \"You coward who only bullies the elderly, I'll beat you to death!\"","\"Zong Jincheng? How dare you show up?\" Zhai Yao recognized who his attacker was and, ignoring the pain on his face, charged forward with red eyes, \"I'm going to fight you to the death!\"","The two boys wrestled together, throwing punches at each other. Both were notorious troublemakers in the Capital City, and they were both skilled fighters.","However, Zhai Yao hadn't eaten in a day and was physically exhausted. Eventually, Zong Jincheng pinned him to the ground and started beating him up: \"I'll teach you to lay hands on me! Do you know who I am? I'm the strongest fighter in the entire Capital City! Today, I'll beat you until you're crawling around looking for your teeth!\"","Buyan and Shunzi, who were behind him: \"...\"","When did you become the strongest fighter in the Capital City? Who gave you that title? Save us...","Grandpa Zhao was a timid man. He had taken in Zhai Yao only because he was tempted by the grain they provided, but now seeing the boy being beaten so badly, he was afraid of causing trouble and wanted to intervene. However, Jing Zhe stopped him.","\"Grandpa Zhao, don't interfere. Zhai Yao was sent here because he offended Zong Jincheng. This time, he pushed you, which makes him even more in the wrong. Let Zong Jincheng teach him a good lesson for you.\"","Grandpa Zhao stood there in a daze, nodding tearfully, \"Alright... alright...\"","Zhai Yao was isolated and helpless here. The two guards at the door were only responsible for keeping him from leaving, and they didn't intervene in anything else. Buyan and Shunzi also didn't step in, so Zong Jincheng was free to beat him up without restraint.","But not long after, a group of people suddenly rushed in, shouting, \"Release our young master!\"","Shunzi turned around and saw it was Steward Zhai.","Buyan, who had been standing with his arms crossed, immediately went on alert, positioning himself in front of his young master and preparing for a fight.","Seeing his young master covered in blood, Steward Zhai roared, \"Stop! All of you, stop! Zong Jincheng, if you dare touch our young master again!\"","Zong Jincheng responded by throwing another punch, taunting him, \"I did it. What are you going to do about it?\"","The little devil's face was also bruised, but he still smiled, his cheek dimples adorably showing, though his actions were as mischievous as a little demon's.","Even so, Shunzi knew this was his young master's true nature.","The number one troublemaker in the Capital City, fearless and unrestrained.","Steward Zhai shouted angrily, \"Attack! Save the young master!\"","As soon as he finished speaking, more than a dozen burly men surged forward. Shunzi wisely retreated, while Buyan picked up the broken stool that Zhai Yao had thrown earlier and charged at the Zhai household's men.","\"Bang——\"","\"Ah——\"","\"Ahhh——\"","Buyan was like a war god from the underworld, wielding the stool with one hand, cutting down anyone in his path.","The filthy slum was filled with cries of pain.","Steward Zhai had thought it would be an easy victory with more than a dozen men against just Buyan, but instead, the Marquis Manor's men were scattered and fleeing.","\"It's Buyan! He's from the Marquis Manor! He was the training partner for the young marquis!\"","\"That's him! He's the training partner of the martial champion, capable of defeating a hundred men!\"","\"We're no match for him!\"","Someone recognized Buyan's identity, and the would-be attackers all retreated, their faces filled with fear.","Seeing this, Steward Zhai panicked and shouted, \"Charge! All of you, charge! If you can't win, call for reinforcements! Call more people!\"","The Crown Prince had ordered that no one was to privately assist Zhai Yao, but Madam Zhai was worried and had sent the household's guards and servants to wait outside the slum, fearing someone might harm her son.","So when the call for reinforcements came, a large crowd arrived.","Zong Jincheng: \"???\"","Counting roughly, there were over a hundred people.","Were they really going to make Buyan fight a hundred men alone?","Shunzi swallowed hard, protecting his young master and retreating, \"Young master, step back a bit. Although Buyan can handle them, there are too many. If he has to fend off some to come after you, I'll die defending you!\"","This was probably the most loyal thing a non-fighter could say.","Zong Jincheng pushed him away, shouting, \"You can't fight, get out of here. I can protect myself!\"","Shunzi's eyes immediately filled with tears.","His young master was so kind!","He might be the first servant ever to be protected by his master!","Shunzi decided that even if he died here today, he would be Zong Jincheng's most loyal subordinate!","But before he could act, his young master charged into the battlefield, not out of necessity, but seemingly eager to join the fray!","However, the opponents were all professional fighters, all adults, and in terms of both size and skill, they were far superior to Zong Jincheng. The little devil, full of bravado, was soon grabbed by the neck and lifted off the ground.","Shunzi's eyes widened: \"Young master!!!\"","Save him!!!","Who would save his young master!!!","The Zhai household's fighter lifted Zong Jincheng and slammed him toward the wall. If this hit, it would definitely result in a head injury, possibly even death or permanent disability!","\"Stop!!!\"","At this critical moment, a light green figure suddenly flew in from the sky, landing on the crumbling rooftops on both sides, heading straight for Zong Jincheng. With a kick, she knocked the Zhai servant to the ground.","Zong Jincheng, who had been in mid-air, was saved and, upon closer look, saw that it was—","\"Cui Liu! Why are you here?!\"","It was none other than Cui Liu, the top female fighter of the Marquis Manor, left by the old madam to protect Xu Wan.","Seeing her, Shunzi exclaimed in surprise, \"It's Madam! It must be Madam who sent her! We're saved now!\"","With Buyan fighting in the front and Cui Liu protecting the young master from behind, even if they couldn't defeat the Zhai household, at least the young master wouldn't get hurt.","Cui Liu's usually cold face showed a rare smile as she reassured, \"Young master, don't be afraid. Madam is also here.\"","\"Ah?\" Zong Jincheng quickly turned his head.","Sure enough, a red-clad figure appeared at the narrow alley entrance.","Tall, composed, and strategic.","Behind her, countless servants rushed in, all from the Marquis Manor, here to help them!"]},{"number":41,"title":"Chapter 41: Xu Wan Stands by His Side Again","paragraphs":["Xu Wan walked calmly towards them, her eyes taking in the scene as the people from Marquis Manor surrounded the Zhai family.","The previously unfavorable situation had suddenly reversed!","\"Without the permission of our Marquis Manor, who dares to touch Zong Jincheng?\" Her voice was firm and powerful, just as confident as when she used to bully him, but this time her words were aimed at outsiders.","This was the second time Xu Wan had sided with him.","Zong Jincheng's heart raced with warmth, but the proud little brat didn't want to admit it. He turned his face away, deliberately avoiding her gaze.","Seeing the person in charge arrive, Steward Zhai immediately called for a halt, and all the enforcers on both sides stopped.","\"Madam Zong, your son Zong Jincheng suddenly came to our house and beat up our young master. We need to settle this account!\"","Zong Jincheng didn't even bother to explain, directly shouting back, \"You dare to talk to us about settling accounts? Zhai Yao, that bastard, I didn't even beat him enough. If it weren't for you stopping me, I could have kept going!\"","\"You!\" Steward Zhai fumed, \"Madam Zong, what do you think about this? Our master and mistress don't even know about this yet, otherwise, this matter would never be resolved so easily!\"","Shunzi stepped forward to explain for his young master, \"Madam, it was Young Master Zhai Yao who kicked over Grandpa Zhao, and Young Master Jincheng couldn't stand by and watch.\"","Xu Wan followed his gaze and saw Grandpa Zhao being supported by Jingzhe, his face full of pain.","She immediately understood and spoke to Steward Zhai with sharp words, \"Jincheng's actions may not have been rational, but it was your Young Master Zhai who was in the wrong first. Moreover, they are both eight or nine-year-old children, and it's normal for children to fight. But you, Steward Zhai, have escalated the matter by bringing a hundred men to surround the direct grandson of our Marquis Manor. What is your intention?\"","Zong Jincheng listened, stunned.","How did she make it sound like the Zhai family was entirely at fault?","No, it was the Zhai family's fault. She's right!","The little devil, who had been prepared to face punishment, suddenly felt a surge of confidence, as if he had a big backer. Shunzi couldn't help but twitch the corner of his mouth.","This madam... it feels like she's become a new backer for Young Master Jincheng.","Although she always opposes him, she's always united when dealing with outsiders.","Steward Zhai, being an old fox, wasn't easily fooled by Xu Wan. He coldly said, \"It seems Madam Zong is deliberately playing dumb. Fine, we'll return to the manor and report this to our master and mistress, let them go to the Crown Prince and settle the matter!\"","\"Go ahead,\" Xu Wan smiled, \"But I must remind you to think carefully. Why was Zhai Yao punished by the Crown Prince? And why was he beaten by Jincheng this time? Don't end up being punished again after complaining.\"","Xu Wan's words were sincere.","Based on her understanding of the Crown Prince, Zhai Yao might very well face another punishment.","\"We don't need Madam Zong to worry about how the Zhai family handles this!\" Steward Zhai said, then turned to his subordinates, \"Take Young Master back to the manor to see the doctor!\"","\"Stop!\" Two guards from the Crown Prince's palace suddenly spoke up, \"The Crown Prince has ordered that no one is to take Zhai Yao away.\"","Steward Zhai, seeing them pop up at this moment, was almost driven to spit out blood!","He angrily shouted, \"You are supposed to be watching over our young master, but when Zong Jincheng beat him up, why didn't you stop it?!\"","The guards coldly replied, \"The Crown Prince never gave that order.\"","\"You! You!\" Steward Zhai almost vomited blood, completely overwhelmed by anger.","Even Xu Wan couldn't help but rub her forehead.","The guards from the Crown Prince's palace were indeed quite... unique.","Normally, in such situations, they would at least try to report back to the palace.","But these two did absolutely nothing...","It made one wonder if they were just slacking off.","However, this question was soon answered. Xu Wan took Zong Jincheng back to the manor to apply medicine. Just as they finished, they heard Cui Liu reporting the latest developments.","\"Madam, the Zhai family's master and mistress indeed went to the Crown Prince's palace to complain.\"","\"Oh? And then?\" Xu Wan was curious.","The little devil also leaned forward, wanting to know what happened next.","Cui Liu paused for a moment before saying, \"Then they were refused an audience by the Crown Princess.\"","\"Pfft...\" Xu Wan was the first to laugh out loud.","The little devil and Zong Wenxiu also burst into laughter, along with Shunzi and Cui Zhi, who were covering their mouths, trying not to laugh.","Xu Wan chuckled, \"The Crown Princess is really quite... unique. I thought she was gentle, but every time she ends up playing the role of the offender, she's truly a model wife.\"","Cui Liu added, \"The Crown Princess's exact words were that the Crown Prince is not in good health, and she asked the Zhai family not to bother him with such trivial matters. The Zhai couple didn't even get to see the Crown Princess, let alone the Crown Prince.\"","Xu Wan nodded, \"That's good. It saves the trouble of the Zhai family truly losing their minds if Zhai Yao were to be punished too harshly.\"","Zong Jincheng suddenly chimed in, \"But Zhai Yao really deserved it.\"","Zong Wenxiu also rarely agreed with a nod.","Xu Wan smiled and delivered a sharp blow to the little devil, \"Indeed, you are truly one of the four young dandy heirs of the capital.\"","Zong Jincheng: \"!\"","The friendship boat didn't even last half a day before it capsized!","Even the next day, when going to Qingbo Academy to check the results, the little devil was still angrily glaring from inside the carriage.","The little brat, who usually had no backbone, was sitting straight this time, trying his best to kill the woman in the carriage with his eyes.","Xu Wan still had that playful look, teasing, \"Kid, I hope you still have the energy to glare at me after seeing the results.\"","Zong Jincheng snorted, \"I have full confidence in my abilities! I'll definitely make you and those two lose so badly you won't even be able to lift your heads!\"","“Bragging,” Xu Wan objectively commented.","Zong Wenxiu also secretly gave a thumbs up.","Such words were only said by Madam in the entire Marquis Manor. Others, including himself, would probably be chased around by his brother if they said something like that.","Zong Jincheng was furious, \"You're so annoying! Why are you coming to see the results?!\"","Xu Wan replied casually, \"Of course, I want to see your bragging fall flat in person.\"","\"Pfft...\" Zong Wenxiu couldn't hold back and burst out laughing, covering his eyes and trying to reduce his presence.","Zong Jincheng was so angry he was grinding his teeth, \"Well, I really appreciate your attention, old lady!\"","“You're welcome. It's my duty as a mother,” Xu Wan said, showing a warm yet indifferent demeanor, infuriating others without any consequences.","Zong Jincheng snorted and moved closer to Zong Wenxiu, wanting to stay as far away from Xu Wan as possible.","After teasing the little devil, Xu Wan calmly turned to Zong Wenxiu, \"This time, consider it a mock exam. Although you've been studying very hard every day, the time is still too short. So it's normal if you don't do well. Don't feel too bad about it. You can do better next time.\""]},{"number":42,"title":"Chapter 42: The Little Demon Causes Havoc at the Academy","paragraphs":["She had a premonition that if Zong Wenxiu and Zong Jincheng took the same exam, they would both perform well, but the one Zong Wenxiu took was more difficult. Having only studied for half a year, he was competing against others who had been studying for years. Losing was only natural.","But Wenxiu was different. Introverted and meticulous, he was prone to getting stuck in his own high standards, trapped in a mental breakdown.","Zong Wenxiu was indeed very nervous. He wanted to see his results but was afraid of performing poorly. Hearing Xu Wan's words, he felt warmth in his heart. Sometimes, from Madam Xu, he could see the shadow of his mother.","Madam Xu treated him exceptionally well.","Zong Wenxiu gratefully said, \"Thank you, Madam. I will take your words to heart.\"","Xu Wan smiled at him.","The little troublemaker, on the other hand, grew increasingly annoyed listening to them. He glared at the two who seemed to ignore him and dryly mocked Xu Wan, \"So you can say nice things after all!\"","\"It's just that you never get them!\"","Xu Wan lazily replied, \"Nice words are meant for the right people. Some are inspired and work harder after hearing them, while others become overconfident and complacent. Isn't that right, Young Master Jincheng?\"","Zong Jincheng felt the burn again. His lips pouted higher than a teapot. Finally, unable to bear the humiliation, he shouted out the window, \"Stop the carriage! I'm getting off! Who wants to sit with her anyway?\"","The coachman stopped the carriage, and Zong Jincheng jumped off.","Zong Wenxiu wanted to stop him but couldn't. He looked at Xu Wan, who wasn't in a hurry. She said, \"We're almost at the academy. Let him walk.\"","\"This kid isn't stupid. He knows it's just a short distance, so he dares to throw a tantrum. He's got the makings of a good official.\"","\"Huh?\" Zong Wenxiu was puzzled. Where did that come from?","Xu Wan explained, \"He knows how to adapt. Being an official requires tact.\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","Couldn't understand, but felt deeply impressed.","Every month after the Qingbo Academy exams, they would mimic the imperial examinations by posting the students' rankings, only up to the top 120.","So, after the academy exams, students would greet each other with, \"Did you make the list?\"","The rankings were from left to right, with the left being the top and the right the bottom.","Zong Jincheng, having listened to Xu Wan's lecture in the carriage, curiously pulled Zong Wenxiu to find his ranking. Zong Wenxiu wasn't confident and started from the bottom.","Not long after, he found his name.","Grade B, 106th place.","The exam results were divided into four grades: A, B, C, and D, with each grade further ranked by accuracy. Students in the top 120 were at least Grade B.","Seeing this result, Zong Wenxiu wasn't sure if he should feel happy or not, but he smiled at his brother as usual, \"I made the list. That's good enough.\"","Zong Jincheng, however, was far from satisfied. He questioned, \"How could it be only 106th place?\"","This ranking meant that among the same grade at Qingbo Academy, there were 105 students better than Zong Wenxiu?","That's way too many!","In Zong Jincheng's eyes, Zong Wenxiu might not be as smart, cute, or good at memorizing as himself, but at least he worked hard. Every day, he woke up before dawn to study and stayed up late reading. How could someone like that only score so low?","Zong Wenxiu smiled, \"It's normal. After all, I'm two years older than you, and there's still so much more to learn. Let's go find your result. You must have done better than me.\"","Speaking of Zong Jincheng's results, the little troublemaker was extremely confident. Without needing Zong Wenxiu to lead the way, Zong Jincheng proudly walked toward the top.","He, Zong Xiaogongzi, would surely be the top of the academy!","\"First place, Grade A, Qin Ye.\"","\"It's him again! This guy has been unbeatable since he enrolled, never dropping below second place.\"","Before Zong Jincheng even reached the top, he heard this and his face immediately changed: \"The first place isn't me??\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","Such confidence is something I'll never have.","Zong Jincheng stood on tiptoe to look inside, only to find that not only was the first place not him, but the second place was also someone named Zhang Zhi.","\"How could it be him??\" Zong Jincheng was bewildered.","Zong Wenxiu was also confused: \"Madam Xu said that Zhang Zhi always scored Grade B. How did he suddenly jump to Grade A and rank second?\"","This was so strange that even Zong Wenxiu felt something was off.","Zong Wenxiu quickly scanned down the list and found two names at the bottom:","119th place, Grade B, Zong Jincheng.","120th place, Grade B, Wu Shusen.","\"How could this be...\" Zong Wenxiu couldn't believe his eyes.","Although his brother memorized texts by rote and didn't understand the true meaning or thoughts behind them, he had memorized the translations. At this age, the exams didn't go that deep. His brother should have been unstoppable.","How could he only score Grade B?","And that Zhang Zhi, wasn't he at the same level as Wu Shusen?","How did he suddenly jump to second place?","Zong Jincheng, seeing him go to the bottom, angrily shouted, \"Why are you looking for me there? How could I be at the bottom?!\"","He ran over, but before he could even focus on the list, Zong Wenxiu grabbed his sleeve and firmly said, \"This list must be fake.\"","Zong Jincheng was stunned, thinking he was upset about his own result. He immediately agreed, \"I think so too. How could you only score Grade B!\"","Zong Wenxiu shook his head, denying, \"No, scoring Grade B might be normal for me, but for you, it's definitely not normal!\"","Zong Jincheng's eyes widened, and his head instantly turned to the list. He saw his name right next to Wu Shusen, at the very bottom.","Zong Jincheng: \"!!!\"","How could he only score Grade B!","Absolutely impossible!!!","Zong Wenxiu pulled him away, \"Let's go find Madam Xu and ask her to help investigate. Something must be wrong!\"","Zong Jincheng, initially stunned, snapped out of it and violently shook off his hand, jumping in anger, \"What's the point of looking into it? There's definitely a problem! This lousy academy dared to rank me at the bottom? That's an insult!\"","\"Damn it! They even posted it for everyone to see. Double insult! I'll smash them!\"","With that, the little troublemaker turned back, forcefully pushing through the crowd, kicking over a nearby desk, and tearing down the red list!","The long red paper was quickly shredded, shocking everyone. Zong Jincheng threw the scraps everywhere and, still not satisfied, stomped on them several times!","The students watching the rankings had never seen such a scene. What kind of arrogant behavior was this?!","When they finally reacted, they shouted, \"Who are you? Why did you tear down the list!\"","\"Exactly! Who is this brat? Qingbo Academy is no place for you to cause trouble!\""]},{"number":43,"title":"Chapter 43: Jin Cheng's Handwriting is Ugly","paragraphs":["Zong Wenxiu had never encountered such an unfair situation before. If it had been him, he would have gritted his teeth and endured it, but his brother was different. How could such a proud heir to the Marquis Manor endure such humiliation?","But what he didn't expect was that, unlike his own courage to seek help from Madam Xu Wan, the little devil himself had directly overturned the table!","Zong Jincheng had roamed the Capital City for years, and even the most unruly sons of noble families dared not claim to be the boss in front of him. He was willful and unrestrained, unafraid of offending anyone, and started smashing things with a stool.","Zhang Zhi, seeing this, clapped his hands and walked out, mocking, \"Oh, isn't this the kid who was bragging the other day? Couldn't pass the exam, so now you're tearing down the rankings? Can't take losing, huh?\"","Wu Shusen also stood beside him, although he was one rank lower than Zong Jincheng, his friend had at least won. He lifted his head and joined in the mockery, \"I think it's because he couldn't pass the exam, that's why he's losing his temper and going crazy in the academy.\"","Zong Jincheng retorted loudly, \"Who are you saying couldn't pass the exam? With your results, how could you possibly rank second? You must have cheated! And you, the last place, what's your name?\"","Zhang Zhi rebuked, \"What are you talking about! I answered every question on the exam myself!\"","Wu Shusen also retorted, \"So what if I'm last? At least I'm not as shameless as you, the second to last, to mock me!\"","Zong Jincheng snorted coldly, \"Answer my ass. Those exam papers were so easy. If you hadn't cheated, how could I have ranked so low?\"","Zhang Zhi laughed angrily, \"You little punk, do you even know what cheating is? Cheating is falsifying your own exam paper, what does that have to do with your terrible performance? Did someone force you to fail?\"","The two argued endlessly, moving from their poor exam results to the fairness of the exam itself.","The onlooking students finally reacted and hurried to call someone in charge.","After Zong Jincheng and Zong Wenxiu ran over to check the results, Xu Wan went straight to the Principal's office. She wanted to take a look at the two boys' exam papers to determine the direction of their future education based on their mistakes.","Before she could find the papers, she heard students rushing in, gasping for breath, \"Principal... Principal, something terrible has happened! A student who didn't do well on the exam tore down the rankings! He's still smashing tables!\"","Xu Wan wasn't sure if she was being overly sensitive, but as soon as she heard about such an arrogant student, she immediately thought of the little devil.","\"What?\" The Principal slammed the table and stood up, too busy to continue helping Xu Wan find the papers. He followed the students out, asking as he walked, \"Tell me quickly, what's going on?\"","Xu Wan also followed closely behind.","When they arrived, they saw the little devil indeed arguing with others. If it weren't for Zong Wenxiu holding him back, the brat would have been eager to start a fight.","The Principal, seeing Zong Jincheng, realized who the troublemaker was.","Indeed, it was the notorious troublemaker from the Capital City.","He knew that letting Zong Jincheng into the academy would lead to this day, but there was no way around it. The Marquis Manor had offered far too much.","Who could refuse that...","The Principal's eyes welled up with tears as he pulled the three arguing students apart. He then addressed Zong Jincheng, \"Master Zong, is there some misunderstanding?\"","Zong Jincheng snorted and crossed his arms, even more arrogant in his posture.","Zhang Zhi cried out, \"Principal, he can't take losing! He got last place and tore down the leaderboard, making it impossible for us to see the results!\"","Wu Shusen also stepped forward, \"That's right, Principal. We were just trying to stop him, and he started arguing with us. How can such a reckless student be allowed to stay in our academy?\"","Zong Wenxiu, seeing they were only telling the parts that benefited them, quickly spoke up to explain for his brother, \"It's not like that, Madam. I suspected their results were falsified, which is why my brother got so impulsive and tore down the list.\"","\"Falsified results?\" This time, Xu Wan didn't need Zong Wenxiu to explain further. She had a pretty good idea of what had happened.","The little devil must have gotten an extremely poor ranking.","But it didn't match his actual abilities.","Others might not know Zong Jincheng's true level, but she and Zong Wenxiu did. Thinking this, she said to the Principal, \"Principal, perhaps we should first check the two boys' exam papers? I also want to see how Jincheng did.\"","The Principal nodded, \"Alright, then come with me to check the papers.\"","They followed him and first found Zong Wenxiu's exam paper.","Xu Wan took it and heard the Principal say, \"Wenxiu's paper is actually quite good. He answered all the questions he attempted correctly, so it seems he's just a bit behind in his studies.\"","Xu Wan nodded, \"Yes, the Principal has a keen eye.\"","The Principal then found Zong Jincheng's exam paper and said, \"Jincheng's answers are also quite good. Although his translation skills need some work, his handwriting is very beautiful.\"","At this, Xu Wan and Zong Wenxiu both looked over simultaneously.","The little devil's handwriting is good?","That compliment could only be accepted by Zong Jincheng himself, with his thick skin.","Zong Wenxiu gave Xu Wan a look, as if to say, see, there's definitely something wrong with the paper.","His brother had only been learning to write for a short time. Even with his talent, his handwriting had never been particularly good. Yet now, the Principal was praising it separately, which was highly unusual.","Xu Wan took the paper and looked at it. Indeed, the handwriting was unfamiliar.","Someone had switched the little devil's exam paper.","At this point, Zong Wenxiu whispered to Xu Wan, \"Madam, Zhang Zhi ranked second this time. I find that suspicious.\"","Xu Wan immediately understood and asked the Principal, \"Could you please also bring out Zhang Zhi's exam paper?\"","\"Why do you want to see my paper?\" Zhang Zhi was so nervous he stammered.","The Principal also looked over with confusion.","Xu Wan smiled and replied, \"Because I suspect you stole Jincheng's results.\"","The Principal: \"!!!\"","Good heavens! How could that be possible?!","He had been so careful with the people from the Marquis Manor, yet someone in the academy was pulling his leg behind the scenes?","Zhang Zhi shouted, \"Why do you have the right to see my paper? That's my personal property, I don't allow anyone to look at it!\"","Xu Wan asked him, \"Are you feeling guilty?\"","Zhang Zhi's face turned red to the roots of his neck. He yelled, \"Who's feeling guilty! I'm just protecting my privacy!\"","Xu Wan replied, \"The ink, paper, and even the writing brush for the monthly exam are all provided by the academy. The Principal has the right to view the results of any student.\"","\"Then... then only the Principal can look at it!\"","\"Fine,\" Xu Wan smiled and said to Zong Wenxiu, \"Wenxiu, take Jincheng over there and write a few words for the Principal to compare the handwriting.\"","She didn't directly ask Jincheng to write because, given the boy's rebellious attitude towards her, he probably wouldn't cooperate.","But with Zong Wenxiu in between, Zong Jincheng, though reluctantly, still went over and wrote a few lines from the first two sentences of the \"Strategies of the Warring States.\"","Zong Wenxiu brought the handwriting over, and Xu Wan handed it to the Principal to compare with the second-to-last place paper in his hand.","The Principal's mouth twitched as he looked at it.","The handwriting was truly ugly.","Almost every character was twice the size of normal, filling the entire paper, a stark contrast to the neat, small handwriting on the exam paper."]},{"number":44,"title":"Chapter 44: Hit a Snag","paragraphs":["Zhang Zhi glanced at the situation and defended, \"Maybe he intentionally wrote ugly characters, or switched hands to write!\"","\"My brother writes with his right hand,\" Zong Wenxiu said.","\"Who knows if he's left-handed!\"","\"...\"","Although Zhang Zhi kept making excuses, what he said wasn't entirely without reason. The headmaster began to waver as well.","Xu Wan suggested, \"Then please have the headmaster compare the handwriting of Jincheng's and the second-place student's exam papers.\"","Upon hearing this, Zong Jincheng protested unhappily, \"Why not compare with the first place? There's no way I could have come in second!\"","Xu Wan shot him a glance and said, \"Because the first place is really strong, stronger than you.\"","Zong Jincheng was unconvinced: \"Nonsense! I want to compete for the first place!\"","\"You're asking for trouble.\"","Zong Jincheng: \"!!!\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","Even in such a tense moment, his brother still had the mood to bicker with his wife. His mental state was truly remarkable.","The headmaster took out Zhang Zhi's exam paper. As soon as he opened it, the ugly handwriting felt like it had flipped his skull over.","Every sentence in this exam paper was written at the top of the line, with some even trying to spill over the margins. The headmaster had managed Qingbo Academy for so many years and had never seen such a bizarre and ugly handwriting.","However, at the same time, this ugly handwriting was indeed the same as what Zong Jincheng had just written!","\"This...\" The headmaster quickly realized the issue and angrily ordered, \"Someone, go get the examiner who graded the papers!\"","Zhang Zhi instantly became tense, his face dripping with cold sweat.","Zong Jincheng also stretched his neck, eager to know the result. The second-place paper definitely wasn't his!","That woman looked down on him. If it were up to him, he would have started by checking the first-place paper!","Seeing this, Xu Wan knew the truth was out, and now they just had to wait for the headmaster's verdict.","In the meantime, the headmaster gave Zhang Zhi another chance to write a sentence on the spot for a handwriting comparison.","Zhang Zhi's hands trembled as he deliberately wrote ugly characters.","The headmaster, with a black face, said, \"If you don't cooperate, I have plenty of ways to verify. I still have last year's exam papers archived, and comparing your handwriting with those would reveal the issue. It might just take some time!\"","Zhang Zhi's mental defenses crumbled, and he was utterly panicked.","The following moments felt like waiting for a verdict. When the year-end exam papers were compared, the handwriting on the paper that had replaced Zong Jincheng's score was indeed Zhang Zhi's.","The examiner, seeing the evidence, was terrified and quickly admitted his mistake: \"Headmaster, I'm sorry! It was because I was blinded by money. Yesterday, Zhang Zhi secretly gave me two taels of silver, and I thought, since the exam papers wouldn't be seen by the students, I...\"","The headmaster was so furious he kicked the examiner: \"What do you mean, 'I thought'! For just two taels of silver, you dared to tamper with Zong Jincheng's results! Do you know who he is? The hundred-year reputation of Qingbo Academy could be ruined because of you!\"","Zong Jincheng was almost furious.","\"Two taels of silver? Two taels of silver bought my results??\"","He looked incredulously at Zong Wenxiu, his big eyes filled with the anger of being insulted!","Two taels of silver was the price of a dish of goose that Zong Jincheng would eat.","But someone had swallowed his results.","The damage wasn't significant, but the insult was extreme!","Seeing this brat about to explode, Xu Wan had Zong Wenxiu hold him back to prevent any trouble.","Zong Wenxiu was struggling.","His brother's strength was too much; he was about to lose his grip!","Meanwhile, the headmaster was pronouncing the verdict: \"The examiner tampered with students' papers, affecting the fairness of the monthly exam. Effective immediately, Qingbo Academy will no longer employ this person!\"","\"Zhang Zhi, for bribing the examiner and fabricating results, you are expelled from Qingbo Academy effective immediately!\"","The examiner pleaded desperately, \"Headmaster! Please forgive me; it was my first time taking a bribe. I will change!\"","Zhang Zhi quickly followed suit: \"Headmaster! It was my first mistake too. I'm still young and don't know the weight of my actions. Please give me another chance!\"","The headmaster angrily shouted, \"Get out of the academy!\"","The two masterminds were quickly dragged away. There was also a Wu Shusen, who hadn't participated in the cheating, so he wasn't punished. But since he was associated with Zhang Zhi, he was also at a loss and flustered.","The headmaster sternly said, \"You too, pack up and get out.\"","Wu Shusen was instantly stunned: \"No, Headmaster, I didn't participate! I didn't tamper with his paper! I didn't do anything wrong!!\"","The headmaster said, \"You aided and abetted Zhang Zhi, knowing about it but not reporting it. With such character, Qingbo Academy, a hundred-year institution of integrity, cannot accept you! Take him away!\"","Wu Shusen wailed as he was dragged away along with the others.","On the other side, the headmaster ordered the examiner to rewrite the monthly exam rankings. This time, Zong Jincheng watched as his name climbed to the top.","He was now at the top of the first column, ranked A.","Second place.","Zong Jincheng still wasn't satisfied: \"I want to check the first place's paper!\"","The headmaster asked, \"Do you have a grudge with the first place?\"","\"I don't know him!\" Zong Jincheng confidently said, \"But he couldn't have done better than me!\"","The headmaster: \"...\"","Although you're very strong, don't be too confident.","He thought about his words and gently advised, \"Qin Ye always comes in first. His results are not fake.\"","\"I don't care; I want to check his paper!\"","The headmaster sighed and still had someone fetch Qin Ye's paper. He thought for a moment and first handed it to Xu Wan.","Xu Wan took it and looked it over.","Compared to the little demon's ugly handwriting, Qin Ye's was beautiful, almost like printed text. The exam paper was full, with not a single mistake.","Looking at his dictation and translations, his answers were all excellent.","Truly perfect.","Normally, the little demon could have done well by rote memorization, but Qingbo Academy's questions weren't directly from the books. The final big question asked students to write about the similarities and differences based on the general ideas of several books.","Such questions were difficult to answer perfectly through rote memorization alone.","So Qin Ye outperforming Zong Jincheng was well deserved.","Xu Wan handed the paper to the little demon, who took it and quickly furrowed his brows.","Although the little demon was usually very confident, he wasn't without basic aesthetics. He could clearly see the gap between himself and the other person.","But...","\"Did a real person write this? Or was it printed?\"","The handwriting of the answerer was too similar to the exam paper's text, making it seem like it wasn't written by a human.","Zong Wenxiu also looked over and agreed; it didn't look like human handwriting. But if it was a fake score, that would be fine. If it was real, then Qin Ye was truly terrifying.","Xu Wan smiled and said, \"Headmaster, it seems our child isn't convinced. Could we invite this student Qin Ye to come over for a discussion? Jincheng wants to see the first place's prowess.\"","In fact, she had sent someone to investigate Qin Ye's background over the past two days. His father was a fifth-rank official and a former top scholar from six years ago's imperial exams.","Qin Ye had been influenced by his family's scholarly atmosphere since childhood. He had started reading and writing early and worked hard, which was why he was so far ahead of his peers.","This time, the little demon had really bumped into a tough opponent."]},{"number":45,"title":"Chapter 45: Little Demon Meets Strong Rival","paragraphs":["Zong Jincheng protested unwillingly, correcting: \"It's exposing, exposing his fraud! Who wants to witness his charm? What's there to see in fraud?\"","Xu Wan chuckled lightly and gave him a sidelong glance.","Zong Jincheng raised his fist, unwilling to back down.","The headmaster didn't get annoyed and laughed, asking someone to call Qin Ye, who was their prized possession, a top talent destined to secure a place in the first division. Of course, he could showcase him!","The little devil waited in the courtyard, his bottom unable to sit still like it had grown nails. He would stand up from time to time, kick the stone bench occasionally, making Xu Wan want to close her eyes.","She held her forehead and complained, \"I see you have too much energy; it would be more suitable to go to the Martial Academy and burn off some energy. Old Marquis and Old Madam are also like this; going to the Martial Academy doesn't necessarily mean you'll become a military general in the future. With your attitude of fishing for three days and sunbathing for two days, even as a soldier, you'd be disliked by the military camp.\"","Zong Jincheng couldn't stand the provocation.","He jumped up directly, shouting to her: \"Who wants to go to the Martial Academy? Rolling around in the mud every day, sweating all over, it's so dirty, I don't care about practicing martial arts!\"","Xu Wan nodded perfunctorily and said, \"Yes, yes, yes, you don't do things that are tiring, you don't do things that are dirty, you don't do things that require persistence, and you also don't do things that are boring and uninteresting. Anyway, you just don't want to do anything, Young Master.\"","Zong Jincheng wanted to say \"yes,\" but in response to her sarcastic remarks, no matter how he replied, it seemed like admitting defeat.","He snorted, continuing to look towards the gate.","\"Why hasn't he come yet?\" The little devil's patience was gradually wearing off.","Meanwhile, Zong Wenxiu was studying Qin Ye's exam paper, examining each question from start to finish. This person was two years younger than him, but his handwriting was truly neat, and his translation answered word for word, exactly the same as the translations that Madam had organized for her brother.","Flipping through the back of the exam paper, Qin Ye's understanding of the \"Meng Qiu\" was not only profound but also referenced various texts to strengthen his arguments. \"Meng Qiu\" was something Zong Wenxiu had only memorized last month, clearly Qin Ye was much stronger than him.","Compared to Zong Jincheng's impatience, Zong Wenxiu's back had already started to feel cold; it was the first time he deeply felt how big the gap was between his own knowledge and that of others.","After a long time, the headmaster finally returned.","Following behind him was a cold-faced young boy, who had no ornaments on him, only wearing a deep blue robe with a plain belt around his waist, simple and neat.","Qin Ye looked up, his gaze extremely cold.","The headmaster smiled and said: \"Madam Zong, you've waited for a long time. Just now, Qin Ye was still in class and only came out after the teacher finished. You see, this child is Qin Ye; he personally answered the exam paper.\"","Zong Jincheng examined him; the other person was about the same height as him, but their personalities were completely opposite, cold enough to freeze the people around them.","His eyes showed no annoyance, only impatience.","Zong Jincheng understood, immediately responding with an even more impatient tone: \"Then write it down, I want to see if this is his handwriting!\"","The little devil spoke in a very poor tone, like questioning and doubting. Anyone who heard it for no reason would be unable to hold back their anger.","The headmaster also fears that Qin Ye might suddenly turn against him and argue.","Because although this kid was academically strong, his temper was really strange, completely opposite to his father's charm who was good at dealing with people.","Unexpectedly, Qin Ye didn't even ask and directly walked to the table, picking up a pen and starting to write. The young boy wrote quickly, even Zong Wenxiu, who was diligent and hardworking, felt somewhat inferior.","In no time, he had already written two lines of text.","Qin Ye stood up, saying to the dean: \"Can I leave? I haven't finished the homework the teacher left.\"","The headmaster's mouth twitched, the teacher's assignments were usually meant to be done on rest days, but this kid hadn't even finished today's class yet, and he was already rushing to complete it, really anxious.","He picked up the paper, seeing the familiar handwriting, and said with satisfaction: \"Alright, you can go back now.\"","Zong Jincheng heard this and quickly interjected, \"Why are you leaving so urgently? We haven't seen each other yet!\"","He took the Xuan paper from the headmaster's hand, seeing that the handwriting on it was indeed consistent with that on the exam paper, neat as if it had been printed.","Zong Jincheng had seen it with his own eyes, but still felt it was unbelievable.","He flipped the paper back and forth to inspect it, not only finding no signs of cheating, but also discovering that this person had excellent control over their writing pressure; even the back of the rice paper had no ink stains.","Perfect, to the point of not being able to find a flaw.","Zong Jincheng turned his head to look at him, unconsciously saying: \"How could you have taken my first place?\"","Qin Ye's cold eyelids lifted, looking at him with certainty: \"Because...\"","“First is mine, no one can take it.”","The young boy didn't actually have much aggression, but the confidence in his eyes firmly pierced the little devil's fragile heart.","Zong Jincheng's voice couldn't help but rise several degrees: \"What did you say?\"","Qin Ye didn't repeat it a second time; he never liked wasting time on meaningless arguments, so he turned his head and was about to leave.","Zong Jincheng went around to face him, threatening, \"Say it again.\"","Qin Ye tried to go around him.","But no matter how he tried to get away, the little devil just clung to him and wouldn't let him go.","Qin Ye's gaze grew even colder.","He coldly said, \"Say it again a hundred times, it’s still like this, you can’t pass me.\"","After saying that, he pushed the little devil to the side and strode towards the door.","Zong Jincheng was pushed and almost fell to the ground.","He probably has never encountered someone who could be even more arrogant than himself in this life; the other person was so proud that they didn't even take him seriously.","Qin Ye even...","Even didn't ask what his name was!","Zong Jincheng was about to explode!","Insult! It's simply an insult!","He jumped up and down in both anger and rage, shaking Zong Wenxiu and shouting: \"This guy is so arrogant! He doesn't take me seriously at all! What does he mean by 'the first that can't be taken away'? Who told him that the first place belongs to him? The first place is mine! Mine! Where on earth did he get his confidence from!!!\"","Xu Wan had also asked the little demon king this question, but the answer was that he was merely blindly confident, with no factual basis.","But Qin Ye was different; his confidence came from his strength.","A child who had never lacked money or love since childhood, and who could always take first place in every exam, his confidence was so strong that no one could compete with him.","Xu Wan watched the little demon king go mad quietly by his side, with no intention of comforting him at all.","On the contrary, Zong Wenxiu kept persuading him: \"You just haven't studied for long, you're starting from a later starting line than him. If you study for the same amount of time as he does, you will definitely be able to pass him easily!\"","Zong Jincheng's eyes lit up: \"That's right, I only studied for two months to get second place. If I study for one more month, he won't stand a chance!\"","Xu Wan couldn't help but chuckle.","Zong Jincheng was once again pierced in his fragile little heart by this laughter, and he roared: \"What are you laughing at!!!\""]},{"number":46,"title":"Chapter 46: Jincheng is Stimulated","paragraphs":["Xu Wan smiled and said, \"I'm laughing at how easily your confidence comes back. I hope your strength can catch up with your confidence soon.\"","After saying that, she patted his shoulder and added, \"Kid, keep it up.\"","Zong Jincheng clenched his fists and stood still.","To him, this encouragement sounded no different from an insult.","He thought of Qin Ye's arrogance just before he left, and it felt like a fire had been lit in his chest, burning him up!","\"So what if he's the first place? This young master will take it back and show him!\"","Zong Jincheng's competitive spirit was ignited. Ignoring Zong Wenxiu's calls from behind, he ran out of the academy.","Zong Wenxiu chased after him and asked, \"Brother, where are you going?\"","Zong Jincheng kept running faster and faster, his head down.","It was as if a sudden surge of strength had entered his body, making him more agile and powerful than before.","In the vast academy, only the sound of his running and the words carried by the wind could be heard:","\"Home, to study!\"","Zong Jincheng's effort came more fiercely than Xu Wan had expected.","She thought the boy would continue to cram by rote, forcing all the knowledge into his head using his extraordinary eidetic memory.","But instead, as soon as he got home, he had Shunzi gather all the books Qin Ye had mentioned in his answers.","\"Historical Chronicles, Geography Records,\" Shunzi reported the book titles as Zong Jincheng recited the sentences, growing more and more astonished, \"Young Master, did Qin Ye really answer with these books? Even Master Zong hasn't studied these at this age.\"","Zong Jincheng gritted his teeth and said fiercely, \"Yes, that's what he answered with!\"","Shunzi's knowledge was excellent; otherwise, he wouldn't have been specially assigned to Zong Jincheng by his grandmother. But even Shunzi found Qin Ye impressive, which only made Zong Jincheng even more furious.","\"This annoying little brat, I'll beat him down soon!\"","Zong Jincheng grabbed the books from Shunzi's hands and no longer had the patience to listen to him read them out loud for him to memorize.","Reading and memorizing on his own was faster!","However, Zong Jincheng had started learning late and had limited literacy skills. He often encountered unfamiliar characters while reading and had to ask Shunzi about their pronunciations.","When Xu Wan came to visit him three days later, she heard the young master's frustrated howl before even entering the room: \"What does this word even mean?!\"","Xu Wan couldn't help but laugh.","This boy was finally tasting the bitterness of swallowing things whole.","With a shaky foundation and always looking for shortcuts, his later studies would only get more difficult.","She stepped into the room and addressed the frantic Shunzi, \"What books is Jincheng going to study next? You should annotate them with phonetic marks so he can recognize the pronunciations when he reads them himself.\"","\"Phonetic marks?\" Shunzi asked.","Xu Wan nodded and said, \"Many characters have the same pronunciation. Jincheng knows some simple ones, but for the complex ones, you can annotate them with homophones.\"","She had learned to read using pinyin, but since pinyin didn't exist here, Xu Wan didn't want to appear unusual, so she decided to try using the direct phonetic method as a substitute.","Shunzi was clever and caught on immediately.","He exclaimed excitedly, \"Madam is truly amazing! I'll get right on it!\"","Zong Jincheng listened in a daze, and it took him a few seconds to grasp the concept of phonetic annotations. His gaze at Xu Wan became even more curious.","How did this woman come up with this?","Could she really be that smart?","Xu Wan saw the suspicious look in his eyes and didn't need to ask to know what was going through his head. But unlike Zong Jincheng, she wasn't easily inflated with pride and simply moved past the topic.","With the help of phonetic annotations, Zong Jincheng's studies became much more convenient.","When Baili Xi came to teach at Marquis Manor, he was astonished by the dramatic change in the young master and couldn't help but give Xu Wan a thumbs up.","\"A complete transformation, a complete transformation!\" he praised her repeatedly.","Xu Wan watched Zong Jincheng diligently writing in the study and asked Baili Xi, \"Master, how long do you think it will take for Jincheng to catch up with Qin Ye's progress?\"","Her question was quite clever.","Instead of asking if he could catch up, she asked when he could, showing her confidence in Zong Jincheng's learning ability.","Baili Xi glanced at her and smiled, \"That depends on how long this drive of his can last.\"","Xu Wan also smiled, \"Master has foresight. He's holding on to this breath of determination, and he won't stop until he surpasses Qin Ye.\"","But Baili Xi shook his head and warned, \"Not necessarily, not necessarily.\"","\"Hmm?\" Xu Wan looked puzzled.","Baili Xi pointed at Zong Jincheng and said, \"A child who has been lazy all along can't sustain this drive for too long. His laziness will gradually take over, and then Madam will have to worry again.\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","It made perfect sense, but the truth was really hard to hear...","No wonder people don't like to listen to honest advice!","In the following days, Zong Jincheng continued to study at Marquis Manor, this time willingly, and no one could get him to go out.","Even the monthly reward of fifty taels of silver that Xu Wan had promised him was completely forgotten.","This period of hard work lasted a full month.","The monthly exam at Qingbo Academy had arrived.","With Baili Xi as their teacher, Zong Jincheng and Zong Wenxiu didn't need to attend Qingbo Academy, but Xu Wan had continued to pay their tuition to keep their spots and allow them to participate in the academy's various exams to constantly assess their progress.","Zong Jincheng had studied diligently for a month. Not only had he memorized and understood hundreds of books, but he also frequently consulted Baili Xi on how to cite classical works and integrate the ideas of multiple books.","Baili Xi's sense of accomplishment soared. Every day when he came to teach at Marquis Manor, he no longer had the previous gloomy expression and even looked forward to arriving early.","Zong Wenxiu, inspired by his brother's dedication, also started getting up an hour earlier to study, making rapid progress in his learning.","Today, the students of Qingbo Academy were more numerous than usual.","When Zong Jincheng and Zong Wenxiu arrived, they immediately felt the crowd, and they were quite puzzled about what was happening.","After asking other students, they learned, \"Didn't you receive the notice? This month's exam is a joint exam with the top three academies in the capital!\"","Zong Jincheng never feared such challenges: \"So what? We just have to beat them!\"","The student, seeing his confidence, couldn't help but twitch his mouth, \"But our academy always ranks last in the joint exams, never even surpassing the second to last.\"","Zong Jincheng: \"...\"","Was the academy Xu Wan chose for him so bad?","Did she look down on him?!","Just as Zong Jincheng was about to get angry, Zong Wenxiu quickly asked, \"Is the joint exam a tradition? Since we always lose, why do we still compete with them instead of choosing a slightly weaker academy?\"","\"Because our principal loves a challenge,\" the student explained.","Zong Wenxiu: \"Ah?\"","\"Students at Qingbo Academy have been suffering setbacks since enrollment and have long given up struggling!\"","\"But this year might be different. I heard there's a student named Qin Ye who's exceptionally talented. The principal has already made a big promise to rely on Qin Ye to turn the tide for us!\""]},{"number":47,"title":"Chapter 47: The Lost Jade Pendant","paragraphs":["“Is it the eight-year-old Qin Ye? I’ve also heard that he recently approached the headmaster to request a transfer to a more advanced class after this exam.”","“He’s really strong, probably aiming to take the child prodigy exam in a couple of years.”","“With him around, we’re sure to have someone make the cut this year!”","Zong Jincheng listened to them chattering away, their conversation constantly revolving around Qin Ye. In the eyes of the students at Qingbo Academy, Qin Ye was practically a savior.","This made Zong Jincheng extremely jealous.","He raised his fist and declared, “This time, I’ll show you all how I’ll beat that Qin Ye kid!”","“You?” The group looked at him, clearly skeptical.","“Never seen him.”","“Don’t know him.”","“Is he bragging?”","“First, you need to make the cut before you can even think about beating Qin Ye. Big talker, do you think you’re Qin Ye or something?”","Zong Jincheng: “!! I’m going to fight you all!!”","Zong Wenxiu was terrified, fearing his brother might get into a fight before the exam. He quickly pulled the little troublemaker aside and explained, “Don’t underestimate him. My brother is also very talented. Last month’s exam, he came in second, right after Qin Ye.”","Zong Jincheng hated being second, but mentioning this rank could prove his abilities, so he gritted his teeth and huffed in agreement.","The group was momentarily stunned, then retorted, “So what? There are thousands of students from the four academies taking this joint exam, and only 120 make the cut. In previous years, the other three academies always dominated, and Qingbo Academy never even had one on the list. Qin Ye might have a shot this year, but you? Forget it.”","Furious, Zong Jincheng shouted at Zong Wenxiu, “Don’t hold me back! Today, I’ll show them just how strong the top student of the joint exam can be!”","Zong Wenxiu: “......”","His brother’s boasts were getting bigger and bigger.","No... his confidence was just growing stronger and stronger.","“Hmph, another crazy one.”","“Let’s go, arguing with a fool is pointless.”","Zong Jincheng yelled at their retreating backs, “Damn it, you bunch of snobs! Open your eyes wide and watch this, this year I, Zong Jincheng, will definitely claim the top spot!”","The bustling academy was too noisy for anyone to take his words seriously, though a few passersby chuckled.","Zong Jincheng: (#-.-).","Seeing his brother’s dejected expression, Zong Wenxiu couldn’t help but want to laugh, but he managed to hold it in.","He gently reassured him, “It’s okay, brother. I believe in you. This month’s exam, you’ll definitely do great!”","At the very least, it would be better than last time.","After all, Zong Jincheng had been studying with incredible vigor this month. With his intelligence, his progress had been advancing at an astonishing speed.","Zong Jincheng huffed, “Let’s go, into the exam room. I’ll show them all!”","“Yeah!”","The joint exam of the four academies mimics the timing of the child prodigy exam. The test content is less in volume than Qingbo Academy’s monthly exams but significantly more difficult, focusing not just on memorization and translation, but on comprehension and application.","It’s practically a mini imperial examination.","Fortunately, Zong Jincheng had been practicing this type of test all month, so he answered smoothly and left the exam room brimming with confidence.","The other students at the academy were a different story, emerging one by one, looking defeated.","“I’m done for. I probably won’t make the cut this year. The questions were too hard.”","“It’s unbelievable how the other three academies always perform so well.”","“If this keeps up, I don’t even dare to take the child prodigy exam. I’ll just end up crushing my self-esteem.”","“Ah, back to burning the midnight oil, I guess.”","While others were miserable, Zong Jincheng was the most confident. The feeling of being the only one who could do it was simply exhilarating, and a strong sense of accomplishment surged within him.","As for that so-called genius, Qin Ye, he could just step aside. This year, the top spot was Zong Jincheng’s!","The Marquis’s carriage was waiting outside Qingbo Academy. As the brothers Zong Jincheng and Zong Wenxiu prepared to board, Zong Wenxiu suddenly exclaimed, “My jade pendant is missing!”","“Ah? Where did you lose it?” Zong Jincheng turned to Shunzi and ordered, “Quick, take people and help him look for it.”","“Yes.” Shunzi led the servants and maids to search.","Zong Wenxiu was frantic, returning to the academy to look for it himself, scanning the ground everywhere, terrified it might have been stepped on and broken.","Zong Jincheng, who usually didn’t care much about such ornaments—after all, he had once traded a thousand-tael jade pendant for a meal—couldn’t help but join the search when he saw Zong Wenxiu so distressed.","“What kind of jade pendant is it? Is it very valuable? There were so many outsiders at the academy today, it’s probably lost for good. Just ask Xu Wan to buy you a new one when you get back.”","After all, that woman was stingy with him but generous with others, especially Zong Wenxiu.","He had seen it several times—Xu Wan often had people bring things to Zong Wenxiu’s courtyard.","Zong Wenxiu grew more and more anxious, his eyes turning red. His voice trembled as he said, “It’s the jade pendant my father gave to my mother. It was through this pendant that my grandmother discovered our existence. My mother gave it to me, and it’s my fault for not keeping it safe...”","Zong Wenxiu was filled with regret. How could he have worn such an important pendant? If he could find it, he would keep it safe and never lose it again!","But regret was useless. Finding a lost item was as difficult as reaching for the sky.","Zong Wenxiu mustered his courage and shouted loudly, “Has anyone seen my jade pendant? It’s very important to me. If someone has found it, could you please return it to me? The reward is one tael of silver.”","According to the laws of the Great Chu Dynasty, when returning a lost item, the owner must offer a reward equal to a quarter of the item’s value as a thank-you gift.","One tael of silver was a quarter of the pendant’s value.","Many people were passing through the academy, and while they were briefly tempted by the offer, a quick glance around revealed no sign of the pendant, so they gave up.","A tael of silver was a considerable sum for children of their age, but the tuition at Qingbo Academy was relatively high, and students who could afford to study there weren’t short of money. They wouldn’t care about a single tael.","No one helped Zong Wenxiu look for it.","Even as he continued to shout, no one offered to help.","Shunzi and the others were limited in their efforts, and the search would take a lot of time.","Zong Wenxiu collapsed to the ground, tears welling in his eyes.","“Mother, I’m sorry. It’s all my fault. It’s all my fault...”","Seeing him like this, Zong Jincheng felt bad too. He instructed Shunzi, “Go and announce that the reward is now five hundred taels.”","Shunzi: “!!!!!!”","“Young master, that jade pendant is only worth four taels. Are you sure you want to spend five hundred taels to help Sir Wenxiu find it??”","That's the price of a purebred Akhal-Teke horse!","Zong Jincheng snapped, “Yes! Can’t you see he’s about to cry?”","Shunzi hesitated, “But you only have fifty taels in your private funds...”","That was what he had just received this month.","Zong Jincheng was silent for a few seconds, then looked at Zong Wenxiu and said, “Charge it to him. Ask Xu Wan for the money!”","Shunzi: “............”","Hopefully, Madam Xu will accept such a ridiculous logic."]},{"number":48,"title":"Chapter 48: Jincheng Offers a Bounty of Five Hundred Taels","paragraphs":["With the promise of five hundred taels of silver from Zong Jincheng, the students at Qingbo Academy went absolutely wild!","Students who were originally eager to go home decided to stay, and even called their servants to join them in the search within the academy.","Qingbo Academy was in an uproar.","Not only did the students go crazy, but even the teaching scholars were swept up in the frenzy. The entire academy was mobilized to help find the missing jade pendant.","\"Quick, quick! Go to the examination hall where Zong Wenxiu spent the most time. He must have lost it there!\"","\"Alright, alright, we're going... but sir, there are too many people searching that hall. We can't get through!\"","\"You have to get through! That's five hundred taels of silver we're talking about!!\"","\"Oh, and don't forget to check the latrines. He must have been there today!\"","\"And the path to the examination hall!\"","\"We should also search the road from the academy to his home!\"","\"And the area around his carriage!\"","\"Can we even check inside his carriage?\"","\"...\"","Qin Ye, after finishing his exam, was summoned by the academy's headmaster for a conversation about his performance in the recent four-academy joint exam.","He disliked any interruptions to his studies, including those from the headmaster, so he simply muttered an acknowledgment and quickly steered the conversation elsewhere, bringing up the matter of changing shifts. Only after getting the headmaster's approval did he feel that his time had not been wasted.","However, as soon as he stepped out of the headmaster's office, he was nearly knocked over by the chaotic crowd of students. Qin Ye's already cold expression turned even more frigid. \"What is going on here?\"","His servant, struggling to clear a path for him, explained, \"Sir, it's because Zong Wenxiu from Marquis Manor lost his jade pendant. His brother, Zong Jincheng, offered a reward of five hundred taels to anyone who finds it.\"","Qin Ye: \"...\" What a ridiculous and absurd move.","He continued walking forward, his face still dark, clearly harboring even worse impressions of those two names.","Another three pages of his book wasted thanks to these interruptions.","Zong Jincheng, busy searching for the pendant, didn't run into Qin Ye. If he had, there would have been no shortage of sarcastic remarks.","As for Qin Ye, he still hadn't made the connection between Zong Jincheng and the name.","\"I found it! I found it!!!\"","\"The five hundred taels is mine! Hahaha! It's mine!!\"","\"Hey! What are you doing! Don't take my pendant! This is robbery! Outright robbery!!\"","Hearing this commotion, Zong Wenxiu rushed over, but the crowd was too dense to push through.","The person who found the pendant was waving it high above his head, the jade dancing in the air, at risk of being crushed if it fell.","Zong Wenxiu anxiously called out, \"Be careful! Be careful!\"","Zong Jincheng strode forward and ordered, \"Buyan, retrieve the pendant!\"","Buyan, with his exceptional martial arts and superb lightness skills, leaped into the air, performed a somersault, and snatched the pendant from the chaos. Those who had been trying to grab it, seeing his formidable skills, immediately backed off.","The grand search for the pendant finally came to an end, and the crowd, disappointed, began to disperse.","Only the boy who had found the pendant remained, both elated and anxious as he approached. \"I found it! You took it from my hands!\"","He was thrilled at the prospect of receiving five hundred taels but was also nervous, fearing they might renege on the reward. His nerves were on edge.","Buyan handed the pendant to Zong Jincheng, who casually examined it. It was ordinary, nothing special. He passed it to Zong Wenxiu, who, like a precious treasure, first wiped it clean before carefully inspecting it.","Zong Wenxiu's eyes welled with tears of joy. \"It's mine! It's my jade pendant!\"","The boy, relieved, cautiously asked, \"Then, about the reward...\"","Zong Wenxiu's body stiffened at the mention of the reward. The pendant had been found only because his brother had offered five hundred taels, prompting everyone to search so diligently.","But five hundred taels... he didn't have that kind of money.","He had only managed to save a little over a hundred taels so far...","Zong Jincheng patted Zong Wenxiu on the shoulder. \"Don't worry, we have money at home. Take him back to the manor and have Xu Wan handle it.\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","Would Madam Xu really pay?","That was five hundred taels...","Madam Xu had always been strict with Zong Jincheng's spending, and she herself rarely made large expenditures. Five hundred taels was no small sum for her.","When Xu Wan heard that she was expected to pay, she nearly laughed in anger.","But with an outsider present, she had to maintain her composure. She instructed Steward Liu to take the boy who found the pendant to the front hall to rest.","In the side hall, Xu Wan launched into a scolding tirade. \"Well, well, Zong Jincheng, our esteemed young master, sure knows how to throw money around! Spending five hundred taels to find a jade pendant worth just four taels! People would think you're some prince incognito!\"","Zong Jincheng retorted, \"Princes don't have money. Only the richest people do.\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","Ugh, this little brat is too good at picking apart her words!","She snapped, \"Even if we were the richest, that's your grandmother's family's money, not ours!\"","Zong Jincheng argued confidently, \"Grandmother is an only child. All that money is ours. I'm the eldest grandson of the Zong family. It's all meant for me to spend.\"","Xu Wan clutched her head in agony. This profligate behavior...","How was it that after three months of teaching, he was still like this?","She began to deeply reflect on her methods.","Zong Wenxiu timidly spoke up, \"I'm sorry, Madam Xu. This was all my fault. I will pay the five hundred taels.\" He then remembered he didn't have that much and added, \"You can deduct it from my monthly allowance.\"","His monthly allowance was twenty taels, so deducting four hundred taels would take over a year and a half.","Xu Wan said, \"This incident isn't your fault. The legal minimum reward for finding lost items is one tael, which wasn't enough to motivate the crowd. But... you shouldn't have raised it to five hundred taels! Zong Jincheng, do you think money grows on trees?\"","Zong Jincheng plugged his ears to block out her shouting. With his eyes closed, he said, \"Well, you have to pay anyway. The boy is waiting outside. You wouldn't want Marquis Manor to lose face, would you?\"","\"You caused this mess. Why should I clean it up?\"","\"Because you're my mother right now!\" Zong Jincheng shouted back.","Both of them froze.","Even Zong Wenxiu was a bit stunned.","It seemed this was the first time he had heard his brother utter that word.","Zong Jincheng was the first to recover. He quickly explained, \"No, I mean, who else would take care of it since you're the one acting as my... well, you have to handle it.\"","The little tyrant was uncharacteristically awkward, his tone revealing a hint of dependence, even a touch of coquettishness and submission.","Xu Wan's heart softened.","The boy, with that innocent, harmless face, was once again working his charm."]},{"number":49,"title":"Chapter 49: The Crown Prince's Favorite","paragraphs":["Xu Wan closed her eyes and sat back down in her seat.","She silently recited the Heart-Clearing Mantra over and over, while mentally reinforcing to herself:","Don't be seduced by the little demon king, this can't start, otherwise he'll be coming up with ways every day to break the rules she's set.","But he called me \"mother\" ah, my maternal love is about to overflow...","Hold it in, hold it in...","A doting mother spoils the child, without rules, there's no order...","Xu Wan took a series of deep breaths, trying her best to keep her mind calm.","Soon, the ruthless stepmother was back in action.","\"I don't care.\"","Zong Jincheng: \"!!!\"","This woman!","This hateful woman!","She has no heart at all!!!","Xu Wan cleared her throat and continued, \"However, since the finder of the lost item is already waiting outside, it wouldn't be right to go back on our word, but the accounting office won't approve...\"","Cui Zhi: \"...\"","Madam is about to set a trap for the young master again.","What's with the \"can't approve\"? Now that the Hou Mansion is under her control, a mere five hundred taels of silver expenditure, even if she has no reason for it, the accounting office wouldn't dare to question her.","The little demon king didn't catch onto the loophole in her words and continued listening to her: \"Well, seeing as you're my son, I can advance this sum for you, and then deduct it from your monthly allowance. Your allowance is high, it'll be paid back in ten months.\"","The little demon king instinctively retorted, \"Who's your son!\"","Xu Wan \"oh\"ed and replied with his own words, \"Nominally.\"","Zong Jincheng: \"...\"","He pouted and glared at her, then continued thinking about her proposal. It was feasible; after all, ten months was much faster than Zong Wenxiu's nearly two years.","Zong Wenxiu also chimed in, \"I have a hundred taels here, I can return it to Madam first.\"","The boy's intention was to help the little demon king.","It was well-meaning, but it was actually causing more trouble.","Xu Wan ruthlessly rejected, \"No.\"","\"Why not??\" Zong Jincheng immediately protested.","With Zong Wenxiu's hundred taels, he could pay back the debt two months earlier!","Xu Wan leisurely said, \"The trouble was caused by you, why should Wenxiu share the responsibility with you?\"","\"But I did it to help him find his jade pendant!\"","\"Hmm, strictly speaking, it was indeed to help Wenxiu find his jade pendant,\" Xu Wan suddenly agreed with the little demon king's statement.","Zong Jincheng was about to continue his argument when it got stuck in his throat. But knowing Xu Wan, how could she so easily change her mind just because he said so?","There must be a catch!","Sure enough, in the little demon king's suspicious gaze, Xu Wan said, \"The reward for finding the jade pendant is one tael, Wenxiu's money should indeed be paid by you.\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","It was indeed his responsibility.","But one tael? Wouldn't that infuriate his brother?","Sure enough, looking over, Zong Jincheng's face turned red instantly.","He knew damn well there wasn't going to be an easy way out!","The little demon king was furious, he raged, \"What's the difference between four hundred ninety-nine taels and five hundred taels!!!\"","Xu Wan corrected, \"How is there no difference? Don't you remember how much a pound of grain costs on the street? Five coins, one tael can buy...\"","Hearing her start calculating again, the little demon king instinctively covered his ears, not wanting to hear another word from her: \"Fine, fine, I'll pay, I'll pay, alright!!!\"","Xu Wan nodded in satisfaction, \"Good. At least you have some sense of responsibility.\"","The little demon king shot her a glare.","Cui Zhi shook her head helplessly, returning to Xu Wan's bedroom to fetch the five hundred taels to advance for the young master. Steward Liu handed it over to the finder, who left ecstatic.","In the private courtyard, Zong Jincheng was counting on his fingers, \"Saved fifty taels, Zong Wenxiu paid one tael, still short four hundred forty-nine taels, another nine months to go...\"","He suddenly howled to the sky, \"Why do I still have to study for so long!\"","The birds in the yard were startled by the noise and flapped around, eventually crashing into a cage and fainting from the impact.","The cat that Zong Jincheng often used to scare the birds was lazily lying under the eaves, occasionally meowing.","Baili Xi was right, a momentary whim couldn't last long. Zong Jincheng, aiming to surpass Qin Ye, had diligently studied for a whole month, confident he could win after the monthly exam, but now he was back to slacking off.","\"The four academy joint exam results take seven days to come out, how inefficient! With this, how dare the other three academies claim to be better than Qingbo Academy?\"","Zong Jincheng didn't understand how the academies were ranked, but judging from the time it took to release the results, the other three academies weren't much to boast about.","Thinking of this, he became even more confident. What Qingbo Academy's top student, he was going to be the first in the four academy joint exam!","\"Young Master, we should go to the study room to read,\" Shunzi came to call Zong Jincheng early in the morning.","Normally, the young master would have already gotten up by this time, studying intensely.","But without a goal, the little demon king had reverted to his uninterested attitude towards studying: \"Ah, stop nagging, let me sleep a little more, I haven't slept well for a whole month!\"","Shunzi was on the verge of tears, reminding, \"But we still have to go to the study room to learn, you haven't forgotten the remaining four hundred forty-nine taels, have you...\"","The little demon king rolled over and pulled the blanket over his head.","Clearly showing the attitude of 'I don't care about anything, I'm going to sleep till I die'.","Shunzi was helpless.","Fortunately, Xu Wan didn't send anyone to urge him, so he could only be a good servant who didn't annoy the master.","Around midday, a sudden message came from outside, saying that the eighteenth princess had arrived. Shunzi was stunned.","The princess visiting the Marquis's Mansion must be a big deal!","He hurriedly woke the sleeping young master.","Zong Jincheng rubbed his eyes and said, \"What eighteenth princess, I don't know her. Besides, she didn't specifically ask to see me, maybe she's here to pick a fight with Xu Wan.\"","Shunzi said, \"The eighteenth princess is fourteen this year, the Emperor's most beloved daughter, the Crown Prince's most beloved sister. She's willful; if she really is here to pick a fight with Madam, our marquisate is definitely going to be in trouble!\"","Zong Jincheng, though a troublemaker, immediately woke up with a start when he heard the family might be in trouble.","He didn't like Xu Wan, but she represented the Marquis's Mansion, and if something happened to her while the grandmother wasn't around... that would be bad!","“Why is the eighteenth princess coming to our residence?” Zong Jincheng asked while putting on his clothes, hastily slipping on his shoes.","Shunzi thought for a moment and said, \"After all, the eighteenth princess's brother is the Crown Prince, and the Crown Prince likes you, so it shouldn't be... no, the eighteenth princess's mother is Madam Zhai's sister, Madam Zhai is the eighteenth princess's aunt!\"","\"It's about Zhai Yao's matter!\" Zong Jincheng understood.","Zhai Yao had been punished by the Crown Prince to live in the slums, and had been there for a month. Madam Zhai's attempts to appeal to the Crown Prince and Princess Pingyang had failed, so this time she turned to the willful eighteenth princess.","It seemed she was determined to have the princess cause a ruckus.","\"Quick, if she really starts causing trouble, we'll go to the Eastern Palace to find the Crown Prince!\"","\"But the Crown Prince is not in good health, and those who have requested an audience with the Crown Prince regarding Zhai Yao's matter have all been refused by the Crown Princess.\"","\"How can that be the same? The Crown Prince likes me the most, and doesn't like the Zhai family!\"","Shunzi: \"...\"","Although you're always overconfident, what you say does make some sense."]},{"number":50,"title":"Chapter 50: The Disobedient Stepson","paragraphs":["However, by the time Zong Jincheng rushed to the front hall, half-dressed and in a fluster, he found a charming young lady laughing heartily with Xu Wan.","Zong Jincheng: \"...\"","He felt like a fool for worrying about her.","Gritting his teeth, he turned to Shunzi and said, \"Didn't you say that Princess Zhao Rong was here to pick a fight over Zhai Yao? What are they laughing about??\"","Shunzi stammered, unable to come up with an answer: \"Y-yes, it's Princess Zhao Rong...\"","But... how did things turn out like this?","The world had gone mad in ways they couldn't have imagined!","Princess Zhao Rong had indeed come initially to confront Xu Wan about Zhai Yao. Zhai's mother had told her about Zhai Yao's dire situation, the Crown Prince's bias, and the arrogance of the Marquis's Mansion. Believing her, Zhao Rong had come with her head held high, demanding that Xu Wan plead with the Crown Prince to release Zhai Yao.","However, she had run into Xu Wan, who was a master at reading people. Xu Wan quickly realized that Zhao Rong was being used as a pawn and calmly explained the entire situation with Zhai Yao. By the end of the story, Zhao Rong was so impressed that she slammed the table and praised the Crown Prince for his just punishment!","Zhao Rong, who had spent most of her life in the palace, had only ever encountered people who either fawned over her, feared her reputation, or openly opposed her.","She had never met someone like Xu Wan, who neither got angry nor intimidated by her commanding tone, but instead spoke softly and eloquently, making her completely convinced and feeling like she had found a kindred spirit.","The two then moved from discussing the Zhai family to the Crown Prince, from the Marquis's residence to the palace, and the more they talked, the more they hit it off—","They ended up becoming sisters.","\"Oh? Is this your unruly stepson?\" Zhao Rong said bluntly, looking at the boy at the door, \"He doesn't seem very presentable, not even properly dressed.\"","Zong Jincheng: \"...\"","He hated women who talked bad about others without any restraint!","Zhao Rong continued, \"Oh, he's glaring at me. He really is a little devil. Maybe that's why the Crown Prince likes him so much? No wonder he favors me the most.\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","How did the mockery turn into self-deprecation?","Was this the trait of someone who couldn't keep their thoughts to themselves?","Zong Jincheng, who was already annoyed with her, felt a bit less angry upon hearing this. At least she had some self-awareness!","The little devil had rushed over in a hurry, and now that he saw everything was fine, he stopped to tidy himself up, while the conversation between the two women continued.","Zhao Rong said, \"But I can't come all this way for nothing. My aunt keeps crying in my palace, saying that Zhai Yao has been frequently feverish and hasn't recovered from his cold. I'm worried something might happen to him in the slums.\"","Xu Wan replied, \"I understand. I'll go to the Eastern Palace later to beg the Crown Prince to end Zhai Yao's punishment.\"","Zong Jincheng immediately objected: \"The Crown Prince sentenced him to stay in the slums. Why should he be let out? Don't you remember how he kicked Grandpa Zhao?\"","Xu Wan hadn't forgotten.","However, \"Zhai Yao made a mistake, but it doesn't warrant a death sentence.\"","The Crown Prince's intention was to discipline the child, not to kill a nine-year-old. He probably didn't realize how difficult it would be for Zhai Yao to survive in the slums.","If Zhai Yao were to die, it would likely cause trouble for the Crown Prince.","\"Is it really that serious?\" Zong Jincheng frowned, \"Jing Zhe suffered much worse injuries than him, and he didn't end up like Zhai Yao, half-dead.\"","\"Jing Zhe and Zhai Yao grew up in different environments. Jing Zhe's adaptability is much stronger than Zhai Yao's. The Crown Prince has strictly controlled the slums, so Zhai Yao has even fewer medicinal resources than what we provided for Jing Zhe. If this continues, he might really be in danger.\" Xu Wan asked him, \"If Zhai Yao dies, do you think it's a trivial matter?\"","An eight or nine-year-old child already understands the concept of death. A living person disappearing forever, leaving their loved ones in agony.","Zong Jincheng thought about it and realized that if Zhai Yao really died, it would be too serious.","But he couldn't bring himself to admit it, so he retorted, \"So we just let him out like that? Who knows if he's changed? If he's still the same, I don't want him causing trouble again...\"","Xu Wan said, \"Then we'll leave it to the Crown Prince to decide his fate. We just need to do our part, and the rest is up to fate.\"","Zong Jincheng grunted, \"Fine, you go. I'm not going.\"","\"I didn't ask you to,\" Xu Wan shot him a look.","Zong Jincheng stuck his tongue out at her and ran off.","Zhao Rong, watching their exchange, was intrigued. \"Is this how you usually discipline him? It looks so tiring, having to explain so many big truths.\"","Xu Wan smiled, \"Children's understanding is still shallow. If you explain things well, they can understand.\"","Zhao Rong blushed, \"Actually, I know you're only doing this because of me. No matter what, I'll remember this favor. If you ever need anything, just send someone to me. It's much easier to get into my palace than the Crown Prince's Eastern Palace.\"","\"Hahaha...\" Xu Wan laughed along with her, \"Since the princess is here, I'll show you around the Marquis's Mansion.\"","\"Sure, let me see the study room where your two children read. I heard your study is huge.\"","\"It was built by my mother-in-law for my husband. He's always loved reading since he was young.\"","\"Then Zong Jincheng is really unlike him.\"","\"Maybe he takes after his grandfather. I heard my father-in-law didn't like reading either.\"","\"Hahaha... That makes sense.\"","After seeing off Zhao Rong, Xu Wan tidied herself up and headed to the Eastern Palace to request an audience with the Crown Princess.","The Crown Prince's health was fragile, so she didn't dare to disturb him. Moreover, as a woman, it was more appropriate for her to seek an audience with the Crown Princess.","Sure enough, as soon as the Crown Princess heard of her request, she immediately summoned her.","I am Xu Wan, daughter-in-law of the Hou family, greeting the Crown Princess. May Your Highness be in good health.","“Rise,” the Crown Princess said with a smile, “Come, here is a seat for the Marquis’s wife.”","\"Thank you, Your Highness.\"","After sitting down, Xu Wan recounted the entire incident of Zhao Rong coming to the Marquis's Residence to plead for Zhai Yao, and concluded with her own request, hoping the Crown Prince would release Zhai Yao.","The Crown Princess looked at her thoughtfully and said with a smile, \"You're quite clever, knowing to come to me. Previously, anyone who came to plead for Zhai Yao was turned away by the Crown Prince.\"","Xu Wan looked up, surprised.","It turned out that it wasn't just a rumor, but the Crown Prince himself who had refused them?"]},{"number":51,"title":"Chapter 51: The Little Scoundrel Who Loves to Jump the Wall","paragraphs":["Xu Wan silently sighed: This Crown Princess truly has a great capacity for tolerance, silently bearing a heap of criticism for the Crown Prince, and seemingly enjoying it.","The Crown Princess descended and spoke softly: \"The Crown Prince has little understanding of the slums and didn't anticipate that Zhai Yao would struggle to survive there. I will discuss the situation with him later, and I believe with his soft-hearted nature, he will agree to bring Zhai Yao back.\"","Xu Wan quickly stood up and said: \"Thank you very much, Your Highness Crown Princess.\"","The Crown Princess stepped forward, amicably holding her hand, and whispered: \"I hear that you've been working with Baili Xi to rapidly improve Jin Cheng's studies. It must have been quite taxing.\"","Xu Wan thought, of course it's tiring, dealing with a mischievous boy like Jin Cheng is more exhausting than managing ten scholarly disciples.","But she still humbly replied: \"It's what I should do.\"","\"You always say that, but the actual effort is evident to everyone.\" The Crown Princess's tone shifted suddenly, asking: \"By the way, when is Jin Cheng's birthday?\"","Xu Wan truthfully answered: \"June 16th.\"","\"Oh... so he was conceived at the end of August...\" The Crown Princess murmured.","Xu Wan calculated and said: \"Yes, that's the time.\"","The Crown Princess then asked her: \"Do you know who Jin Cheng's biological mother is?\"","Xu Wan's heart skipped a beat; she finally understood.","That day, the Crown Prince showed an unusual fondness for Jin Cheng and mentioned holding him as a newborn, which was easily misinterpreted. The Crown Princess had indeed started to wonder.","The Crown Princess married into the Eastern Palace five years ago, and three years before that, there were no women serving in the Crown Prince's residence. But... who knows if there was someone else?","The Crown Princess had been pondering this for some time, unable to recall any noblewoman in the capital who disappeared for a year eight years ago to give birth. So, she decided to ask Xu Wan.","A mother would never bear to be apart from her child, but if she had secretly visited Jin Cheng, Xu Wan, as the head of the household, would have noticed.","Xu Wan lowered her head and said: \"I know nothing about Jin Cheng's birth mother. I only know that my husband brought him to Marquis Manor eight years ago and had his father register him as the first legitimate grandson. For more details, you might need to ask his father.\"","When it came to the Crown Prince, Xu Wan dared not even think in that direction.","Knowing Jin Cheng was from Marquis Manor, she could manage without pressure; if he were a royal child, even with eight hundred times the courage, she wouldn't dare discipline such a mischievous child!","The Crown Princess was silent for a few seconds, eventually deciding not to pursue the matter further.","Xu Wan stood for a long time without hearing her speak, so she politely took her leave: \"Your Highness, I have matters at home, so I won't stay and disturb you.\"","The Crown Princess smiled: \"Go ahead. At the end of the month, the Crown Prince will hold a hunting event at Autumn Sun Mountain. You can bring Jin Cheng and the others to join in the fun.\"","\"Yes, thank you, Your Highness.\"","Xu Wan finished her thanks and left the Eastern Palace, only to run into the Duchess of Jin just as she stepped out.","The noblewoman she had offended at the last banquet.","If not for the Crown Prince and Crown Princess's intervention, the Duchess of Jin would not have apologized to them.","Seeing Xu Wan, the Duchess of Jin's eyes practically grew on top of her head as she sneered: \"Back at the Eastern Palace to fawn over the Crown Princess again?\"","Xu Wan stopped and, looking at the direction the Duchess of Jin was heading, retorted: \"Aren't you, Your Grace?\"","The Duchess of Jin, hit where it hurt, was so angry she wanted to lunge forward, but her maid managed to restrain her.","Finally, she said: \"A neglected daughter of a noble family, married into a merchant-focused Marquis Manor, gaining nothing from either side. I wonder how you have the confidence to challenge me!\"","Xu Wan smiled: \"I wouldn't dare. As long as Your Grace doesn't trouble us, we certainly don't wish to offend Duke Jin's Manor.\"","The Duchess of Jin snorted: \"Smooth talker. You and your simple-minded sister are worlds apart!\"","Simple-minded sister...","Xu Wan remembered. Xu Lian'er's marriage had been arranged with Duke Jin's Manor, and the wedding would take place next month.","But the word \"simple-minded\" associated with Xu Lian'er? The Duchess of Jin had clearly been deceived too easily.","Knowing the background, Xu Wan now looked at the Duchess of Jin with a sense of pity. Hopefully, this fiery mother-in-law could withstand Xu Lian'er's gentle tactics in the future.","Returning to Marquis Manor.","Xu Wan asked: \"Is Jin Cheng in the study?\"","Though it seemed unlikely, what if?","What if he just refused to sleep, refused to play with birds and cats, and absolutely wanted to immerse himself in the sea of knowledge...","Cui Liu, with a wooden expression, matter-of-factly said: \"Young Master has gone out to play.\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","Alright, he absolutely refused to study.","This damn rascal.","Xu Wan asked again: \"Where did he go to play? Did he go to find Jing Zhe again?\"","Recently, Jin Cheng had been frequently visiting the slums, which had caused quite a stir there. Fortunately, his presence had deterred anyone from bullying Jing Zhe's family.","Cui Liu's face grew even more wooden, saying: \"He went to Minister of War's Mansion, to He Zheng's place.\"","\"He Zheng? Sounds familiar.\" Xu Wan had some impression but couldn't recall who it was.","Seemed like a friend of the little rascal.","But the little rascal's previous friends were all...","\"One of the Four Young Scoundrels,\" Cui Zhi reminded.","Xu Wan: \"...\"","Alright, her worries were finally laid to rest.","Xu Wan wearily lay on the chaise lounge, closing her eyes: \"Come, tell me how this He Zheng is also a scoundrel.\"","After meeting the little rascal and Zhai Yao, she had no good impressions of the Four Young Scoundrels. Any one of them was a headache for life.","Fortunately, they were raised by four influential families. If they were all in one household, it would truly be a case of crying to heaven and earth for help.","Cui Liu brought over a booklet and handed it to Cui Zhi to read:","\"He Zheng, nine years old, third son of the Minister of War, legitimate birth. Once broke his arm climbing the wall of the Minister of War's Mansion, broke his arm again climbing the wall of the academy, broke his arm a third time climbing the wall of the training ground, broke his arm a fourth time climbing...\"","\"Stop, stop, stop...\" Xu Wan opened her eyes and shouted, \"Did you pick up the wrong booklet from the hospital? He's a legitimate son of the Minister of War, not a performer in a martial arts troupe. With such a precious status, breaking his arm every day, can he even keep that arm?\"","Cui Liu rigorously explained: \"Once the arm is broken, it becomes fragile and easily breaks again upon further stimulation. This is normal.\"","Xu Wan: \"...\" Normal, my foot!","She rubbed her forehead, unable to help feeling sorry for He Zheng's parents. Raising such a child who plays recklessly with his own life would scare anyone without a heart condition.","Xu Wan took a deep breath and asked: \"Why does he keep climbing walls? Does he have a wall-climbing obsession?\""]},{"number":52,"title":"Chapter 52: Did the Marquis's Mansion Go to Catch Adultery","paragraphs":["Cui Zhi flipped the page and continued, \"Oh, it says here that He Zheng is an avid reader, but since Minister He's family has been military generals for generations, all the male heirs, both legitimate and illegitimate, are trained in martial arts. That's why Minister He forced He Zheng to abandon literature and take up martial arts instead.\"","Xu Wan frowned and said, \"What is this nonsense? Is Minister He a stubborn mule? If his son doesn't like martial arts, let him study literature! Does he really think a family full of warriors is impressive? And who knows, maybe He Zheng could become like Zong Zhao and achieve the dual title of both literary and martial champions!\"","Cui Zhi flipped two more pages and found the reason, \"It's because Minister He was impeached by the civil officials and has developed a deep hatred for them. He even declared that anyone in the family who dares to sneak into the literary academy will have their legs broken.\"","\"So... were any legs broken?\" Xu Wan's first thought was this.","Given how many times Little Playboy He Zheng has broken his arms, what about his legs? Are they still intact?","Cui Zhi flipped another page and said, \"They were about to break his legs, but He Zheng's mother threw herself in the way to stop it, so they remained unharmed.\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","Minister He really needs to see a doctor. This lack of discipline in He Zheng is truly his father's fault.","\"Jin Cheng!\" Xu Wan suddenly jumped up from her comfortable chaise lounge, panicking, \"He went to Minister's Mansion, could it be to help He Zheng climb over the wall?!\"","Cui Zhi: \"!!!\"","Cui Liu: \"!!!\"","He Zheng, who had narrowly escaped having his legs broken while trying to escape by climbing over the wall, if Jin Cheng helps him, would their legs be at risk too?","Although both come from influential families, and such incidents are usually not made public, Minister He sounds terrifying, and anything could happen!","\"Quick, quick, prepare the horse! We must rush to the Minister of War's Mansion. If we're late, their legs might not be saved.\" Xu Wan frantically got up, scared out of her wits.","Cui Zhi had never seen Xu Wan so flustered before. Every previous encounter with Young Master Cheng had seen her calm and composed, always in control.","Little did anyone know, Xu Wan was almost going crazy with worry.","She had never even laid a hand on the little devil herself. If something happened to him at Minister He's mansion, Old Marquis and Old Marchioness would surely come back and devour her!","Xu Wan and her group rushed to the Minister of War's Mansion, the carriage speeding along, kicking up clouds of dust.","The onlooking common folk whispered among themselves, making their usual kind-hearted guesses.","\"What's going on at the Marquis Manor? It looks like they're fleeing for their lives!\"","\"I think they're catching a cheater. Otherwise, why would they bring all the maids and servants? Someone to hold them down, someone to cover their mouths, someone to kick them, right?\"","\"Catching a cheater? Who's cheating? The Young Marquis of Yangyuan Marquis Manor hasn't returned yet, and his son is only eight years old. No matter how precocious, he wouldn't be involved in such things, would he?\"","\"Then could it be...\"","\"Could it be...\"","\"Old Marquis?!\"","\"...\"","Old Marquis, far away in his villa, sneezed violently.","Old Marchioness brought him a cloak and said, \"My lord, you must take care. The villa is near the mountains, and even early summer can be cold.\"","Old Marquis rubbed his nose and confidently said, \"I'm not cold. It must be Jin Cheng missing me!\"","Old Marchioness: \"...\"","Hopefully, their little ancestor really does miss you.","On the way, Xu Wan ordered Cui Liu to scout ahead, especially to check if the little devil was lurking by any wall, planning to climb over it.","Only after Cui Liu had disappeared into the distance did Xu Wan remember that the little devil was accompanied by Buyan, a highly skilled martial artist.","\"Buyan is there. Nothing serious should happen.\"","Even if the people from the Minister's Mansion wanted to catch the little devil, Buyan could hold them off for a while.","Thinking this, Xu Wan calmed herself slightly, at least on the surface.","As soon as they alighted from the carriage, they requested an audience with the Minister's wife at the gate. On the way to the courtyard, Cui Liu spotted a figure.","She quickly grabbed Xu Wan and pointed to the corner.","Xu Wan focused her gaze and nearly lost two of her three souls!","Under a wall nearly 10 feet high, a stack of over ten stools wobbled in the wind, on the verge of toppling over at any moment. And there, her little devil was helping another kid climb onto the precarious stack.","The safety of this setup was so poor that they wouldn't just fail to climb over the wall—they'd probably fall off the stools right away!","He Zheng's already broken arms were in even more danger...","\"Cui Liu, quickly save them!\"","Xu Wan couldn't care less that they were in someone else's home. The immediate priority was to pull the little devil back, or her family would be in trouble.","\"Yes.\"","Cui Liu responded and flew over.","\"Ah... who are you? Let me go! Put me down! If you ruin my plans, do you want me to break your legs?!\"","Xu Wan heard He Zheng's shouting and was utterly speechless.","You two really are father and son, using the same threat!","\"Buyan, bring Jin Cheng back.\" Xu Wan called out.","She looked at the two figures behind the little devil—Shunzi, terrified and hesitant, and Buyan, expressionless. It seemed they had been instructed by the little devil not to interfere, so neither had dared to act.","Buyan was obedient. When the little devil was around, he listened to the little devil; when Xu Wan was around, he listened to Xu Wan.","This order of priority had been set by Old Marchioness before she left.","\"Buyan! Are you rebelling? I'm your master! Why are you listening to her? Don't pull me, I can walk myself!\"","Zong Jincheng kept chattering nonstop, but it didn't stop him from being carried away like a little chick by Buyan.","\"Damn it, why are your arms so strong!\" Unable to break free from Buyan's grip, the little devil started raging impotently.","The servant leading Xu Wan to the courtyard saw the commotion and hurriedly said, \"Young Master Zheng is trying to climb over the wall again! Quickly, inform the mistress!\"","Xu Wan, watching the chaos, didn't want to get involved in someone else's family matters, so she said, \"Please inform your mistress that Jin Cheng has homework to do at home and will visit your young master another day.\"","Zong Jincheng's eyes widened in disbelief. \"I've already finished my exams; what homework is there? You... mmm... Shunzi, mmm...\"","At Xu Wan's nod, Shunzi covered his young master's mouth, ready to drag him away. But He Zheng clung tightly to Zong Jincheng, refusing to let go.","He cried and shouted, \"Don't leave, Jin Cheng! You're my best friend! Everyone is against me; you have to help me! We were almost successful...\"","Zong Jincheng, with his mouth covered, could only mumble, the two of them acting like a pair of star-crossed lovers being forcibly separated, performing a tragic farewell.","\"Pfft...\" Xu Wan couldn't help but laugh.","Damn it, that's the downside of having a low laugh threshold.","These two little devils are just too funny...","Xu Wan covered her smile with one hand, laughing and anxious, \"Quick, pull them away! If we're late, Minister He will come out and break their legs.\""]},{"number":53,"title":"Chapter 53: The Bookish Young Master","paragraphs":["Little did Xu Wan know that her words made it seem as if there was an affair going on.","Cui Zhi's mouth twitched as she and Shunzi pulled their young master, separating the hands of this quarrelsome couple.","\"Jincheng...\"","\"He Zheng...\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","She couldn’t dwell on it any longer, or else she might feel like playing a melancholic tune.","The two youngsters were wailing and screaming, but they were no match for Xu Wan's ruthless determination. The wicked stepmother fulfilled her duty by dragging Zong Jincheng away. Before they even reached the door, they heard the furious voice of a middle-aged man: \"Where is that little brat?\"","Xu Wan: \"!\"","Minister He had indeed arrived, and his voice was so fierce that it sounded like he was the type of father who would resort to domestic violence.","Zong Jincheng struggled free from Shunzi's grip and turned back to run inside.","Xu Wan hurriedly called out, \"Jincheng, come back! This is someone else's family matter. Do you want to get your legs broken too?\"","Zong Jincheng shouted back as he ran, \"He’s my brother! If I don’t go back, he’ll definitely be beaten to death!\"","Xu Wan rolled her eyes, thinking he was being overly dramatic.","No matter how much Minister He despised scholars, he wouldn’t actually beat his own son to death. However, by the time she thought to have Buyan catch him, the little troublemaker had already disappeared.","Xu Wan sighed and quickly chased after him.","\"Smack—\"","\"Ah—\"","\"Will you change? Will you change? Do you dare sneak out to study again?\" Minister He glared fiercely as the servants carried out the punishment.","A long, wide board struck the nine-year-old child with full force, drawing blood with the first blow.","He Zheng, drenched in sweat, lay on the bench. The pain made him grip the bench tightly, his teeth clenched, but he stubbornly shouted back, \"I won’t change! I’d rather die than change! You can beat me to death, but I will keep studying! I refuse to learn martial arts!!\"","Zong Jincheng arrived just in time to hear these words.","Before him was still the same brother who always tried to climb over walls, but He Zheng’s unyielding spirit left him in awe.","Even in excruciating pain, even with such an unreasonable father, he still bravely and firmly declared his passion...","It was strange, yet it stirred that same strange feeling in him again.","The little troublemaker couldn’t understand it.","He thought about his own hobbies: bird-watching, teasing cats, cricket fights, soccer... He liked them all.","But if he had to break his arm from climbing walls or get beaten bloody by his father for the sake of these hobbies...","Then he wouldn’t like them as much anymore.","From Zong Jincheng’s perspective, he saw a young man’s stubborn pursuit of his dreams, while Xu Wan saw... two stubborn fools!","Each was stubborn in their own way, refusing to listen to the other.","Minister He, in his prime and skilled in martial arts, could easily beat He Zheng without breaking a sweat. But relying on force to subdue someone was never a long-term solution. He Zheng was one of the infamous \"Four Young Rascals.\" If this boy wasn’t properly educated, he would undoubtedly grow up to be someone who would beat his own father.","Sure enough, when Xu Wan glanced over, she didn’t miss the flash of hatred in He Zheng’s eyes.","It was genuine hatred, born from pain and unmet desires.","Yet the father, still in the midst of his violent outburst, remained completely oblivious. He ordered the servants to continue the beating: \"Hit him! Hit him hard! Beat him until he submits! This unfilial son, I’d rather have raised a dog—it would’ve been more obedient than him!\"","He Zheng closed his eyes and clenched his fists.","He didn’t make a sound anymore.","It’s natural for a child to cry out when beaten, but if even the tears stop, it means they’ve reached a point of utter despair and are resolved to die...","Xu Wan quickly intervened, \"Minister He, please wait! Young Master He Zheng seems to have passed out from the pain.\"","In her panic, she blurted out an excuse, only for the boy with clenched fists and closed eyes to suddenly open them and look at her in shock, sweat dripping from his jaw.","Xu Wan: \"...\"","I’m trying to save you, kid! Can’t you cooperate a little?","Minister He immediately turned to look, but He Zheng showed no signs of fainting. Enraged, he shouted at Xu Wan, \"Who are you?\"","\"Sir, this is the wife of the young master of the Yangyuan Marquis Manor,\" a servant whispered in reminder.","Minister He had a favorable impression of the Yangyuan Marquis Manor. Both families had a long history of military service, and he naturally wanted He Zheng to associate more with children from such martial families.","His attitude softened. \"So you are Lady Zong of the Yangyuan Marquis Manor. Someone, bring seats for the lady and the young master.\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","At a time like this, he’s offering them seats? Does he want them to sit and watch He Zheng get beaten?","To her surprise, Minister He added, \"My son is disobedient and unruly. He needs to be taught a lesson. Please stay and watch, so he can understand what it means to be humiliated.\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","This father... is truly cruel.","Deliberately grinding his child’s dignity into the dirt...","In comparison, she felt her own approach to educating Zong Jincheng was nothing but gentle.","She tried to reason with him, \"Minister He, why be so strict with a child? If he enjoys studying, let him study. My husband once achieved top honors in both civil and military examinations, and it didn’t hinder his martial arts training.\"","The little troublemaker chimed in, \"Yeah, my dad is amazing at studying!\"","\"Zong Zhao?\" Minister He recalled the memory of that spirited young man, who had once been the talk of the capital. Not only was he adored by countless young women, but even the elders spoke highly of him.","Minister He admired Zong Zhao’s martial prowess, but his scholarly achievements? Not so much. If it weren’t for his success in the imperial exams and his entry into the Hanlin Academy, he wouldn’t have been indoctrinated by those old scholars, always preaching about loyalty, filial piety, and righteousness.","But in front of Zong Zhao’s wife and son, Minister He held back his disdain for scholarly pursuits. After all, it’s impolite to insult someone’s weaknesses.","If Xu Wan knew that he considered a civil examination champion a weakness, she’d probably be furious enough to fight on behalf of all the scholars in the academies.","\"Sir... Zheng’er... Oh heavens, how could you be beaten like this! Who dared lay a hand on you?\" Madam He finally arrived, rushing over to pull He Zheng off the bench. \"Someone, call the House Physician immediately!!\"","When the House Physician arrived to examine He Zheng’s wounds, the boy stubbornly pushed him away.","Madam He said, \"Yes, yes, his injuries are on his body. Let’s take him inside to be treated.\"","Everyone helped carry He Zheng into the house. Madam He was about to follow in a hurry when a maid stopped her and whispered about what had just happened.","Madam He paused, instructing the maid to watch over He Zheng inside while she stayed behind to speak with Xu Wan. \"Lady Zong, thank you for stepping in earlier. Otherwise, Zheng’er would have suffered even more blows...\"","As she spoke, she wiped away tears. Her face, though only in her thirties, bore traces of exhaustion and worry, no doubt from the stress of raising her third son.","Xu Wan felt pity for her and sighed. \"It was the least I could do. Even though I’ve never been a mother, I know how much a mother’s heart aches for her child. The way Young Master He Zheng and his father interact is problematic. You should think of a way to resolve this soon.\""]},{"number":54,"title":"Chapter 54: Jincheng's Goal","paragraphs":["Madam He's expression shifted, and she stepped forward to take Xu Wan's hand, speaking with an overly enthusiastic tone, \"Sister, I have a favor to ask...\"","Xu Wan instinctively pulled her hand back and took a step back.","This scene was all too reminiscent of when the Old Marchioness had entrusted the little troublemaker to her.","She smiled cautiously and said, \"Please go ahead, Madam.\"","Madam He was momentarily taken aback by Xu Wan's retreat, a flicker of embarrassment crossing her eyes. She explained, \"You see, my husband is quite fond of Yangyuan Marquis Manor and would like Zheng Er to practice martial arts with your child. I thought that if the two of them played together, they might develop an interest in martial arts. Would it be possible for him to accompany Jin Cheng?\"","Xu Wan was momentarily speechless before replying, \"To be honest, Jin Cheng doesn’t actually practice martial arts.\"","\"How could that be?\" Madam He exclaimed in surprise. \"Your family has been a line of military officers for generations, and the Old Marquis is a highly decorated veteran. Could it be that Jin Cheng prefers studying over martial arts?\"","Xu Wan wanted to say, \"He doesn’t love studying at all...\"","He doesn’t love learning anything—he just loves playing!","Xu Wan explained, \"It’s the Old Marquis’s decision. My second uncle died in battle, and my husband has been missing for many years. The Old Marquis is getting on in years and can’t bear the thought of anything happening to his grandson, so...\"","Madam He was stunned by this revelation. She murmured, \"The Old Marquis would think that way... Yes, I can understand... If only my husband could see it that way, things wouldn’t be so strained with Zheng Er. Our family already has too many children practicing martial arts; it’s not as if we’re short of Zheng Er doing it too...\"","As she spoke, Madam He seemed on the verge of tears. Xu Wan wanted to comfort her but didn’t know where to start.","Unexpectedly, Madam He suddenly grabbed Xu Wan’s arm and said, \"Sister! I think it would be best for Zheng Er to go to your house and play with Jin Cheng. That way, he won’t keep sneaking out by climbing over the wall!\"","Xu Wan was baffled. \"Jin Cheng has to study at home. If He Zheng joins him, your husband would go mad.\"","\"Jin Cheng is studying??\" Madam He was well aware of Zong Jincheng’s reputation.","Wasn’t that boy the ringleader of the four little troublemakers, always causing mischief with others?","Just moments ago, a maid had mentioned that it was Zong Jincheng who helped Zheng Er climb over the wall. What ordinary child would dare do such a thing? Could he really be sitting at home studying so obediently?","Xu Wan nodded. \"Yes, Jin Cheng has recently taken an interest in studying. He’s been diligently reading every day and even goes to the academy every month to take exams, trying to catch up with his classmates who are performing better.\"","Just then, the house physician arrived to tend to He Zheng’s injuries, and Zong Jincheng didn’t stay long before leaving. As soon as he stepped out, he overheard the woman talking about how much he loved studying.","He loved studying... like hell!","Zong Jincheng couldn’t stand Xu Wan tarnishing his reputation like this, so he stormed over and declared, \"I’m not going to study anymore, not even a single page! What’s this about catching up with classmates? Do they even need me to catch up? They’re all losers compared to me!\"","Xu Wan’s lips twitched. \"The results of the four-academy joint exam haven’t even been released yet. You might not even make it onto the list, you overconfident little brat.\"","\"Impossible! I’m definitely going to be first in this exam, no doubt about it!\"","\"It definitely won’t be you. You can’t even surpass Qin Ye.\"","\"Nonsense! I’m definitely going to knock Qin Ye off his pedestal this time!\"","\"Oh, please. There’s no hope. I suggest you start burning the midnight oil now. Don’t wait until after the results come out to start studying again, wasting precious time.\"","\"Impossible! I won’t study! I don’t need to study at all!\"","Zong Jincheng and Xu Wan argued fiercely, their faces red with anger, their conversation entirely focused on academics. Madam He couldn’t get a word in edgewise and had no choice but to temporarily abandon her plan to send her son to the marquis manor.","True to his word, Zong Jincheng refused to study, convinced that he would soon see his name at the top of the exam results.","But that night, he tossed and turned, unable to sleep.","His mind kept drifting to He Zheng’s earnest desire to study and Xu Wan’s firm assertion that he couldn’t surpass Qin Ye.","Zong Jincheng was a supremely confident person—how could he accept such a definitive assumption? Yet, Xu Wan’s predictions were rarely wrong...","But... but nonsense!","She must be wrong this time!","How could he, the great Young Master Zong, lose to someone else, especially to that cold, rude, and emotionless Qin Ye?","Impossible!","He absolutely wouldn’t lose!","The little troublemaker pulled the blanket over his head, trying to calm his racing mind with the darkness.","Unfortunately, he was unusually wide awake.","Zong Jincheng was suffering from insomnia.","He threw off the blanket and noticed that the sky outside was beginning to lighten—dawn was approaching.","But lying in bed was unbearable, so he called out that he was getting up. Buyan, who was on night duty, entered the room.","\"Young Master, you’re up so early?\"","Zong Jincheng grunted in response. \"Couldn’t sleep. I’m going out for a walk.\"","At this hour, there wouldn’t be much to do.","If it were Shunzi on duty, he would have nagged endlessly, urging the young master to wait until daylight. But Buyan was obedient and spoke little. Without asking any questions, he accompanied Zong Jincheng out of the manor.","The morning air was crisp and refreshing. Zong Jincheng’s dark, bright eyes blinked as he looked around. The marquis manor was eerily quiet and dark, except for one spot of light.","\"That’s...\"","Buyan replied, \"That’s Young Master Xiu’s room. He must already be up, studying.\"","Zong Jincheng frowned and muttered, \"Bookworm, always studying.\"","He couldn’t care less about Zong Wenxiu’s diligent efforts. He strolled comfortably out of the manor and headed toward the busiest street in town.","The early morning vendors were pushing their carts, busily setting up their stalls. The steam from the freshly steamed buns in the breakfast shops filled the air with a tantalizing aroma, mixed with a hint of rawness—the scent of food still in the process of being cooked.","Since they were still preparing for the day, there were no calls to attract customers or enthusiastic greetings. The vendors were focused on their work, and no one noticed the young master wandering around so early.","It was Zong Jincheng’s first time seeing the city at its earliest hour, and everything felt new and intriguing. Yet, something inside him kept stirring. \"They all have goals they’re working toward.\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Having a goal seems so interesting. It gives you something to strive for.\"","\"Yes, yes,\" Buyan responded, trying his best to be a conversational companion.","The little troublemaker pondered, \"Then what’s my goal?\" He looked up at Buyan, his eyes filled with confusion.","Buyan didn’t know how to answer. He wasn’t as eloquent as Madam Xu, nor did he have Shunzi’s knack for comforting the young master.","But he noticed something behind Zong Jincheng.","The little troublemaker turned around and saw the plaque of a mansion.","The Qin Residence."]},{"number":55,"title":"Chapter 55: Leaning on the Wall of Qin Ye's House at Night","paragraphs":["Among the people Zong Jincheng hated the most, Xu Wan would rank first, and the second would undoubtedly be that Qin guy.","Little Demon King didn't expect that even a morning stroll could lead him to encounter this surname, instantly shattering his calm and healing mood.","\"Hmph!\"","Zong Jincheng turned and walked in another direction, but the location of the Qin residence was awkwardly placed. He either had to go back the way he came or inevitably pass by the Qin family's courtyard wall.","The Little Demon King grew angrier as he walked, finally stopping and asking, \"This isn't Qin Ye's house, is it?\"","Buyan replied, \"It seems to be his home.\"","Qin Ye's father was a fifth-rank official, and their residence was located in this area.","Zong Jincheng snorted again and strode forward quickly.","Buyan hurried to keep up.","Unexpectedly, the young master suddenly stopped short, and if not for Buyan's exceptional martial arts, he might have knocked Zong Jincheng flying.","Zong Jincheng turned to him and said, \"Qin Ye is really lazy. He's still not up reading at this hour.\"","The Qin residence was pitch black, with not a single candlelight visible.","Buyan thought for a moment and said, \"Master, today is a rest day.\"","\"So what?\" The Little Demon King replied arrogantly, \"Even Zong Wenxiu is up reading. Only Qin Ye is still lazing in bed. Hmph, and he dares to compete with me for the first place? He'll be flattened, flattened, flattened in no time.\"","As Zong Jincheng spoke, he ground his foot on the ground, almost stepping on a few innocent ants.","Buyan: \"......\"","He couldn't understand this childish operation.","Finally, Buyan, lacking the ability to read the room, reminded, \"Master, I see a light in one direction of the Qin residence.\"","\"Where?\" Zong Jincheng looked up but couldn't see anything.","Buyan thought, given your height, it's normal not to see it.","Without a word, he picked up the Little Demon King and placed him on his shoulder.","Zong Jincheng's vision immediately widened. He glanced inside and sure enough, there was a room lit up. \"Move a bit forward.\"","The Little Demon King clung to the wall, peering inside. His vision was still a bit blurry, so he stepped on Buyan's shoulder and leaped onto the wall, hanging like a little gecko.","Perhaps the noise was too loud, and the room below suddenly opened a window, revealing a pair of extremely cold eyes.","It was Qin Ye.","Zong Jincheng stared at him for a few seconds before finally reacting and shouting, \"It really is him!\"","Qin Ye might not have recognized Zong Jincheng, but upon seeing someone disturbing his reading, he slammed the window shut with a loud bang, the sound clearly audible outside the wall.","Zong Jincheng vaguely remembered that the person had a book in his hand before closing the window, flipping through it as if he was genuinely reading, not just pretending.","He froze for a moment, his brows furrowed.","Somehow, he felt uncomfortable all over. Thinking of this morning on a rest day, Zong Wenxiu was reading to catch up, and Qin Ye was also reading.","Qin Ye was already first; why was he still rushing to catch up?","The Little Demon King tilted his head and thought for a long time before finally concluding, \"He must think I'm going to snatch the first place, so he's frantically trying to keep up with me!\"","Buyan: \"......\"","He suddenly remembered Shunzi's famous saying: Never take the young master's words seriously, and never overanalyze them.","Otherwise, even someone like him with no expression would easily lose control.","Despite this, on the way back, Zong Jincheng kept rambling, \"But how did he know I would surpass him? Did he see my potential to surpass him last time? Or did he secretly investigate me at Marquis Manor to see how hard I've been studying this month?\"","Buyan listened and didn't know how to respond.","He thought none of these possibilities were likely, but he also didn't know how to answer the young master, only praying to return to the manor quickly so Shunzi could take over the task of answering.","Zong Jincheng continued to mutter to himself, \"Anyway, he must be paying attention to me. Of course, anyone who encounters such an excellent rival as me would feel the pressure!\"","Buyan: \"......\"","Why hasn't he reached home yet!","The road back to Marquis Manor feels endless!","Zong Jincheng couldn't hear Buyan's inner screams and continued to walk, his steps getting faster and faster.","He was walking and jumping, in a great mood.","Buyan's silence was deafening.","When Xu Wan woke up, she heard Cui Liu reporting the Little Demon King's progress. As she wiped her face, she asked, \"What was he up to last night? Not sleeping again?\"","\"The young master just strolled around the street and then passed by the Qin residence. It's said he even peeked over their wall for a while.\"","\"Huh?\" Xu Wan paused with the towel in her hand, \"The Qin residence? Qin Ye's house? What was he doing peeking over their wall?\"","Cui Zhi suppressed her laughter and said, \"According to Shunzi, the young master thought Qin Ye was secretly studying to catch up with Master Zong.\"","Xu Wan's mouth twitched, another day of being speechless over the Little Demon King's delusional confidence.","She continued to apply the towel to her face lazily, \"Qin Ye is a child with both talent and hard work. How could he possibly work hard just to surpass that lazy Zong Jincheng? To be honest, he probably doesn't even know who Zong Jincheng is. What an arrogant little brat.\"","Cui Zhi chuckled, \"Madam, should we send an invitation to the Qin residence, inviting Master Qin Ye to come to our manor to study with the young master for a day?\"","Xu Wan raised an eyebrow, amused, \"You want Qin Ye to reject the invitation and let Zong Jincheng know that the other party doesn't even recognize him?\"","Cui Zhi replied, \"We need to deflate the young master's arrogance a bit, or he'll never study.\"","Xu Wan pondered for a moment before shaking her head, \"Forget it. Qin Ye studies diligently, and we shouldn't disturb him. Anyway, the results will be out soon.\"","Cui Zhi was surprised. It wouldn't take long to invite Qin Ye, yet the madam seemed overly cautious, almost afraid to disturb him.","She tentatively asked, \"Madam, it seems you quite like this young master from the Qin family?\"","Xu Wan was also very straightforward, \"Yes, who wouldn't like a hardworking child?\"","She had come out of a small mountain village step by step, so she knew the hardships of exams and how much hardworking students cherished their time.","Having been through the rain herself, she didn't want to cause others to get wet because of her.","Cui Zhi replied, \"That's true. The madam also likes Master Zong Wenxiu very much.\"","Xu Wan laughed, \"Actually, I like Zong Jincheng too.\"","\"Ah?\" Cui Zhi was stunned.","This was really unexpected, especially from Master Zong himself.","Xu Wan laughed loudly, \"Haha, but I have to suppress my liking for him. Otherwise, if this kid feels it, he'll become even more arrogant!\"","\"That's true,\" Cui Zhi praised, \"Madam is wise.\"","When Xu Wan went to the front hall for breakfast, she only saw Zong Wenxiu and not Zong Jincheng.","She chuckled and asked, \"Has the kid finally gotten tired?\"","Steward Liu replied, \"The young master was very energetic today and couldn't fall asleep. The court physician was afraid he would harm his body, so he gave him a couple of acupuncture needles.\"","\"?\" Xu Wan was amazed, \"A couple of needles can make him fall asleep quickly?\""]},{"number":56,"title":"Chapter 56: Heavily Paid Private Tutor","paragraphs":["\"Yes,\" Xu Wan gave a thumbs up. \"Great medical skills!\"","Zong Jincheng slept until it was dark outside.","He got up from the bed, stretched, and called out with his eyes still closed, \"Shunzi, I'm hungry!\"","\"Coming, young master! The food will be served right away!\"","Zong Jincheng yawned and asked, \"What time is it now?\"","\"It's just past 9-11 pm. The lights in the madam's courtyard have already been turned off.\"","\"Oh, she really sleeps early,\" Zong Jincheng remarked as Buyan helped him wash up and prepare for his meal. He grabbed a steamed bun and took two big bites.","Once he felt less hungry, he suddenly remembered another question. \"Has Zong Wenxiu gone to bed yet?\"","Shunzi replied, \"Not yet. Young Master Wenxiu usually stays up until after 11 pm - 1 am.\"","\"What?\" Zong Jincheng frowned. \"Staying up so late and waking up so early, doesn’t he feel awful? Is he still studying?\"","Shunzi answered, \"Yes, ever since Young Master Wenxiu returned to the Marquis Manor, this has been his daily routine.\"","It had been three months since Zong Jincheng started studying with Zong Wenxiu, yet he only now thought to ask about his sleep schedule. It seemed he paid little attention to others’ lives.","Unlike his young master, Shunzi loved hearing gossip. There wasn’t a single secret or important matter in the entire Marquis Manor that he didn’t know about.","Zong Jincheng then recalled the scene he had witnessed outside the Qin Mansion’s walls that morning.","Was Qin Ye also burning the midnight oil like Zong Wenxiu?","The thought made Zong Jincheng feel uneasy, though he couldn’t quite pinpoint why.","If Xu Wan knew, she would have accurately told him, \"Congratulations, kid, you’ve been caught up in the competition.\"","The third bun in his hand suddenly didn’t taste as good. Zong Jincheng gulped down a bowl of chicken soup, grabbed a handful of peeled lychees, and ran outside.","The candle in Zong Wenxiu’s room was nearly burnt out. A servant came in to replace it, and the dim room brightened again.","The little troublemaker stood outside his window, munching on lychees but not entering.","The window was closed, so from outside, he could only see the flickering shadow of the candle and Zong Wenxiu’s movements as he flipped through books and wrote.","Zong Jincheng spat out lychee seeds as he watched, and soon the ground was littered with them. Since the courtyard was cleaned daily, Shunzi didn’t bother to stop him.","Curious, Zong Jincheng asked, \"Shunzi, how long do you think it’ll take for him to catch up to Qin Ye’s progress?\"","Shunzi was stumped.","This was a tricky question to answer.","Seeing his hesitation, Zong Jincheng immediately scowled. \"Just tell me the truth.\"","Shunzi wanted to be honest, but the truth wasn’t pleasant. \"I think... Young Master Wenxiu might never catch up to Qin Ye’s progress...\"","\"What did you say?!\" Zong Jincheng was furious and kicked Shunzi’s leg. \"Why are you boosting their morale and dampening our own? Whose side are you on?\"","Shunzi clutched his leg, yelping in pain, but Zong Jincheng glared at him to keep quiet. \"You told me to be honest...\"","Zong Jincheng raised his foot to kick him again, but seeing Shunzi instinctively protect his leg, he stopped and asked, \"Why can’t he catch up? Zong Wenxiu is even two years older than Qin Ye!\"","Shunzi sighed. \"Studying has nothing to do with age. Some people pass the provincial exams in their teens, while others remain entry-level examinees even at eighty.\"","\"What’s an entry-level examinee?\"","\"It’s the lowest rank in the imperial examination system, two levels below a provincial graduate.\"","\"Oh... So even with all his effort, Zong Wenxiu can’t surpass Qin Ye?\"","Shunzi reminded him, \"Qin Ye is also working very hard.\"","Zong Jincheng was puzzled. \"Zong Wenxiu studies to have more options in the future, but why does Qin Ye do it? Isn’t he the eldest son in his family? His father is still young and holds a decent position as a fifth-rank official.\"","Shunzi thought for a moment. \"Maybe he wants to follow in his father’s footsteps. Qin Ye was only two when his father became the top scorer in the imperial examination. He probably grew up watching his father study diligently.\"","\"Following in his father’s footsteps...\" Zong Jincheng murmured. \"My father became the top scorer in both civil and military exams at fifteen. He’s much more impressive than Qin Ye’s father.\"","Shunzi nodded in agreement.","Zong Jincheng looked up at the sky. \"It seems I’m the only one who can compete with Qin Ye for the title of top scorer.\"","Shunzi: \"?\"","Zong Jincheng continued, \"This family really can’t do without me.\"","Shunzi: \"??\"","Zong Jincheng turned back. \"Let’s go. It’s time to work hard for the birth of the next top scorer!\"","Shunzi: \"???\"","Are you okay? Are you sleepwalking or something? I...","Shunzi, still in shock, hurried after him but slipped on something smooth, landing hard on his backside.","\"Lychee... lychee seeds...\" Shunzi didn’t make it to the next day’s cleaning.","The world had dealt him pain, but he responded with a song.","Shunzi sang a mournful tune in the manor physician’s room.","Zong Jincheng didn’t return to his room directly. Instead, he went to the main study, which he hadn’t entered in two days. Still, after studying there for three months, he knew exactly where each book was.","He picked up a book at random and started reading. Buyan helped him grind ink while Zong Jincheng focused on writing, completely unaware that Shunzi had gone to see the manor physician about his bruised backside.","The next morning, Xu Wan stood at the study door, surveying the chaos. Books were strewn everywhere, and ink stains dotted the floor, evidence of the reader’s frustration. What had made him so agitated while studying?","Buyan explained, \"Young Master studied until 11 pm - 1 am and fell asleep on the small couch in the study.\"","Xu Wan picked up one of the books from the floor and flipped through it. The content was dense and difficult, with none of the phonetic annotations she had prepared earlier. Given Zong Jincheng’s limited vocabulary, he must have stumbled over many unfamiliar words.","No wonder he grew more frustrated as he read.","She turned to Cui Zhi and said, \"Have someone annotate all the books in this room with phonetic guides. Also, bring the translated versions and number the pages of both the original and translated books so Jincheng can easily cross-reference them.\"","\"All of them? These belong to the young marquis...\" Cui Zhi hesitantly reminded her. \"He never allows anyone to touch his things.\"","Xu Wan waved it off. \"It’s just annotations. If he minds, we’ll buy him new books later.\"","The main study contained a comprehensive collection of books, and replicating it elsewhere would be challenging.","Cui Zhi: \"...Alright then.\"","After all, the madam was now in charge of the Marquis Manor. Her word was law.","Xu Wan added, \"Invite two of this year’s provincial graduates to tutor Jincheng.\"","\"Provincial graduates?\" Cui Zhi was surprised. \"They’re qualified to hold official positions. Even the prestigious Hanlin Academy struggles to hire a few provincial graduates as tutors, and you want two... both from this year?\"","Xu Wan smiled. \"Ordinary people might not be able to hire them, but we can.\"","\"How?\"","\"With money.\""]},{"number":57,"title":"Chapter 57: Teasing the Master","paragraphs":["The financial prowess of the Yangyuan Marquis Manor was no joke. Just by mentioning their name, three to five scholars came knocking on their door, but it seemed like they had all conspired to be equally stubborn.","\"I am a scholar who just passed the provincial examination last year. Many wealthy young masters have sought me out to be their tutor, but I have declined them all.\"","\"We are all scholars who passed the same examination, but I was the only one in my county to succeed. Even the county magistrate personally came to invite me to be his advisor.\"","\"I teach at the best academy in the capital, and most of the students who pass the imperial examinations come from our academy. When it comes to teaching children, you need a professional tutor.\"","\"Cut the nonsense! We all passed the same examination. You've only been a tutor for a little over a year. What does it have to do with you if students from your academy passed in previous years?\"","\"How is it not my business? Many of the students who will pass next year will surely be my disciples!\"","\"Bragging!\"","\"Who's bragging? How can you call a scholar's words bragging?\"","\"...\"","Xu Wan sat above them, watching their endless bickering. She tapped the table and said, \"Esteemed scholars, could we get to the point... Are you willing to come to our manor to teach our children?\"","\"That depends on how much sincerity your manor shows. I'm quite comfortable at Hanlin Academy.\"","\"Exactly. If we were to take up an official post, it would be quite prestigious.\"","\"If it weren't for your steward's earnest invitation, we wouldn't have come at all. Private tutors rarely gain any fame, and when a student succeeds, it's their own glory.\"","Two others remained on the fence, but like the first three, they were waiting to see what the manor had to offer.","Cui Zhi frowned and whispered, \"Madam, why are these people like this? I thought scholars were supposed to have integrity and disdain money.\"","Xu Wan chuckled and replied, \"People need food to survive, and they have emotions and desires. They have families to support too.\"","As fellow workers, she understood their feelings. As long as the money was right, everything else could be negotiated.","She straightened up and said, \"Gentlemen, our manor offers a monthly salary of one hundred taels for private tutors, with a three-year contract.\"","\"One hundred taels for three years? That's a bit low...\"","\"One hundred taels per month for three years! Are you deaf?\"","\"What? One hundred taels a month??\"","\"One hundred taels a month???\"","The scholars were stunned. They started counting on their fingers: one hundred taels a month, one thousand two hundred taels a year, three thousand six hundred taels in three years...","Good heavens!","If they could earn that much, they'd never have to worry about money again!","One scholar, still in disbelief, turned to his companion and asked, \"How... how much do you earn at Hanlin Academy? Do tutors really make this much now?\"","\"Eight... eight taels... And other academies are worse, four or five taels is considered high...\"","The scholars were shocked!","They all exclaimed in unison, \"I'll take the job!\"","\"Let me do it! I have experience in passing the examination. I'll ensure the young master passes before he comes of age!\"","\"Me! I have teaching experience at Hanlin Academy. With me, it's impossible for the students not to pass!\"","\"You only have one year of teaching experience...\"","\"That's still better than you, a scholar with no job!\"","The five of them started arguing again, each vying for the position.","Xu Wan sighed inwardly, thinking how useful money could be.","One hundred taels was equivalent to about a hundred thousand dollars in modern terms. If someone had offered her that much to be a tutor back when she was working, she would have fought tooth and nail for it too.","\"Our manor is only hiring two tutors. Please write a resume detailing your academic and examination experiences, and we will make a selection based on that,\" Xu Wan instructed. \"Cui Zhi, please take them to the side hall to write.\"","\"Yes, Madam.\"","\"Oh, and one more thing,\" Xu Wan added with a smile, \"Our Yangyuan Marquis Manor has good relations with the Ministry of Rites. If anyone falsifies their resume, don't say we didn't warn you.\"","The scholars exchanged glances, some looking guilty as they bent over to write, while others nodded approvingly at Xu Wan.","This was for the best. Otherwise, with such a high salary, people might be tempted to fabricate their credentials.","But once they left, Cui Zhi grew anxious. She whispered, \"Madam, we don't actually have connections in the Ministry of Rites...\"","Not only did they lack connections there, but the manor had been so detached from worldly affairs for so long that they hardly interacted with other families. Even if they wanted to ask someone for a favor, they wouldn't know who to turn to.","Xu Wan raised an eyebrow and asked, \"If we were familiar with the Ministry of Rites, could they really help us verify all the scholars' examination records?\"","Cui Zhi: \"...\" Couldn't they?","So Madam was bluffing???","Xu Wan thought that perhaps they could, but setting aside whether this would count as leaking confidential information, the scholars came from various regions, and checking all the records would be a massive undertaking.","She smiled and said, \"A resume doesn't just show a person's experiences. It also reveals their writing style, logical thinking, and even their approach to studying. These things can't be faked.\"","\"Can Madam really discern all that?\" Cui Zhi asked.","Xu Wan shook her head honestly. \"I might not be able to see everything myself. I'll need Baili Xi to help me review them.\"","\"Then I'll have them write their resumes and wait for our notification. If we decide to hire them, we'll send them a letter of appointment, and they can come to the manor to sign the contract.\"","\"That sounds good.\"","Cui Zhi smiled. \"I'll make the arrangements.\"","As Cui Zhi headed to the side hall, Xu Wan got up and went to the main study to inform Baili Xi.","The two children were already there, sitting neatly in the study.","Baili Xi seemed much more energetic while teaching, vividly recounting historical anecdotes, occasionally stroking his beard, clearly in a good mood.","Zong Wenxiu was listening attentively, taking notes from time to time.","As for Zong Jincheng, that mischievous boy seemed lively, holding a brush and doodling on paper, appearing as if he wasn't paying attention, but his eyes never strayed.","He was multitasking but not missing the lesson.","Xu Wan sighed. Such a clever child was both enviable and exasperating.","In the room, Baili Xi said, \"Alright, that's all for today's lesson. Please write down what you learned yesterday, and I'll collect it afterward.\"","With that, he yawned, propped his head on his hand, and closed his eyes for a quick nap.","Xu Wan thought that Baili Xi had indeed been overworked lately. Since the little troublemaker had started studying seriously, he always had endless questions. While the boy's boundless energy was no issue, it had visibly aged Baili Xi. This was one of the reasons she wanted to hire two more private tutors.","Just as she was pondering how to have the two new tutors assist Baili Xi in educating Zong Jincheng, she saw the little troublemaker, who was supposed to be quietly writing, tiptoeing toward the lectern with a brush in hand—","His eyes were fixed on Baili Xi's graying beard.","Xu Wan: \"!!!\"","Good heavens, the brush was dripping with red ink!!!"]},{"number":58,"title":"Chapter 58: Save My Brother Next Time","paragraphs":["What is this little rascal trying to do?!","Is he planning to paint Baili Xi's beard with that red ink?!","\"Zong Jincheng!!!\" Xu Wan shouted to stop him.","No matter where he intended to paint, he shouldn't have targeted Baili Xi. After all, Baili Xi was not only his teacher but also his father's mentor.","Baili Xi was startled by the loud shout and, upon opening his eyes, saw Zong Jincheng standing before him with a red brush in hand. The boy quickly hid the brush behind his back when he realized Baili Xi was awake.","Baili Xi, stroking his beard, asked, \"Jincheng, what are you doing with that brush?\"","Zong Jincheng, caught red-handed, put on an innocent smile. \"Nothing, you must be mistaken. I just came to ask you how to write this passage...\"","The little devil glared at Xu Wan through the window, shooting her a venomous look. This woman had ruined his plans again.","Xu Wan was furious. How dare this brat glare at her? He showed no remorse whatsoever!","\"Cui Liu, bring the hand paddle.\"","At these words, not only did the little devil freeze in fear, but even Zong Wenxiu and Baili Xi were taken aback.","Zong Wenxiu had known Xu Wan for a long time but had never seen her so angry. What had just happened? He had been focused on copying the text and hadn’t noticed anything. And what was his brother doing with that brush?","Baili Xi, having taught for many years, had seen it all. While no one had ever dared to mess with him, he had heard stories of mischievous children who liked to doodle on their teachers' faces.","Knowing Zong Jincheng, the boy was definitely capable of such a prank. And it was clear now—","He had tried to play a trick on his teacher but was caught in the act by his mother.","Cui Liu was quick to act, returning with the hand paddle in an instant.","The little devil turned pale at the sight of the paddle. What was this? A hand paddle? Was she going to hit his hand?","Zong Jincheng quickly threw the brush aside, backing away with a nervous laugh. \"It’s a misunderstanding! Don’t accuse me. I was just asking the teacher a question.\"","The little devil was clever. Even though he was panicking inside, he kept up his innocent act, a skill he had mastered to deceive adults.","Baili Xi seemed to fall for it. He hurriedly intervened, \"Madam, let it go. It’s normal for children to be a bit mischievous. No harm was done, after all.\"","Xu Wan reminded him, \"If I hadn’t shouted just now, Zong Jincheng would have painted your beard red with ink.\"","Baili Xi: \"!\"","He imagined his long beard suddenly turning red. Wouldn’t he look like Zhong Kui himself?","Baili Xi fell silent.","\"Hold out your hand,\" Xu Wan ordered.","Seeing that his innocent act wasn’t working, Zong Jincheng immediately switched to threats. \"If you dare hit me... my grandmother will be furious when she returns. She’ll take away your housekeeping keys and kick you out of the Marquis Manor!\"","Xu Wan sneered, \"We’ll see about that. Cui Liu, give him three strikes.\"","The little devil wailed, \"Shunzi, Buyan, save me!!\"","But Shunzi and Buyan were stopped by Cui Zhi at the door and couldn’t enter.","\"Wenxiu! Save me! Brother! My dear brother! Help me!\" The little devil pulled out all the stops, calling Zong Wenxiu \"brother\" in a desperate attempt to appeal to the only family bond he had left in the manor.","Zong Wenxiu, overwhelmed by this sudden display of brotherly affection, stood up to help. \"Brother, I’ll save you!\"","Just as a heroic rescue seemed imminent, the \"wicked stepmother\" stepped in front of the would-be savior.","Remembering Xu Wan’s kindness to his mother, Zong Wenxiu hesitated for a few seconds before saying, \"Brother, I’ll save you next time!\"","Baili Xi: \"...\"","The brotherly bond had lasted all of a few seconds.","Zong Jincheng cried out to no avail. His hands were firmly grasped by Cui Liu, who held the paddle in her right hand.","The little devil was terrified. \"Don’t hit me with your right hand! It hurts more. Use your left hand. We don’t have any deep grudges. When I grow up, I’ll be in charge of the Marquis Manor. Aren’t you afraid of offending... Ah!\"","\"Smack!\"—the first strike.","It was the little devil’s first time being hit. The pain shot from his palm throughout his entire body.","\"You’re really hitting me? That’s too hard! Can’t you go easy on me? I’m sorry, I’m sorry... I’ll never mess with the teacher again. The books say that those who admit their mistakes are good children. You should give me a chance to change... Ah!\"","\"Smack!\"—the second strike.","The little devil’s tears streamed down his face. The pain made it impossible to keep up his act of remorse. He started shouting in anger, \"Xu Wan! I’ll never forgive you! When I take over the Marquis Manor, I’ll banish you to the countryside! You’ll never see anyone, never go shopping, just get bitten by mosquitoes, listen to frogs croaking, and watch... Ah!\"","\"Smack!\"—the third strike landed.","The punishment was over. Cui Liu released his hand, leaving the little devil to stare at his reddened palms, howling as he collapsed to the floor.","Shunzi and Buyan rushed in to help him up, but the little devil continued to wail, his face defiant even as tears streamed down his cheeks.","Xu Wan picked up the essay Zong Jincheng had been copying. It was flawless, with not a single mistake or typo, though the handwriting was as messy as ever.","She crouched down in front of the little devil and said, \"Kid, if you want to kick me out of the Marquis Manor, you’d better grow stronger fast. With your current weakling self... if you dare disrespect your teacher again, it won’t just be three strikes.\"","The little devil glared at her with red eyes, \"Just you wait!\"","Xu Wan patted his head, teasing, \"I hope I won’t have to wait until I’m old and gray.\"","The little devil shook off her hand and yelled, \"Buyan, carry me back! I don’t want to see this evil woman anymore!\"","\"Yes,\" Buyan moved to comply.","Xu Wan rolled her eyes, \"What’s there to carry? Your hands were hit, not your legs. Walk back yourself.\"","\"None of your business!\" The little devil extended his reddened hand, leaning on Buyan’s shoulder as he was carried away, his glare at Xu Wan even fiercer.","Zong Wenxiu stood there, unsure of what to do. He glanced at his brother, then at Xu Wan, and stammered, \"I... I’ve finished copying. I’ll go find the manor’s doctor to check on my brother’s hand! Madam, Teacher, goodbye.\"","Once only Xu Wan and Baili Xi remained, Baili Xi chuckled, as if recalling something amusing. He sighed deeply and said, \"Madam, you’ve really made an enemy of Jincheng this time.\"","Xu Wan smiled, \"I’ve always been on his bad side. I just never acted on it before. But his mischievous nature has gone too far. If he’s not disciplined, he’ll never learn.\"","Baili Xi nodded, \"True. It’s fortunate that the old Marquis and his wife are open-minded. Otherwise, being a stepmother wouldn’t be easy for you.\"","Being a stepmother was no simple task. Any form of discipline could be labeled as abuse, but neglecting the child would be seen as indifference. After all, she wasn’t his birth mother."]},{"number":59,"title":"Chapter 59: The Little Devil's Deception","paragraphs":["Xu Wan smiled and replied, \"I am deeply grateful for the trust of my father-in-law and mother-in-law, and even more so for your generous guidance, Master.\"","\"Haha... You're too kind, too kind,\" Baili Xi said, stroking his beard with delight. \"Madam, do you have anything else to discuss today?\"","Xu Wan explained her plan to hire private tutors. Baili Xi raised an eyebrow and asked, \"You want them to continue tutoring Jincheng after my lessons, even on rest days?\"","Xu Wan nodded. \"That boy has boundless energy, and studying after class doesn't tire him out. I initially had someone prepare translations and phonetic notes for difficult characters, but it's still not efficient enough. He needs someone to accompany him at all times.\"","Baili Xi pondered for a moment and found the idea reasonable. \"That's not a bad plan. It will keep him motivated and help him solve problems promptly. I think it's feasible. Bring me the resumes of those candidates, and I'll review them for you now.\"","Xu Wan was pleased. \"Thank you for your trouble, Master.\"","Cui Zhi had already arranged for the resumes to be brought over. Xu Wan handed them to Baili Xi and waited for his evaluation.","Baili Xi quickly skimmed through them and noticed that all five were recent provincial graduates. He realized this was no coincidence. Candidates who had just finished the imperial exams would still have fresh knowledge and exam techniques, making them more effective than those from three years ago.","Once again, Baili Xi was impressed by Xu Wan's thoroughness and gave her an approving look.","Xu Wan smiled and asked, \"Master, what do you think?\"","Baili Xi replied, \"The first resume is falsified. He is not the top graduate from Wenyang County. The actual top graduate from that county is the child of an old friend of mine.\"","\"The second candidate is too old, at sixty-seven. He probably wouldn't be able to keep up with Jincheng's demanding schedule.\"","Xu Wan chuckled. \"That's true.\" The imperial exams were open to candidates of all ages, and this man had achieved his success with gray hair.","\"The remaining three are all good, especially this one from Hanlin Academy. I think he's worth considering more seriously,\" Baili Xi said. \"The teaching methods at the academy are also excellent. Jincheng shouldn't be too isolated while studying at the manor. He should interact with others, discuss exams, and stay informed about current affairs.\"","Xu Wan nodded and reviewed the other two resumes. They were indeed evenly matched. \"They're both quite good. It's hard to decide.\"","Baili Xi agreed but couldn't offer a definitive recommendation, so he left the final decision to Xu Wan.","After a moment of thought, Xu Wan decisively said, \"Then I'll hire all three.\" When you're wealthy, you don't have to choose.","Baili Xi: \"...\"","Sometimes he felt that everyone in the Yangyuan Marquis Manor was quite extravagant.","Xu Wan instructed Cui Zhi to draft the employment contracts and notify the three tutors to come to the manor to sign the agreements and begin their duties on an appointed day.","Meanwhile, in another courtyard, cries of pain echoed.","\"Ouch... it hurts... be gentle...\"","\"My hand... it's swollen like a red carrot... waaah...\"","Zong Jincheng sat on the edge of the bed, extending his hand for the manor physician to apply medicine. Shunzi held his arm to prevent him from moving and worsening the pain.","The teary-eyed little troublemaker looked pitiful, his bright black eyes even more striking, making it hard for anyone to bear seeing him in such a state. It was a mystery how Xu Wan could bring herself to discipline him so harshly.","The physician reassured him, \"Young Master Jincheng, the injury isn't too severe. It's just a bit swollen with some blood streaks. Apply the medicine for a few days, and it will heal. Avoid using your hands during this time, rest well, eat light meals, and don't stay up late...\"","The physician listed a long series of precautions, turning the little troublemaker's hand pain into a headache. He wailed, \"My hand hurts, and now you're telling me to watch my diet and rest? You're even stricter than Xu Wan!\"","The physician: \"...\" These are just standard medical instructions!","But with the little troublemaker in a foul mood, the physician didn't dare argue. Zong Wenxiu signaled that he could leave, and the physician quickly grabbed his medical kit and fled.","The little troublemaker's hands were wrapped in white bandages, turning them from red carrots to white ones, resembling two big clubs.","He flopped backward onto the bed, kicking his legs and shouting, \"Xu Wan, Xu Wan, Xu Wan! I hate her!!... Ouch!\" In his emotional outburst, he accidentally hit his hand on the bed frame.","\"Brother!\" Zong Wenxiu hurried over to help him up and checked to make sure his hand wasn't bleeding.","Hearing this, Zong Jincheng became even more aggrieved and cried out, \"Don't call me brother! I thought of you as my real brother, but you sided with Xu Wan. Not only did you not shield me from the punishment, you didn't even try to stop her!\"","Shunzi stood to the side, his lips twitching. The young master really had high expectations—not only wanting someone to stop the punishment but also to take the hit for him.","Zong Wenxiu paused, lowered his head, and said, \"I'm sorry. I can't defy Madam. I... I... Next time, I'll definitely shield you!\"","The little troublemaker snorted. \"There won't be a next time. Next time, I'll be the one hitting Xu Wan's hand!\"","Shunzi: \"...\" Even Buyan would be speechless at this.","Hitting Madam's hand? Who do you think you are?","You'll probably end up being hung up and beaten by Madam...","Buyan entered the room. \"Young Master, the medicine is ready.\"","\"What? I have to drink medicine too?\" The little troublemaker wilted like a frostbitten eggplant.","Zong Wenxiu understood and took the medicine bowl, comforting him, \"Using both external and internal treatments will help you recover faster. Shunzi, bring some candied fruit.\"","\"Yes, right away.\"","The little troublemaker reluctantly opened his mouth, waiting for his brother to feed him.","The medicine was spooned into his mouth, bitter but bearable with the candied fruit.","Zong Wenxiu was very patient, testing the temperature before feeding him, wiping his mouth after each sip, and even picking the largest pieces of candied fruit for him.","This wasn't the first time the little troublemaker had been fed medicine, but it had been a long time since he'd experienced such care. It felt warm and comforting, just like when his grandparents were in the manor, focusing all their attention on him.","It had been months since he last saw his grandparents, and Zong Jincheng missed them dearly. His eyes began to redden at the thought.","Zong Wenxiu quickly asked, \"What's wrong, Jincheng? Is the medicine too bitter? I'll get you more candied fruit.\"","\"Brother,\" Zong Jincheng called out softly, his voice filled with pitiful longing.","Zong Wenxiu paused. This was the second time his brother had called him \"brother,\" and he felt a surge of familial affection, as if he had finally been accepted.","The little troublemaker frowned and murmured, \"You owe me this time, so I forgive you. But don't help Xu Wan bully me anymore. Xu Wan only asked you to repay her by accompanying me in my studies, nothing else.\"","Zong Wenxiu thought about it and realized that was true. His brother had also been part of the group that saved their mother, so he shouldn't side with Madam against him.","\"Alright,\" he agreed. \"From now on, I'll always stand by you.\"","Zong Jincheng's eyes lit up, and his voice grew louder. \"Really? You're not lying to me?\"","Zong Wenxiu replied earnestly, \"Really. I'll do everything in my power to protect you.\"","Shunzi, standing behind them: \"...\"","Great, the little troublemaker has tricked another one. Carry him away."]},{"number":60,"title":"Chapter 60: Mother and Son Face Off Again","paragraphs":["Zong Jincheng immediately smiled with great satisfaction.","As expected, his charm was still unmatched, and now his mood was even better. He sweetly called out, \"Brother, I want to eat candied dates and seven-flavor cakes.\"","\"I'll have someone buy them for you. They'll be back soon.\"","\"Brother, I also want to go outside and bask in the sun. Can you carry me there?\"","\"Sure, I'll carry you.\"","Shunzi: \"...\"","He really wanted to shout like Madam Xu Wan: Don’t you have legs of your own??","But when the Little Demon King acted sweet and spoiled, no one could resist him except Xu Wan. Even the Old Marquis and Old Marchioness, who had raised two outstanding sons, had fallen under the spell of this boy, watching helplessly as he grew into a mischievous troublemaker.","Outside the house, the two brothers were enjoying themselves—one comfortably squinting in the sunlight, while the other busily served tea and water.","Zong Jincheng lounged on the chair, completely at ease, and instructed, \"Buyan, go ask Steward Liu to bring another recliner for my brother.\"","\"Yes.\"","The Little Demon King added, \"Make sure to tell Steward Liu that the recliner should stay here permanently. My brother will often come to sunbathe with me!\"","\"Yes.\"","Earlier, Xu Wan had ordered all the valuable items in the Little Demon King’s courtyard to be removed, leaving only one recliner. But now, since it was for Zong Wenxiu, Steward Liu wouldn’t refuse.","Zong Wenxiu was also delighted, his eyes nearly disappearing into a smile. He said gently, \"Brother, since you can’t write these days, I’ll bring the books you need to read and have Shunzi read them aloud for you to memorize.\"","\"Okay,\" Zong Jincheng replied with a squinting smile.","For the next few days, the Little Demon King didn’t study in his own courtyard. Instead, he insisted on being carried by Buyan to the large study to read with Zong Wenxiu.","The way he clung to his brother, calling him \"Brother\" repeatedly, made Xu Wan’s skin crawl. She asked Cui Zhi, \"Was he like this with the Old Marchioness too?\"","Cui Zhi chuckled, \"Yes, the Old Marchioness couldn’t resist him. Whatever the Little Young Master asked for, she would give it to him.\"","Xu Wan’s face was filled with confusion.","She glanced through the window at the overly attentive Little Demon King and still felt something was off. \"There’s always a reason for unusual behavior. Keep an eye on Wenxiu to make sure Jincheng isn’t scheming something behind his back.\"","\"Ah? You mean Young Master Jincheng might be using Young Master Wenxiu for something...\" Cui Zhi widened her eyes, finding it hard to believe.","Her Young Master Jincheng was indeed clever and sharp, but he was only eight years old. Surely he couldn’t... could he?","Xu Wan snorted, \"I don’t know what he’s up to, but it’s definitely no good. Keep watching him and report anything unusual to me.\"","\"Yes, yes...\"","Before leaving, Cui Zhi took another look at Zong Jincheng.","Nothing seemed wrong—he acted the same way he did with the Old Marchioness, except this time it had been going on for a while...","Wait! It had been going on for too long!","Whenever the Little Demon King acted spoiled with the Old Marchioness, it was always because he wanted something. Once he got it, he wouldn’t be so clingy.","But he had been clinging to Zong Wenxiu for several days now.","There was definitely something going on!!!","That afternoon, Zong Wenxiu was sunbathing in Zong Jincheng’s courtyard while Zong Jincheng waited inside for Shunzi.","Shunzi came in and said, \"Young Master, the lychees have been washed.\" He glanced at Zong Wenxiu outside, trying to signal him, but Zong Wenxiu was too absorbed in the sunlight to notice.","Afraid Shunzi might ruin his plan, Zong Jincheng quickly said, \"You and Buyan go to the kitchen and make me some scallion pancakes. I want both of you to make them together.\"","Shunzi: \"...Yes.\"","Neither he nor Buyan had ever stepped foot in the kitchen. Making pancakes together? The Little Young Master was clearly trying to get rid of them. Poor Zong Wenxiu was about to fall into a trap.","Unable to bear it, Shunzi whispered, \"Young Master, this isn’t right. If Madam finds out, it’ll harm Young Master Wenxiu.\"","Zong Jincheng glared at him and said, \"If Xu Wan finds out, I’ll take the blame and clear his name. At most, I’ll get another beating. I won’t drag him into this.\"","Shunzi urged, \"But... why go through all this trouble just to get beaten again?\"","Zong Jincheng snorted, \"Don’t worry about it. Even if I have to suffer, I’ll make sure Xu Wan pays for it too!\"","\"Now, you and Buyan get out of here. Go, go, don’t get in my way!\" Zong Jincheng nudged him with his elbow.","Shunzi looked reluctantly at his young master’s still-injured hand, thinking that by the time they returned, another part of him might be wrapped up like a white radish.","\"Brother, come in and have some lychees. They’re chilled!\" Zong Jincheng called out.","On the table were two plates of chilled lychees.","As soon as Zong Wenxiu entered, Zong Jincheng said, \"I want the bigger plate.\"","Both plates were similar in size, but the one Zong Jincheng pointed to had a particularly large lychee on top. Zong Wenxiu picked it up and said, \"Let me peel this one for you.\"","After peeling it, he fed it to Zong Jincheng, who ate it happily.","Zong Wenxiu said, \"It’s still early summer. If we eat all these chilled lychees, we might get stomachaches.\"","Zong Jincheng nodded, \"Shunzi made a mistake. He said this plate was originally meant for Xu Wan. I don’t want to give it to her, so I’m keeping it.\"","Zong Wenxiu hummed in acknowledgment but didn’t say anything.","The Little Demon King grew anxious.","Why aren’t you saying anything? Why aren’t you telling me not to hog the lychees? Speak up!","But no matter how much the Little Demon King’s mind raced, it was useless. Zong Wenxiu was focused on pleasing his brother and didn’t want to upset him.","After all, there were more chilled lychees in the kitchen. They could always prepare another batch.","But since Zong Wenxiu didn’t speak up, Zong Jincheng couldn’t hold back. These chilled lychees were actually spoiled ones he had asked Shunzi to prepare days ago. The chilling masked their taste, so by the time Xu Wan realized, she would have eaten enough to get a stomachache!","Hmph, that wicked woman dared to slap my hand three times. Now she’ll face my revenge!","Pretending to have reformed, Zong Jincheng said, \"I’ve thought about it, and I’ll let her have the lychees. Even though she hit me, I was in the wrong first. I admit it.\"","Zong Wenxiu’s eyes lit up with pride. \"Brother, you’ve grown up.\"","Zong Jincheng smiled innocently on the surface.","But in his heart, he thought, Grown up? Even if I was wrong, she shouldn’t have slapped my hand over such a small matter. She’s just looking for excuses to hit me!","Zong Jincheng said with a sweet smile, \"Then you can take the lychees to her. They’ll melt soon.\"","\"What do you want Wenxiu to bring me? I’ll come and get it myself,\" Xu Wan said as she walked in, her eyes narrowing as she stared at the two plates of lychees."]},{"number":61,"title":"Chapter 61: Caught Red-Handed","paragraphs":["Cui Zhi covered her face, almost too afraid to open her eyes.","Young Master Cheng had gone too far this time—not only did he try to harm Madam with spoiled lychees, but he also had Young Master Xiu deliver them.","This was clearly a recipe for disaster.","Zong Wenxiu, unaware of the situation, stood up to defend his younger brother: \"Madam, my brother knows he was wrong and holds no grudge against you. He even asked me to deliver the mistakenly picked lychees to you.\"","Zong Jincheng was so nervous he kept fidgeting with his hands.","But his hands were still as pale as white radishes, and every pinch hurt like hell.","He hissed in pain and instinctively stood up from the table, eyeing her warily.","Xu Wan looked at the lychees and smiled. \"This year's lychees are quite good. I see there’s a particularly large one here. Let’s pick it out for Jincheng to try.\"","Zong Jincheng’s face turned green.","Who would want to eat that spoiled lychee, especially the biggest one!","Zong Wenxiu responded, \"Alright, I’ll pick it out and peel it for my brother to eat later.\"","Xu Wan smiled sweetly. \"Why wait? Peel it now. I’ll watch him eat it.\"","Zong Jincheng: \"!\"","This woman... did she know?","The air grew tense, and the room was so quiet you could hear a pin drop.","Zong Jincheng watched helplessly as his brother peeled the spoiled, largest lychee and brought it to his lips.","The little devil refused to open his mouth.","Xu Wan asked with a smile, \"Why aren’t you eating? Do you dislike Wenxiu feeding you? Should I do it instead?\"","Zong Jincheng glanced sideways and swatted the spoiled lychee away with his arm, angrily retorting, \"I don’t want to eat that lychee! I don’t like big ones, is that a crime?\"","\"Of course not. Wenxiu, peel a smaller one for him,\" Xu Wan instructed, adding, \"Oh, and make sure it’s from the plate meant for me.\"","At this point, not only did the little devil understand, but even Zong Wenxiu sensed something was off.","He looked at his brother and Madam in confusion. \"What’s wrong with this plate of lychees?\"","To him, the two plates looked identical, with no noticeable difference or strange smell.","Xu Wan smiled and said, \"Ask your dear brother who served them to you.\"","Seeing that his scheme had been exposed, Zong Jincheng didn’t want Zong Wenxiu to take the blame for him. He admitted fiercely but honestly, \"Yes, this plate is the spoiled lychees I prepared for you. You can’t eat them!\"","Zong Wenxiu looked at him in shock. \"Spoiled lychees... You wanted to make Madam sick?\"","Xu Wan snorted. \"If you’re upset with me, fine, but why involve Wenxiu? Do you know what his life in this household is like? If something had happened to me, do you realize the gossip and rumors he would face?\"","Zong Jincheng snapped, \"Stop yelling! I’m the one who did it. I knew you wouldn’t eat the lychees if I sent them, so I tricked him into delivering them. I’ll take full responsibility. Punish me however you want, but leave him out of it!\"","\"You tricked me?\" Zong Wenxiu looked at him.","Though the ten-year-old boy was slightly taller, his clear eyes now held a hint of hurt. He couldn’t accept being used by his younger brother.","Zong Wenxiu lowered his head, his eyes red as he apologized to Xu Wan. \"I’m sorry, Madam. I almost harmed you... Punish me however you see fit. Whether it’s spanking my hands or my back, I’ll accept it without complaint.\"","Xu Wan patted his shoulder, comforting him. \"You were just too honest and got tricked. It’s not your fault. Go back, and stay away from this kid so he can’t deceive you again.\"","\"Okay,\" Zong Wenxiu choked back a sob, not even glancing at Zong Jincheng before turning and leaving.","\"I... I didn’t mean to make you take the blame!\" Zong Jincheng wanted to chase after him, but Cui Zhi stopped him.","Madam wasn’t done settling accounts with Young Master Cheng yet.","Zong Jincheng growled, \"Why are you telling him to stay away from me? He’s my brother, not yours!\"","Xu Wan scoffed. \"Please, with the way you used him, you should be ashamed to even call him your brother. I feel embarrassed for you.\"","\"You!\"","\"Zong Jincheng, I know you’re clever and full of mischief. I also know you’ve been spoiled rotten and no one’s ever taught you this, so I’ll spell it out for you today: You hurt Wenxiu.\"","\"What did I do?\" Zong Jincheng didn’t understand, his voice tinged with frustration. \"I didn’t make him take the blame for me. How many times do I have to say it before you—\"","\"But you used him,\" Xu Wan interrupted. \"He sees you as family, but you treated him like a tool to achieve your own ends, tricking him into doing something he would despise.\"","\"I... I didn’t.\"","Xu Wan ordered the spoiled lychees to be thrown away and continued, \"People are different. What you see as a harmless prank might be a serious breach of someone else’s morals. You’ve been studying the classics for months now, and it’s not just rote memorization anymore. Don’t you understand that?\"","Zong Jincheng didn’t understand.","Or rather, he saw books as books and people as people. He was used to acting recklessly without considering others’ feelings. As long as he was in the mood, he would act out, never caring if others were upset. His own happiness was all that mattered.","Xu Wan’s lecture only half-registered with him. He felt both annoyed and uneasy.","The little rascal glared at her defiantly. \"Are you done? If you’re going to punish me, just get on with it!\"","Xu Wan smiled. \"Punish you? You’re not afraid of being punished now?\"","The little devil snorted. \"Because I’m strong-willed and mentally tough. You can only beat my body, but you can’t break my spirit! I’ll remember every bit of this, and one day, I’ll make you pay for it all!\"","Xu Wan stared at the boy’s resolute expression, unfazed. Originally, he was definitely due for a beating today, but Xu Wan decided against it.","If a child gets used to being punished, the punishment loses its impact. She couldn’t rely solely on physical discipline to teach him.","So, she smiled again, patting the little devil’s cheek like a wicked queen. \"Kid, I won’t punish you today, but you’ll have to face the consequences.\"","The little devil brushed her hand away, rolling his eyes. \"Whatever, stop pretending to be nice. You’ll never redeem yourself in my eyes!\"","Xu Wan snorted. \"Cui Zhi, let’s go.\"","\"Huh? Oh... okay.\" Cui Zhi was baffled.","Wasn’t the plan to teach Young Master Cheng to take responsibility, even without punishment?","How was he supposed to learn?","Madam had left—who was going to teach him?","But Cui Zhi’s confusion was soon cleared up when a servant came to report: Young Master Xiu had volunteered to kneel in the ancestral hall.","Zong Jincheng was a bit dazed by Xu Wan’s sudden departure. As soon as they left, Shunzi and Buyan returned with a plate of charred scallion pancakes. \"Young Master, the pancakes are ready.\"","Zong Jincheng glanced at the blackened mess and snapped, \"Are you two trying to poison someone?\"","Buyan: \"...\"","Shunzi said sheepishly, \"Young Master, neither of us has ever been in the kitchen. At least these are cooked...\"","\"Enough, enough,\" Zong Jincheng stood up. \"Zong Wenxiu is upset. I’m going to find him.\"","\"Huh?\" Shunzi looked at the table, where only one plate of lychees remained. \"Did Young Master Xiu discover the plan before we could deliver them?\""]},{"number":62,"title":"Chapter 62: Brothers Kneeling Together in the Ancestral Hall","paragraphs":["“It was Xu Wan who exposed it!” Zong Jincheng couldn’t understand how Xu Wan had found out so quickly and so clearly!","Shunzi panicked and immediately started checking him over, asking, “Did you get hit? Why are there no marks? Were you hit somewhere not visible? Or maybe she used needles? I’ve heard that’s both cruel and hard to detect!”","“Get out of my way,” Zong Jincheng brushed him off irritably, holding his head high as he marched toward Zong Wenxiu’s courtyard.","But he arrived to find it empty.","Upon hearing that Zong Wenxiu was kneeling in the ancestral hall, Zong Jincheng stormed off in a rage, shouting as he ran, “Xu Wan! You’re blaming the wrong person!!”","His shouts echoed through the Marquis Manor, causing the maids and servants to turn their heads, some even covering their mouths to stifle their laughter. It seemed Young Master Cheng had been disciplined by the Madam again.","The manor was certainly lively these days.","In the ancestral hall, Zong Wenxiu knelt inside. Hearing the commotion at the door, he turned his head and saw his younger brother’s furious expression. His own emotions were complicated.","Nevertheless, he defended the Madam, saying, “The Madam didn’t punish me. I came here on my own. When you do something wrong, you must take responsibility.”","Zong Jincheng was stunned. “What did you do wrong? I was the one who prepared those bad lychees to trick Xu Wan. Besides, you didn’t even serve them to her yet. Why are you taking all the blame?”","Zong Wenxiu shook his head solemnly. “It’s only because the Madam is wise and noticed something was wrong in time that she stopped what could have happened. If she hadn’t arrived when she did, I would have already taken that plate of lychees to her and made her sick. Even if you were the mastermind, I was still an accomplice—a executioner.”","“An executioner...?” Zong Jincheng’s head was spinning. Wasn’t that someone who carried out executions?","Such a metaphor was too difficult for a pampered young master like him to grasp.","Zong Wenxiu didn’t explain further and continued kneeling, his posture straight and unwavering.","Zong Jincheng frowned and asked, “How long are you going to kneel?”","“A full day and night.”","Zong Jincheng was shocked. “What about sleep? Can you even sleep while kneeling?”","Zong Wenxiu replied calmly, “If this is about atonement, how can I think about my own comfort? I won’t sleep.”","“You...” Zong Jincheng was speechless. “I’ve never seen anyone so eager to torture themselves!”","The little troublemaker turned and left. If Zong Wenxiu wanted to kneel, let him kneel! He certainly wasn’t going to join him!","And staying up all night? He wouldn’t even kneel for a full day!","He stormed out of the ancestral hall, even angrier than when he had arrived. Shunzi hurried after him and asked, “Young Master, did Master Wenxiu refuse to come out with you?”","Zong Jincheng snapped, “Of course he didn’t! That pedantic bookworm has lost his mind from reading too much. Even Jing Zhe is smarter than him!”","Shunzi was at a loss. “Then... what should we do?”","“I don’t know, and I don’t care!” The little troublemaker was still fuming.","Shunzi tried to reason with him. “But Master Wenxiu is punishing himself because of you. Are you really just going to leave him like this?”","Zong Jincheng retorted, “What else am I supposed to do? Kneel in the ancestral hall for a day and night like that bookworm? I’d have to be kicked in the head by a donkey to do that!”","Shunzi: “...” Well, that’s more like the heartless young master we know.","Zong Jincheng turned and strode out of the courtyard, but his steps grew smaller and slower until he finally came to a halt.","Shunzi, following closely behind, almost bumped into him and quickly veered to the side, only to lose his balance and fall flat on the ground with a thud.","“Ow...” Shunzi’s cry of pain went unnoticed.","Zong Jincheng turned and ran back.","He ran faster and faster, his strides growing larger until he burst into the ancestral hall, sweating and panting, and dropped to his knees on the cushion with a loud thud.","“Thump—”","The sound was so startling that Shunzi forgot about the pain in his backside.","From the doorway, he stared in disbelief at the blur that had just rushed past and the little troublemaker now kneeling inside. His mind was in turmoil!","Didn’t he just say he’d have to be kicked in the head by a donkey to kneel?","Was he really kicked by a donkey...?","Zong Wenxiu was also startled and turned to look. “You... why are you here?”","Zong Jincheng, still angry, knelt with his arms crossed, exuding an air of superiority. “If my accomplice and executioner are kneeling, shouldn’t I, the mastermind, save face too?”","Zong Wenxiu: “...”","Well, that made sense, but...","“You can go back to sleep after kneeling until evening. The ancestral hall gets too cold at night.”","Zong Jincheng snorted. “I’ll leave when you leave.”","Zong Wenxiu couldn’t leave. He said, “Then have Shunzi bring you a blanket.”","Zong Jincheng: “!”","That pedantic bookworm!","Couldn’t he just take the opportunity to leave with me at night?","Zong Jincheng was both angry and frustrated. He snorted and turned his face away.","But Zong Wenxiu didn’t say anything more. The ancestral hall was filled with the tablets of ancestors, so quiet that they could hear the birds chirping outside and the occasional gasps of the maids passing by.","After kneeling for just half an hour, Zong Jincheng was already fidgeting, scratching his hands and playing with his hair. He had already memorized the names of all hundred-plus ancestors of the Zong family, and there was nothing interesting to look at or play with in the ancestral hall. It was so boring.","“Hey, are you bored?” Zong Jincheng asked.","Zong Wenxiu, hearing the term “hey,” felt a pang of sadness. He asked, “Were you only calling me ‘brother’ these past few days to get me to deliver the lychees today?”","“I...” Zong Jincheng blinked.","He hadn’t thought about that.","When he used to sweet-talk his grandmother, he would call her “dearest grandmother” or “the best grandmother in the world,” but he couldn’t do that every day—it was too sappy.","Calling Zong Wenxiu “brother” was... well, it was for the lychees. After all, strictly speaking, he was only his cousin. It wasn’t like they were that close.","But looking at Zong Wenxiu’s expression, it seemed like he was even more hurt than when Xu Wan had exposed their scheme.","Why was he hurt?","Because I stopped calling him “brother”?","Before the little troublemaker could figure it out, Zong Wenxiu stopped asking. It seemed he had already assumed the answer.","But he also stopped engaging with Zong Jincheng.","Zong Jincheng started to feel uneasy.","What’s going on? Is he mad at me? But I even came to kneel with him in the ancestral hall. Why is he still mad at me? Is there no justice in this world??","Zong Jincheng tilted his head, thinking for a while but still couldn’t understand why. In the end, his body reacted before his mind could.","In the silence of the ancestral hall, he heard himself tentatively call out, “Brother?”"]},{"number":63,"title":"Chapter 63: Ancestral Hall Endorsement, Ancestors Are Speechless","paragraphs":["Zong Wenxiu paused, turned to look at him, his eyes filled with confusion.","\"Brother,\" Zong Jincheng called out again.","The little troublemaker was never stingy with words, and it was his natural instinct to make others like him. Even before his mind could fully process things, his mouth and body had already taken the first step.","However, Zong Wenxiu didn’t seem particularly pleased.","He still ignored the little troublemaker, not even responding, just staring at him with a probing gaze.","Zong Jincheng didn’t know what he was looking at. He grabbed the cushion under his knees and shuffled closer to him, then asked, \"Brother, are you still mad at me?\"","Zong Wenxiu’s gaze was complicated as he asked, \"What do you want me to do for you?\"","\"What?\" Zong Jincheng was taken aback.","Zong Wenxiu repeated, \"I said, you’re calling me ‘brother.’ What do you want me to do for you this time?\"","Zong Jincheng: \"...\"","It felt like a silent slap across his face.","Zong Jincheng was someone who cared deeply about his pride.","Angrily, he shuffled back to his original spot on the cushion.","The little troublemaker’s cheeks puffed up in anger. His body, already tired from kneeling for half an hour, now straightened up again due to his frustration.","As if unable to contain his anger, he glanced at Zong Wenxiu and glared at him. Seeing that the other still ignored him, he turned his head back, his chest heaving with indignation.","The little troublemaker thought: If I say another word to him, I’ll be a little turtle!","However, not even a quarter of an hour later.","The little troublemaker shuffled back over, intentionally bumping into Zong Wenxiu as if seeking attention. If he didn’t get a reaction the first time, he’d bump him again.","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","He couldn’t take it anymore. \"What exactly do you want?\"","Zong Jincheng immediately perked up.","Hmph, he’s the one who spoke to me first.","So that doesn’t count as being a little turtle!","His dark eyes blinked as he pulled out the script he’d prepared in his mind, raising his hand to declare, \"First of all, I didn’t mean to hurt you on purpose.\"","Afraid that Zong Wenxiu wouldn’t believe him, he added, \"Really, I just got my hands smacked by Xu Wan the other day, and I was so angry and in pain that I didn’t think it through. I didn’t expect you to take it so seriously... Oh, no, I mean I didn’t expect you to be so upset. If I’d known, I would’ve done it myself.\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","He admitted his mistake, but it didn’t seem like he truly understood it.","Thinking about having to deal with such a brother, Zong Wenxiu felt a headache coming on for Xu Wan.","Zong Wenxiu asked, \"Do you really think it’s not your fault for retaliating against Xu Wan like that?\"","\"I... I did something wrong...\" Zong Jincheng said stubbornly, \"But she hit me too, so she’s also at fault.\"","Deep down, he knew he deserved the smacking, but he just couldn’t get over it. The little troublemaker had never been hit before in his life, and it was a blow to both his pride and his heart, which made it even harder for him to admit it.","Zong Wenxiu was silent for a few seconds before asking, \"Will you still mess with Baili Fuzi after this?\"","Zong Jincheng raised his white hand and waved it, \"Do I dare?\"","\"Is it that you don’t dare, or that you don’t want to?\"","Zong Jincheng frowned, \"Why are you so insistent on getting to the bottom of this today? What’s the difference between not daring and not wanting to?\"","Zong Wenxiu said, \"Not daring is because you’re afraid of punishment, not wanting to is out of respect for your teacher. Of course, they’re different. Baili Fuzi is at an age where he should be enjoying his retirement, yet he’s willingly come to our household to teach us without charging a single penny. He’s poured his heart and soul into this, and yet you’ve repaid him with pranks. Do you think you’ve treated him fairly?\"","\"I...\" Zong Jincheng’s face turned red.","At the time, he’d only been thinking about how interesting Baili Fuzi’s beard looked, and he’d been fascinated by the colorful inks. Driven by curiosity, he’d wanted to try painting them on. He hadn’t thought much about it, let alone considered how it might hurt Baili Fuzi’s feelings.","Now, after hearing Zong Wenxiu’s words, he felt like a terrible person.","Zong Jincheng’s big head drooped down like a dejected little lion, his lips pouting unhappily.","Zong Wenxiu asked him again, \"Do you still think those three smacks were too much?\"","Zong Jincheng muttered to himself in frustration, \"It wasn’t enough.\"","Seeing him like this, Zong Wenxiu couldn’t help but chuckle. He reached out and ruffled his younger brother’s soft hair, advising, \"From now on, don’t try to harm Xu Wan anymore. She’s only doing what’s best for you.\"","\"Got it...\" Then, Zong Jincheng looked up at him in confusion, \"Is that all you wanted to say to me?\"","\"What else is there?\"","Zong Jincheng thought, he’d just told him not to mess with Baili Fuzi or Xu Wan anymore, but what about himself?","\"Aren’t you going to tell me not to lie to you anymore?\"","Zong Wenxiu laughed, \"Will you still lie to me?\"","Zong Jincheng quickly shook his head, \"You’re my brother. I’ll never lie to you again!\"","Zong Wenxiu smiled.","Seeing him smile, Zong Jincheng smiled too.","The last rays of the setting sun shone into the ancestral hall, illuminating the two reconciled brothers, casting a warm glow over them.","It was the little troublemaker who broke the silence first, \"Brother, kneeling like this is so boring. Why don’t we recite some books instead?\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"??\"","Was this really his brother’s suggestion? He could still think about studying at a time like this?","Zong Jincheng, seeing his surprised look, pouted, \"Can’t I think about studying? Even though Qin Ye, that loser, will definitely lose to me, becoming the top scholar is still hard. I need to work harder and memorize more.\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","Confirmed, it was still the same overconfident brother.","After thinking for a moment, he said, \"Then let’s start with the ‘Meng Qiu.’ You’ve probably already learned this, so we’ll review it together.\"","\"Okay.\"","\"Wang Rong was concise, Pei Kai was clear and thorough. Kong Ming was the sleeping dragon, Lü Wang was no ordinary bear. Yang Zhen was from west of the pass, Ding Kuan was from east of the Yi...\"","Outside the ancestral hall.","Xu Wan watched the two brothers reciting together, one hand on her forehead, unable to suppress a smile.","Cui Zhi was both amused and exasperated, \"Young Master Wenxiu really loves studying. Even while kneeling in the ancestral hall, he doesn’t forget his books, and he’s even getting Young Master Jincheng to recite with him. A good example has a strong influence.\"","Xu Wan’s brow furrowed with three question marks as she turned to ask, \"You think Wenxiu started it?\"","\"Isn’t... isn’t that the case...\" Cui Zhi said, \"Young Master Jincheng doesn’t seem like the type to study on his own...\"","Xu Wan chuckled, \"The ancestors of the Zong family were all military generals who hated these wordy books. Their descendants come here to be punished, yet they’re reciting books right in front of them. Do you really think Wenxiu would be the one to start such an absurd thing?\"","Cui Zhi: \"...\"","It was better not to think too deeply about it, or else one could feel the ancestors’ despair.","The ancestors’ despair lasted from the afternoon until the evening.","By midnight, Xu Wan was still awake. Hearing from Cui Zhi that the two children were still in the ancestral hall, she couldn’t sleep.","\"I’ll go check on them.\"","When Xu Wan arrived outside the ancestral hall, she didn’t hear any reciting. Worried that the children might have fallen asleep, and knowing how cold the ancestral hall could get at night, she quickened her steps.","Upon entering, she saw Zong Wenxiu still kneeling upright, his lips moving silently as if reciting passages to stay awake, his posture as proper as a model student.","As for the little rascal, he was already sprawled out on the cushion, fast asleep. His own cushion wasn’t enough, so he’d squeezed onto Zong Wenxiu’s, leaving the other with barely any space.","Xu Wan couldn’t help but feel both annoyed and amused, completely at a loss with this boy."]},{"number":64,"title":"Chapter 64: Who Gives You the Confidence","paragraphs":["She turned to Cui Zhi and said, “Tell Buyan to take Zong Jincheng back to sleep.”","“Yes.”","Zong Wenxiu heard her voice and looked over, greeting her softly, “Madam.”","Xu Wan smiled at him.","Buyan picked up Zong Jincheng, letting the boy’s arms rest on his shoulders and his head nestle against his neck. The little troublemaker drowsily opened his eyes, catching a glimpse of a blurry female figure, but the weight of sleep was too much, and he clung to Buyan, drifting back into slumber.","After the little rascal was gone, Xu Wan remained where she was.","Zong Wenxiu was somewhat surprised. He had assumed that the madam had come to fetch his younger brother, as she was his stepmother.","Xu Wan walked over, helped him up, and said with a smile, “Come on, get up. With your stubborn nature, if the ancestors saw you like this, they’d think I was a cruel aunt, bullying a child.”","Zong Wenxiu had been kneeling for too long, and when he stood up abruptly, he wobbled unsteadily. Xu Wan steadied him and had him sit on the prayer cushion until the numbness in his legs subsided.","She then sat down on Zong Jincheng’s cushion, aligning her gaze with Zong Wenxiu’s. Between adults and children, there is a gap in age and height, but when their eyes meet at the same level, the relationship feels much closer.","Zong Wenxiu had never felt as close to the madam as he did at that moment, as if she were a good friend, making him feel at ease both physically and emotionally.","Xu Wan said, “All this trouble was caused by Jincheng. I know it’s hard for you to let it go, but don’t dwell on it too much. Otherwise, following this little troublemaker, you’ll be kneeling in the ancestral hall forever.”","Zong Wenxiu chuckled awkwardly, “That won’t happen, Madam. Jincheng just promised me that he won’t prank the teacher anymore, won’t cause you any trouble, and won’t lie to me again.”","Xu Wan smiled, “That’s indeed the best outcome. But knowing that little troublemaker, there are more than just three kinds of mischief in this world.”","Zong Wenxiu: “...”","The glimmer of hope he had just seen was instantly snuffed out.","Seeing his stunned expression, Xu Wan couldn’t help but laugh and reminded him, “Of course, don’t be too pessimistic. At least these three things are important. Once he fixes these, the rest will be easier.”","Hearing this, Zong Wenxiu breathed a sigh of relief and smiled, “Yes, my brother is very smart. He grasps things quickly. He’s just stubborn and soft-hearted. He might say harsh things, but his actions are always good. Otherwise, he wouldn’t have come to kneel in the ancestral hall with me.”","Xu Wan smiled, “Yes, smart. His intelligence is both a blessing and a curse. Such children are a mix of love and frustration, and raising them requires a lot of mental effort.”","In truth, she had met a child like Zong Jincheng before, one whose intelligence and emotional maturity far surpassed his peers, even leaving many adults in awe. But such children are harder to guide than ordinary ones. They have an insatiable curiosity, a restless mind, and a knack for causing trouble. Yet, adults often try to educate them using conventional methods, leading to more and more chaos.","Xu Wan recalled the last time she saw that child—in a police station visitation room. He was sixteen, arrested for breaking and entering. He smiled innocently at her and said, “Don’t you think this is fun?”","Xu Wan closed her eyes, refusing to dwell on the memory.","Now, encountering another overly intelligent child, she didn’t want to see him go down the wrong path again.","Zong Wenxiu spoke up at the right moment, “Madam, I also want to help my brother stay on the right path.”","Xu Wan smiled, “You’re already helping him. Today’s outcome is largely thanks to you. Because you were here, because I know your character, and because I know you can influence him, I chose not to punish him. Staying on the right path doesn’t always require force; the influence of those around you is also crucial. In your books of wisdom, it’s called ‘one takes on the color of one’s company,’ right?”","Zong Wenxiu was momentarily stunned, then smiled, “Yes.”","Xu Wan patted his shoulder and helped him up, “Let’s go, it’s time to sleep. Tomorrow, you two have to go to Qingbo Academy to check the results of the Four Academies Joint Exam. Don’t oversleep.”","Zong Wenxiu, reminded of this, felt a pang of worry despite his earlier relief, “My brother seems very confident that he’ll outperform Qin Ye...”","Xu Wan snorted, “Not just that. Didn’t he also boast about taking first place in the Four Academies Joint Exam?”","Zong Wenxiu chuckled, “He’ll have his chance in the future.”","“Well, let’s see if he cries tomorrow,” Xu Wan said with a hint of nostalgia, “Actually, Jincheng looks quite adorable when he cries, with his round face and tearful eyes... It’s a shame he doesn’t cry often. What a pity.”","Zong Wenxiu: “...”","The madam has quite the peculiar taste, actually enjoying seeing his brother cry.","The next morning, the little troublemaker woke up and immediately demanded that the bandage on his hand be removed.","After a few days of care, his hand, which wasn’t seriously injured to begin with, had almost healed. However, the young master was quite pampered, yelping every time the medicine was applied and insisting that the physician wrap it thickly, afraid that even the slightest bump would cause pain.","Shunzi asked, “Young Master, there’s still a small part that hasn’t fully healed. Should we wrap it with a smaller bandage?”","Zong Jincheng pushed him away with his arm and refused, “No, no! It looks terrible. How can the genius who’s going to take first place in the Four Academies Joint Exam have his hand wrapped up like a dumpling?”","Shunzi: “...”","The results aren’t even out yet, and you’re already calling yourself the top scorer. Where on earth did you get such confidence?","The results of the Four Academies Joint Exam were posted at each academy, so Xu Wan took the two boys to Qingbo Academy early in the morning. How could she miss out on checking the results?","If the little troublemaker failed and decided to cause a scene at the academy, she’d need to be there to mediate.","Qingbo Academy was bustling with activity early in the morning. Before even entering, they could hear the students inside shouting:","“They made it! Two students from the eight-year-old class made it onto the Four Academies Joint Exam ranking list! That’s the top 120 in the entire capital!!!”","“The top scorer in the Four Academies Joint Exam is from our Qingbo Academy!!! This is incredible!!!”","“Heavens! Our academy’s reputation as the eternal fourth is finally being washed away!!”","“Quick, quick! Set off the firecrackers! Hang up the banners!!!”","“...”","As Xu Wan and the two brothers got out of the carriage, they were greeted by the lively commotion inside. She picked out the key details and raised an eyebrow, “Two eight-year-olds made the list, and one of them took first place in the Four Academies Joint Exam.”","Zong Jincheng declared confidently, “It must be me!”","Although Qin Ye probably also made the list, it was surely by luck. As for him, Zong Jincheng—smart, hardworking, and talented—he was the only one capable of surpassing the students of the capital’s three prestigious academies!"]},{"number":65,"title":"Chapter 65: Jincheng Learns to Speak","paragraphs":["Zong Wenxiu rubbed his forehead, feeling a headache coming on.","He was hesitating whether to give his younger brother a heads-up to avoid disappointment later.","But then he turned to look at his wife, Xu Wan, who was trying hard to suppress her laughter.","\"...\" She was clearly enjoying her brother-in-law's antics again.","Zong Jincheng, completely oblivious, walked cheerfully into the academy.","On the way, he ran into some students who knew him, and they warmly congratulated him: \"Congratulations, Jincheng! You’re one of the two hopes of our academy!\"","\"Yeah, yeah! Who would’ve thought you’d perform so well against three top academies!\"","\"I heard you only started studying a few months ago. How did you learn so fast? Teach us your secrets someday!\"","Zong Jincheng had been praised many times growing up, but those compliments were usually about his boldness, cleverness, or his fortunate family background. This was the first time so many people had praised him for his academic achievements.","Look, they were all congratulating him.","No jealousy, no resentment, no ill will.","Zong Jincheng felt on top of the world—powerful and unstoppable.","He cleared his throat, straightened his posture, and said in a lofty tone, \"Oh, it’s nothing. I just took the exam casually, and I’ve only shown less than half of my true potential. Although the gap between you and me is still quite large, if you study hard, you might catch up to me a little.\"","\"......\"","The students exchanged awkward glances, their lips twitching, and they quickly walked away.","The conversation had been thoroughly killed.","Zong Jincheng watched as the people who had just praised him suddenly left and asked Zong Wenxiu in confusion, \"Why did they all leave so suddenly?\"","Zong Wenxiu chuckled helplessly, \"The way you spoke to them, it’s no wonder they got upset.\"","\"Was I wrong?\" Zong Jincheng said matter-of-factly. \"They’re just not as smart as me. Who else could achieve so much after only three months of studying?\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","You’re not wrong, but...","\"Jincheng, there’s an art to speaking. When they praised you, did it make you feel good?\"","Zong Jincheng nodded.","Zong Wenxiu continued, \"But when you told them to study hard, you also said they’d only catch up to you a little. No one would feel good hearing that.\"","Zong Jincheng frowned, \"But I was telling the truth.\"","The exhausted older brother tried to explain, \"The truth isn’t always pleasant to hear.\"","\"So, should I lie? Tell them that if they study for three months, they’ll become as good as me?\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\" That’s not necessary.","Xu Wan walked over and chimed in, \"You could just hold back your honest thoughts and simply thank them, then wish them good luck on their next exam. No one expects you to answer every question. Since when did Young Master Zong become so obedient?\"","Zong Jincheng glared at her defiantly.","She looked at the little troublemaker and continued, \"Speaking is an art. One wrong word could cost you a good friend, even if you didn’t mean to offend them.\"","Zong Jincheng turned his head away, ignoring her.","On the surface, he seemed to be thinking, \"I won’t listen to this bad woman’s advice,\" or \"Her suggestions must be wrong, and I’ll only regret it if I follow them.\"","But the next time a student came over to congratulate him, the little troublemaker casually replied, \"Thank you. I hope you do well on your next exam too.\"","As soon as the words left his mouth, Zong Jincheng covered it in shock.","Damn it, how did he learn so quickly?","This was practically admitting defeat to Xu Wan!","However, Xu Wan didn’t laugh at him, and the guilt-ridden Zong Jincheng didn’t dare look back. The student in front of him, pleasantly surprised, continued to praise him, \"Thank you for your kind words. I didn’t expect you to be so easygoing, without any airs of a young master.\"","Unlike the students who had walked away earlier, this group now liked Zong Jincheng even more, and the difference was obvious.","Zong Jincheng couldn’t help but smile and added, \"Come visit me at the Marquis Manor sometime. I’ll teach you how to study!\"","\"Sure, sure! Thank you, Jincheng. We’ll definitely come.\"","After they left, Zong Jincheng turned to Zong Wenxiu and boasted, \"See? He said I’m approachable. They like me!\"","Zong Wenxiu smiled and said, \"You’re talented, well-behaved, and polite. Of course, people will like you.\"","Zong Jincheng snorted proudly, \"Of course. I’m not like Qin Ye. That guy’s always so arrogant and annoying. He probably doesn’t have any friends.\"","Zong Wenxiu shook his head with a smile but didn’t say anything.","In fact, he thought that someone like Qin Ye, who was completely dedicated to his studies, probably didn’t want to make friends because he’d see it as a distraction.","The two of them walked forward and arrived at the results board once again.","The bright red board was longer than before, with each student’s name followed by their academy. At a glance, the list was filled with straight A’s and the name \"Hanlin Academy.\"","\"With four academies participating, only the top-tier students made the list,\" Zong Wenxiu said. \"Hanlin Academy truly lives up to its reputation as the top academy in the capital. They’ve almost completely dominated the board.\"","Zong Jincheng looked at the sea of Hanlin Academy names and snorted, \"So what if they’re all on the list? They’ll just be stepping stones for me to climb over.\"","Zong Wenxiu chuckled and shook his head helplessly.","Zong Jincheng pulled Zong Wenxiu straight to the top of the list. Since this was the first place in the four-academy joint exam, it had to be someone who had crushed all the other students.","But the area was crowded with students. Hearing that someone from Qingbo Academy had taken first place, kids of all ages had gathered to see the spectacle, as if they’d won a major victory.","Zong Jincheng, being young and short, couldn’t squeeze through, and even jumping didn’t help. He shouted, \"Buyan, lift me up so I can see!\"","Buyan hoisted him up, and Zong Jincheng’s height suddenly increased by a significant margin. He craned his neck to look ahead.","\"The results of the four-academy joint exam are as follows: First place, A, Qingbo Academy, Qin Ye.\"","\"......\"","The academy was buzzing with noise, the students’ cheers and shouts were deafening, and among them were countless exclamations of \"Qin Ye is amazing!\" The excitement had reached its peak.","Meanwhile, Zong Jincheng felt like he’d been struck by lightning.","\"How... how could this be...?\"","Wasn’t he supposed to be first in the four-academy joint exam?","Just now, so many people had congratulated him...","How did Qin Ye end up taking the top spot? How did Qin Ye do it???","Why wasn’t it him, the smart, hardworking, and talented Zong Jincheng???","No, this couldn’t be right. He must have done well too; otherwise, why would they all congratulate him?","Zong Jincheng pulled himself together and continued scanning the rankings, but all he saw was a sea of Hanlin Academy names, which made him want to punch something.","Just moments ago, he thought these people would be his stepping stones, but now he couldn’t find his own name. Those stepping stones had turned into heavy weights, crushing him until he could barely stand straight!","\"Buyan, move to the left. Let’s check the next column.\"","\"Move left again.\"","\"Check the next column.\"","\"Keep looking...\""]},{"number":66,"title":"Chapter 66: The North Court of the Hanlin Academy is Too Competitive","paragraphs":["Row after row of Hanlin Academy, Hanlin Academy, Hanlin Academy—even Buyan, who couldn’t read, found it ridiculous. Couldn’t they change a few characters? By the later rows, Yanqing Academy and Random Academy began to appear, finally breaking the monopoly of Hanlin Academy, except for Qin Ye.","And Zong Jincheng finally found his ranking.","“One hundred and twentieth place, Class A, Qingbo Academy, Zong Jincheng.”","“..................”","The list only had one hundred and twenty names, and he was the last one, with Qingbo Academy’s name, sitting lonely at the bottom.","The last place in the joint examination of the four academies...","The little devil was stunned, gradually grew furious, became enraged, jealous, indignant, and was about to lose his mind...","“Buyan! Put me down!”","Zong Jincheng turned around and left, muttering to himself, “What a lousy academy! I’m never coming back!”","And those people even congratulated him!","What was there to congratulate? Congratulations for what?","Being on the list meant nothing!","What’s there to celebrate about being dead last?","Zong Wenxiu had been by his side the whole time. Though he couldn’t see the words on the list, he noticed his brother stopping at the bottom, clearly having found his name and being deeply affected by it.","He quickly chased after him, noticing Cui Liu whispering to Xu Wan, likely reporting the results to her.","“Madam, Jincheng is leaving,” Zong Wenxiu said anxiously.","Xu Wan nodded. “Expected. Let’s go back too.”","“Aren’t you worried, Madam? Jincheng said he’s never coming back to the academy.”","Xu Wan shrugged. “He’s said that countless times. What’s the difference between that and crying wolf?”","Zong Wenxiu: “...”","She had a point.","But even so, Zong Wenxiu couldn’t help but worry and went to comfort his brother.","“Jincheng, wait for me.”","Hearing his voice, Zong Jincheng stopped and turned around, looking at him with a pout, his lips puckered like a teapot.","“Brother, I did so poorly,” the little devil said, his eyelashes fluttering, his eyes slightly red.","He had probably never faced such a setback before. He had worked so hard and was so confident that he had done well, but the result was far from what he expected.","But he still had his pride. A man doesn’t cry easily—crying would mean admitting defeat, and he would never cry.","Zong Jincheng would never be defeated to the point of tears!","Zong Wenxiu felt a pang of sympathy. He ruffled his brother’s soft hair and comforted him, “You didn’t do poorly. Otherwise, why would so many people congratulate you? Look, I’ve been studying much longer than you, and I didn’t even make the list.”","“Aren’t you upset?” the little devil asked, puzzled.","Zong Wenxiu chuckled. “Of course I’m upset. Not just upset, but also disappointed. But I know that even though I’ve worked hard, I’ve only been studying for a little over half a year. How could I possibly catch up to someone who’s been studying for five or six years? If progress were that easy to make, what would be the point of studying for so many years?”","Zong Jincheng followed his train of thought and realized he had a point.","If he had been studying for five or six years and was surpassed by someone who had only studied for a few months, he’d probably never want to touch a book again in his life.","The little devil was quickly comforted, but he was still unhappy. He grumbled resentfully, “That Hanlin Academy is so annoying. I was exhausted looking through the list—it was all their students, all of them ranked above me.”","Zong Wenxiu thought for a moment and said, “I know about this. Hanlin Academy is the strongest academy in the capital. If you do well on the entrance exam, tuition is waived, and they provide food and lodging. That’s why students from all over the capital and even other regions flock there, and Hanlin Academy’s strength continues to grow.”","Zong Jincheng snorted. “Just wait. Next time, I’m going to crush them in the joint exam! I’ll trample them, trample them all!!”","Zong Wenxiu laughed. “That’s right! With your learning speed, you’ll definitely crush them next time!”","“Hahaha...”","Seeing the boy laughing again, Xu Wan knew that her little helper, Wenxiu, had successfully calmed down the little devil.","She stepped forward and said, “Children, since you’re so curious about Hanlin Academy, why don’t we take a look at their daily study environment?”","“Huh?” “Huh?”","The Zong brothers—one who had never seen the world and the other who had only seen its twisted side—had only ever known Qingbo Academy. They thought all academies were like that.","Little did they know, Xu Wan had chosen Qingbo Academy for them at this stage—a place that wasn’t so elite as to make them feel discouraged, nor so mediocre as to kill their competitive spirit.","But the true top academy in the capital, with the most intense study atmosphere, was still Hanlin Academy’s North Campus.","Zong Jincheng had heard Xu Wan talk about this academy before, so now he used his impressive memory to show off to Zong Wenxiu: “Hanlin Academy is divided into the South Campus and the North Campus. The South Campus is for those who pay their way in, while the North Campus is for those who pass the entrance exam.”","“Every top scholar in the Great Chu Dynasty has come from Hanlin’s North Campus. That’s why people say, ‘Entering Hanlin is like taking a step into officialdom.’ But I have to correct one thing—my father didn’t come from here. He was taught by Master Baili!”","Zong Wenxiu was getting excited, especially by the last part. He said, “Then let’s strive to be the next top scholars who didn’t come from Hanlin’s North Campus!”","Zong Jincheng proudly high-fived him. “Great minds think alike!”","After getting off the carriage, the three of them headed straight for the North Campus.","The South Campus was in the outer area and looked similar to Qingbo Academy, but once they reached the inner area, the students of the North Campus were clearly different.","There were very few students in the North Campus, and the area wasn’t large, but each of them walked incredibly fast, some even jogging. Some carried books while muttering to themselves, while others frowned, deep in thought.","Unlike the curious students of the South Campus, the North Campus students seemed completely absorbed in their own worlds, paying no attention to the strange strangers wandering around the academy.","Zong Wenxiu looked around and said blankly, “Brother, I feel like I’m seeing countless Qin Yes.”","Zong Jincheng nodded in agreement. “I take back what I said earlier.”","“Huh?”","The little devil gritted his teeth. “I suddenly feel like Qin Ye isn’t that cold-hearted after all. Sure, he’s a bit arrogant, domineering, rude, and unlikeable. But at least he’s normal—when he walks, he’s steady and focused. He’s not insane enough to run while reciting books!”"]},{"number":67,"title":"Chapter 67: Qin Ye Wants to Take the Child Scholar Examination","paragraphs":["Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","He could already sense the depth of his younger brother's resentment toward Qin Ye. In that long sentence, not a single positive word was used.","Of course, compared to Qin Ye, the people at Hanlin North Academy were even more intimidating, with an air of studying as if their lives depended on it.","Xu Wan took a step forward and guided with a smile, \"Take a closer look. What else is different about these people?\"","Zong Jincheng snorted proudly, \"Their ages, obviously. Hanlin North Academy even admits children. I wonder how difficult their entrance exams are. Good thing I didn’t fall for your trick and take the exam there, or else...\"","Or else he would have been utterly crushed.","Zong Wenxiu pondered for a moment and said, \"Their clothing is very simple, with almost no luxurious accessories. This suggests two things: first, they might be so focused on studying that they don’t care about their appearance; second, they might come from poor families. Hanlin North Academy likely only provides them with food and shelter, not clothing.\"","\"Poor families?\" Zong Jincheng followed his gaze, trying to understand.","The little guy couldn’t tell the quality of the fabric, nor could he distinguish between linen, cotton, or silk. All he noticed was that their clothes had many wrinkles, something that never happened to his own clothes.","Xu Wan nodded, \"Yes, poor families, struggling at the bottom of society for generations. For them, studying isn’t just about making a name for themselves in the future. More importantly, studying at Hanlin North Academy is their only chance to turn their lives around. It’s a do-or-die situation. If they fail, there’s no second chance.\"","Zong Wenxiu understood and nodded, \"No wonder they look so desperate. It’s completely different from the students at Qingbo Academy, where all the kids come from wealthy families. It’s hard to feel that sense of desperation there.\"","\"The atmosphere at Hanlin North Academy is like that. Even if you threw a student from Qingbo Academy in there, they’d be influenced by it,\" Xu Wan said with a smile. \"There’s a term for it: involution. When you see others working so hard, you feel pressured and start working hard too. That’s how it becomes what you’re seeing now.\"","\"Involution?\" Zong Jincheng had an epiphany and suddenly understood why he felt so uncomfortable that day on Qin Ye’s wall.","That despicable kid had been secretly outworking him!","No wonder he couldn’t beat Qin Ye!!","Xu Wan called to them, \"Let’s go. There’s no point in watching any longer. They probably won’t even spare us a glance.\"","Zong Jincheng raised his thumb, then flipped it downward, making a gesture to show they weren’t up to par. He declared arrogantly, \"Just wait. I’ll defeat them one by one!\"","Zong Wenxiu chuckled lightly and was about to follow when he turned his head and spotted a surprising young boy. \"Qin Ye?\"","\"Qin Ye?!\" Zong Jincheng whipped his head around frantically, asking, \"Where? Where? I don’t see him!\"","Zong Wenxiu patted his shoulder and pointed in a direction. Sure enough, Qin Ye was talking to a boy around ten years old. Qin Ye was shorter than the other boy, but the older boy kept nodding, as if Qin Ye was giving him instructions.","After finishing the conversation, the boy headed toward Hanlin North Academy, and Qin Ye walked out.","Zong Jincheng immediately pushed Zong Wenxiu aside and blocked Qin Ye’s path, ready to pick a fight.","Qin Ye raised an eyebrow and said coldly, \"It’s you again.\"","Zong Jincheng declared proudly, \"Yes, it’s me! One of the only two students from Qingbo Academy to make it onto the four-academy joint exam rankings!\"","Qin Ye finally gave him a proper look. \"What rank?\"","\"Uh...\" The little demon king’s heart was instantly pierced, and his proud expression faltered.","The 120th rank sounded terrible, a whole list away from Qin Ye. Saying it out loud would be humiliating.","Qin Ye didn’t miss his reaction and sneered dismissively.","This arrogant demeanor infuriated the little demon king. He was always the one acting like this toward others; how dare someone treat him this way?","He shouted angrily, \"What are you so smug about? I’ve only been studying for three months, and I’ve already made it onto the rankings. Beating you is just a matter of a few months. Piece of cake. Just wait to become my defeated opponent!\"","\"Suit yourself. I’ve switched classes anyway,\" Qin Ye said indifferently, turning to leave, not wanting to waste any more time.","\"Switched classes? To which class?\" Zong Jincheng was stunned and shouted at his retreating figure, \"We’re not even in the same class! I’ve been studying at home!\"","Qin Ye’s figure grew smaller and smaller, not pausing for a moment.","It seemed he truly had no competitive spirit, or perhaps he simply didn’t care about Zong Jincheng and didn’t see him as a threat to his top position.","The little demon king was still howling in frustration behind him, but unfortunately, the person who had provoked him was long gone.","He turned to Zong Wenxiu and asked, \"Brother, what does switching classes mean? Is he going to study at Hanlin North Academy?\"","Zong Wenxiu shook his head and denied, \"No, switching academies is called transferring. Switching classes means he doesn’t want to stay in the eight-year-old class anymore. Qingbo Academy groups students by age, and the content, exam scope, and rankings are different for each age group.\"","Zong Jincheng said, \"So once Qin Ye switches classes, I’ll never have the chance to be on the same ranking as him again? I’ll never get to beat him?\"","Zong Wenxiu nodded honestly, \"Exactly. After seeing his exam papers last time, I realized that even if he jumped straight to our ten-year-old class, he’d still take first place without any trouble. Qin Ye’s knowledge is really profound.\"","Zong Jincheng frowned, \"Then I want to take the same exams as you guys.\"","Xu Wan said leisurely, \"Keep dreaming. Qin Ye is going to the Child Prodigy Class.\"","Zong Wenxiu was surprised, \"Madam, you know about this?\"","Xu Wan smiled, \"Of course. I’ve made sure to gather all the information on our young master’s rival.\"","Zong Jincheng perked up his ears and asked curiously, \"What’s the Child Prodigy Class?\"","\"The Child Prodigy Class, as the name suggests, is for selecting prodigies for the imperial court. Only children under twelve can participate. If they pass the exam, they can bypass the usual age restriction of ten for the imperial exams and skip the preliminary exams like the child scholar and scholar exams.\"","\"Qingbo Academy’s Child Prodigy Class was established for this purpose. The class isn’t grouped by age but includes all children under twelve. If they exceed the age limit and still fail the exam, they’ll be sent back to their original class.\"","Zong Jincheng’s frown was so deep it could crush a mosquito. He gritted his teeth and said, \"That Qin Ye, he’s already aiming for the imperial exams at such a young age!\"","Xu Wan chuckled, \"Yes, that kid is really confident.\"","\"I’m going to take that exam too!\" Zong Jincheng refused to admit defeat and was ready to join the intense competition.","\"You?\" Xu Wan patted his shoulder and said with a laugh, \"Focus on breaking into the top ten first. Think about the 119 students ahead of you. If you can’t even beat these eight-year-olds, how are you going to compete with the kids in the Child Prodigy Class?\"","Zong Jincheng protested loudly, \"I’m not waiting for the next four-academy joint exam. That’s at least two months away. In that time, I could’ve already beaten Qin Ye!\"","Xu Wan smiled and said, \"According to the latest news I’ve received, Hanlin North Academy will hold a joint exam with Qingbo Academy next month. This is your last chance.\""]},{"number":68,"title":"Chapter 68: Key Class Inauguration","paragraphs":["“A separate joint exam?” Zong Jincheng and Zong Wenxiu exchanged puzzled glances.","It wasn’t a four-academy joint exam anymore, but a two-academy one. Another joint exam, and they’d chosen the most formidable opponent... The dean of Qingbo Academy was truly undeterred by setbacks.","Zong Wenxiu sighed, “I never expected Hanlin North Academy to be so fond of exams, organizing joint exams with other academies every month.”","Zong Jincheng was about to nod in agreement when Xu Wan suddenly interjected, “No, it’s because of Qin Ye.”","“Huh? Did Qin Ye request to take another exam with Hanlin Academy?” Zong Wenxiu asked in surprise.","Zong Jincheng immediately retorted, “How could that be! What does Qin Ye matter? There’s no way Hanlin North Academy would bring their entire academy to take an exam just because he wanted to!”","Even if it were because of one person, it could only be him, Zong Jincheng. What did Qin Ye amount to?","Hmph, that arrogant brat.","Unexpectedly, Xu Wan explained, “It’s because Hanlin North Academy, a place that always strives to be first, couldn’t accept Qin Ye surpassing all their geniuses. That’s why they proposed a separate joint exam to redeem themselves next month.”","Zong Wenxiu: “...”","So, it was actually Hanlin Academy that initiated the challenge? They were the ones who wanted to face Qin Ye again?!","Zong Jincheng: “!!!”","Damn, the feeling of infuriating the Capital City’s top academy is so satisfying!","Why couldn’t it have been him who caused this?!","If he had been the top scorer in the last joint exam, it would be Hanlin North Academy going crazy over his name, Zong Jincheng!","Yes!","Top scorer in the joint exam!","He would also achieve that!","He, Zong Jincheng, would also relish the feeling of outshining all the geniuses!","“Let’s go home. I need to prepare for next month’s joint exam. Watch me defeat all the geniuses of Hanlin North Academy!”","The little devil was brimming with determination, dragging Zong Wenxiu back to the manor to study.","Seeing that her goal had been surpassed, Xu Wan’s brow relaxed. This trip had gone surprisingly smoothly.","Cui Zhi praised her, “Madam, you’re truly brilliant. No wonder you’ve always had us keep an eye on Qin Ye. As soon as we found out he was coming to Hanlin to visit his brother, you immediately brought the two young masters here.”","Xu Wan smiled, “Zong Jincheng is too overconfident. Only someone as strong and proud as Qin Ye can keep his arrogance in check.”","Cui Zhi said, “With the example of Hanlin North Academy’s students fighting with their backs against the wall, I feel that the two young masters will study even harder this month, burning the midnight oil every night.”","Xu Wan shook her head, “Burning the midnight oil isn’t necessary. I’ve always thought Wenxiu spends too much time studying. Children of this age need plenty of sleep for proper growth. We can’t end up with two shorties.”","“Then... how can they improve their studies in the shortest time possible?”","Xu Wan replied mysteriously, “That’s where our three private tutors, each earning a hundred taels of silver a month, come into play.”","“Huh?”","At Yangyuan Marquis Manor.","The plaque bearing the words “Virtue Carries All” above the grand study was taken down, and a brand-new plaque was hung in its place. Servants and maids gathered to watch the spectacle, and even the Zong brothers peeked over to see.","“Marquis Manor Elite Class.”","Study plaques usually featured four-character idioms, appearing both majestic and awe-inspiring. But with this peculiar new name, the study felt more like a school—a prestigious one at that.","“What does this mean?” the little devil asked.","Xu Wan made a grand entrance with the three private tutors and introduced with a smile, “The Marquis Manor Elite Class: focused teaching, tailored education, high-quality one-on-three tutoring, helping you overtake and surpass all the geniuses in the Capital City!”","Zong Jincheng: “Huh?”","Zong Wenxiu: “Huh?”","The three private tutors, all in their twenties or thirties, were full of energy. After being trained by Xu Wan for a few days, they were not only in awe of her teaching methods but also filled with hope for the future.","With such a dedicated mistress and two intelligent, hardworking students, they felt their own prospects were bright and inspiring.","“Greetings, young masters. I’m Cheng Zhidong. Over the past few days, I’ve assessed your current progress. Here’s the list of study materials I’ve carefully selected for you, tailored to your needs. It will guide you from the simple to the complex, ensuring no effort is wasted.”","“Greetings, young masters. I’m Pan Hongzhi. I’ve compiled all the mistakes from your past exam papers and summarized your common errors. This way, you won’t need to redo all the questions to master the key points you’ve missed.”","“Greetings, young masters. I’m Zhao Yin. I’ve analyzed past exam papers for students your age and highlighted the most important topics. This will allow you to focus on the core content first, saving time to learn new material.”","“..................”","Baili Xi, seated at the head of the room, had initially been quite relaxed, curious to see how the three newly appointed tutors would assist him in teaching. But as soon as they began speaking, their approaches were unconventional yet sounded incredibly effective. His relaxed posture gradually straightened.","By the time they finished, he couldn’t help but ask in amazement, “Has Hanlin North Academy’s teaching methods become this advanced?”","He had merely suggested that Xu Wan hire a tutor from Hanlin Academy, never expecting such a groundbreaking impact.","Pan Hongzhi, the tutor from Hanlin Academy, clasped his hands and explained, “You’ve misunderstood, sir. These methods were all taught by Madam. Hanlin Academy hasn’t yet adopted such refined and comprehensive approaches.”","The other two tutors chimed in agreement.","Though they were all accomplished scholars in their own right, Xu Wan’s methods enabled them to impart their knowledge to the two boys with precision and efficiency. Her ability to bring out their potential was remarkable, and it was no wonder she dared to offer them such high salaries.","Baili Xi was even more astonished. He not only gave Xu Wan an approving look but also turned to the boys and said, “Having a mother and aunt who cares for you so deeply is truly a blessing.”","Zong Wenxiu wholeheartedly agreed and immediately responded, “Thank you, Madam. I will study diligently and live up to the teachings of all the tutors!”","Zong Jincheng, however, was still in a daze.","The three tutors seemed incredibly capable, their methods sounded brilliant, and even Baili Xi had praised them.","But they said all these great ideas came from Xu Wan. This woman... this so-called “bad woman”... didn’t seem so bad after all... and seemed quite impressive?","How did she become so capable?","Was she also a brilliant scholar and exam-taker?","Or perhaps she had secretly earned the top honors in the imperial exams and returned incognito to live as an ordinary person?"]},{"number":69,"title":"Chapter 69: I Can Still Keep Up","paragraphs":["The little demon king's confusion was written all over his face, so simple it was almost laughable.","Xu Wan, though not a top scholar, had clawed her way out of a poverty-stricken mountainous region in a highly competitive province for college entrance exams. With scarce educational resources and fierce competition, it took everything she had to rise above. Behind her were a group of siblings from the welfare home who had no one else to rely on. She, too, had her own desperate battle to fight.","\"Jincheng, do you think they’ll be helpful for your studies?\" Xu Wan asked with a smile.","Zong Jincheng was sure they would be, but the proud little demon king would never admit it, let alone thank her—that would be too embarrassing.","He stubbornly replied, \"I’ll definitely get first place this time.\"","After all, if he did well, Xu Wan would also gain some prestige, since she was his nominal mother. Their fates were intertwined—glory for one meant glory for the other, and failure for one meant failure for both.","Xu Wan chuckled. \"Alright, alright. I’ll look forward to seeing your results in next month’s joint exam. Don’t put too much pressure on yourself, though. If Wenxiu can make it onto the top ten list for your age group, that’s good enough. As for Jincheng, getting into the top fifty would be impressive.\"","Zong Wenxiu nodded obediently. \"Understood.\"","The little demon king stuck out his tongue at her. \"Don’t underestimate me! I’m definitely going to get first place and blow your mind!\"","Xu Wan raised an eyebrow skeptically, clearly not buying it.","The little demon king fumed, waving his fist in the air as if to show off his strength.","Xu Wan rolled her eyes at him.","The little demon king: \"!\"","Zong Wenxiu couldn’t help but laugh. His brother and Xu Wan were at it again, their childish bickering never-ending.","The tutors began their intensive coaching sessions, staying with the boys from morning till night, ready to explain anything they didn’t understand.","Baili Xi was in charge of the daily lessons, speeding up the teaching pace to match the boys’ learning speed.","The content of the children’s exams wasn’t particularly deep, mostly involving memorization, analysis, and comprehension. For Zong Jincheng, who had a photographic memory, one read-through was enough to retain everything. Though Zong Wenxiu wasn’t as naturally gifted, he was still far ahead of most children, and he worked tirelessly to keep up.","Half a month passed.","Baili Xi sighed to the heavens. \"I feel like I’ve taught two months’ worth of material in just half a month. How are these kids catching on so fast? Even Zong Zhao wasn’t this driven back in the day.\"","Xu Wan wanted to say that Zong Zhao had been focused on both martial arts and academics, with the old marquis keeping an eye on him, so he hadn’t thrown himself entirely into studying. But these two boys were different. With dedicated private tutors, all they had to do was absorb the knowledge being fed to them, saving a lot of energy in the process.","Thinking this, she had someone prepare some ginseng to boost Baili Xi’s health and also assigned him an assistant to handle lesson preparation and summaries.","It was another day of new experiences for Baili Xi.","Over the past two weeks, the boys had thrown themselves into their studies, becoming more and more competitive. If Xu Wan hadn’t enforced a strict schedule of studying from 8 a.m. to 8 p.m., the little demon king, with his boundless energy, would have followed Zong Wenxiu in studying from 6 a.m. to midnight.","While other students at the academy had a five-day study week with two days off, these two didn’t want to rest at all. One was desperate to climb the rankings, and the other was determined to outshine all the geniuses in the capital. They studied until their eyes turned red.","Even a capitalist would have wept at their dedication.","Finally, Xu Wan couldn’t take it anymore. \"Take a day off. No more studying!\"","Zong Wenxiu obediently put down his book, always following Xu Wan’s lead.","The little demon king, eyes bloodshot, slammed the table. \"Don’t stop me! I can keep going!\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","This is madness...","If she had a camera, she would have recorded this and sent it to the old lady, as well as to the little demon king from three and a half months ago.","The little demon king continued his grandiose declarations: \"I, Zong Jincheng, will definitely take first place in the joint exam and crush all those stepping stones at Hanlin North Academy!\"","Xu Wan facepalmed.","She was starting to wonder if she’d pushed the little demon king too hard. The kid was like a perpetual motion machine, showing no signs of fatigue.","While this approach was certainly effective in boosting grades, Xu Wan, being a conscientious worker, knew that a balance of work and rest was essential for long-term growth.","She had Cui Zhi bring over an invitation and handed it to Zong Jincheng and Zong Wenxiu.","\"Tomorrow, the Crown Prince is hosting a hunt at Autumn Sun Mountain and has invited the children from our household to attend.\"","At the mention of the Crown Prince, Zong Jincheng’s expression immediately lit up. He quickly took the invitation and, seeing his name listed first, grinned from ear to ear. \"The Crown Prince definitely likes me the most!\"","He passed the invitation to his brother. Zong Wenxiu saw his name and was also delighted, surprised that the Crown Prince even knew about him. But then...","\"Brother, you’ve gotten so good! You can read all the words on the invitation now?\"","Zong Jincheng was reminded of this and realized, indeed, he used to either have Shunzi read it to him or stumble over many of the characters. But now, he had read it smoothly.","Was this the power of knowledge?","The little demon king grew even more excited but tried to play it cool. \"Brother, I feel like I’m terrifyingly strong now!\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...You really are terrifying.\"","Xu Wan was both amused and exasperated.","The kid’s confidence was also like a perpetual motion machine, endlessly self-replenishing.","Autumn Sun Mountain Hunting Grounds.","The children of military families had all received invitations and arrived in full force, ready for action. Among them were two boys who had abandoned martial arts for academics.","Bu Yanzheng was checking the arrows in the boys’ quivers, occasionally explaining archery techniques. Though they were amateur archers, their recent academic obsession had changed their mindset—they now wanted to excel at everything, so they listened intently.","\"You two should stick together later. It doesn’t matter if you hit anything. We’re not martial artists, so there’s no need to compete in this.\"","The little demon king twirled his bow in boredom. \"Yeah, no need to compete. Archery’s not fun anyway—just a lot of effort with nothing to show for it. Brother, once I get first place, I’ll teach you how to play cuju.\"","Zong Wenxiu smiled and nodded. \"Alright.\"","He’d only read about cuju in books and was nowhere near as skilled as Jincheng, so he was happy to hear his brother offer to teach him.","\"Oh, so you’re calling him ‘brother’ now, Jincheng? Since when did you have a brother?\"","Xu Wan was sitting not far away, chatting with Madam He from the Minister of War's Mansion. He Zheng had come along today after hearing that Jincheng would be there, and Madam He seized the opportunity to exchange parenting tips with Xu Wan.","While talking to her, Xu Wan kept an eye on the two brothers. When a young boy approached Jincheng, she asked Madam He, \"Whose child is that?\"","Madam He glanced over. \"Oh, that’s the youngest son of the Right Censor of the Imperial Censorate, Wei Xinglu.\"","Xu Wan mentally noted: the last of the four young troublemakers of the capital.","Zong Jincheng, Zhai Yao, He Zheng, Wei Xinglu.","She’d now met all of them."]},{"number":70,"title":"Chapter 70: Jin Cheng Protects His Brother","paragraphs":["Madam He, seeing her worried expression, quickly reassured her, \"Don’t worry, Jincheng gets along well with them. They’ll keep each other company during the hunt, so nothing will happen.\"","Xu Wan smiled politely on the surface, but inwardly she thought, *That’s exactly why I’m worried!*","She didn’t know much about Wei Xinglu and feared that this boy might undo all the progress she’d made with her little troublemaker.","Meanwhile, Zong Jincheng, completely unaware, replied, \"His name is Zong Wenxiu. He’s from my second uncle’s family, my cousin. He just returned to the manor earlier this year.\"","Wei Xinglu let out a long \"Oh\" and said, \"So, he’s that country bumpkin of a half-brother of yours. Hearing you call him ‘brother’ so affectionately, I thought your father had somehow produced another legitimate heir.\"","Zong Wenxiu, hearing this, looked hurt and took a step back.","Zong Jincheng was stunned and immediately flared up. He shouted at Wei Xinglu, \"Are you deaf? I just said he’s my cousin! Why would you say something like that? Don’t you realize how much that hurts people? Do you have any tact at all?\"","Buyan, standing behind them, was quite surprised.","He vaguely remembered when Wenxiu first returned to the manor, Wei Xinglu had told Jincheng that he now had a country bumpkin for a brother. Back then, Jincheng hadn’t just failed to defend him—he’d even joined in on the mockery.","Who would have thought that just a few months later, Jincheng would have changed so much?","Wei Xinglu, too, was taken aback by this side of Zong Jincheng. He scratched his head and said, \"What’s gotten into you, Jincheng? I only said one thing about him, and you’re throwing a fit. Why are you so protective of a half-brother who’s not even close to you? The others are going to laugh at us.\"","\"You’re still talking? I’ll fight you!\" Zong Jincheng looked around for a brick but, finding none, grabbed his bow instead and charged at Wei Xinglu.","Wei Xinglu, terrified, ran around in circles, yelling, \"Have you lost your mind, Jincheng? What’s happened to you in these few months? We were supposed to be troublemakers together till we’re ninety-nine!\"","Zong Jincheng, bow in hand, chased after him, shouting, \"Who’s troublemaking with you? I’m studying hard now, aiming to become the most talented genius in the Capital City!\"","\"Ahhh! Studying? You’ve gone mad! Zong Jincheng’s been possessed by a ghost!!!\"","\"You’re the mad one! Stop running!\"","Wei Xinglu was chased around like a rabbit, and the onlookers burst into laughter. It was quite a sight to see the four little troublemakers turning on each other. They used to be inseparable, causing headaches wherever they went.","Xu Wan finally let out a sigh of relief. The boy was teachable after all, and her efforts were bearing some fruit.","Madam He exclaimed in amazement, \"In just three and a half months, Jincheng seems like a completely different person. Madam Zong’s skills are truly admirable. If you were a man, my husband would definitely invite you to the Ministry of War for guidance.\"","Xu Wan chuckled, \"You flatter me, Madam He. Your husband is quite impressive himself.\"","After all, he’d almost turned his son into his mortal enemy—truly a unique father.","\"Ah...\" Madam He sighed, unable to bring herself to discuss it further. Every family had its own struggles.","\"The Crown Prince has arrived, and the Crown Princess as well.\"","Everyone quickly rose to their feet to pay their respects. After seeing the Crown Prince off to the hunting grounds, they sat down with the Crown Princess to enjoy the flowers and fruits, patiently waiting for their children to return from the hunt.","Meanwhile, Zong Jincheng was still chasing Wei Xinglu. It wasn’t until Zong Wenxiu stepped in to pull him away that the little troublemaker finally relented. Before leaving, Jincheng didn’t forget to throw out a threat, \"If you dare badmouth my brother again, I’ll chase you to your house and beat you up!\"","Wei Xinglu patted his chest, relieved, and muttered to those around him, \"This guy... has he lost his mind?\"","The servants didn’t dare to breathe a word, but inwardly, they all gave a thumbs up. The quartet of troublemakers had finally split, and their young masters would surely be easier to manage from now on.","After running around, Zong Jincheng, though panting, quickly regained his energy. He picked up his bow and inspected it, asking, \"It’s not broken, is it?\"","Buyan didn’t even want to respond.","*Whatever, it’s not like you’re going to hit anything anyway.*","Zong Wenxiu offered, \"Why don’t we switch? You can use mine.\"","Zong Jincheng waved his hand, \"No need, no need. It looks fine. Let’s go hunting.\"","\"Alright.\"","\"Brother, what kind of prey do you like? I’ll hunt it for you.\"","\"Me? Anything’s fine...\"","\"Then I’ll get you a fox fur for a scarf!\"","\"Sure.\"","Zong Jincheng loved horseback riding and had stopped letting others lead his horse once he’d learned how to ride. Zong Wenxiu, however, wasn’t as skilled, so Jincheng assigned Buyan to lead his brother’s horse while he took his bow and chased after a little fox.","\"Whoosh—\" Missed.","\"Whoosh—\" Missed again.","Zong Jincheng stared at the fleeing red fox, nudged his horse with his heels, and commanded, \"Go, let’s chase it!\"","After a long pursuit, the red fox hid behind a tree, its tail peeking out. Zong Jincheng dismounted and crept forward, careful not to startle it.","He considered pouncing on it but feared the fox might bite him in desperation. Instead, he quietly drew an arrow from his quiver, placed it on his bow, and waited until he was close enough to strike.","The little troublemaker thought to himself, *Hmph, at this distance, I’m definitely going to catch you this time!*","In the next moment, he swiftly moved around the tree and let the arrow fly, hitting the little fox squarely.","The red fox kicked its legs and died.","The little troublemaker, satisfied, picked up the fox, only to turn around and find his horse gone.","\"Wait... where’s my horse?\"","In the vast hunting grounds, surrounded by lush trees, even with his photographic memory, Zong Jincheng knew that without his horse, he’d be walking until dark.","Grumbling, he carried the fox and started walking back, thinking he’d surely run into someone who could give him a ride.","It didn’t take long before he heard familiar voices.","Looking up, he was delighted to see a familiar face and called out, \"Crown Prince!\"","But then he noticed something was off.","The Crown Prince was pointing his sword at the chest of a young general, who in turn had an arrow aimed at the Crown Prince. However, the arrow was too short to reach the Crown Prince’s neck.","Zong Jincheng was shocked. \"Are... are you trying to assassinate the Crown Prince?\"","This was the hunting grounds, surrounded by guards and the Crown Prince’s entourage. If this man dared to kill the Crown Prince, he’d be signing his own death warrant. And judging by his attire, he seemed to be a high-ranking official. What was going on?","The young general was in the most precarious position. A single push from the Crown Prince, and the sword would end his life. Yet, he showed no fear, his expression cold and even slightly disdainful.","The young general looked at the Crown Prince’s pale, sickly face, his thin, frail arms, and the calluses on his palms that had been worn away by years of medicine. The hand holding the sword trembled slightly.","For a swordsman, a shaky hand was a fatal flaw.","The young general sneered, \"Crown Prince, can your sword still kill?\""]},{"number":71,"title":"Chapter 71: The Little Devil's Tricks Are Growing","paragraphs":["The Crown Prince’s sword trembled slightly in his hand, and beads of cold sweat formed on his pale forehead. The weight of the blade grew heavier with each shake, to the point where his arm could barely lift it.","His lips turned blue, and his complexion grew even paler, yet he forced himself to speak sternly, “General Luo, are you trying to take advantage of this moment to claim my life?”","The young man standing before him was none other than Luo Jingfeng, the Great General of Pacifying the West and the highest-ranking military official in the court. His elder brother, Luo Jingyun, was the Prince of Southern Pacification, commanding a formidable army.","With such military power in their hands, even the Emperor had to tread carefully around them, let alone a sickly Crown Prince.","Luo Jingfeng sneered, “How could I dare? I merely wished to see if Your Highness, once hailed alongside Zong Zhao as the top martial artist in the Capital City, still possesses the courage to wield a sword after eight years of illness... and if you can still kill.”","After a mocking glance at the Crown Prince, he added, “It seems you cannot. Your hand has been trembling the entire time.”","The Crown Prince glared at him and warned, “Your actions are tantamount to rebellion. Even if I were to kill you today, it would be justified.”","“Then give it a try. I’m eager to see Your Highness make a fool of himself,” Luo Jingfeng retorted, utterly unconvinced that the Crown Prince still had the strength to strike.","After all, hadn’t all those medicines been fed to him for nothing?","“You!” The Crown Prince’s blood surged, his pale face flushing red with anger. He coughed violently, his grip on the sword loosening further.","Just as the sword tip wavered, a small arm reached out, pressing the Crown Prince’s hand forward. With a sharp *thud*, the blade pierced Luo Jingfeng’s chest.","Both men turned to see Zong Jincheng, who had pushed the sword, standing there innocently. “Did I help Your Highness?”","“...”","Luo Jingfeng spat out a mouthful of blood. The wound wasn’t deep; he was simply enraged.","This child... how dare he strike him?!","Even the Crown Prince, who had been in a daze, snapped back to reality. He withdrew the sword, letting Luo Jingfeng collapse to his knees, clutching his chest as blood dripped from the wound.","Zong Jincheng hadn’t fully understood their conversation. All he knew was that this General Luo was bullying the Crown Prince, and the Crown Prince was a good person who couldn’t possibly be in the wrong.","So, whoever he was, Zong Jincheng decided to strike first and ask questions later.","Even if it meant nothing more than standing up for the Crown Prince, he would do it!","After all, he was the Crown Prince’s favorite child!","“Heh, heh,” Luo Jingfeng wiped the blood from his chest and glared at the Crown Prince. “Your Highness’s luck remains as impeccable as ever. In the Eastern Palace, you have the Crown Princess to protect you, and even here at the hunting grounds, a child shields you. Truly, you are blessed.”","Zong Jincheng boldly stepped in front of the Crown Prince and declared, “The Eastern Palace guards will be here soon. If you dare harm His Highness again, your head will roll!”","Luo Jingfeng scoffed, “You naive child. Ask the Crown Prince standing beside you—does he dare say such a thing? Even if the Emperor himself were here, would he dare lay a finger on me?”","Zong Jincheng’s mind was reeling.","Wasn’t the Emperor the highest authority, followed by the Crown Prince?","How could this man be so confident, as if he were above the Emperor?","His worldview was being shattered.","Zong Jincheng wanted to argue further, but the Crown Prince pulled him back and shook his head, silently confirming Luo Jingfeng’s words.","Luo Jingfeng picked up his bow and left. Not long after, the Eastern Palace guards arrived.","The Crown Prince turned to Zong Jincheng and said, “What happened today is our little secret. Don’t tell anyone. Go back, sleep well, and forget all about it, okay?”","Zong Jincheng nodded.","But in his heart, he thought, *Forgetting might be hard. The curse of having a good memory.*","However, after this incident, Zong Jincheng’s bond with the Crown Prince grew even stronger. The little troublemaker skipped out of the hunting grounds, carrying a red fox and admiring a beautiful jade pendant in his hand.","“Jincheng, what’s that?” Xu Wan asked.","The pendant looked incredibly valuable, easily worth thousands of taels of silver.","Zong Jincheng proudly boasted, “This is a gift from the Crown Prince!”","Then, with a sly grin, he added, “His Highness said that with this pendant, no one would dare harm me!” He emphasized the words *no one* with particular weight.","Xu Wan: “...”","Damn it, I quit!","This is practically a get-out-of-jail-free card!","She was beginning to suspect that if she ever tried to discipline Zong Jincheng again, the Crown Prince would send someone to confiscate her Marquis Manor!","Xu Wan’s frustration was palpable, as if she were on the verge of exploding. This was the biggest obstacle she had ever faced in her mission to tame the little troublemaker.","However, her worries didn’t last long. A maid from the Crown Princess approached and whispered something in her ear.","Zong Jincheng watched as Xu Wan’s expression changed as swiftly as the weather in June.","She immediately handed the red fox to his brother and dashed off without a second thought!","Zong Wenxiu: “?? What’s wrong with my brother?”","Xu Wan gritted her teeth and said, “He lied and got caught. He’s running away to avoid a beating!”","The Crown Princess had informed her that the pendant was only meant to protect Zong Jincheng from external threats and would not interfere with her disciplinary methods.","That little rascal!","He had the audacity to play word games with her!","It seemed that his education hadn’t just filled his once-illiterate brain—it had also given him a knack for mischief!","Xu Wan clutched her handkerchief, imagining it was Zong Jincheng, and squeezed it fiercely, back and forth, back and forth...","Zong Jincheng hadn’t run far when Zong Wenxiu caught up with him. The two brothers encountered Wei Xinglu, who was complaining to He Zheng about Zong Jincheng’s misdeeds.","The little troublemaker’s temper flared instantly. He shouted, “Wei Xinglu, are you trying to ruin my friendship with He Zheng?!”","The four troublemakers had grown up together, as close as brothers, and had never been at odds before.","Wei Xinglu, caught off guard, hesitated for a moment before retorting, “It’s your fault! You took back the blood-sweating horses you gave us, sided with your half-brother against me, and I let that slide. But Zhai Yao, who’s been with us for years—you sent him to the slums for a month of torment, and he’s still bedridden. And now the Crown Prince has ordered him to copy the Analects a hundred times! The Analects! That’s over ten thousand characters! He won’t finish until next year!”","Wei Xinglu grew more indignant as he spoke, feeling as though one of his closest friends had betrayed another, which left him deeply unsettled.","Zong Jincheng yelled, “Zhai Yao called someone a lowly commoner and kicked an innocent old man who was caring for him. Do you think he was in the right?”","Wei Xinglu replied matter-of-factly, “But he’s always been like that. You’re the one who’s changed.”","“...I#✘#%...” Zong Jincheng was so furious he couldn’t even form coherent words.","He suddenly felt that Xu Wan was incredibly patient. Hearing his past arrogant remarks, she hadn’t lost her temper but had instead laughed while devising ways to teach him a lesson.","If it were up to him to discipline Zhai Yao and Wei Xinglu, he would have grabbed a frying pan and beaten them until they cried for mercy!"]},{"number":72,"title":"Chapter 72: Jincheng's Showcase of Endorsements","paragraphs":["In the end, it was Zong Wenxiu who explained on his behalf: \"My brother has changed because he’s been reading a lot lately and has gained a better understanding of things, which is why he’s made the right choice. He’s improved compared to before, and this change is a good one. Otherwise, the Crown Prince wouldn’t have been so angry and actively proposed punishing Zhai Yao.\"","Zong Jincheng snorted, feeling entirely comfortable as he added, \"Did you all understand? My brother makes perfect sense!\"","His brother was his perfect spokesperson!","Wei Xinglu was momentarily stunned but then continued chatting with He Zheng: \"I told you he was possessed by a ghost, and you didn’t believe me. Now he listens to everything that half-brother of his says. It’s such an embarrassment to us brothers.\"","Zong Jincheng: \"!!!\"","Damn, why was he even wasting time with Wei Xinglu?","That jerk could just keep being one of the four little troublemakers until he’s ninety-nine!","Zong Jincheng grabbed Zong Wenxiu and walked away, \"Brother, let’s go. Don’t bother with them anymore; they’re all too dumb.\"","Zong Wenxiu thought about it and agreed. It would take too long to reform a troublemaker, so he might as well focus all his energy on making his younger brother even better.","Unexpectedly, as soon as He Zheng heard they were leaving, he hurriedly called out, \"Jincheng, don’t go! I believe in you. You’re still my best brother!\"","Wei Xinglu was dumbfounded and chased after them, \"What? Am I not your best brother? He Zheng, explain yourself. Who’s your closest brother here?\"","Zong Jincheng turned his head, seeing He Zheng’s sparkling eyes, and asked, \"You think I’m right?\"","He Zheng nodded vigorously, \"As long as you keep helping me climb over walls, even if you set Zhai Yao’s house on fire, I’d still think you’re right!\"","Zong Jincheng: \"............\"","Who could understand this? I really want to curse!","Why would I even set Zhai Yao’s house on fire?","He gritted his teeth and asked, \"So, in your mind, there’s no right or wrong. Whoever helps you climb walls is your god, right?\"","He Zheng nodded eagerly, \"My real dad isn’t that great anyway.\"","Zong Jincheng rolled his eyes to the sky.","He said, \"Let’s go, brother. Hurry up. Don’t hang out with these two idiots, or the knowledge I’ve worked so hard to fill my head with will get contaminated!\"","\"!!!\" He Zheng wasn’t happy about being called an idiot, but he latched onto the word \"knowledge\" and excitedly asked, \"A head full of knowledge? Jincheng, have you been reading lately? What have you been reading? Have you read the *Thousand Character Classic*?\"","Mentioning books, the little troublemaker’s desire to show off was immediately ignited, and he stopped in his tracks!","He lifted his head proudly and said, \"Such a basic introductory book? Of course, I’ve read it. Not only have I read it, but I can also recite it!\"","\"Really?\" He Zheng exclaimed in delight, \"Can you recite it for me? I only heard a little bit last time before my dad took the book away!\"","\"What’s so hard about that?\" Zong Jincheng opened his mouth and started reciting, even thoughtfully repeating the translation afterward.","He Zheng’s eyes were filled with admiration and envy!","\"What about the *Three Character Classic*? You must know that one too, right?\"","\"That’s even simpler than the *Thousand Character Classic*...\"","Wei Xinglu watched as the two started reciting books, and his eyes nearly popped out of his head, \"Wait... are you serious? We’re the four little troublemakers, not the four great scholars!\"","Zong Jincheng continued, \"I can even recite the *Strategies of the Warring States*!\"","He Zheng: \"That’s amazing!!!\"","\"......\"","Wei Xinglu went from standing and rolling his eyes to sitting on the ground and rolling his eyes, eventually chewing on a piece of grass while listening to Zong Jincheng recite from the *Strategies of the Warring States* all the way to the *Geographical Records*.","He Zheng clapped enthusiastically, praising Zong Jincheng until he was practically unrecognizable, and so another round of reciting began...","Wei Xinglu spat out the grass in his mouth, unable to take it anymore, and muttered, \"If this isn’t possession by a ghost, how else could Zong Jincheng go from a troublemaker to a scholar in just three months?\"","The servant beside him twitched his lips, thinking to himself that the young master just couldn’t stand seeing someone else work harder than him.","Wei Xinglu stood up seriously and said, \"No, I can’t let my brother’s body be taken over by a ghost. Go, hire a ghost exorcist at any cost. I need to save my brother!\"","So what if he’s a troublemaker? He’s still my brother. This ghost who can recite books is terrifying!","\"......\" The servant suppressed a sigh, \"Yes, sir.\"","The recital finally ended when He Zheng’s father showed up. If it weren’t for the servant’s timely warning, He Zheng would have almost been caught secretly listening to books.","Back at the hunting grounds, people were bustling about, returning with their hands full of prey, praising the Crown Prince’s generosity.","The Zong brothers had been forced by Xu Wan to come and relax, so they had no competitive spirit for hunting and weren’t bothered by others’ bountiful returns.","Especially Zong Jincheng, who had been showing off in front of He Zheng and Wei Xinglu all afternoon, his pride growing uncontrollably.","On the way back, he was like a lovesick girl, occasionally sighing to Zong Wenxiu, \"Ah, brother, how am I so amazing?\"","Xu Wan: \"......\"","I’m right here, and you’re completely ignoring me, huh?","Zong Wenxiu, on the other hand, didn’t hold back his praise, \"You really are the smartest kid I’ve ever met. Even someone as talented as Qin Ye can’t memorize things after just one read, but you can. This proves you’re a natural learner, and you’ll definitely become a great scholar in the future!\"","Hearing that he was better than Qin Ye, Zong Jincheng was so pleased he started kicking his legs, laughing, \"A great scholar, a great scholar! I’ll be the greatest scholar, and no one will be as knowledgeable as me!\"","First, it was He Zheng who admired him, then his brother, then Qin Ye, the tutors, Baili Fuzi, and even the Crown Prince!","Zong Jincheng got lost in his daydream, his little feet kicking wildly again.","\"Hey!\" Xu Wan called out impatiently.","Zong Jincheng frowned at her voice and asked, \"What? I’m not ‘hey.’ That’s so rude!\"","Xu Wan glared at him, \"You’re kicking my foot.\"","Zong Jincheng looked down and saw his foot was indeed stepping on Xu Wan’s embroidered shoe, so he quickly pulled it back.","He pretended nothing happened, \"The carriage is just too small, you know... it’s too cramped. Wait, why are you even squeezing into the same carriage as us? Can’t you find another one?\"","Xu Wan smiled sweetly, \"Carriages are expensive, you know?\"","Zong Jincheng: \"...... The Marquis’s estate isn’t poor. Why are you being so frugal?\"","Xu Wan nodded, \"Then you can run back to the estate. Wenxiu and I will fit just fine.\"","Zong Jincheng: \"!\"","One day, he’d make Xu Wan admire him so much that she’d never casually mock him again!"]},{"number":73,"title":"Chapter 73: The Soft-hearted Brother","paragraphs":["There was still quite a distance to the Marquis Manor, and the little troublemaker, being quite perceptive, naturally didn’t get out of the carriage. Instead, he let out a deliberately haughty hum and turned his head toward the window.","Xu Wan, addressing Zong Wenxiu, who had returned empty-handed from the hunt, said, “Don’t take today’s events too seriously. The hunt is more about participation. Our goal was just to relax and enjoy the ride. By the way, if you find it too noisy, next time we’ll have Jincheng take you to the football field. It’s much quieter there.”","Zong Wenxiu, ever warm-hearted, replied earnestly, “Thank you for your comfort, Madam. I’m not upset. My brother even caught a fox for me.”","Zong Jincheng snorted at Xu Wan and said, “Taking credit for someone else’s effort.”","It was he who had first suggested playing football, and now this woman made it sound like he was taking Zong Wenxiu there for her sake.","Xu Wan shot him a glance. “You’re quite good at using idioms now, aren’t you?”","Zong Jincheng puffed up with pride. “Of course! I’m going to be the top scorer in the joint exams.”","“Oh,” Xu Wan rolled her eyes and didn’t continue the conversation.","The little troublemaker was waiting for Xu Wan to praise him or comfort him, just as she had done with Zong Wenxiu, for only catching a small fox during the hunt. But no matter how long he waited, it never came.","Her! Was she only going to comfort Zong Wenxiu?","What about me? I’m right here!","I didn’t win the hunt either, and I’m upset too!","The little troublemaker’s gaze at Xu Wan shifted from hopeful to angry, and finally to sheer frustration. Yet, she didn’t even glance at him, closing her eyes to feign sleep instead.","Zong Jincheng: “!!” She’s so annoying!!","Xu Wan earned another harsh mark in his grudge book. By the time they reached home, the little troublemaker was the first to get out of the carriage, letting out a loud, exaggerated hum.","Xu Wan: “...” Such a childish way to seek attention.","Zong Wenxiu hesitated and said, “Madam, I think my brother also wants your comfort and praise.”","Xu Wan smiled. “I know.”","Children’s thoughts are the easiest to guess, especially when it comes to the little troublemaker. His desires were as clear as day.","“Then why... Don’t you like my brother?” From Zong Wenxiu’s perspective, Xu Wan seemed very attentive to his brother.","No, she was extremely, extremely, extremely attentive.","Xu Wan patted his head and said, “That rascal has a certain charm that makes people quickly like him, obey him, and protect him.”","Zong Wenxiu nodded in agreement.","He already liked his brother very much and wanted to do everything for him.","Xu Wan continued, “But once you start obeying him, he’ll push his luck, testing the boundaries step by step. It’s human nature, but he just shows it more clearly.”","Zong Wenxiu: “...Really?”","Xu Wan patted him again. “Just wait and see. Let’s go home.”","That evening, after dinner, the two brothers coincidentally went to study together.","Their three private tutors were off for the day, so the two of them practiced writing silently.","The little troublemaker had a pen dipped in colorful ink in his mouth, chewing on it from time to time. His lively nature made it impossible for him to sit still. He couldn’t maintain a proper sitting posture for more than a quarter of an hour before he started fidgeting—sometimes slumping over the table to write, sometimes asking for a cushion to be placed on his chair.","This time, he had the table and chair moved behind Zong Wenxiu, leaning against his back while writing. But even this wasn’t enough to keep him still. He would bump into his brother occasionally, move away, and then suddenly lean back again.","Zong Wenxiu couldn’t take it anymore. He stopped writing and turned around. “Jincheng, stop moving around while you’re writing.”","The little troublemaker, fully immersed in his writing, hadn’t even noticed what his body was doing.","He looked up, confused. “Brother, what’s wrong?”","Zong Wenxiu: “...”","He hadn’t expected to understand Xu Wan’s words so quickly.","Agreeing to sit back-to-back with his brother while writing had been a mistake from the start.","Once you give in to his demands, his unreasonable requests multiply, and they’re often wrong. At first, Zong Wenxiu thought they were minor issues and let them slide, but those small mistakes grew until they became unbearable.","Zong Wenxiu took a deep breath and patiently explained, “You should sit properly. A messy posture not only makes your handwriting look bad but also harms your spine.”","The little troublemaker straightened up and glanced at his spine... which he couldn’t see.","He shrugged. “It’s probably fine. The doctor checks on me regularly.”","Zong Wenxiu: “...”","Alright.","He decided to play his trump card. “You’re disturbing my writing.”","His brother had just defended him in front of Wei Xinglu earlier that day, so surely he cared about his feelings. This should work, right?","But the little troublemaker froze for a moment, then looked deeply hurt.","His dark eyes shimmered like a pitiful puppy’s as he said in a soft, pleading voice, “I’m sorry, brother... I just can’t help it.”","“I...” Zong Wenxiu’s words of reprimand got stuck in his throat.","Who could possibly scold such an adorable brother?","How did Xu Wan manage to stay so firm-hearted??","The little troublemaker continued, his voice as soft as a kitten’s purr. “I just feel so calm and relaxed when I lean on you while writing. It’s not the same as leaning on Shunzi.”","Zong Wenxiu’s heart melted.","My brother depends on me!","He trusts me more than Shunzi, who’s been taking care of him for years!","How could I have been so harsh to tell him he was disturbing my writing?","Zong Wenxiu was already mentally berating himself.","It must be my fault. How could my brother be wrong when he’s so reliant on others?","He’s just a child!!","After a moment, Zong Wenxiu convinced himself. “It’s fine. Let’s keep writing.”","The little troublemaker beamed. “Brother, you’re the best!”","Shunzi: “...”","I told you Zong Wenxiu wouldn’t be able to resist.","From the moment he decided to be kind to the little troublemaker, he was destined to be manipulated, intentionally or unintentionally, at any moment.","He never stood a chance.","For the rest of the session, Zong Wenxiu continued to suffer from the disruptions, but every time he thought of stopping his brother, the thought of how sad he’d look made him hold his tongue.","This round: Soft-hearted brother, fails to discipline.","The next day during class, Xu Wan noticed their odd seating arrangement and immediately put a stop to it:","“What kind of behavior is this, sitting with your back to the teacher? Shunzi, move him back. If he dares to move the table again, I’ll have it welded to the floor so he can’t budge!”","Zong Wenxiu thought to himself, it’s only Xu Wan’s iron will that can keep his brother in line.","The little troublemaker wailed loudly, “This is exploitation! Tyranny! I protest!!”","Xu Wan could hear him even with her ears covered."]},{"number":74,"title":"Chapter 74: Rescuing a Good Brother","paragraphs":["Xu Wan rolled her eyes at him and said, \"Young master, it seems you’ve grown in knowledge but not in brains. Can the term 'tyranny' really be applied to me? If someone with ill intentions overhears, could you bear the consequences?\"","The little troublemaker’s face turned red with anger, his eyes glaring at her like an enraged frog, his chest heaving with frustration.","He held it in, he held it in.","Once he passed the imperial exams with top honors, he would immediately send Xu Wan off to the villa and never lay eyes on her again!","Seeing that the little troublemaker was unusually quiet, Xu Wan noticed a glint in his eyes that hadn’t been there before. The kid was probably plotting how to get back at her after acing the exams.","It was laughable. Once she secured that hundred million and retired in glory, she would rush straight to the villa, live in a grand mansion, and spend lavishly. She had no intention of seeing this little nuisance every day.","When Baili Xi arrived to give his lecture, Xu Wan finally left the study.","As soon as she stepped out, she turned to Cui Zhi and asked, \"Did you find out what happened at the hunting grounds yesterday?\"","The Crown Prince had suddenly gifted Jin Cheng something so valuable, and even the Crown Princess hadn’t kept it a secret. In fact, the Crown Princess had personally come to remind her. What were the two of them scheming?","Cui Zhi shook her head. \"I couldn’t find out. The Crown Prince was alone at the time, and it seemed only he and Young Master Jin Cheng were there. Buyan wasn’t present either, and Young Master Jin Cheng refused to say anything when asked.\"","Xu Wan frowned. \"Given his boastful nature, it’s unlike him to stay silent...\"","Cui Zhi reassured her, \"In any case, Young Master Jin Cheng now has the Crown Prince’s protection, which is a major advantage. It’s more good than harm, isn’t it?\"","Xu Wan shook her head.","She firmly believed that good things didn’t just fall from the sky, and the little troublemaker’s charm, while undeniable, shouldn’t be enough to sway an adult like the Crown Prince.","Gifting a jade pendant wasn’t just a casual gesture of affection.","Xu Wan said, \"The Crown Prince said it was for Jin Cheng’s protection. I’m wondering if Jin Cheng has offended someone.\"","Since marrying into the Marquis Manor, she had focused entirely on educating the little troublemaker, ignoring even her scoundrel father and stepmother. The only time she’d offended anyone was during her visit to the Eastern Palace, where she’d crossed the Duchess of Jin.","Oh, and Madam Zhai as well.","But both incidents were because of the little troublemaker. If offending these two hadn’t prompted the Crown Prince to gift a jade pendant, then perhaps it was someone even more powerful...","Cui Zhi disagreed. \"Madam, you might be overthinking it. Our young master is just a bit mischievous, and he’s been improving lately. It’s unlikely he’s offended anyone of great importance.\"","Xu Wan still felt it was something she couldn’t ignore.","She asked, \"Are the four servants who haven’t returned to Jin Cheng’s quarters skilled in martial arts?\"","Cui Zhi thought for a moment. \"I don’t think so. They were just there to play with the young master.\"","Xu Wan nodded. \"Alright, none of them need to come back.\"","Cui Zhi chuckled. \"The young master has been behaving so well lately that he hasn’t even mentioned them. He’s too busy to go out and cause trouble.\"","Xu Wan wasn’t in the mood for jokes. She pressed on, \"Are there any other guards in the Marquis Manor as skilled as Buyan or Cui Liu?\"","Cui Zhi replied, \"Not currently, but if Madam needs them, I’m sure the Old Marquis could provide some.\"","Xu Wan sent a request to the Old Marquis, and that very night, he sent over a team of skilled guards.","Among them was a special individual.","\"Madam, I am An Ying, formerly the young marquis’s shadow guard.\" An Ying’s appearance and build were unremarkable, the kind of person who would blend into a crowd unnoticed—perfect for a shadow guard.","Xu Wan met with him privately.","She gave him his orders: \"From now on, you will secretly protect Jin Cheng. If anyone threatens his life, you must save him.\"","An Ying bowed. \"Understood. I will protect Young Master Jin Cheng with my life.\"","\"Go. You don’t need to report to me,\" Xu Wan added, \"Jin Cheng is always getting into trouble, but unless it’s a matter of life and death, even if he breaks an arm, don’t reveal yourself. No one must know of your existence.\"","If anyone became aware of him, they would take precautions, and a single shadow guard might not be enough to save the day.","An Ying nodded. \"Understood. I will take my leave.\"","After giving instructions to the shadow guard, Xu Wan turned her attention to the remaining ten guards, pondering how to assign them.","She called Cui Zhi over and instructed, \"Send one to Zong Wenxiu’s quarters. The others can stay on standby in the manor.\"","\"Yes.\"","Cui Zhi didn’t fully understand, but since Xu Wan didn’t elaborate, she didn’t press further and soon forgot about it.","The little troublemaker’s presence was simply too overwhelming. He was constantly howling in the study—sometimes about the sheer volume of books he had to memorize, sometimes about how uncomfortable the chair was, and other times about how the imperial exams were taking too long to arrive, hindering his path to first place.","The Marquis Manor was in a constant uproar. Despite only having two children, it felt like an army of thousands, with most of the noise coming from one of them.","Xu Wan even dreamed of the little troublemaker’s howls during her nap, no matter how much she yelled in her dream, \"Cry already! Shed some tears! Haven’t you had any water?\" The little troublemaker in her dream remained tearless.","When she woke up in frustration, the howls from the study were still ongoing.","Xu Wan sat up, rolling her eyes dramatically.","\"That noisy little brat!\"","She got up, put on her shoes, and stormed toward the study, muttering, \"It’s midday nap time. If he wants to study, fine, but he’s disturbing everyone else’s rest. That little rascal... I’m going to glue his mouth shut with fish glue today!\"","Xu Wan charged over with murderous intent, only to find the study empty.","Zong Wenxiu was quietly writing, but the little troublemaker’s seat was vacant. Not only that, but Shunzi and Buyan were also missing. It didn’t seem like they’d just stepped out for a moment.","\"Where’s Jin Cheng?\" Xu Wan asked.","Zong Wenxiu looked up. \"Someone came to report that Wei Xinglu was here to see him, so he went out.\"","\"Wei Xinglu?\" Xu Wan frowned.","One of the four notorious troublemakers. What good could come from his visit?","She turned around swiftly and headed for the entrance. \"Come on, Cui Zhi, let’s see what they’re up to. I don’t want them causing any more trouble.\"","At the entrance of the Marquis Manor, Wei Xinglu and Zong Jincheng finally met. The little troublemaker, frustrated with his studies, was thrilled to have a friend come by to play.","\"Xinglu, come in! It’s been so long since you’ve visited the Marquis Manor.\" Zong Jincheng wasn’t one to hold grudges against his friends. A little argument was forgotten in a few days.","Wei Xinglu, touched by his enthusiasm, was nearly in tears. Jin Cheng was still his best friend, the kind of friend who wouldn’t argue with him or force him to memorize books.","Wei Xinglu missed the old days with the little troublemaker, so he’d come today to rescue his friend and bring him back to his true self!","His eyes gleamed as he concocted a plan. \"Jin Cheng, I’ve come up with a great idea for He Zheng to escape over the wall, but we need a place to test it. Can we try it here at the Marquis Manor?\""]},{"number":75,"title":"Chapter 75: Jincheng Being Sprayed with Talisman Water","paragraphs":["Zong Jincheng replied, \"Of course I can.\" He was also quite eager to help He Zheng out of his predicament.","Wei Xinglu's eyes lit up as he pointed to the wall beside the gate, saying, \"Then let's use this wall. I think it's the same height as He Zheng's house.\"","\"Alright, what else do we need? I'll have Buyan fetch it,\" Zong Jincheng said.","Wei Xinglu quickly added, \"A ladder!\"","Zong Jincheng: \"...\"","He looked at Wei Xinglu as if he were an idiot and asked, \"Is this the brilliant plan you came up with to help He Zheng scale the wall? If he could find a ladder at home, would we have had to stack stools last time?\"","Wei Xinglu coughed awkwardly, realizing how ridiculous his idea sounded, and quickly improvised, \"I meant a human ladder! A real human ladder!\"","\"Huh?\"","Wei Xinglu enthusiastically explained, \"The wall is about ten feet high. If you stand on two human ladders, you can easily get over it. Here, let Buyan and Shunzi try it out for you!\"","Zong Jincheng glanced at the two of them; their height was sufficient.","Shunzi waved his hands in panic, \"No, no, Young Master! I’m as weak as a kitten. If you stand on my shoulders, I won’t be able to get up...\"","Zong Jincheng thought about the scenario and realized it was indeed possible.","Wei Xinglu, however, kept pushing his absurd idea, \"It’ll work! Just stand on Buyan’s shoulders first, then Zong Jincheng can climb up. Finally, Buyan can stand up, and it’ll be perfect!\"","Shunzi: \"...\"","So, you’re determined to climb that wall today, huh?","\"Young Master, I think...\"","Before Shunzi could finish his protest, Zong Jincheng instinctively cut him off, \"Don’t think anymore. He Zheng is my good brother, and I’m definitely going to help him. Let’s start!\"","\"Alright!\" Wei Xinglu slapped his thigh and shouted, \"Ready, go!\"","Zong Jincheng climbed up, utterly confused. Why was Wei Xinglu shouting slogans for something as simple as climbing a wall?","Before he could ponder further, Buyan stood up, and Shunzi lifted the young troublemaker higher. The two adults formed a human ladder, successfully hoisting the young master above the height of the wall.","The young master grabbed the edge of the wall, about to speak, when suddenly a head popped up from the other side and sprayed a mouthful of holy water straight at his adorable face!","\"Heaven and earth, spirits and demons, reveal yourselves!\"","\"...\"","Shunzi, unable to see what was happening below, felt water dripping onto his head and shouted in confusion, \"What’s going on? Young Master! Is it raining?\"","The young master had instinctively closed his eyes but was still drenched in holy water, his hair dripping wet.","He clenched his fists and roared, \"Wei! Xing! Lu! I’m going to kill you!!!\"","The roar was so loud it scared the nearby birds into a frenzy.","Wei Xinglu, still below, taunted, \"You book-devouring ghost, get out of my brother’s body right now!\"","His brother, Zong Jincheng, was the leader of the four young troublemakers of the capital. There was no way he could be the little genius who could recite astronomy and geography backward!","\"You!!\" Zong Jincheng yelled, \"Buyan! Put me down! I’m going to kill this little bastard!\"","Buyan obeyed immediately and lowered the young master.","Wei Xinglu panicked and ran around, screaming, \"Help... help! Why is this ghost so powerful? The holy water didn’t work!\"","Zong Jincheng pounced on him, pinning him to the ground, and started shaking him by the neck, \"Who’s the ghost? You’re the ghost, you jerk! You dared to have someone spray dirty water on my face. I’m going to end you today!!\"","\"Cough... cough... Master, Master, save me...\" Wei Xinglu choked, his eyes rolling back as he looked around for help.","The next moment, two ghost hunters jumped over the wall, one holding a whisk and the other a star chart, both pointing at Zong Jincheng and shouting, \"Demon, show your true form at once!\"","\"...\"","Zong Jincheng’s face turned red.","Then purple.","Then black.","Even Shunzi, standing nearby, could barely hold him back, feeling as if the young master was about to blow up the entire Marquis Manor.","Then, the young master furiously ordered, \"Buyan, arrest these two frauds!\"","\"Yes!\"","With a single move, Buyan subdued the two men and handed them over to the guards at the gate of the Marquis Manor.","\"Hahahahaha...\" Xu Wan, who had just arrived, burst into laughter after witnessing the entire scene, almost rolling on the ground.","The young master, his hair disheveled and still fuming, saw Xu Wan laughing at him and, in a fit of frustration, turned back to continue strangling Wei Xinglu, \"You jerk, how dare you make fun of me! You think I’m a pushover?!\"","Wei Xinglu was already gasping for air. Xu Wan ordered Cui Liu to rescue him, while other maids quickly brought water and towels to clean up the young master.","Zong Jincheng stood there, his chest heaving with anger, his eyes fixed on Wei Xinglu, afraid that Xu Wan might secretly let him escape.","Wei Xinglu coughed for a while before finally catching his breath. Pointing at Zong Jincheng, he weakly accused, \"You powerful little ghost, I warn you, get out of my brother’s body right now. Otherwise, even if I die... even if I’m strangled to death, I’ll haunt you as a ghost!\"","Zong Jincheng, infuriated, wanted to charge at him again.","But Xu Wan held him back, smiling as she tried to reason with him, \"Your brother here cares about you, doesn’t he? He’s worried you’ve been possessed by a ghost and is risking his life to save you.\"","Zong Jincheng exploded, \"Who’s the one possessed by a ghost here?!\"","Damn it, why was everyone against him today?","First Xu Wan, and now even his own brother was making a fool of him!","The young master felt like he had lost all dignity today!","Wei Xinglu, still coughing, pointed at Zong Jincheng and accused, \"If you’re not a ghost, how come after not seeing you for three months, you suddenly know how to recite so many books? I’ve been forced to study for five or six years by my father, and I can’t recite as much as you did that day!\"","Zong Jincheng snapped, \"That’s because I’m naturally talented! I have a photographic memory! Do you understand? I only need to read something once, and I can remember it all! I can even recite it backward!\"","\"Bull!\" Wei Xinglu shot back, \"I know my brother too well. He doesn’t have that kind of ability!\"","Zong Jincheng immediately started looking around for something.","Wei Xinglu asked, \"What are you looking for?\"","Zong Jincheng replied, \"I’m looking for a stick to beat you to death!\"","This idiot actually thought of him as nothing more than a good-for-nothing brat!","Who did he think he was looking down on?","Wei Xinglu: \"...\"","Seeing Zong Jincheng about to lose his temper again, this fiery temper was indeed characteristic of his brother, but...","\"Are you really Zong Jincheng?\" he tentatively asked.","Zong Jincheng finally found a stick and swung it at him, \"I’m your father!!\"","\"Ahhh! Help!! Madam Zong, save me! Save me, save me, save me!!\""]},{"number":76,"title":"Chapter 76: Photographic Memory","paragraphs":["The two children were chasing each other around the courtyard, creating a lively and warm atmosphere, reminiscent of the good old days at the orphanage.","Xu Wan watched for a while before smiling and stopping them, saying, \"Young Master Wei, Jincheng is telling the truth. His memory is excellent, which is why he’s made such rapid progress. If you don’t believe me, you can have him read a new book and recite it for you on the spot.\"","\"I agree, I agree!\" Wei Xinglu, who had been relentlessly chased, had no other choice but to comply.","Zong Jincheng snorted, his face filled with pride.","Wei Xinglu was led to the grand study. Before even entering, he saw the plaque at the entrance and read it aloud: \"Marquis Manor Elite Class... What a strange plaque.\"","Shunzi, standing nearby, took the opportunity to explain the concept of the elite class. After hearing it, Wei Xinglu was first surprised, then shivered all over, saying, \"This elite class sounds terrifying. How miserable must those who study here be?\"","Shunzi’s lips twitched, thinking to himself, *You wouldn’t even qualify to join if you tried.*","In the entire capital—no, in all of Great Chu—there was only one place like this.","However, once Wei Xinglu stepped inside, he couldn’t help but exclaim, \"Wow, Jincheng, your study is enormous! It’s like a library in here!\"","He wasn’t wrong. The grand study had indeed been built by the old Marquis Zong Zhao to resemble a library. Besides the first floor, which served as a classroom and housed over a thousand commonly used books, the second floor contained countless rare texts, paintings, and treasures, rivaling the collection of an ordinary academy’s library.","However, the two Zong brothers usually studied on the first floor, where the books were more than enough for them, so they rarely ventured to the second floor.","Zong Wenxiu, who had been studying, looked up in confusion at the sudden arrival of an outsider. He glanced at his mother and younger brother, only to see the little devil raise his head proudly and declare, \"Pick any book you like here, and I’ll recite it for you on the spot.\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"?\" *Is my brother challenging someone to a recitation contest?*","He put down his brush, curious to see how this would unfold. When it came to reciting books, his brother was unbeatable.","Wei Xinglu began to seriously browse the shelves. Although he was also a bit of a troublemaker, his family was strict, so he had read quite a few books himself. He had studied the same texts that Jincheng and He Zheng had recited that day, which was why he knew just how terrifying the so-called \"recitation ghost\" was.","But what if it wasn’t a ghost? What if it really was Jincheng...","Wei Xinglu didn’t dare dwell on the thought and quickly continued searching the shelves. After some deliberation, he picked a less common and rarely tested medical text—*Treatise on Cold Damage and Miscellaneous Diseases*.","\"Recite this one. I don’t need much—just ten pages within half an hour, and I’ll admit you’re not possessed by a ghost.\"","Zong Jincheng rolled his eyes at him, took the book, and began skimming through it at lightning speed.","Wei Xinglu continued to make sarcastic remarks, \"Sure, take your time skimming through it first. There are probably plenty of difficult characters you don’t recognize.\"","Zong Jincheng ignored him, still reading intently without even sitting down.","Wei Xinglu sat down first, his eyes wandering around the grand study as he offered some friendly advice, \"Why don’t you sit down to recite? I’ll give you half an hour.\"","Zong Jincheng still didn’t respond.","Feeling ignored, Wei Xinglu turned to Zong Wenxiu and asked, \"Has Jincheng been studying with you recently?\"","Zong Wenxiu nodded.","Wei Xinglu nodded knowingly, \"No wonder he’s so protective of you. Studying together does create a strong bond, especially when you’re both in the same tough spot!\"","Zong Wenxiu smiled but didn’t say anything.","Wei Xinglu continued rambling, \"But don’t you think he’s been possessed? Reciting so many books in just three months? He’s not some reincarnated deity. How could he possibly be this good...\"","Zong Wenxiu frowned, \"Possessed?\"","He glanced at his brother and then at Xu Wan, who had been quietly observing. It seemed he now understood why Wei Xinglu was here.","Zong Wenxiu explained earnestly, \"You’ve misunderstood. Jincheng is still Jincheng. He’s just started applying himself. He enjoys studying now.\"","Wei Xinglu scoffed, \"Come on, who in the world enjoys something as boring as studying? Especially Jincheng! He’d rather play soccer, race horses, or fight crickets than sit at home reading books!\"","Zong Wenxiu replied, \"But that’s exactly what he’s doing now.\"","Wei Xinglu: \"...\"","Fine, keep defending him. When Jincheng fails to recite the book, you’ll be just as desperate as I am to exorcise the ghost!","Wei Xinglu was still convinced that the two masters his family had hired weren’t skilled enough. If the Marquis Manor spent a fortune to find someone better, they’d surely succeed.","Wei Xinglu was already dreaming of the day his troublemaking buddy would return, and they could once again indulge in carefree fun, feasting, and living life to the fullest!","\"Wake up, I’m done,\" Zong Jincheng shattered his daydream.","\"What? Has it already been half an hour? That was fast!\" Wei Xinglu exclaimed.","Zong Jincheng pointed at the teacup beside him, \"The tea I poured for you is still scalding hot.\"","Wei Xinglu took a sip and immediately jumped up, \"Pfft... Does your Marquis Manor serve tea hot enough to burn your tongue?!\"","\"Only yours, dummy,\" Zong Jincheng tossed the book back to him. \"Listen carefully, I’m starting the recitation.\"","\"Taiyang disease, whether already feverish or not yet feverish, must be accompanied by chills, body aches, nausea, and a tight pulse in both the yin and yang meridians. This is called cold damage...\"","Wei Xinglu quickly flipped through the book as Zong Jincheng recited the first volume of the *Treatise on Cold Damage*. His heart pounded like a drum. How had he memorized the book so quickly? In this amount of time, he should’ve only been able to read it once!","\"Photographic memory! Do you understand?!\" Zong Jincheng’s triumphant voice echoed in his ears.","As Zong Jincheng flawlessly recited every word, Wei Xinglu felt like screaming a thousand curses.","Damn.","He really does have a photographic memory!","Wei Xinglu was filled with frustration. The feeling of being overtaken by his best friend in just three months was utterly miserable.","As he listened to the little devil recite, Wei Xinglu flipped through the book and noticed that all the difficult characters had been annotated with simpler phonetic equivalents. This meant that even if Zong Jincheng didn’t recognize a character, he could still read and memorize it using the phonetic guide.","Wei Xinglu was even more horrified. He flipped through the book and saw that all 50,000 characters of the first volume had been annotated by hand.","Damn, that’s an immense amount of work!","He suddenly remembered Shunzi’s explanation of the plaque when he first entered the study. Good heavens, was this really a classroom? It was nothing like the classrooms he had seen or imagined!","By then, Zong Jincheng had finished reciting all ten pages, looking at him with pride and confidence. \"Well? Are you convinced now?\"","Such speed in memorization was unparalleled in the entire world!","Even that arrogant Qin Ye, who thought he was better than everyone else, couldn’t match this!","Only he—only Zong Jincheng—could do this!"]},{"number":77,"title":"Chapter 77: The Strongest in the Entire Capital","paragraphs":["Wei Xinglu swallowed hard and said, \"You're practically inhuman...\" If the children of those hardworking scholar-officials knew about this talent, they'd be green with envy.","Zong Jincheng's face darkened upon hearing this, thinking he was being accused of being possessed by a ghost again. Furious, he started looking around for a stick.","Wei Xinglu quickly jumped onto a stool, clasped his hands together in surrender, and said, \"Stop, stop, stop! I’m sorry, brother, I was wrong, I was wrong! I shouldn’t have misunderstood you. You’re amazing, the best in the Capital City!\"","Only then did Zong Jincheng stop, crossing his arms and letting out a proud huff.","After apologizing, Wei Xinglu chatted warmly with him. Being naturally sociable and emotionally intelligent, he quickly managed to calm the little devil down.","The little devil even patted his shoulder and said, \"Good brother, if you ever can’t figure something out, come to me for help!\"","Wei Xinglu’s mouth twitched, but he forced a smile and agreed.","This little rascal had grown stronger, but his personality was still the same—still unmistakably Zong Jincheng.","\"Then I’ll head home. I’ll come back to play another day.\"","\"I’ll have Shunzi see you out.\"","\"Alright.\"","As he was leaving, Wei Xinglu suddenly stopped and turned to look at the plaque above the grand study door. The five characters were still as striking as ever, strange yet unique.","After a moment, he muttered, \"So bizarre...\"","After the commotion ended, the little devil immersed himself in his studies again, competing fiercely with Zong Wenxiu.","Soon, another half-month passed, and the day of the joint academy exam arrived.","The little devil woke up early, standing on his bed and shouting, \"Defeat Qin Ye!\"","Shunzi: \"...\"","He really had an endless supply of energy.","But as a sensible servant, Shunzi smiled and gave him a look of unwavering trust to avoid upsetting the young master.","However, Buyan, who lacked tact, was different. Thinking he was being helpful, he reminded, \"Young Master, Qin Ye’s exam paper is different from yours today. You can’t defeat him.\"","Shunzi: \"!!!\"","Buyan! Why did you suddenly decide to speak up now?","Who’s going to put out the fire if this house burns down?!","Zong Jincheng’s expression immediately changed.","He glared at Buyan, then at Shunzi.","Shunzi, feeling wronged: \"?\"","What does this have to do with me? I’m not the head of this household!","Zong Jincheng snorted and said gravely, \"I’ll defeat Qin Ye sooner or later, whether it’s next month or the month after. It’ll definitely be this year!\"","Shunzi quickly chimed in, \"Young Master Zong is the strongest in the Capital City! You’ll definitely succeed!\"","After saying this, he kicked Buyan, signaling him to join in.","Buyan not only missed the hint but also glared back at him.","Shunzi: \"...\" This kid is hopeless.","Zong Jincheng didn’t pay attention. He was lost in his own world, thinking about the students from Hanlin North Academy he was going to defeat today. His fighting spirit burned fiercely, rising straight to the sky.","\"Let’s go! Crush Hanlin North Academy!\"","\"Let’s do it!\" Shunzi cheered him on while helping him get ready, smiling all the while.","The atmosphere today was clearly different. The little devil’s high spirits and confidence were infectious, filling the entire hall with energy. Even Zong Wenxiu felt a surge of strength.","He encouraged them, \"Jincheng, we’re going to do great on the exam today!\"","Zong Jincheng bumped fists with him and said confidently, \"Of course!\"","As the carriage set off, the two continued to silently review their notes, as if they were heading to an important entrance exam.","Xu Wan didn’t disturb them. Last-minute cramming could be useful, so there was no need to stop them.","After getting out of the carriage, the three walked toward the academy. Since the two boys were well-prepared and had taken many exams before, Xu Wan didn’t offer any further advice and prepared to see them off.","But just a few steps away, they heard a man accompanying his child to the exam nagging, \"Lin Yu, look at Zong Jincheng. He’s only been studying for a few months and is already second in your class. And then there’s you, not studying hard, just playing around. If you don’t make the rankings this time, don’t call yourself my son!\"","Zong Jincheng suddenly heard his name mentioned in such a proud and complimentary way, and he couldn’t stop grinning. He nudged Zong Wenxiu, signaling him to listen too.","But Zong Wenxiu shook his head and gestured toward the child.","The boy named Lin Yu looked about the same age as the little devil and was likely in the same class. He was being scolded harshly as he was sent to take the exam, but he wasn’t crying. Instead, his face was full of defiance and resentment.","Zong Jincheng initially thought Lin Yu was challenging him and was about to go over and say something. But the boy suddenly stopped in his tracks and exploded.","He shouted at his father, \"How can you say I’m not studying hard? Do you know what time I get up to study? Have you ever seen me reading late into the night? All you do is go out drinking and come back dead drunk. Have you ever cared about me? Have you even looked at my exam papers? All you notice is that my ranking dropped, but have you seen how much stronger I’ve become?\"","This outburst shocked Zong Jincheng and Zong Wenxiu, as well as the students passing by. Even Xu Wan stopped in her tracks and turned to look.","\"Who is this? So brave, daring to talk back to his father.\"","\"Disobedient, disobedient. He’s going to be beaten for sure.\"","\"I doubt he’ll be able to take the exam today.\"","\"I’m afraid he won’t be able to continue his studies after this.\"","\"But don’t you think he has a point?\"","\"It does seem like he’s right...\"","The students whispered among themselves, initially watching for the drama but eventually starting to discuss the issue of parental education, gradually agreeing that the child was right.","Lin’s father, who had never been defied by his child before and felt humiliated in front of so many people, raised his hand menacingly to strike.","But Lin Yu didn’t flinch, standing his ground and speaking with conviction, \"Zong Jincheng can rank second because he’s wealthy and influential, with a good mother and the best tutors. What do I have? What have you provided for me? How many times have I told you I’m falling behind and need a private tutor to help me? And what did you say? That I’m incompetent and stupid for not keeping up in class. You only know how to criticize me. Have you ever listened to my pleas? How can you, as a father, be so self-righteous in blaming me?\"","Lin Yu’s gaze was both earnest and perplexed, but he still didn’t cry. He felt wronged, but he didn’t think he was the one at fault.","\"Well said!\" someone in the crowd shouted.","\"I feel the same way!\"","\"Support! Lin Yu, you’re right!\"","The students were moved by his words, feeling as if he had spoken directly to their hearts, and they stepped forward to support him."]},{"number":78,"title":"Chapter 78: Envy You for Having Xu Wan","paragraphs":["Zong Jincheng and Zong Wenxiu simultaneously stepped in front of Lin Yu, forming a human shield to prevent Lin's Father from landing that slap on Lin Yu.","Lin's Father trembled with rage, his voice shaking as he said, \"You... you students are completely out of control... This is disobedience to elders, a grave offense! Hasn’t the teacher at Qingbo Academy taught you this?\"","\"Disobedience to elders? You’re not our father, nor are you our relative!\"","\"We’re just standing up for what’s right, lending a helping hand!\"","\"That’s right, that’s right!\"","Zong Jincheng raised his voice even louder, \"The teacher has taught us so much, but I doubt you’ve learned any of it. For example, the Book of Rites says: What is human righteousness? A father’s kindness and a son’s filial piety. Have you shown kindness as a father?\"","\"That’s right! Have you shown kindness as a father?\"","\"If you can’t even do that, why should Lin Yu listen to you?\"","The students’ protests grew louder, and with Zong Jincheng, the fearless troublemaker, leading the charge, it was clear they were determined to stand by Lin Yu.","Xu Wan was surprised that Zong Jincheng could now quote classics to help others. Not bad, his studies were improving.","She gave him a silent thumbs-up.","Lin's Father kept trying to take action, but Zong Jincheng and the crowd of students pushed him further and further away from Lin Yu.","The commotion was so loud that it caught the attention of the teachers at Qingbo Academy.","Finally, the headmaster stepped in and said, \"It’s almost time for the exam. Students, stop gathering here and follow your teachers into the examination hall. Lin's Father, come with me.\"","Lin's Father shouted, \"What exam? Lin Yu isn’t taking it! Such an unfilial son, why should I keep paying for his education?\"","This statement reignited the students’ anger.","Lin Yu wasn’t surprised.","His father had always been like this.","The headmaster, usually mild-mannered, was also angered by this remark. He snapped, \"Teacher Zhang, hurry and take the students in for the exam.\"","Teacher Zhang quickly responded, \"Yes, yes, we’re going. Children, follow me. Leave this to the headmaster.\"","Zong Jincheng pulled Lin Yu along as they walked, comforting him, \"Don’t worry about him. The headmaster will handle it. Let’s focus on the exam.\"","Lin Yu said gratefully, \"Thank you, Zong Jincheng.\"","Zong Jincheng raised an eyebrow and chuckled, \"You really know me? I don’t remember you.\"","He was secretly thrilled. It must have been because of his outstanding performance in the last exam, which had made him famous throughout Qingbo Academy.","After all, he was one of only two students from the academy who had made it onto the Four-Academy Joint Exam ranking!","Now he finally felt that Xu Wan had chosen a good academy for him. With his classmates’ abilities far inferior to his, they all looked up to him as a god of exams. It felt amazing!","Lin Yu said, \"Because I was third.\"","\"Ah? So you were just one spot away from making the ranking?\" After all, Zong Jincheng was at the very bottom of the Four-Academy Joint Exam ranking.","Lin Yu replied honestly, \"Actually, in the previous monthly exam, I was right behind you. You probably didn’t notice me, just like Qin Ye didn’t notice you.\"","Zong Jincheng: \"...!\"","His smirk instantly disappeared.","He even felt like cursing.","This guy not only knew how to argue with his father but also how to roast others.","Scary!","\"But we all pay attention to the person above us and hope to surpass them,\" Lin Yu said. \"So I know you, and I understand you well.\"","Zong Jincheng thought back to his earlier remarks and commented, \"You do know me well. You know my family has power and influence, and the best teachers... but a good mother? Forget it! That bad woman is always finding ways to bully me!\"","\"But without her, you wouldn’t have become who you are,\" Lin Yu said.","Zong Jincheng immediately turned to look at Zong Wenxiu.","Zong Wenxiu nodded in agreement. Lin Yu was right; Xu Wan was a good person.","Zong Jincheng still didn’t want to accept this. He turned his head away and snorted.","Lin Yu said wistfully, \"If only I had an elder like your mother, maybe I could surpass you.\"","Zong Jincheng grew more and more displeased.","Why did everyone like Xu Wan so much, when she was always giving him a hard time?","Zong Jincheng was unhappy and didn’t even want to talk to Lin Yu anymore. He pulled a long face and hurried into the examination hall.","Left behind, Lin Yu said to Zong Wenxiu, \"He really doesn’t know how lucky he is. If he had a father like mine, he’d be crying with no way out.\"","Zong Wenxiu patted his shoulder and said with a smile, \"Do well on the exam. I’m sure you’ll get great results this time.\"","\"Yeah, I don’t want to be third again.\"","The long exam finally ended as the sun set. The students rushed out of the examination hall, some looking troubled, others overjoyed. But they were all young, full of vitality and energy.","As soon as Zong Jincheng saw Zong Wenxiu, he bounded over and slung an arm around his shoulder, boasting, \"Brother, I thought the exam was so easy and familiar. A lot of the questions were from the practice tests we’ve done.\"","Zong Wenxiu bent slightly under his weight but quickly straightened up. He smiled and said, \"Xu Wan really is experienced. She had Teacher Zhao guide us through many past exam papers. No matter how the questions change, the core remains the same.\"","Zong Jincheng said proudly, \"I’m sure I’ll rank first in the joint exam this time!\"","Zong Wenxiu, seeing his brother so confident, didn’t want to discourage him. It wasn’t impossible—Qin Ye had moved to the Child Prodigy Class, and Zong Jincheng’s abilities should dominate the eight-year-old class.","Even if it was the most prestigious Hanlin North Academy in the capital.","\"By the way, has Lin Yu come out yet?\" Zong Jincheng asked.","He was worried that Lin Yu would be chased and beaten by Lin's Father as soon as he left.","Zong Wenxiu shook his head. \"I’m not sure. Let’s ask Xu Wan. I’m sure she’s been keeping an eye on things.\"","\"Oh... maybe. But you go ask. I don’t want to talk to her,\" Zong Jincheng said stubbornly.","Zong Wenxiu laughed. \"Alright.\"","Every time they had an exam, Xu Wan would wait for them at the academy. Usually, the headmaster or a teacher would accompany her, answering her questions about their studies. But this time, because of Lin's Father’s outburst, the headmaster and teachers who weren’t invigilating had gone to reason with him.","Unfortunately, Lin's Father was impossible to reason with.","Xu Wan said, \"Lin's Father said, either the child doesn’t take the exam, and he’ll take him home and beat him to death; or he won’t support or keep the child anymore, and Qingbo Academy can deal with it.\"","Zong Wenxiu exclaimed, \"What? Then what happened? How did the academy handle it?\"","\"Yeah, what did they do?\" Zong Jincheng was also anxious.","Xu Wan smiled mysteriously and teased, \"Guess.\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","Zong Jincheng: \"!!!\"","Guess what?","Xu Wan laughed a few times and guided them, \"Don’t be mad. You need to learn to think for yourselves. If you were the headmaster and teachers, how would you handle a situation like Lin's son’s?\""]},{"number":79,"title":"Chapter 79: The Little Demon King is Jealous","paragraphs":["Although they wouldn’t be tested on interpersonal matters in the short term, it was still beneficial to practice early to stimulate their minds. So, Xu Wan kept the two curious little ones hanging, asking them to think of possible solutions.","The little troublemaker, Zong Jincheng, was certainly not the first to cooperate.","It was the well-behaved and obedient Zong Wenxiu who broke the deadlock: “I think the academy would choose the first option. No matter how bad Lin Yu’s father is, he’s still his father. The dean and teachers can only advise; they can’t interfere in family matters.”","Zong Jincheng initially didn’t want to participate in the guessing, but hearing what Zong Wenxiu said, he immediately retorted, “But didn’t you see that Lin Yu has already fallen out with him? If he goes home with his father, he’ll definitely be beaten to death! I think the latter is more likely—Lin Yu would rather stay with the dean than go home.”","Zong Wenxiu countered, “But Lin Yu needs money for his studies and living expenses. The dean has no relation to him—why would he be willing to support him?”","Zong Jincheng was left speechless: “But we can’t let him go home and be beaten to death...”","Zong Wenxiu replied, “He won’t be beaten to death, though it might be severe. There’s no lasting enmity between father and son; they might reconcile in a few days.”","Zong Jincheng pouted, “I still don’t agree with this decision. That father doesn’t seem like he’ll change in a few days, and Lin Yu will still suffer. If I were the dean, I’d take Lin Yu home. It’s just an extra pair of chopsticks, and our Marquis Manor isn’t short of money.”","Zong Wenxiu reminded him, “Not everyone lives as comfortably as you do. Have you forgotten Jing Zhe?”","The image of the slums flashed in the little troublemaker’s mind, and he instantly had no rebuttal.","After a while, he blinked his big, dark eyes and asked, “So if the dean and teachers don’t intervene, can we take Lin Yu home?”","Zong Wenxiu looked at Xu Wan; it was up to her.","Xu Wan raised an eyebrow and smiled, “So the solution you two came up with is to take responsibility yourselves? What if, in the future, it’s not just one Lin Yu but thousands of them? What would you do then? Use your own money to save everyone from hardship?”","Zong Jincheng, full of impulsive bravery, blurted out, “Why not?”","Zong Wenxiu tugged at him and reluctantly reminded him, “Brother, I know you want to help others, but if it’s thousands of people, we don’t have that much money.”","Zong Jincheng didn’t believe it: “Impossible. My grandmother is as rich as a country.”","Zong Wenxiu sighed, “That’s just an expression. It doesn’t mean she can actually support the entire nation.”","“Huh?” Zong Jincheng was confused. Is that so?","Zong Wenxiu said, “We need to think of more practical solutions, ways to help them become self-reliant rather than taking everything on ourselves. Otherwise, even if we’re crushed, we can’t save thousands of people.”","Xu Wan nodded in approval, “Exactly. It’s better to teach someone to fish than to give them a fish.”","Zong Wenxiu, praised by Xu Wan, shyly nodded.","Zong Jincheng’s expression immediately darkened.","This bad woman, always praising others.","She’s so biased!","Zong Jincheng angrily said, “What fish? I don’t understand what you’re saying.”","Xu Wan explained, “It means that giving someone a fish is less effective than teaching them how to fish. It’s a more sustainable and efficient approach.”","“But Lin Yu is so young. How can he learn to fish?” Zong Jincheng still didn’t get it. “How much money can fishing even make?”","Zong Wenxiu pondered, “Fishing doesn’t earn much, and Lin Yu might not know how to fish. But I think, since he’s a diligent student with excellent grades, his handwriting must be good. He could earn money by copying books—35 coins per book, enough for his living expenses.”","“35... coins?” Hearing the unit “coins” again, Zong Jincheng was still puzzled. “Can he really survive on that? Where would he live?”","Zong Wenxiu nodded, “Yes, it’s been common for poor students to earn a living by copying books since ancient times. And Qingbo Academy has dormitories for students. He can live there without going home and still manage well.”","Zong Jincheng’s mind was suddenly opened.","So even a child his age, if talented enough, could survive without relying on family.","Self-reliance...","A child his age could truly be self-reliant.","Xu Wan also nodded and revealed the answer: “Lin Yu didn’t want to go home, so that’s how the dean handled it. He didn’t give Lin Yu money but instead connected him with someone who buys hand-copied books, giving Lin Yu a way to earn income.”","Zong Wenxiu smiled, pleased that his reasoning had been correct.","The dean was just an ordinary person, doing what he could to help. If he only gave handouts, he might not even be able to support himself.","Zong Jincheng was unhappy again.","His eyes were filled with jealousy, jealous that Zong Wenxiu had guessed correctly, making his own suggestion seem so unrealistic.","“Hmph!” Zong Jincheng made a loud noise and turned to climb into the carriage.","Zong Wenxiu, unsure what was wrong, wanted to follow him.","Xu Wan called from behind, “That kid’s pride is hurt again. He can’t stand losing and blames others for being too good. Such a tsundere. If you comfort him, it’ll never end.”","Zong Wenxiu thought for a moment and said, “Brother just hasn’t been exposed to these things, so he doesn’t understand. He’s learning gradually, and with his intelligence, he’ll probably surpass me soon.”","He spoke sincerely, then ran toward the carriage.","Xu Wan smiled at his words and complained to Cui Zhi, “That child is such a selfless altruist.”","“An altruist?” Cui Zhi didn’t fully understand but managed to respond, “Young Master Wenxiu would rather fail the imperial exam himself than see Young Master Jincheng fail. Even though they’re only cousins, their bond is stronger than many biological brothers.”","Xu Wan chuckled softly and sighed, “Growing up in a place like the slums and still being raised so well—Auntie Hong is an excellent mother.”","Cui Zhi nodded in agreement, “Since Auntie Hong found out that Young Master Wenxiu is studying with Young Master Jincheng under Master Baili in the study, she’s told him not to visit her often and to focus on his studies. She’s even instructed him to listen to you, Madam. It seems like she regards you as the mistress of their branch of the family.”","Auntie Hong had once planned for Zong Wenxiu to be raised in the old madam’s courtyard after her death. Now that her health had improved, she saw hope in Xu Wan.","Like a sensible concubine, she wasn’t interested in power struggles or rising above her station. She only wanted her child to be guided and cared for by the legitimate wife, ensuring a bright future for him.","A parent’s love for their child is measured by their foresight.","Xu Wan understood.","She replied, “A few days ago, the family doctor told me that Auntie Hong has almost fully recovered. She should come out and bask in the sun more often; there’s no need for her to be so reserved.”","“Yes, Madam.”","In the carriage, Zong Jincheng was still sulking.","“Jincheng?” Zong Wenxiu called out.","Zong Jincheng turned his head away and let out another loud huff.","Zong Wenxiu smiled, “Guess what I just said to Madam?”"]},{"number":80,"title":"Chapter 80: Counter-killed by Xu Wan","paragraphs":["As if stepping on a fuse, the already smoldering cannon finally exploded.","The little demon king howled, \"I can’t guess it again! I won’t guess anymore!!!\"","The younger brother had a bad temper and a fragile ego, always erupting in anger at the slightest provocation.","At first, Zong Wenxiu found it hard to adjust, thinking he was difficult to please and had a strange temper. But as he got to know him better, he realized that the younger brother was just tough on the outside but soft on the inside—he was the best brother in the world, the kind who was easy to appease.","Zong Wenxiu patiently sat down beside him and said softly, \"I told Madam that you just haven’t been exposed to the lives of ordinary people, so you couldn’t guess. But you’re very smart, much smarter than me. Once you figure all this out, you’ll definitely be way better than me.\"","The little demon king’s back was still turned, but his ears perked up.","Zong Wenxiu continued, \"Madam also said that you have the makings of a great official. If you ever gain power, you could save thousands of people. That’s much more significant than helping just one Lin Yu.\"","The little demon king immediately turned around, surprised. \"Did she really say that?\"","Zong Wenxiu nodded. \"She did.\" Although the latter part was a dig at his brother’s pragmatism.","The little demon king snorted arrogantly, \"That bad woman, praising me behind my back and trying to keep it from me. Now I know!\"","\"Uh-huh...\" Zong Wenxiu wiped the sweat from his forehead, feeling like he was barely keeping up with the lie.","The little demon king was appeased just that quickly.","By the time Xu Wan got into the carriage, the two were already chatting warmly about the day’s exam questions.","However, there was something slightly off.","As soon as Xu Wan got in, she noticed the little demon king looking at her with a smug and triumphant expression, as if she had secretly slipped him a few hundred taels of silver.","\"Why are you looking at me like that?\" she asked warily.","The little demon king became even more smug, sticking his tongue out at her. \"I’m not telling you!\"","Xu Wan: \"...\" You’re insane.","Zong Wenxiu, sitting beside them, grew increasingly uneasy and tried to make himself as inconspicuous as possible.","The joint exam was only between two academies, and the results would be out in three days. As usual, the little demon king felt he had done exceptionally well and was already thinking about slacking off. Meanwhile, Zong Wenxiu felt there were still areas he hadn’t mastered and continued to burn the midnight oil, seeking extra tutoring.","On Xu Wan’s side, there was a wedding banquet she couldn’t avoid attending.","Her half-sister, Xu Lian'er, was marrying Chen Yunyu, the eldest son of Duke Jin's Manor. It was a high-profile union between the Minister of Justice and Duke Jin's Manor, and the event was highly anticipated, with even the eighteenth princess rumored to be attending.","As the elder sister, Xu Wan couldn’t decline, but Zong Jincheng and Zong Wenxiu could skip it. However, as soon as the little demon king heard it was her half-sister’s wedding, he threw down his brush and immediately insisted on going.","\"Such a lively wedding banquet can’t be without me!\"","Xu Wan didn’t even need to think to know the little brat was up to no good. She rolled her eyes and turned to ask Zong Wenxiu if he was going. Zong Wenxiu said he needed to continue his studies and declined.","In the end, the mother and son, who couldn’t stand each other, sat in the carriage together, their eyes locked in a fierce battle of wills.","Xu Wan warned, \"You’ve offended Duchess Jin before. Today’s wedding is a big event. If you cause trouble and anger Duke Jin's Manor, even Grandpa Marquis won’t be able to save you.\"","The little demon king swung the jade pendant in his hand, nonchalantly replying, \"Whatever. I have the Crown Prince backing me. Who dares touch me?\"","Xu Wan: \"!\"","She knew that jade pendant was trouble. The little brat was way too good at pushing his luck.","The little demon king grinned mischievously, leaning in to ask, \"What’s wrong? Are you scared? If you beg for mercy now and shout a hundred times, 'I’m sorry, Zong Jincheng, I was wrong,' I might consider letting you off the hook and not causing trouble at the banquet. Otherwise, if something happens, you, as the elder, will bear more responsibility than me, a mere child. Hehehe.\"","Hehehe my foot, you idiot!","Xu Wan clenched her fist, smiling sweetly as she threatened, \"Do you believe that if you dare say one wrong word, I’ll have Cui Liu gag you?\"","\"Cui Liu?\" The little demon king’s face immediately paled.","Xu Wan snorted, \"I’ve already switched Cui Liu with Buyan today. If you cause trouble, Cui Liu won’t be as gentle as Buyan.\"","The little demon king: \"!\"","This was a major miscalculation!!!","He hadn’t even arrived yet and had already been outmaneuvered. This round was lost faster than ever!","As always, the little demon king knew when to back down. He quickly said, \"Stop the carriage. I’m going home to study!\"","If he couldn’t cause trouble there, there was no point in going. Better to cut his losses early!","\"Too late,\" Xu Wan replied, now relaxed. \"We’re almost at Duke Jin's Manor. If you want to go back, you’ll have to run. The carriage is staying here to wait for me.\"","The little demon king was furious, shouting in frustration, \"Can’t you just buy another carriage?!\"","Xu Wan calmly replied, \"No, I prefer to be frugal.\"","\"...\" He hated her!","Duke Jin's Manor was already grand, but today, with the wedding of their eldest son, the place was decorated in vibrant red, even more lively than usual.","The steward at the door took their gift list and had someone escort them inside. Before they could even enter, they heard a girl’s voice calling from behind, \"Sister Xu.\"","Xu Wan turned around, surprised to see the eighteenth princess, Zhao Rong.","\"Greetings, Your Highness.\" Everyone quickly bowed.","\"No need for formalities, please rise,\" Zhao Rong waved her hand casually, happily running over to Xu Wan and accidentally bumping the little demon king aside.","The little demon king: \"???\"","Does she have no manners at all?!","Can’t she see I’m standing here?!","Clearly, Zhao Rong hadn’t noticed. She linked arms with Xu Wan and exclaimed, \"Sister Xu, I knew you’d be here today. It’s been so long since I’ve seen you, I’ve missed you so much.\"","Xu Wan smiled, \"I heard you were coming, so I made sure to arrive early. I didn’t expect to run into you right at the entrance.\"","Zhao Rong walked with her inside, chatting, \"There are so many people here today. My nanny said if I arrived late, even more people would be swarming around to greet me. It’s too noisy. I prefer talking to you, and... Oh, your unpleasant stepson is here too?\"","The little demon king’s fists clenched instantly.","Who’s the unpleasant stepson here??","The eighteenth princess’s tone was so annoying. He was the legitimate heir of the Marquis’s household, yet she made it sound like he was some newcomer who had just arrived a few months ago.","Is there no justice in this world?!","Xu Wan smoothed things over, \"Many of Jincheng’s friends are here today. It’s been a while since he’s seen them, so it’s a good chance to catch up.\"","Zhao Rong nodded, \"Oh, good. It’s better that he’s not around. I have so many girl-talk topics to discuss with you.\"","The little demon king: \"...\"","He had made up his mind.","The eighteenth princess had officially secured a spot in the top three of his grudge list."]},{"number":81,"title":"Chapter 81: Good Child, Go Play","paragraphs":["Perhaps sensing the intensity of Zong Jincheng's furious gaze, Zhao Rong finally took pity and remembered to consider the fragile heart of the little boy.","Thus, the fourteen-year-old princess pretended to be a mature elder, patting his shoulder and saying, \"Good child, go play.\"","The little devil: \"!!!\"","Who are you calling a child!!","Are you even that much older than me?!","Play your hammer!!","Zong Jincheng angrily shook off Zhao Rong's arm, wanting to retort but remembering her status as a princess, he snorted heavily and ran off.","Zhao Rong, surprised, turned to Xu Wan and said, \"He’s really troublesome, isn’t he? Look at that rebellious attitude. You must have a hard time.\"","Xu Wan chuckled and explained, \"Actually, Jincheng has been much better recently. He didn’t even snap at you just now.\"","Zhao Rong laughed heartily, \"Let him snap! I promise I won’t use my princess status to pressure him. He’s just an eight-year-old brat. Worst case, we’ll fight it out! I’m pretty good at fighting, you know.\"","Xu Wan: \"...\"","You’re a princess! What are you doing fighting?!","Zhao Rong linked arms with her and continued, \"I’ve loved martial arts since I was a child. Even my brother the Crown Prince’s martial arts instructor praised my talent. It’s a pity I’m a girl. Not only can I not go to the battlefield, but I can’t even decide my own marriage.\"","Hearing her mention marriage, Xu Wan asked, \"Your Highness is still a year away from coming of age. Has the palace already started looking for a husband for you?\"","Zhao Rong shook her head, \"Not yet, but it’s coming soon. My father has been thinking about arranging a political marriage for the past few years. There are only a few unmarried princesses of the right age. If I don’t marry soon, I might end up being sent off for a political alliance.\"","Though a princess marrying for political reasons strengthens the bond between two nations, it also means enduring a lifetime of separation from her family and homeland.","Xu Wan pondered and said, \"As far as I know, Princess Suining was in the same situation. She quickly married a consort as soon as she came of age, and half a year later, when envoys came to propose a political marriage, the Emperor had to send a cousin instead.\"","Zhao Rong nodded vigorously, \"Exactly! That’s why my mother also agrees that I should settle on a consort first and marry as soon as I come of age.\"","Xu Wan understood and asked, \"So, Your Highness, are you planning to look for a consort while you’re out of the palace today?\"","Zhao Rong, having her thoughts exposed, shyly pulled Xu Wan into a secluded pavilion and whispered in her ear, \"Actually, I already have someone in mind.\"","Xu Wan turned to her in disbelief, \"So soon?\"","What she really wanted to say was, \"So young!\"","Although people married early in ancient times, at this age, in her time, it would be considered middle school puppy love, and the parents would have a fit.","So Xu Wan swallowed her words and kept reminding herself: Stay calm, don’t act rashly. She’s only a year away from coming of age. At most, it’s just an engagement for a year. Arranged marriages can happen even earlier than this.","Zhao Rong shyly said, \"It’s Chen Shigeng, the younger brother of today’s groom, Chen Yunyu.\"","\"Who?!\" Xu Wan was shocked, \"Chen Shigeng?\"","A month ago, when she found out that Xu Lian'er was marrying Chen Yunyu, Cui Liu had filled her in on the situation at Duke Jin's Manor.","The eldest son, Chen Yunyu, had already achieved a fourth-rank official position by the age of twenty. On the surface, he was a highly sought-after bachelor among the noble daughters of the capital, but in reality, he had a mistress from a brothel, hidden away, waiting to be brought into the manor after his official marriage.","Xu Wan had even complained to Cui Liu that he was a wolf in sheep’s clothing, only to hear that Chen Yunyu’s younger brother, Chen Shigeng, was also a scoundrel who followed in his brother’s footsteps, keeping multiple mistresses outside.","Zhao Rong, still oblivious, excitedly said, \"Yes, Chen Shigeng! He’s incredibly skilled in martial arts. Last time, when the swing rope broke in the palace and I was about to fall, he saved me. I would’ve been badly hurt otherwise.\"","Xu Wan took a deep breath, trying to calm herself.","Although she hadn’t known the eighteenth princess for long, she felt a motherly rage, as if her daughter had been deceived by some scoundrel. At this age, young girls are particularly impressionable, and if she were to expose Chen Shigeng’s true nature directly, it would only make Zhao Rong defensive and unwilling to believe her.","Meanwhile, the lovestruck Zhao Rong was still daydreaming, clasping her hands to her chest and saying, \"You don’t know how handsome he was at that moment, like a god descending from heaven. I crashed into him, and his chest was so firm, yet it felt so safe. My heart was pounding so fast, and the nanny said my face turned red. The books say that’s what love feels like!\"","Xu Wan: \"..................\"","That’s the suspension bridge effect, girl! That’s not love!!","Even though Xu Wan was screaming internally, she had to remain calm and explain, \"In such a situation, anyone’s heart would race, and their face would flush. Your Highness, this is just a misunderstanding. Don’t mistake nervousness for love.\"","\"Ah... ah?\" Zhao Rong stopped her fantasy and looked at her, puzzled.","Xu Wan tried to keep her tone gentle and caring, \"If you don’t believe me, I can have Cui Liu help you experience it again.\"","...","\"Ahhh!\" Zhao Rong screamed as Cui Liu brought her down from the sky, still shaken.","She gasped for breath and asked, \"Is martial arts always this thrilling?\"","Xu Wan said, \"A racing heart, flushed cheeks, and rapid breathing—these are all signs of love according to the books. How can Your Highness tell if it’s love or not?\"","\"Of course I can tell. Cui Liu is a woman,\" the lovestruck princess replied honestly.","Xu Wan facepalmed, thinking, \"Your Highness, as a princess, no man would dare touch you. Besides, you were in the palace at the time. There should have been maids skilled in martial arts to protect you. Why would Chen Shigeng need to step in to save you?\"","Upon closer thought, he was even an inconsiderate rogue.","But Xu Wan didn’t dare to say too much, fearing that Zhao Rong would turn against her, which would only backfire.","Even so, Zhao Rong was a bit displeased. She asked, \"Do you have a bias against Chen Shigeng? You don’t want me to marry him, do you?\"","Xu Wan smiled and said, \"Not at all. I just think Your Highness is still young. Choosing a consort should be done with great care to avoid being deceived. After all, marriage is a lifelong commitment, and I want Your Highness to be happy every day.\"","Zhao Rong smiled again, linking arms with her and saying, \"I understand, Sister Xu. Don’t worry, I’ll have my mother help me vet him carefully. I won’t be easily fooled.\"","Xu Wan nodded, still concerned.","She thought to herself, \"I hope the vetting goes well.\"","After speaking with Zhao Rong, Xu Wan hurried to the main hall, where the bride and groom were performing the wedding ceremony.","The little devil was there too.","But because he couldn’t squeeze in and was too short to see anything, he was sitting on Bu Yan’s shoulders, craning his neck to get a look.","Zhao Rong laughed and teased, \"This kid sure loves a spectacle. Nothing can stop him. By the way, when you married into the Marquis’s household, he must have found a great spot to watch the ceremony.\""]},{"number":82,"title":"Chapter 82: Being Hammered by Xu Wan","paragraphs":["Xu Wan was reminded of an embarrassing memory and gritted her teeth, saying, \"He didn’t just find the best spot to watch—he even used firecrackers to blow my veil off.\"","\"What???\" Zhao Rong was shocked beyond belief. \"That little rascal is such a troublemaker!\"","\"Yeah...\"","\"Didn’t you beat him up afterward?\" Zhao Rong asked.","Xu Wan: \"...\" Well, family scandals shouldn’t be aired in public.","Not only did she not beat him, she didn’t even punish him. Saying it out loud would be even more humiliating.","\"The ceremony is complete. Escort the bride to the bridal chamber.\"","The cheerful voice of the wedding matron rang out, and the crowd in the room dispersed. Xu Wan also pulled Zhao Rong to the corridor to avoid being jostled by the exiting crowd.","The bride was escorted to the bridal chamber, and the groom, surrounded by people, walked out. Chen Yunyu, with his jade-like face and starry eyes, looked every bit the elegant young gentleman—at least in appearance.","Too bad he’s a wolf in sheep’s clothing.","Xu Wan only glanced at him before turning back to continue her conversation with Zhao Rong.","However, Chen Yunyu’s gaze lingered for a moment. His eyes fell on a woman dressed in a luxurious purple gown. Her fair skin, calm eyes, and delicate, arched brows made her stunningly beautiful, impossible to look away from.","\"Let’s go, groom. The bride’s already in the bridal chamber.\"","Chen Yunyu snapped out of his daze and quickly averted his gaze, hurrying after the bride.","On the way, he whispered to a servant, \"Who was that woman in the purple dress under the eaves?\"","The servant replied, \"That’s your sister-in-law.\"","\"...\"","Xu Wan was completely unaware of the exchange and was still trying to talk to Zhao Rong when the sharp-eyed little troublemaker noticed her.","He came over gleefully to mock her, \"Some people manage to offend others without even saying a word. Honestly, they’re nothing like me—so charming and likable.\"","As soon as Zong Jincheng arrived, Zhao Rong immediately clenched her fists, ready to defend Xu Wan. \"Who says you’re likable? You’re the one who blew off Xu Wan’s veil with firecrackers. Anyone would call you a little rascal. It’s only because Xu Wan has a good temper that she didn’t beat you up. If it were me, I’d have smacked you eighteen times a day.\"","\"Who’s a little rascal?\" Zong Jincheng was indignant.","Zhao Rong was even more defiant. \"You are, you little rascal. Are you so young that your ears don’t work properly?\"","Zong Jincheng was furious. \"How can a princess be so good at insulting people? Are you even a girl?\"","Zhao Rong snorted. \"Funny you should mention it. I happen to hold the title of the top female troublemaker in the palace. With my father and the Crown Prince doting on me, and a whole group of maids and eunuchs spoiling me, I’ve got way more influence than you, the so-called leader of the four little troublemakers of the capital.\"","Zong Jincheng was speechless for a moment, then retorted, \"The Crown Prince likes me the most.\"","\"He likes me the most—I’m his sister.\"","\"He likes me the most—he even gave me a jade pendant.\"","\"Well, he gave me a hairpin.\"","\"He definitely likes me the most!\"","\"He likes me!\"","\"He likes me!\"","\"...\"","These two childish brats went from arguing about who was the bigger troublemaker to who the Crown Prince liked more, their faces red with anger as they bickered in someone else’s house. Xu Wan wanted to cover her ears.","They were so loud.","She couldn’t help but wonder if they were siblings from the same womb.","When the wedding banquet ended, Zong Jincheng climbed into the carriage, still muttering about Zhao Rong. \"Hmph, she’s only like this because she’s a princess. If she weren’t, she’d have been beaten up long ago. Who would indulge her like this?\"","Xu Wan rolled her eyes and jabbed, \"If you weren’t born into privilege, you’d have been beaten to death long ago too.\"","Zong Jincheng: \"!\"","She never had a kind word for him.","She always opposed him.","She’d rather side with an outsider like Princess Zhao Rong than help him.","Zong Jincheng was furious and shot back, \"At least I’m better off than you. Your father doesn’t care about you, your mother doesn’t love you, and even your sister and brother-in-law don’t like you.\"","\"Hmm?\" Xu Wan raised an eyebrow. \"What did you just see? How do you know Chen Yunyu dislikes me?\"","She had only glanced at Chen Yunyu earlier and then focused on talking to Zhao Rong, noticing nothing else.","But Zong Jincheng had been at the door, sitting on Bu Yan’s shoulders, so he must have seen everything clearly.","Zong Jincheng crossed his arms and leaned back lazily in the carriage, smugly saying, \"Of course I know. He looked at you several times and even asked who you were. I bet he wanted to write your name in his grudge book so he could get back at you later.\"","Xu Wan frowned. \"What nonsense are you talking about? Do you think everyone is as childish as you? A grudge book? Only someone as immature as you would keep one.\"","She didn’t need to think twice—she and Qin Ye were probably at the top of Zong Jincheng’s grudge list.","Zong Jincheng stuck out his tongue at her. \"Say what you want, but you’re on your own. I’m definitely not going to help you. Hmph.\"","Xu Wan rolled her eyes and said, \"Don’t flatter yourself, kid. I don’t need your help. Focus on your studies instead of getting beaten up by Qin Ye all the time.\"","\"What did you say?\" Zong Jincheng exploded at the mention of Qin Ye. \"Who gets beaten up by Qin Ye all the time? We’re not even on the same ranking anymore!\"","Xu Wan snorted. \"Whether you’re on the same ranking or not, you’re still no match for him. The gap between you and Qin Ye is like heaven and earth. You’ll never catch up to him, no matter how hard you try.\"","\"Ahhh! I’m going to kill you!\" Zong Jincheng went berserk and lunged at her, ready to fight.","Xu Wan wasn’t one to back down either. Pinning down an eight-year-old was as easy as child’s play for her. She pressed the little troublemaker to the carriage floor, holding him down with both hands while lecturing him. \"Still trying to rebel? Did you think I was weak?\"","Zong Jincheng was stunned, completely overpowered.","He had been in plenty of fights growing up and had never lost to Zhai Yao and the others. Even if he couldn’t beat an adult man, he shouldn’t have been pinned down by a seemingly delicate woman like Xu Wan.","Where did she get all that strength?","What did she eat growing up?","Xu Wan, the overachiever, had done all kinds of hard labor since childhood. Even during college, she worked three jobs a day to earn money. Her physical and mental stamina far surpassed her peers.","Zong Jincheng was pinned down, but he could still talk. \"Let go of me. Release me.\"","Xu Wan said, \"I was just thinking about something, and you had to come looking for trouble. If you keep this up, I won’t even need Cui Liu to help me pin you down before I teach you a lesson.\"","Today, she had found out that Zhao Rong had been deceived by Chen Shigeng and was still figuring out how to make the princess see his true colors. She also learned that Chen Yunyu had looked at her several times, probably because Xu Lian'er had badmouthed her to him. She could expect trouble from him in the future.","Thinking about it, she seemed to clash with everyone in Duke Jin's Manor. Not a single person there was easy to deal with.","Zong Jincheng quickly said, \"Fine, fine, I won’t bother you anymore. Let me go.\"","Xu Wan released him and flexed her wrist, still glaring at him.","Zong Jincheng’s face was filled with resentment.","He clearly wasn’t going to let this go.","Xu Wan saw through him but didn’t say anything. As they neared home, she noticed Zong Jincheng sitting still—he was usually the first to jump out of the carriage.","She smirked inwardly, lifted the carriage curtain, and stepped out, quickly moving to the side.","The next moment, Zong Jincheng shot out of the carriage like a cannonball, shouting fiercely, \"I’m going to crush you!\""]},{"number":83,"title":"Chapter 83: My Best Brother in the World","paragraphs":["The weight of an eight-year-old boy is only a few dozen pounds, and the force of him leaping off the carriage would at most cause someone to stumble, not inflict any serious harm.","However, the little devil always made a big show of his anger—first threatening to kill her with his glare, then attempting to crush her with his small frame. Whether he could actually do it was another matter, but he certainly made sure to put on a full display of bravado.","Unfortunately, while Zong Jincheng thought he was clever, Xu Wan was always one step ahead.","Xu Wan anticipated the little devil's childish antics and swiftly dodged to the side. Turning around, she saw the little cannonball fly off the carriage like a toad.","\"Ahhh—\"","\"Thud—\" The muffled sound of his body hitting the ground.","\"Young Master Jincheng!\" The maids and servants exclaimed in shock.","But after a long moment, no one came to help him up. Instead, a pair of embroidered shoes appeared in front of him, and Xu Wan's teasing voice rang out from above: \"Let me see, has our young master lost his front teeth?\"","Zong Jincheng had hit his head on the ground, and a large bump was slowly forming on his forehead. In pain and frustration, he punched the ground and howled, \"Damn it!\"","Why does he always fail?","Why has he never succeeded?","Does Xu Wan have eyes on the back of her head?","How does she manage to dodge him every single time?","Xu Wan chuckled as she crouched down, patting his back and advising, \"Little toad, go back and think it over carefully. That way, you might have a chance of succeeding next time.\"","Then, she stood up and smiled at Shunzi, saying, \"Everyone, listen up. No one is allowed to help him figure it out.\"","\"Yes...\"","The servants lowered their heads and quickly came over to pull the little devil up and escort him back to his courtyard. Without a word, they hurried to call the family physician.","When Zong Wenxiu heard in the study that his younger brother had fallen, he immediately put down his brush and rushed to see him. Before even reaching the courtyard, he could hear the little one's continuous cries of pain: \"Ah... be gentle, be gentle! Why are you so rough, physician? Did Xu Wan send you here to take revenge on me? You bunch of petty, grudge-holding people.\"","Shunzi wanted to say, who’s the petty and grudge-holding one here...","\"Jincheng,\" Zong Wenxiu called as he entered.","Seeing his beloved brother, the little devil immediately broke down and wailed, \"Brother, they’re bullying me again...\"","The physician, who was applying an ice pack to his forehead: \"???\"","Who’s \"they\"?","Who’s bullying you?","Who dares to bully you!","\"Huh?\" Zong Wenxiu looked at the large bump on his brother’s forehead and the ice pack in the physician’s hand, confused. \"Isn’t the physician helping to reduce the swelling?\"","The physician nodded tearfully, grateful that at least Wenxiu was reasonable. This Jincheng was utterly unreasonable and so difficult to deal with.","Zong Wenxiu took the ice pack and said, \"I’ll take care of it. You can leave now.\"","\"Alright, alright.\" The physician felt as if he had been rescued and quickly made his escape.","Zong Jincheng stuck his tongue out at the physician’s retreating figure, then immediately put on his sweetest smile for his brother, acting like the perfect little angel.","Zong Wenxiu couldn’t help but laugh softly. \"Weren’t you attending a wedding banquet today? How did you end up with a big bump on your head?\"","\"It’s all Xu Wan’s fault! She hit me,\" Zong Jincheng began fabricating another story.","\"But it looks more like you bumped into something.\"","Zong Wenxiu knew the difference between a bruise from being hit and one from falling. He glanced at Shunzi, who then explained the whole situation.","Zong Wenxiu sighed and gently applied the ice pack, saying, \"Just give up. Madam is very clever. You’re no match for her.\"","Zong Jincheng stubbornly retorted, \"No way! I’m the smartest person in the world!\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","But you’re only eight years old. How could you possibly outwit Madam?","Zong Jincheng continued muttering, \"She told me to go back and think it over. I’m still trying to figure out how she noticed me. She doesn’t have eyes on the back of her head...\"","\"Hmm?\" Zong Wenxiu was puzzled.","Zong Jincheng’s eyes lit up, and he quickly asked, \"Brother, do you know how she did it?\"","\"I...\" Zong Wenxiu was about to say that it was quite obvious if one paid more attention to others, but his brother was always too focused on himself.","Shunzi quickly interjected, \"Young Master Wenxiu, Madam has instructed that no one is allowed to help Young Master Jincheng figure it out. He needs to think it through himself.\"","\"Shunzi!\" Zong Jincheng shouted angrily. \"Get out!\"","Shunzi replied resentfully, \"...Yes.\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","Zong Jincheng then began to whine, \"Brother, my dear brother, the best brother in the world, please tell me. What did I do wrong? How come everyone else knows, but I don’t?\"","Zong Wenxiu firmly sealed his lips.","This time, he absolutely couldn’t give in. He couldn’t fall for his brother’s tricks again.","\"Brother? Brother? Don’t ignore me. I’m dying to know!\"","\"Brother, please tell me. It’ll help me become smarter, and you’ll be proud of me!\"","\"Brother, brother? Brother, brother, brother...\"","Zong Wenxiu kept his eyes fixed and his heart hardened, determined not to give in, even though his brother’s pleas were melting his resolve.","He sighed, \"Jincheng, if you keep squirming, I’ll stop applying the ice pack.\"","Zong Jincheng immediately froze.","The physician wasn’t as gentle as his brother, always hitting his bump with the ice pack, which hurt like hell.","He tilted his head and asked weakly one last time, \"Brother, can’t you really tell me...?\"","Zong Wenxiu nodded and said, \"We must listen to Madam. You need to figure it out yourself. Otherwise, wouldn’t it be like what you said before—a gentleman doesn’t accept handouts?\"","Zong Jincheng: \"...\"","He had been hoisted by his own petard.","The boomerang was truly terrifying.","The ice pack helped reduce the swelling a little, but it didn’t disappear completely. By the morning of the third day, when they were about to check the exam results, the bump was still visible.","Today, Xu Wan wasn’t just accompanying the two boys to check their results. She also had to return to the Minister's Mansion by noon because Xu Lian'er was bringing Chen Yunyu back for the bridal visit.","So, she had sent someone early to hurry the boys along. However, the more urgent the situation, the more obstacles seemed to arise. The little devil still hadn’t gotten out of bed.","Xu Wan frowned. \"Why isn’t he up yet? Doesn’t he usually recite passages with Wenxiu by this time?\"","Zong Wenxiu was also puzzled and quickly said, \"Madam, don’t worry. I’ll go wake him up.\"","\"Alright, tell him to hurry up and not dawdle.\"","Zong Wenxiu rushed to his brother’s courtyard. As soon as he entered, he saw Shunzi pacing around with clothes in hand, constantly reminding, \"Young Master, Madam and Young Master Wenxiu are waiting for you. You need to get up.\"","But the little devil on the bed remained completely still, his head buried under the blanket.","Zong Wenxiu approached and asked, \"What’s wrong, Shunzi? Is Jincheng embarrassed to go out because the bump on his head hasn’t gone down?\""]},{"number":84,"title":"Chapter 84: The Little Demon King Has an Epiphany","paragraphs":["Shunzi was utterly confused. \"The bag hasn't disappeared, but that can't be. Young Master Cheng has never cared about such things.\"","The little devil was moody, and sometimes even he, a high-EQ servant who had served for many years, couldn't understand what was going on in the little master's head.","Zong Wenxiu nodded. \"Alright, I understand. You all go out first, I'll talk to Jin Cheng.\"","\"Yes,\" Shunzi handed him the clothes and left the room with Buyan.","Zong Wenxiu took the clothes and gently pushed the little one wrapped in the blanket, chuckling. \"Jin Cheng, how old are you still lazing in bed? Aren't you going to get up and see the new clothes? Madam just had them made for you, they're very beautiful. You'll surely get lots of compliments when you wear them.\"","The little devil, usually so vain, didn't react at all to this, remaining motionless.","Zong Wenxiu was surprised and added, \"The results are out today, aren't you curious? Our Jin Cheng is going to trample all the students of Hanlin Academy first, then go to the Child Prodigy Class to trample Qin Ye. You're about to complete the first step.\"","Hearing this, the little devil moved. He pulled down the blanket, revealing a pair of big, shiny black eyes, and said somewhat evasively, \"Brother, I'm a bit nervous.\"","Zong Wenxiu couldn't help but laugh and teased, \"You're nervous? I thought with your personality, you'd be up early, excited to rush to the academy to see the results.\"","The little devil pouted, blinked his eyes, and didn't respond, as if feeling guilty.","After a while, he finally said, \"Brother, I don't want to ride in the same carriage as Xu Wan today.\"","If he didn't do well, that woman would surely laugh at him. The little devil cared about his face and didn't want to be embarrassed again.","Zong Wenxiu thoughtfully said, \"Then I'll have Shunzi go ask?\"","\"Mm,\" the little devil nodded.","Zong Wenxiu went out to give instructions, and when Shunzi returned saying Xu Wan had agreed, he said to him, \"Alright, get up now. Let's go see the results. Jin Cheng will surely do well today.\"","Hearing this, the little devil finally slowly got up and dressed, but his spirits were still low, like a wilted eggplant, all limp.","\"Brother, what place do you think I'll get today?\"","Zong Wenxiu thought for a moment and said, \"You were 120th last time, but more than half of those were from other academies. There are actually only fifty eight-year-old students in Hanlin North Academy. Now that it's a joint exam between the two academies, I think you'll definitely make it into the top twenty, because you've improved so quickly, faster than anyone else.\"","\"Only twentieth...\" the little devil pouted, \"I can't even get first place.\"","How could someone as weak as him say he was going to defeat Qin Ye, who was first in all four academies...","Zong Wenxiu brought him his shoes and comforted him, \"If first place were that easy to get, wouldn't all the students of Hanlin North Academy be jumping off buildings? Give them some breathing room, okay?\"","The little devil still couldn't muster any enthusiasm. He put on his shoes and went to wash up, holding two big meat buns his brother had given him as he climbed into the new carriage, munching on them as he went.","Zong Wenxiu sat in the carriage and tentatively asked, \"Jin Cheng, are you feeling down because of what happened the day before yesterday with Madam?\"","His brother had dark circles under his eyes, clearly not having slept well.","Zong Jincheng pouted unhappily, \"I just can't understand... why do I always lose, and why can't I ever get first place? Brother, are you lying to me? Am I just an ordinary person, not some great talent, right?\"","Zong Wenxiu felt his heart melt.","His brother was so pitiful, he couldn't help but want to tell the truth... but he held back.","Zong Wenxiu said, \"You'll know when you see the results. No one has your strong learning ability and speed of improvement. All the students will be so jealous of you they'll go crazy.\"","\"Really?\" The little devil still looked dejected and defeated, not quite believing it.","When they arrived at Qingbo Academy, Xu Wan didn't get out of the carriage, nor did she speak to them.","Zong Wenxiu dragged the reluctant little devil out to see the results. The little brat was very resistant, his palms sweaty with nervousness.","Just as they were about to step out of the carriage, the little devil suddenly stopped in his tracks, a flash of light speeding through his mind.","Zong Wenxiu couldn't pull him along and asked instead, \"What's wrong, Jin Cheng?\"","Zong Jincheng's eyes suddenly lit up, those black eyes becoming lively again, and he exclaimed in delight, \"I know! I know! I know why she can predict my behavior!!\"","\"Huh?\" Zong Wenxiu hadn't expected him to still be thinking about this.","The little devil jumped out of the carriage excitedly, gesturing animatedly, \"Because my actions are too predictable. Once they deviate from the norm, they're bound to be noticed. Like how I'm always the first to get out of the carriage, and how I always believe I'll do well on exams—these are all patterns! That's why you can easily see through my plans and predict my actions!\"","Zong Wenxiu was surprised, then laughed, praising him, \"That's right, exactly. I always said Jin Cheng is the smartest, figuring it out so quickly.\"","The little devil proudly raised his little tail, immediately floating on air, forgetting who he was. He confidently declared, \"Not only am I smart, but I can also apply what I learn! By observing someone's fixed behavior patterns, once I notice any anomalies, I can detect changes and prepare accordingly. Hmph, I'm going to observe Xu Wan closely from now on, find her weaknesses, and strike her hard!\"","\"Heh... heh...\" Zong Wenxiu couldn't laugh anymore. \"Madam was helping you understand, how can you think of using this against her?\"","The gloom that had been weighing on Zong Jincheng for the past two days dissipated, and he was in an extremely good mood. Even his brother speaking up for Xu Wan didn't seem so bad now. He waved his hand good-naturedly, \"Alright, alright, I won't use it on her. I'll go observe other people's anomalies instead!\"","\"Huh?\"","\"Let's go, brother, let's go see the results!\" The fully revived little devil grabbed Zong Wenxiu's hand and ran, pushing through the crowd.","On the other side, Xu Wan lifted the curtain of the carriage and watched their retreating figures, smiling. \"That kid's mood changes faster than June rain.\"","Cui Zhi laughed, \"Then, Madam, will we still need two carriages?\"","Xu Wan said lightly, \"Of course not. After we send them back to the manor today, tell Steward Liu to put that carriage away. We'll continue to be frugal.\"","\"Yes.\"","As the little devil ran through the crowd, he kept analyzing his insights to Zong Wenxiu, \"I've seen this person before. Every time he looks at the results, he's dejected. He's so happy this time, he must have done well!\"","\"And this person usually walks slowly, but he's walking so fast now, it must be because he hasn't seen his results yet!\"","\"And this one, this one! He's usually as timid as a mouse, but today he's running to the teacher's courtyard. He must be going to brag, he definitely made the list!\""]},{"number":85,"title":"Chapter 85: The Guilty Younger Brother","paragraphs":["Zong Wenxiu listened in astonishment, but quickly regained his composure and praised, \"Jincheng, you’re learning so fast. That’s right, as long as you pay attention to others, you’ll notice their unusual behavior. This is called reading people.\"","Zong Jincheng hopped around, proudly saying, \"Of course, I’m the smartest person in the world! I can understand everything!\"","Zong Wenxiu smiled with relief. His younger brother’s confidence, which had been lost for half a day, had returned. This was much more comfortable to see.","At Qingbo Academy, the students were already buzzing:","\"Lin Yu made it to the list, 48th place! He’s now second in the rankings!\"","\"Qin Ye left, and ahead of him is Zong Jincheng, who’s still in third place.\"","\"It’s fine. His father only cares about rankings. He’ll probably come to pick him up soon. Lin Yu, on the other hand, can stay at the academy for a month.\"","Zong Wenxiu and Zong Jincheng overheard the conversation and hurried over to check the list. Sure enough, at the 48th spot, it read: Qingbo Academy, Class A, Lin Yu.","He had surpassed four students from Hanlin North Academy and made it onto the list.","\"Lin Yu’s progress is impressive too,\" Zong Wenxiu remarked.","Zong Jincheng laughed, \"Haha, not bad, not bad. Although he’s still a bit behind me, he’s already better than many others.\"","Zong Wenxiu quickly covered his mouth, warning, \"Stop talking like that. These are real people. You’ll end up offending everyone.\"","\"Mmph...\" Zong Jincheng was dragged toward the top of the list to find his own ranking, secretly fuming that these people were so thin-skinned and couldn’t handle the truth.","Then, his brother’s voice rang out excitedly, \"Ninth! You’re ninth! Jincheng, you surpassed 42 students from Hanlin North Academy in just one month! Just one month! That’s incredible!\"","Originally, he had thought that making it into the top 20 would be a great achievement for his brother, considering the top ranks were dominated by the studious maniacs from Hanlin North Academy. Surpassing half of them would have been impressive enough, but his brother had outdone them all.","Other students also congratulated him:","\"Jincheng is amazing! Last time, he was at the bottom of the list, and now he’s almost at the top. We can’t even catch up.\"","\"Exactly! He improved so much in just one month. I heard he didn’t even come to the academy to study. Did he undergo some special training at home?\"","\"He’s from the Yangyuan Marquis Manor, which is insanely wealthy. I heard they hired a teacher from Hanlin North Academy to tutor him privately. One-on-one lessons must be way more effective than what we get here.\"","\"Ah... I’m so jealous. I wonder how much the Hanlin North Academy teacher earns in a month. I wish my father could hire one for me too.\"","\"Haha, we can’t afford it. I heard it’s a hundred taels of silver a month.\"","\"A hundred taels???\"","\"Damn!\"","\"Money really does blind people...\"","The little demon ignored the chatter around him. He looked at the names of the eight people ahead of him, all from Hanlin North Academy. Although they still overshadowed him, it didn’t feel as suffocating as before.","He turned and asked, \"Brother, where’s Qin Ye’s ranking?\"","Zong Wenxiu replied, \"He’s in the Child Prodigy Class. His ranking should be on that list. Do you want to check?\"","The little demon nodded like a pecking chicken.","The two hurried over to find Qin Ye’s ranking, but as a hot topic at Qingbo Academy, the Child Prodigy Class list was surrounded by a dense crowd.","So, Bùyán (the silent one) made his appearance again.","Zong Jincheng sat on his shoulders and craned his neck to look at the list.","Before looking, he thought, Qin Ye is competing with all the students under twelve years old. With the Child Prodigy Classes from both academies combined, there must be around two hundred students, including a bunch of maniacs from Hanlin North Academy. Even if Qin Ye is talented, there’s no way he could make it into the top fifty, right?","At most, top thirty, he thought.","After all, Qin Ye had defeated him before, so he couldn’t be too far behind.","But the moment Bùyán lifted him up, he saw the glaring ranking at the most prominent spot:","First place, Class A, Qingbo Academy, Qin Ye.","\"Qin Ye, it’s Qin Ye again!\"","\"Hanlin North Academy is definitely going to cry this time. They specially organized this revenge exam for Qin Ye, and yet they suffered another crushing defeat.\"","\"Is he planning to dominate every ranking list he’s on?\"","\"He’s incredible! He’s like an unbeatable god of exams!\"","\"I really don’t understand why he stayed in the eight-year-old class before. Even if he wasn’t at his best, he should have been in the ten-year-old class. What’s the point of competing with eight-year-olds? It’s like bullying chicks.\"","The bullied chick himself clenched his fists in anger.","\"Damn Qin Ye, I’ll definitely defeat you one day!\"","Zong Jincheng’s shout was loud, and the students turned to look at him. Seeing it was him, they weren’t too surprised. The students around here were of various ages, and not many eight-year-olds idolized him. Most were dismissive.","\"His slogans are loud, but who can actually compete with Qin Ye?\"","\"Zong Jincheng, even if he becomes the top of his class, he’s still no match for Qin Ye.\"","\"Dreams are good to have. Who knows, they might come true.\"","\"Haha, true, true...\"","\"This is too much, way too much,\" the little demon muttered, his fists clenched tightly, his anger burning.","Zong Jincheng climbed down from Bùyán’s shoulders and stomped over to Zong Wenxiu, shouting, \"Brother, I want to transfer classes! I’m going to the Child Prodigy Class to crush Qin Ye!\"","What unbeatable myth? What god of exams? What existence that crushes Hanlin North Academy? These titles will belong to Zong Jincheng in the future, not that cold-faced Qin Ye!","Zong Wenxiu was stunned for a moment, then smiled. His brother’s determination was terrifying. He seemed to have endless energy.","But... \"Isn’t that a bit too rushed? The Child Prodigy Class moves fast. You’ll have to wait a few months before you can join.\"","Though that was already considered quick. For others, it would take at least two years to catch up.","\"I don’t care, I don’t care! I want to join that class! I don’t want to stay here playing with a bunch of eight-year-olds. I don’t want to, I don’t want to, I don’t want to...\" The little demon tugged at his sleeve, throwing a tantrum, alternating between whining and mischief. No one could withstand it.","Zong Wenxiu sighed helplessly, \"Alright, let’s go back and ask Madam and the teachers. If they say you can transfer, then we’ll do it.\"","\"Okay, okay,\" the little demon nodded repeatedly. \"Let’s hurry back to the manor. I’m so smart; the teachers will definitely agree to let me transfer!\"","\"Alright...\" Zong Wenxiu scratched his head. \"You get on the carriage first. I need to check my ranking.\"","Zong Jincheng’s hurried steps suddenly stopped.","That’s right. He had been so eager to check his own ranking, and even looked at Qin Ye’s and Lin Yu’s, but he had completely forgotten about his brother’s results.","His brother had always been so good to him, accommodating him in everything, comforting and encouraging him, and even accompanying him to check the rankings.","But he hadn’t thought about his brother at all.","The little demon felt deeply remorseful. \"I’m sorry, Brother. I’ll go with you to check your ranking now!\"","Zong Wenxiu smiled gently. \"It’s alright.\"","As they walked, the little guy’s guilt grew heavier. He even started recalling all the times he had ignored his brother since they had met."]},{"number":86,"title":"Chapter 86: My Brother is Great","paragraphs":["The downside of having an excellent memory was showing again.","He could remember every detail, every word, and even reconstruct every action from a scene. And then he realized how self-centered he was, indifferent to everything except his own affairs.","So, while others could easily spot patterns, it took him days to figure them out.","Discovering one's flaws is a disheartening experience, but what saddened Zong Jincheng even more was that he had been selfishly seeking attention and care from Zong Wenxiu, who never seemed to get angry or mind it at all.","How could there be such a kind person in the world?","Zong Jincheng tilted his head slightly and asked, “Brother, aren’t you mad at me at all?”","“Huh? Why would I be mad?” Zong Wenxiu replied.","Zong Jincheng felt even more defeated. He said, “Like forgetting to accompany you to check your grades. Doesn’t it hurt to be ignored like that?”","He put himself in Zong Wenxiu’s shoes. If Zong Wenxiu had only checked his own grades and then told him to go home, completely forgetting that he also needed to check his results, he would have exploded with anger, like a sunflower bursting into flames, ready to burn everything in sight.","Zong Wenxiu smiled gently. “It’s fine. You’re my younger brother, and I’m your older brother. It’s natural for me to be good to you and to be understanding. Besides, you just forgot this one time. I know you’re focused on advancing to the next class and defeating Qin Ye. That’s a good thing—it shows you’re ambitious. I understand.”","Hearing this, Zong Jincheng felt even guiltier.","How could he have taken advantage of such a wonderful brother without giving anything in return? It was too much.","He pouted and said, “Do you ever get angry at all?”","Zong Wenxiu, who had been walking, suddenly stopped and retorted, “Yes, I do get angry.”","“Huh?” Zong Jincheng looked up in confusion.","Zong Wenxiu said seriously, “I get angry when you take advantage of me. I get angry when you act recklessly without thinking. And I get angry when you fail to appreciate the kindness of others and instead think of repaying them with resentment.”","Zong Jincheng replied honestly, “So you have quite a few things that make you angry.”","Zong Wenxiu: “...”","Not as many as you, though.","How can you, a young master who gets angry eight hundred times a day, have the nerve to say that...","Zong Wenxiu continued, “Anyway, the things that make me angry are usually matters of principle. I won’t get upset over small, everyday things.”","“Oh, I see,” Zong Jincheng replied, though he was still pondering the three principles his brother had mentioned.","Taking advantage, being unreasonable, and lacking gratitude.","Am I really that bad?","The little troublemaker pouted, lost in thought and a bit disgruntled, when he suddenly heard his brother let go of his arm and say, “We’re here. I’ll go take a look ahead.”","Zong Jincheng followed, but unlike Zong Wenxiu, who started searching from the bottom of the list, he began from the top.","Although his brother’s talent wasn’t quite on par with his own, it was still far superior to that of ordinary people. Otherwise, he wouldn’t have been able to catch up so quickly in less than a year.","Moreover, with the help of the seemingly odd but actually highly effective Marquis Manor Elite Class, both of their learning progress had accelerated significantly.","So, he was sure his brother had done exceptionally well this time!","Starting from the top were the names of students from Hanlin North Academy, listed in a dense, orderly fashion. At a glance, none of them were from their academy. But in the second column, he spotted a name from Qingbo Academy!","Nineteenth place, Grade A, Qingbo Academy, Zong Wenxiu.","Zong Jincheng shouted excitedly, “Brother! You’re here! You made it onto the list! And you’re in nineteenth place! You’ve surpassed so many students from Hanlin North Academy!”","Zong Wenxiu, who had been searching at the bottom of the list, turned around abruptly upon hearing this and saw his younger brother jumping up and down excitedly at the top.","His brother said he had made the list, and was in nineteenth place.","In the noisy academy, students crowded around the list, their chaotic discussions almost drowning out individual voices. But his brother’s loud, clear voice was full of energy and excitement.","He heard it.","“I made it onto the list...” Zong Wenxiu hadn’t dared to dream he could do so well.","Perhaps seeing his brother’s high talent and learning ability had made him default to thinking of himself as ordinary. But he had forgotten that he, too, had once been someone who could catch up to his peers in just half a year.","Zong Jincheng ran over from the top of the list, pulling him excitedly, and boasted, “It’s true, it’s true! Come and see, your name is written so beautifully on the list!”","Standing in front of the list, Zong Wenxiu saw his name for the first time. He thought of the long nights of hard study, his mother lying sick in bed, and the endless hunger and despair of the slums.","At that moment, he began to believe: I will have a very, very bright future.","The two brothers, both with excellent exam results, walked together, discussing how much they could improve in the next exam.","“Brother, I think I really need to move up to the next class. What’s the point of getting first place among eight-year-olds? It’s embarrassing. I should at least aim for first place among nine-year-olds.”","“That makes sense. I think you can definitely get first place among nine-year-olds.”","“Haha, of course! I’m going to be a great scholar in the future! Oh, and so are you. You’ll definitely get first place next time and leave all those students from Hanlin North Academy in the dust!”","“Shh... Keep your voice down. I’m afraid they’ll get so angry they’ll want to hit you. That’s such a provoking thing to say.”","“Hmph, I’m not scared. Buyan can handle them.”","“Right, right... You always let Buyan take the hits. He’s always getting into fights because of you.”","“I don’t, I don’t...”","The two brothers bantered and teased each other, their bond warm and affectionate.","However, before they could leave the academy grounds, they saw Lin's Father pointing at Lin Yu and shouting, “You’ve climbed back to second place this time, surpassing four students from Hanlin North Academy. Not bad, not bad. If only you’d worked this hard earlier, you wouldn’t have had to suffer in the academy for a month. Come home with me. If you behave, your old man is still willing to support your studies.”","Zong Jincheng’s fists clenched in anger.","That old man really knew how to hit every nerve.","Lin Yu sneered coldly, walked past him, and headed back into the academy, refusing to say a word to Lin's Father.","Lin's Father grew anxious and chased after him, shouting, “What are you sulking about? Do you really think suffering in the academy is better? Look at your clothes—they’re torn, and you don’t even have money to buy new ones. Our Lin family is a wealthy household. Don’t make people think I’m mistreating you.”"]},{"number":87,"title":"Chapter 87: We Are Mature and Steady","paragraphs":["Lin Yu turned around and retorted, \"How I live my life is none of your concern. You never cared about me before, and now you’re putting on this hypocritical act. Please leave. I can support myself and don’t need your charity to fund my education.\"","\"Support yourself?\" Lin's Father laughed as if he had heard the biggest joke. He grabbed Lin Yu’s arm and said, \"You’re just an eight-year-old child! What ability do you have to support yourself? You dress like a beggar, and I’m ashamed to have a son like you.\"","Lin Yu shook off his hand and said coldly, \"If you’re ashamed, then let’s not be father and son anymore. I’m tired of pretending with you—it’s disgusting.\"","\"You!\" Lin's Father raised his hand and shouted, \"You ungrateful brat! I’ll teach you a lesson today!\"","\"Stop!\"","\"Don’t touch Lin Yu!\"","Zong Jincheng and Zong Wenxiu shouted in unison.","Buyan, the fastest of them, grabbed Lin's Father’s hand and threw him to the ground.","Lin's Father howled, \"Ouch... my back... Who dares to hit someone in Qingbo Academy? Haven’t you heard of Lin Youde from Qingyun Street?\"","The little devil snorted and replied with even more arrogance, \"Well, have you heard of Zong Jincheng, the leader of the four young prodigals of the capital?\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","Are you using evil to suppress evil?","But admittedly, it worked.","Lin's Father immediately felt a chill run down his spine and stammered, \"Zong Jincheng from Yangyuan Marquis Manor?\"","The Lin family was a merchant family, wealthy but without any political power. On the other hand, Yangyuan Marquis Manor was the wealthiest and most influential aristocratic family in the capital, surpassing them in both money and power by leaps and bounds.","Lin's Father immediately cowered, shuffling backward on his bottom and quickly changing his tone to a fawning smile. \"So it’s Young Master Zong! I was blind not to recognize you. I’ve long admired your reputation.\"","Lin Yu sneered, unsurprised by his father’s reaction. This was typical of a merchant—always ready to grovel.","Zong Jincheng proudly lifted his chin and said, \"Lin Yu has already said he doesn’t want to be your son anymore. If you keep harassing him, I won’t be so polite next time.\"","Lin's Father hurriedly waved his hands. \"No, no, I wouldn’t dare! Since Young Master Zong has spoken, I’ll obey. I’ll leave this child to you. I’ll stay far away and never come back to Qingbo Academy!\"","With that, he scrambled to his feet and ran off without looking back.","Lin's Father’s fear of Yangyuan Marquis Manor wasn’t just because it was a noble household. The Marquis’s influence spanned countless industries, and a single word from them could obliterate the Lin family.","Lin Yu was just one of his many sons. This rebellious child could be written off—he had no expectations for Lin Yu’s future anyway. He was sure Lin Yu would eventually come crawling back, begging to return home.","Zong Jincheng watched Lin's Father’s retreating figure and frowned. \"Brother, I wanted to help Lin Yu chase him away, but now that he’s gone so quickly, I feel even more upset. Why is that?\"","Zong Wenxiu thought for a moment and said, \"Maybe it’s because you’re empathizing with Lin Yu. Having such a cold-hearted father is heartbreaking. It’s better to have no father at all.\"","Zong Jincheng nodded solemnly. \"That makes sense.\"","Meanwhile, Lin Yu came over to thank them.","Zong Jincheng waved his hand dismissively. \"It’s nothing, just a small favor.\"","Zong Wenxiu was more polite. He smiled and comforted Lin Yu, \"You’ve improved a lot in your recent exams. Keep it up, and you’ll surely achieve great results, making your father regret his actions.\"","Lin Yu smiled back. \"Thank you. That’s what I’m aiming for.\"","Then he turned to Zong Jincheng. \"After this exam, are you planning to go to the Child Prodigy Class to see Qin Ye?\"","Zong Jincheng tilted his head and thought for a moment. \"Not yet. My brother told me not to rush. Why? Do you want to join the Child Prodigy Class too?\"","Lin Yu shook his head with a smile. \"No, the Child Prodigy Class is for geniuses. I’m just an ordinary person who works hard. I’ll stick to my studies and take the regular imperial exams in a few years. That’s enough for me.\"","\"Huh?\" Zong Jincheng looked puzzled.","After saying goodbye, Lin Yu returned to Qingbo Academy to continue his studies.","Zong Jincheng watched Lin Yu’s retreating figure and asked, \"Brother, why is he so lacking in confidence? He won’t even try the Child Prodigy Class. What if he’s a genius too?\"","Zong Wenxiu chuckled softly. \"Not everyone can be a prodigy. I heard Lin Yu started learning at the age of three and has been studying for five years, yet he only managed to rank third in the eight-year-old class at Qingbo Academy. Outside the academy, there are countless students of different ages who are stronger than him. He doesn’t have a clear advantage.\"","Zong Jincheng nodded in understanding. \"True, not everyone can be as smart, talented, and gifted as me. Otherwise, how would my uniqueness stand out? I get it now.\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","Here we go again.","Can’t my brother share some of that confidence with me?","\"Young Masters, the Madam is heading back to the Minister's Mansion and has asked me to escort you home,\" Steward Liu called out to them.","The brothers were in the middle of a lively conversation. Zong Wenxiu was about to reply when Zong Jincheng quickly covered his mouth.","He turned to Steward Liu and asked, \"Is Duke Jin's Manor attending the gathering? Don’t we need to go too?\"","Steward Liu forced a smile and said, \"Do the two of you wish to attend? The Minister's Mansion will be quite crowded today. Not only will Duke Jin's Manor be there, but the Minister himself will also be present. There must be no mistakes.\"","\"Isn’t that... inappropriate?\" Zong Wenxiu whispered. \"Jincheng, the Minister's Mansion will be packed today. We might cause trouble for Madam.\"","Zong Jincheng’s eyes lit up, and he patted his brother’s hand enthusiastically. \"How could we? We’re mature and responsible. We won’t cause any trouble—absolutely not.\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\" I’m not so sure about that.","Steward Liu: \"??\"","Mature and responsible?","Perhaps Zong Wenxiu fits the description, but what does that have to do with you, the little troublemaker?","Is there even a hint of truth in that?","The reliable steward maintained a calm expression, though he had already mentally criticized Zong Jincheng a thousand times. He smiled politely and remained silent, clearly reluctant to take him along.","Zong Jincheng continued to persuade him. \"I’m serious. I’ve just learned how to read people’s expressions from my brother, and I need more practice. I promise not to speak out of turn. If I do say anything, it’ll be quietly, just to my brother.\"","Steward Liu compromised. \"Then I’ll inform Madam. You two can board the carriage and discuss it on the way.\"","\"Great!\" Zong Jincheng dragged Zong Wenxiu toward the carriage.","As they ran, Zong Wenxiu asked, \"Jincheng, what are you really planning? Steward Liu said today is a formal occasion. We can’t let Madam down.\"","\"Don’t worry, we won’t.\" Zong Jincheng leaned in and whispered something in his ear.","Zong Wenxiu immediately stopped protesting. \"Are you serious?\""]},{"number":88,"title":"Chapter 88: Xu Wan's Probing","paragraphs":["Zong Jincheng nodded and said, \"Really, I’ve promised not to lie to you anymore. Trust me, brother.\"","Zong Wenxiu looked at him steadily and replied seriously, \"Alright, I trust you.\"","While waiting in the carriage, Xu Wan discussed with Cui Zhi how to warn the Eighteenth Princess. After some deliberation, the two tactful women agreed that being too direct would be unwise. Such matters could easily backfire, and blunt honesty might only bring trouble.","However, they couldn’t simply stand by and let the princess be deceived. Instead, they decided to anonymously pass the clues to the princess’s mother, Consort Jing, and let her investigate. As the princess’s biological mother, whatever results she found—good or bad—would carry more weight than anything Xu Wan, who had only met the princess twice, could do. Moreover, they wouldn’t have to worry about the aftermath; the consorts in the palace were all skilled in handling such matters.","Cui Zhi said, \"But we have no way to reach Consort Jing. Would you need to make a special trip to the palace, Madam? The princess mentioned last time that it’s easier to enter her palace than the Eastern Palace.\"","Xu Wan shook her head. \"Even if her palace is easy to enter, it’s no use. The consorts and princesses don’t live in the same place, and it would be inappropriate for me to request an audience with Consort Jing directly.\"","\"Then what should we do...\" Cui Zhi was at a loss.","Xu Wan smiled and said, \"There’s another way.\"","\"What is it?\"","\"The six degrees of separation.\"","\"Ah?\" Cui Zhi was baffled by the new term.","Xu Wan explained, \"In this world, two strangers can be connected through no more than six people.\"","Cui Zhi was even more astonished. \"How is that possible...\"","She instinctively wanted to argue—could she really reach the emperor through just six people?","But after thinking about it carefully... it actually seemed plausible.","She might not even need all six.","..................","Xu Wan mentally mapped out her and the Eighteenth Princess’s social networks. Aside from Lady Zhai and the Duke of Jin’s household, there was one couple who seemed particularly suitable.","\"The Crown Princess.\" \"The Crown Princess!\"","Xu Wan and Cui Zhi spoke the name simultaneously, though the former was calm while the latter was shocked.","Cui Zhi swallowed and said, \"Madam, you’re truly brilliant. The Crown Princess can directly approach Consort Jing in the palace. You can completely bypass the princess and have the Crown Princess relay the message for us.\"","Xu Wan nodded in agreement. \"The Crown Prince dotes on the Eighteenth Princess, and the Crown Princess is fiercely protective of him. She certainly wouldn’t stand idly by. She might not just pass on the message—she might even investigate the matter herself.\"","Cui Zhi added, \"Now that I think about it, the Crown Princess is also closer to the princess than we are.\"","\"Haha, of course. No matter how well we get along, it takes time to build a relationship. It’s nothing compared to the bond of family that’s been nurtured since childhood,\" Xu Wan acknowledged. \"I’ll write a letter to the Crown Princess today and have you deliver it to the palace.\"","\"Understood.\"","After settling these matters, Cui Liu came over with good news:","\"Madam, great news! Both young masters performed very well in the exams. Young Master Jincheng is ranked ninth on the overall list and first in the Hanlin North Academy. Young Master Wenxiu is ranked nineteenth on the overall list and first in his academy.\"","Xu Wan’s eyes lit up, and she smiled. \"That’s wonderful! Wenxiu has made rapid progress.\"","Cui Zhi chuckled. \"Madam, it’s a good thing Young Master Jincheng isn’t here. If he heard you only praising Young Master Wenxiu, he’d probably puff up like a little frog again.\"","\"Hahaha...\" Xu Wan laughed heartily. \"That rascal doesn’t need anyone’s praise. By now, he’s probably already strutting around with his tail in the air.\"","Though he kept saying he wanted to take first place and surpass Qin Ye, defeating a large number of Hanlin North Academy students was already a significant achievement.","The feeling of climbing higher and higher step by step greatly boosted one’s motivation.","Cui Liu chimed in at the right moment, \"I did hear that Young Master Jincheng wants to transfer to the Child Prodigy Class to take down Qin Ye.\"","Xu Wan glanced at Cui Zhi and said knowingly, \"See? I told you he’d get carried away.\"","Cui Zhi: \"......\"","Xu Wan checked the time. It was almost noon, and she was about to head to the Minister's Mansion when the two boys came running over, panting.","Cui Zhi lifted the carriage curtain, and the two boys climbed in.","Zong Jincheng called out to the coachman, \"Let’s go, we’re going to be late.\"","As the carriage started moving, Xu Wan raised an eyebrow and asked, \"Are you two coming back with me?\"","Zong Jincheng crossed his arms and said smugly, \"Yes, we’re both first in our academies. Don’t you want us to show off for you?\"","\"......\" Zong Wenxiu lowered his head and covered his face.","Brother, please, stop bragging for me.","As someone who just climbed to nineteenth place, I’m really not comfortable being called first in the academy.","Xu Wan snorted. \"Are you planning to cause trouble again? Let me remind you, my father, the Minister of Justice, has a terrible temper. If he gets angry and decides to punish you, he won’t care if you’re the eldest grandson.\"","She wasn’t exaggerating. The little troublemaker often caused chaos at home or outside, but her father, who had overseen the Ministry of Justice for years, had a face so stern it could freeze the ground. He could fly into a rage at any moment.","Zong Wenxiu, seeing his brother misunderstood, quickly explained, \"No, Madam, my brother just wants to help you...\"","The little troublemaker immediately covered his mouth and interrupted with a grin, \"Help you show off.\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"......\"","Is this showing off ever going to end?","Xu Wan’s eyes darted between the two of them, and she noticed that Zong Jincheng’s behavior was different from his usual scheming self.","Could it be that this time, he actually had good intentions?","Zong Jincheng was quite relaxed during the journey, snacking on pastries and playing around with his brother. For once, he didn’t argue with Xu Wan.","This made her suspicious, and she decided to test him to see if there were any cracks in his facade.","\"I heard you want to transfer to the Child Prodigy Class?\"","Zong Jincheng turned his head sharply and nodded repeatedly. \"That’s right. If Qin Ye can transfer, so can I. The Child Prodigy Class is nothing to a rare genius like me. It won’t be long before I push Qin Ye down to second place.\"","Xu Wan thought to herself: Good, still as blindly confident as ever.","She said, \"Given your current progress, you might manage a decent ranking if you transfer to the nine-year-old class. At most, you could be in the same class as Wenxiu, but you’d probably fall far behind. As for the Child Prodigy Class, don’t even think about it for now. You wouldn’t be able to keep up.\"","Zong Jincheng immediately bristled. \"How could I not keep up? I’m so smart and talented. Why can’t I transfer directly to the Child Prodigy Class? Why can Qin Ye do it but not me? Are you deliberately holding me back, trying to slow down my progress?\"","Xu Wan said lightly, \"Do you think Qin Ye was on the same ranking as you before just because that’s his actual ability?\"","Zong Jincheng frowned. \"What do you mean?\"","Xu Wan replied, \"You’re underestimating Qin Ye, little troublemaker.\"","\"He only stayed in the same class as his peers for his brother’s sake.\""]},{"number":89,"title":"Chapter 89: The Tool Man Cheng","paragraphs":["“Huh?” “Huh?”","Not only was Zong Jincheng confused, but even Zong Wenxiu looked over curiously and asked, “Qin Ye has an older brother?”","“I thought he was the only son of the Qin family,” Zong Jincheng added.","After all, the last time he and Bu Yan passed by the Qin family and peeked over the wall, they only saw Qin Ye studying alone.","Xu Wan shook her head and explained, “The Qin family has two sons. His older brother is the child you met last time at Hanlin North Academy, named Qin Shi, who is the same age as Wenxiu.”","“The person Qin Ye went to see at Hanlin North Academy last time was his brother?” Zong Wenxiu asked in surprise. “Why don’t they study at the same academy?”","Zong Jincheng’s eyes lit up, and he quickly added, “If Qin Shi studies at Hanlin North Academy, he must be even more knowledgeable than Qin Ye, right? That arrogant kid must have been overshadowed by his brother and came to Qingbo Academy to bully weaker students!”","At the end, he couldn’t help but add, “What a schemer.”","Zong Wenxiu: “...”","What kind of habit is this where his younger brother fills in the blanks with his own imagination and even adds commentary...","Xu Wan chuckled and said, “Young Master, you really have quite the imagination. Didn’t I just say that Qin Ye stayed in the same class as his peers for his brother’s sake? Otherwise, you wouldn’t even have had the chance to be on the same ranking list as him.”","“What did you say?!” The little devil was furious.","How could he possibly not have the chance to be on the same ranking list as Qin Ye?","This was even more insulting than when Qin Ye was at the top of the list and he was at the bottom!","This woman always knew how to hit his buttons.","Hmph!","Zong Wenxiu held his arm and said, “Brother, don’t get angry yet. Let’s listen to what Madam Xu has to say. I’m quite curious. Last time at Hanlin North Academy, it did seem like Qin Ye was explaining something to Qin Shi. Could it be that Qin Ye’s knowledge is even better than his brother’s?”","Zong Jincheng instinctively retorted, “How is that possible? They’re born from the same parents, and Qin Shi is two years older. How could there be such a big difference? Besides, Qin Shi is a student at Hanlin North Academy. How bad could he be?”","Although the students of Hanlin North Academy were all his defeated opponents, they were still from the top academy in the capital. They couldn’t be that bad.","Of course, the reason he insisted on this was to prove just how outstanding he was for defeating them!","The little devil was getting carried away again, crossing his arms and puffing up like a proud lord.","Xu Wan glanced at him, thinking that if he had a tail, it would definitely be wagging right now.","Under the eager gazes of the two boys, Xu Wan revealed the truth: “The Qin family has a strong scholarly tradition. Both Qin brothers started their education at the age of three and studied diligently. Qin Shi was the top among his peers, following in his father’s footsteps. He was admitted to Hanlin North Academy at the age of five and received countless praises from elders. However, his younger brother Qin Ye gradually revealed even greater talent as he grew older. He excelled in memorization and literacy, catching up to Qin Shi’s eight-year-old level by the age of six.”","“This was the turning point. From then on, Qin Shi, despite his own excellence, was overshadowed in the eyes of their father and the Qin family elders. Qin Ye, on the other hand, was seen as the future top scholar, treated like a prodigy and showered with praise. Comparisons between siblings were inevitable. As the older brother, Qin Shi began to face constant ridicule and mockery.”","Zong Jincheng was stunned and exchanged a glance with his brother, puzzled. “Why do they have to compare them? Qin Shi is also excellent; he’s not inferior to anyone else. Are these people just trying to bully him?”","Zong Wenxiu thought for a moment and said, “I can somewhat understand the psychology behind comparing the Qin brothers, but I don’t get why they would mock Qin Shi.”","“It’s envy,” Xu Wan said. “It’s human nature to resent others for being better than oneself, especially when they can’t find a reason to belittle them. Qin Ye’s talent gave them a reason to belittle Qin Shi, and after doing so, they’d say, ‘See, you’re not that great after all. You can’t even surpass your younger brother.’”","Zong Jincheng’s veins bulged in anger as he raised his arm. “My fists are itching.”","Zong Wenxiu: “...”","No need to get so personally invested.","“So what happened after that? Did Qin Ye intentionally stay in the same class as his peers to prevent his brother from being mocked?” Zong Wenxiu asked, suddenly feeling that the cold and aloof Qin Ye wasn’t so devoid of human warmth after all.","Xu Wan smiled and nodded. “Yes, after Qin Ye transferred from Hanlin North Academy to Qingbo Academy, he initially stayed in the eight-year-old class and took first place as usual. But after Qin Shi talked to him about it, Qin Ye started planning to move to the Child Prodigy Class.”","Zong Wenxiu smiled and said, “They reconciled.”","“Huh?” The little devil was slow to catch on. “Did I miss something? When did they fight?”","Zong Wenxiu chuckled. “It’s a psychological reconciliation. The brothers made peace with the outside world’s judgments. Qin Ye no longer suppressed his abilities, and Qin Shi no longer minded that his younger brother was more talented. They each studied at their own pace in their respective academies.”","The little devil: “!” Got it.","So the reason he and Qin Ye were on the same ranking list in the last two exams was all because of Qin Shi.","“Those annoying brothers!” Zong Jincheng, the toolman, grumbled in frustration.","He decided that from today on, he would have an eternal feud with both Qin brothers!","Xu Wan glanced at him.","She thought to herself that with his grudge-holding nature, he probably just added another name to his list of enemies.","Xu Wan said, “The next exam is the monthly test in a month. I’ll give you two options: the top fifty in the nine-year-old class, or not making the list in the ten-year-old class. You decide which one you want to take.”","After all, the Child Prodigy Class was out of the question; he wouldn’t even be able to fill out the exam paper.","Zong Jincheng immediately protested, “How could I possibly not make the list?! My brother is already first at Qingbo Academy. How could I be 120 places behind him?!”","Xu Wan said nonchalantly, “Then give it a try. I think you’re just overconfident and underestimating your brother. Qingbo Academy is, after all, the fourth-best academy in the capital. Don’t take the ten-year-old exam and end up so discouraged that you have to go back to the eight-year-old class.”","“Hmph, don’t underestimate me!” Zong Jincheng said, hands on his hips. “I’m going to skip two age groups, take the ten-year-old exam, and make the list just to prove you wrong!”","Xu Wan was very pleased inside but maintained her skeptical expression. “Sure, sure, go ahead. Who could possibly be as capable as you?”","Zong Jincheng: “!!!”","This woman who always looks down on him!","He would definitely make her see just how amazing he was!","“Just you wait!” the young master declared.","Xu Wan continued to brush him off. “Yeah, yeah, I’ll wait for you to come back crying after failing the exam.”","The little devil was furious. “Who’s going to cry over failing an exam?! No, who’s going to fail the exam?!”","Xu Wan: “Who knows? It definitely won’t be Wenxiu, nor Qin Shi, and certainly not Qin Ye... Ah, Qin Ye is such an amazing child. His parents must be so proud, right?”"]},{"number":90,"title":"Chapter 90: The Lifelong Adversary of Jincheng","paragraphs":["\"Ahhhh! I’m going to fight you! I’m going to fight you!!\"","In the cramped carriage, Zong Wenxiu watched as his brother lunged at Xu Wan like a football. Before he could even scramble to his feet to intervene, his brother was already subdued.","\"...\" That was way too fast.","Zong Wenxiu, halfway up, sat back down.","Xu Wan was indeed formidable.","\"Do you dare try again?\" Xu Wan pressed him down as she asked.","The little troublemaker, pinned to the seat, flushed red and gritted his teeth. \"Don’t choke my neck... don’t press my elbow... ah, my leg!\"","Xu Wan didn’t hold back at all, her grip firm. \"No way. If I let go, you’ll just run away. It’ll take me a few breaths to pin you down again.\"","\"A few breaths...\"","Wasn’t that just a blink of an eye?","Was she saying that, given the difference in their strength, she could knock him down in just a few breaths every time?","That was way too fast!","The little troublemaker felt insulted again, his face red as he tried to resist, but unfortunately, he was completely immobilized by his wicked stepmother.","\"Ugh, you’re just bullying a kid!\"","Xu Wan wasn’t bothered by such childish accusations. Instead, she laughed heartily. \"Exactly, kids are so easy to bully. Look at him, he can’t even get up. Right, Wenxiu?\"","Zong Wenxiu raised his hands in surrender, hoping the two of them would keep him out of their fight.","But the little troublemaker, as if finding a lifeline, quickly shouted, \"Brother, save me! I’m your closest brother!\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","The blade of familial duty cut him deeply once again.","He glanced at Xu Wan, hesitating whether to speak up for his brother.","The little troublemaker pleaded urgently, \"Didn’t you promise to always help me? She only asked you to study with me, not to turn against me!\"","Reminded of their agreement, Zong Wenxiu quickly stood up. \"Madam, I...\"","Xu Wan suddenly realized, \"So this is how you’ve been sweet-talking Wenxiu. No wonder he’s been doting on you more lately. You little rascal, your tricks are getting more polished.\"","Zong Wenxiu was stunned.","Sweet-talking him? He didn’t fully understand, but he was terrified his brother might have tricked him again.","The little troublemaker panicked and yelled, \"I didn’t sweet-talk anyone! I’m telling the truth! You never asked him to help you against me!\"","Xu Wan pinched his ear. \"But I also never asked him to help you against me. You’ve secretly won Wenxiu over, huh? Good job, kid, you’ve been stealing from my side.\"","The little troublemaker winced in pain but still managed to argue, \"You’re talking nonsense! He’s my brother, not yours! He’s always been on my side! If anyone’s stealing, it’s you!\"","Xu Wan snorted and turned to Zong Wenxiu. \"Did you hear that? He didn’t exactly lie to you, but he’s been working hard to win you over. It’s not exploitation, but it’s definitely manipulation. It’s not a big deal, but you should be more careful in the future, or you might end up helping someone count the money after they’ve sold you.\"","Zong Wenxiu was silent for a moment before nodding. \"I understand. Thank you for the advice, Madam.\"","Xu Wan then let go of the little troublemaker.","Now that the fire was lit in the backyard, the little rascal would be too busy putting it out to bother her.","Sure enough, as soon as Zong Jincheng was released, he rushed over pitifully, calling out, \"Brother...\"","Xu Wan rolled her eyes.","The kid was pulling out his sweet-talking tactics again. Disgusting.","Zong Wenxiu had seen this act from the little troublemaker many times. At first, he couldn’t help but soften, but now he was building up some immunity and wasn’t so easily swayed.","He shifted further inside, clearly not wanting to engage with his brother.","The little troublemaker, straightforward as ever, thought, \"If the mountain won’t come to me, I’ll go to the mountain.\"","He quickly scooted closer, clasping his hands in apology. \"Brother, don’t listen to her nonsense. I wasn’t sweet-talking you, I meant every word. We’re brothers. It’s only natural that we care for each other.\"","Zong Wenxiu’s resolve wavered slightly.","After hearing Xu Wan’s words, he felt like his brother had indeed been manipulating him. But what his brother said also made sense, and he couldn’t tell if he’d been fooled or not.","The little troublemaker pressed on, \"Really, sweet-talking is always about getting something. But look, I haven’t asked you for anything. I’ve been so good lately—no lies, no harm to Xu Wan, no disrespect to the teacher. I’ve kept all three promises I made to you.\"","Zong Wenxiu glanced at him.","His brother did have a point—he had been behaving well recently.","Xu Wan chimed in at the perfect moment, \"Weren’t you just asking him to save you?\"","With one sentence, she effortlessly shattered all the little troublemaker’s hard work.","The little troublemaker: \"!\"","Xu Wan! You are my lifelong nemesis!!!","\"Madam, we’ve arrived at the Minister's Mansion,\" Cui Zhi’s voice came from outside.","Xu Wan lifted the curtain and stepped out of the carriage. Seeing another carriage already parked at the entrance, she asked the guard, \"Has Duke Jin's Manor arrived?\"","The guard replied, \"Yes, they just entered.\"","Xu Wan nodded and turned to Cui Liu, \"Take Wenxiu and Jincheng to the courtyard to play. I’ll go speak with the elders for a while.\"","\"Yes, Madam.\"","Inside the carriage, the little troublemaker, who would usually be the first to jump out, was in no hurry this time. Taking advantage of Xu Wan’s absence, he launched another round of familial persuasion.","Zong Wenxiu rubbed his temples. \"Let’s talk about this when we get back to Yangyuan Marquis Manor. Don’t keep Madam waiting. You promised me you wouldn’t cause her any trouble today.\"","Zong Jincheng fell silent, filled with regret for coming here in the first place.","Originally, he had been worried that the couple from Duke Jin's Manor might bully Xu Wan. With their grandparents absent, he figured he was the most senior figure from Yangyuan Marquis Manor. Even though he and Duke Jin's Manor both disliked Xu Wan, she still represented their household, and he couldn’t let outsiders disrespect them.","But now, he’d ended up being bullied by Xu Wan instead... Hmph, he should’ve just stayed out of it!","No good deed goes unpunished!","That wicked woman!","The little troublemaker stepped out of the carriage with a sour expression, glaring at everyone in sight, even the guards at the Minister's Mansion.","This place was full of people with the surname Xu—all of them bad!","As he was stewing, Xu Wan’s stepmother, Madam Liu, came out and spotted the Zong brothers. She barely glanced at Zong Wenxiu, immediately showering the little troublemaker with affection. \"Jincheng, you’re finally here! It’s been months, and you’ve grown even more handsome. Come, let your grandmother take a good look at you.\"","The little troublemaker’s face instantly filled with confusion.","Grandmother?","I don’t even know where my mother is, who are you??"]},{"number":91,"title":"Chapter 91: Jincheng's Counterattack Against the Liu Family","paragraphs":["The Minister of Personnel was in his chamber receiving the new son-in-law of the Duke of Jin's Mansion, and the two were engaged in a pleasant conversation. When Madam Liu saw Xu Wan arriving, she exchanged a few polite words before stepping out to greet Zong Jincheng.","Compared to Xu Wan, he was the person most worthy of her personal attention in the entire Yangyuan Marquis Manor.","However, the little troublemaker, who was already in a foul mood, was in no state to be appeased. The term \"grandmother\" immediately struck a nerve.","Zong Jincheng ignored her with a scowl.","Madam Liu guessed that he had quarreled with Xu Wan again and quickly followed him, saying, \"My daughter has a terrible temper. You’ll have to bear with her, Jincheng. Don’t take it to heart. If you really can’t stand her, I’ll ask your grandmother to arrange for your father to take a few concubines. That way, she’ll be too busy to bother you.\"","Concubines for his missing uncle?","Zong Wenxiu, who had been ignored until now, suddenly looked up and glanced at his brother, worried that he might be deceived by Madam Liu.","Xu Wan had been extremely kind to his brother, as well as to him and his mother. He couldn’t stand by and watch her being treated this way.","\"Huh?\" Zong Jincheng blinked and stopped in his tracks.","What was this old woman talking about? His father wasn’t even home—what was the point of taking concubines?","Moreover, even if they did take concubines, what good would it do? Auntie Hong, who wasn’t even a concubine from the main household, had already been won over by Xu Wan. If the main household had concubines, wouldn’t Xu Wan just gain more allies, forming a group of women to scheme against him?","Zong Jincheng’s mind raced, and he quickly figured it out.","This old woman was clearly up to no good. First, she married Xu Wan into their family, and now she wanted to bring in concubines. She was full of malicious ideas.","But as the little troublemaker studied Madam Liu’s face, he noticed that she was smiling warmly, appearing utterly sincere—a stark contrast to what he had learned about reading people’s intentions.","What was going on... Had he misjudged her?","Zong Jincheng looked at his brother in confusion, about to speak, but Zong Wenxiu shook his head, as if telling him not to ask or agree.","Madam Liu continued, \"If your grandmother can’t find suitable candidates, I can ask the Madam of Vice Minister Zhao to help. She has a few daughters from her side family who are quite lovely and popular with children.\"","The little troublemaker thought to himself: Children like to play with other children, not with a bunch of flamboyant women.","Seeing that he remained silent and his anger seemed to have subsided a little, Madam Liu assumed he was considering her suggestion and smiled even more brightly. \"I’ll visit the Marquis Manor soon and have a good talk with your grandmother.\"","Zong Jincheng smiled sweetly and said, \"Didn’t you know? She’s already been sent to the countryside estate by Xu Wan.\"","\"By... by Xu Wan?\" Madam Liu was stunned. The rumors said that the grandmother had voluntarily gone to the estate.","Good heavens, was that the real reason?","Had Xu Wan’s methods become so sophisticated?","Zong Jincheng mimicked her sincere tone and added, \"Yes, otherwise how could she have so easily taken control of the Marquis Manor’s affairs? It’s all because my grandmother couldn’t outmatch her. By the way, are those concubines you mentioned really capable? What if Xu Wan just sends them straight to the Duke Jin's Manor? Wouldn’t that be a waste of time?\"","Madam Liu: \"...\" She suddenly felt uneasy.","If Xu Wan’s methods were indeed that subtle and effective, then sending concubines to the Marquis Manor might not be a wise move.","Moreover, since this boy dared to say such things, it must mean that Xu Wan had revealed similar tactics in front of him. Otherwise, how could an eight-year-old come up with such a sharp counterargument?","Madam Liu forced an awkward smile and quickly changed the subject. \"We’ll... we’ll talk about it later. Your grandmother hasn’t returned to the manor yet. Come inside. I’ll have someone bring you some pastries. Once your mother finishes her conversation, I’ll call you for dinner.\"","\"Sure,\" Zong Jincheng replied, not pressing the issue or losing his temper. Instead, he began to ponder, his eyes darting around thoughtfully.","Zong Wenxiu, who had been listening from behind, was stunned. He had been worried that his brother might be deceived by Madam Liu, but it seemed like she was the one who had been outsmarted by his brother.","Suddenly, he didn’t feel so bad. If his brother could trick Madam Liu, it was because he was too clever, not because he was foolish. After all, he was much younger than Madam Liu—it was only natural that he couldn’t see through her.","After sending the two boys to enjoy their pastries, Madam Liu’s smile vanished, and her expression darkened.","Zong Jincheng didn’t see her change in demeanor, still lost in his own confusion. Seeing that no one else was around, he quickly asked, \"Brother, why does she seem different from others? She doesn’t look like a bad person.\"","Zong Wenxiu sighed and said, \"Some people are like wolves in sheep’s clothing. They may smile kindly, but their actions are far from good. Reading people isn’t just about observing their expressions—you have to look at what they’re planning to do. Like you, for example. You often say harsh things, but you’ve never actually done anything bad.\"","\"What about the lychee incident? Doesn’t that count?\" Zong Jincheng asked, feeling a bit guilty at being praised.","\"...\" Zong Wenxiu paused for a moment before replying, \"I meant after that.\"","\"Oh, right,\" Zong Jincheng immediately straightened up and said seriously, \"Exactly. Even though Xu Wan, Qin Ye, Princess Eighteen, Zhai Yao, Luo Jingfeng, Qin Shi, Madam Liu, Xu Lian'er, Steward Liu... are all on my grudge list, I haven’t actually taken revenge on any of them. This proves that I’m a very kind person now, capable of repaying evil with good!\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\" That might be true, but hearing it from his brother’s mouth felt a bit off.","And... what was this grudge list?","How many people had he secretly held grudges against?","\"Wait, Steward Liu???\" Zong Wenxiu suddenly realized he had no idea his brother had a grudge against Steward Liu.","Zong Jincheng clenched his fists, his face filled with indignation. \"He was the one who confiscated all my belongings! Everything valuable in my room was taken away, including my pillow, shoes, and clothes! Don’t you think he went too far? It was outright robbery!\"","Zong Wenxiu rubbed his forehead, vaguely recalling the incident.","But that had happened so long ago—how could his brother still remember?","Oh right, he had a photographic memory... Help.","Zong Wenxiu clutched his chest, feeling utterly drained. \"Anyway, you understand now. Reading people isn’t just about their expressions—it’s also about their actions. But I’ve noticed that even if you don’t fully grasp these principles, your instincts guide you.\"","\"Huh? What instincts?\" Zong Jincheng scratched his head.","Zong Wenxiu explained, \"Just now, for example. Madam Liu clearly had ill intentions and wanted to harm Xu Wan. I was so worried earlier. But thankfully, you reacted quickly and suggested sending the concubines to the Duke Jin's Manor. Her expression changed immediately. If it were me, I probably wouldn’t have thought of such a clever response.\"","He added, \"Xu Wan was right—you’re perfect for a career in politics. Your talent is extraordinary.\"","Zong Jincheng wasn’t one to handle praise well.","Especially when his brother’s compliment was followed by Xu Wan’s praise. His little tail of pride immediately perked up.","Zong Jincheng seized the moment and asked, \"Brother, so you’re not mad at me anymore, right?\""]},{"number":92,"title":"Chapter 92: Cui Liu Smashes Minister Xu","paragraphs":["Zong Wenxiu shook his head: \"I'm not angry anymore. It's your strength to be good at comforting people, and it's my weakness to be easily comforted. You're not at fault, and I shouldn't blame you.\"","\"Is... is that so?\" This compliment made the little devil feel uneasy, wondering if his brother was heartbroken.","Zong Wenxiu said earnestly, \"I understand Madam's actions. She exposed you not to deliberately oppose you, but to remind me to learn from you, to learn how you skillfully avoid the main issue when comforting someone.\"","\"Ah?\" The little devil was completely baffled.","Thinking about such complex matters was too taxing on the brain. Since his brother was no longer angry with him, the little devil quickly forgot about it.","\"Come, brother, have some pastries.\"","\"Alright.\"","Xu Wan entered and bowed, greeting her scoundrel of a father.","On the day she returned home after her wedding, Minister Xu had said he was busy at the Ministry of Justice and couldn't come back. Today, for Xu Lian'er's return, he arrived early, seemingly getting along well with his son-in-law. Thinking about it now, it was truly ironic.","However, she had never expected to receive paternal love from her scoundrel father, so she simply smiled faintly and sat down, listening to their conversation.","The new son-in-law took the initiative to greet her: \"You must be the elder sister, right?\"","Xu Wan was wearing a green dress today, a shade that was neither too dark nor too light. It was neither too formal to overshadow her sister nor too casual to appear disrespectful. Paired with her calm and composed demeanor, she looked elegant and graceful.","What a fine young lady, yet she had married into the Yangyuan Marquis Manor and became a widow.","Xu Wan nodded in response: \"Brother-in-law.\"","She was also feeling uneasy, thinking that Chen Yunyu must indeed hold a grudge against her. If Duke Jin's Manor really caused trouble for her, retaliating would delay her efforts to educate the little devil, but enduring without retaliation would be truly frustrating...","Just as she was pondering how to resolve the crisis, she saw Chen Yunyu approach with a plate of pastries and say, \"This is the Seven-Flavored Pastry, which is extremely hard to come by in the Capital City. Lian'er brought some back today. Would you like to try it, sister?\"","Xu Wan smiled, accepted it with thanks, and took a small bite, thinking that even if Chen Yunyu had poisoned it, such a small amount shouldn't cause much harm.","Seeing that as soon as Xu Wan arrived, Chen Yunyu not only stopped talking to her father but also personally served her pastries, Xu Lian'er immediately felt displeased.","She said sarcastically, \"Husband, although the Seven-Flavored Pastry is expensive, the Yangyuan Marquis Manor comes from a merchant background and is never short of money. They must have eaten it often.\"","Xu Wan was wiping her mouth with a handkerchief.","Here it comes, she knew this visit wouldn't go smoothly.","She really couldn't understand why Xu Lian'er couldn't just focus on her own affairs and stop causing trouble for others.","Did she know that her husband had kept a mistress before their marriage?","Had she established her position in Duke Jin's Manor?","If she had nothing better to do, why not read a few pages and prepare to educate her future children?","Xu Lian'er continued to make such remarks, and just as Xu Wan was about to retaliate, Chen Yunyu spoke up first and scolded, \"Lian'er, how can you speak to your elder sister like that?\"","Xu Wan: \"?\"","Was the sky raining red?","Family members were turning against each other?","This newlywed couple didn't seem to be on the same page.","Good, at least they wouldn't have time to cause trouble for her and waste her time.","Xu Wan sat and watched the show as Chen Yunyu began to reprimand Xu Lian'er, saying she was disrespectful to her elder sister and not as obedient as she was in Duke Jin's Manor.","Every word of his reprimand struck a chord with Xu Wan, making her want to stand up and applaud, saying, \"Well said!\"","Chen Yunyu didn't seem foolish, no wonder he had managed to keep his affair with a mistress so well hidden and was favored by many noble ladies in the Capital City.","It seemed Xu Lian'er was in for a rough time, with both her mother-in-law and husband not as easy to fool as her scoundrel father.","\"Alright, Lian'er was indeed in the wrong today. Go apologize to your sister,\" Minister Xu finally spoke, though his expression was grim.","Xu Lian'er was aggrieved, but seeing her husband angry and her father displeased, she quickly came over to apologize: \"Sister, it was my fault. I made you angry. Please forgive me.\"","Xu Wan rolled her eyes inwardly, thinking that even her apology was a trap. Who was she making angry? Clearly, it was her husband who was more upset.","But she didn't want to waste time on Xu Lian'er, so she pretended to be graceful and magnanimous, replying, \"It's fine, sister isn't angry with you.\"","Seeing this, Chen Yunyu's expression improved slightly, and he added, \"Sister, I apologize. In the future, I will make sure Lian'er treats you with respect.\"","Xu Wan let out an awkward laugh.","Thinking to herself, why should she be respectful to me? I'm not her mother.","Minister Xu couldn't stand it any longer and said, \"Lian'er, take Yunyu for a walk in the garden. I have something to discuss with your sister.\"","\"Alright.\" Xu Lian'er was secretly pleased.","She knew her father doted on her the most, and this time he was surely going to give Xu Wan a hard time.","She pulled Chen Yunyu out, but noticed him glance back at Xu Wan, which immediately made her suspicious.","Only the two of them were left in the room.","Minister Xu's face grew even longer, and he angrily scolded, \"Today is your sister's return banquet, and you just watched her make a fool of herself?\"","Xu Wan thought to herself, as expected of her scoundrel father, always taking sides.","She smiled and asked, \"Father, wasn't it Lian'er who started the trouble? Wasn't it my brother-in-law who scolded her? I was just here to make up the numbers. What does this have to do with me?\"","Minister Xu said, \"When Lian'er and Yunyu were arguing, why didn't you say anything? If you had spoken up to smooth things over, Yunyu wouldn't have gotten so angry.\"","\"Father, I don't have the ability to predict when my brother-in-law will get angry. Speaking of which, you seem to have thought it through the most and must be able to predict. Why didn't you stop it?\" Xu Wan retorted.","Minister Xu was once again left speechless, his face visibly darkening. He said, \"After managing the household at the Marquis Manor for a few months, you've started putting on airs here? Let me remind you, this is the Minister's Mansion, not your Yangyuan Marquis Manor.\"","\"Of course, I know this isn't the Yangyuan Marquis Manor,\" Xu Wan said. \"If this were the Marquis Manor, the old madam would have punished my sister by making her copy books, slap her hands, or kneel in the ancestral hall, not just a simple apology. And she certainly wouldn't blame the victim here.\"","\"Father, if you don't care for me, someone else will.\"","In this world, not all relatives are bound by blood. Her biased and unreasonable scoundrel of a father wasn't even worth a finger compared to her mother-in-law.","\"You... you... how dare you talk back to your elders...\" Minister Xu picked up a long box from the table and hurled it at her.","Xu Wan stood firm, showing no fear in her eyes.","The long box flew through the air, heading straight for her face. If it hit, it would surely leave a wound.","But how could she let him succeed?","Cui Liu swiftly extended her arm and struck the long box, sending it flying back toward Minister Xu's face!"]},{"number":93,"title":"Chapter 93: The Scumbag Dad is Fuming with Anger","paragraphs":["Minister Xu was so furious that he couldn't hold back. The moment he threw the box, he regretted it. No matter how much Xu Wan talked back, he shouldn't have acted out on such a day, lest it leave a bad impression on his son-in-law. But to his surprise, the box was sent flying back toward his face.","\"Ah...\"","Minister Xu quickly dodged, the long box narrowly grazing his face, sending his anger through the roof.","\"Xu Wan! How dare you raise a hand against your own father? Kneel down!\" Minister Xu roared, his eyes bloodshot, fuming as he looked around for a stick.","Xu Wan sat in her chair, calmly picking up a teacup. She took a sip before speaking in a steady voice, \"Father, I am already married. Your household rules no longer apply to me.\"","She didn't bother pretending it was an accident—she had done it on purpose.","Cui Liu, her personal guard, stood protectively by her side, ensuring no harm could come to her, even if the threat was her own father.","The Xu Wan of today was no longer afraid to clash with him.","Minister Xu stormed over, shouting, \"Fine, fine! You ungrateful wretch! I raised you for eighteen years, and this is how you repay me? A wolf in sheep's clothing, daring to strike your own father!\"","Xu Wan slammed her teacup on the table, her sharp eyes glaring at him. \"Father, I suggest you calm down before you say something foolish and make a mockery of us both. As the legitimate daughter of the Minister, what kind of life did Xu Lian'er lead, and what kind of life did I endure? While I was surviving on sour fruits, where were you, my dear father? Eighteen years... what a joke. Did I ever have even a fraction of the life Xu Lian'er enjoyed? When Madam Liu bullied me, where were you then?\"","Minister Xu was left speechless, his face red with rage. He could only manage to yell, \"That still doesn't give you the right to raise a hand against your father!\"","Xu Wan scoffed, \"You were about to strike me without even hearing my side. I was merely defending myself. How is that my fault? Father, you are the Minister of Justice, overseeing the nation's laws. If this matter were brought before you, who would you say is in the wrong?\"","\"You...\" Minister Xu knew full well that by law, he was in the wrong. But having ruled his household for so long, he had never been so openly defied, especially by his once meek daughter. \"This is outrageous! A daughter striking her father, defying filial piety! I no longer have a daughter like you!\"","Xu Wan sneered, \"Good. I don't want a father like you either. Since we're in agreement, why don't we settle this today? Let's calculate how much I cost your Minister's Mansion over the past eighteen years, and I'll pay you back every last penny of that miserable sum.\"","Minister Xu was stunned. \"You want to sever our father-daughter relationship? Have you lost your mind?\"","He, one of the six ministers of the court, a high-ranking official of the second rank, being disowned by his own daughter? The scandal would be the talk of the town!","\"Why not?\" Xu Wan smiled. \"It's better than taking this to the authorities to decide who's right and who's wrong. You might not mind the embarrassment, but I certainly do.\"","Minister Xu was so enraged that he spat out blood. \"You... you... get out! Get out of here now!\"","Xu Wan stood up, politely bowed, and said, \"Gladly.\"","Finally, she could leave. Seeing his old face was truly suffocating.","Cui Liu and Cui Zhi quickly followed her out, barely holding back their laughter.","They had often seen Madam Xu angering Young Master Zong, occasionally feeling she was too harsh, fearing he might be too affected. But today, they realized she had always held back.","But confronting a terrible father like this—it was truly satisfying!","On the way, Cui Zhi asked with some concern, \"Madam, are we really going to sever ties with the Minister's Mansion? Although the Dowager will surely support you, Minister Xu is still your father...\"","Xu Wan stopped and explained with a smile, \"Don't worry. My father wouldn't dare sever ties with me. You don't understand how much someone from a humble background values everything they've achieved. He doesn't have the backing of an aristocratic family. Any hint of a bad reputation would be a massive blow to him.\"","\"In this world, it's not about who has the higher status, but who has more to lose.\"","Minister Xu had spent his entire life fearing missteps. He would never dare to openly break ties with her.","Cui Zhi finally relaxed and asked, \"Then are we going back to the manor or to the main hall? Minister Xu seems to be in a terrible state...\"","Xu Wan replied, \"To the main hall. We'll wait for the meal.\"","Cui Zhi's eyes widened, and even Cui Liu looked over in surprise.","\"What? Didn't Minister Xu tell you to...\"","Xu Wan chuckled, \"He told me to get out, but he didn't say I had to leave the manor. Today is Xu Lian'er's return visit. If I leave without even eating, people will think the Minister's Mansion doesn't value Duke Jin's Manor. Do you think my father would dare offend Duke Jin's Manor?\"","Cui Zhi: \"...\" Terrifying.","This meal would likely give Minister Xu a stomach ulcer.","The main hall was already filling up with guests.","However, everyone who arrived seemed to want to talk to Zong Jincheng. The young master, who initially had no interest in engaging, was nudged by Zong Wenxiu to at least nod and greet them politely.","Zong Jincheng's impatience was evident, his cheeks puffing up more and more.","When Chen Yunyu entered, he spotted Zong Jincheng immediately. After a careful look, he walked over with a smile, reaching out to pat the boy's head. \"You must be Madam Xu's Jincheng. How adorable.\"","Zong Jincheng clicked his tongue and dodged the hand. The young master hated having his head touched.","What did they think he was, a pet?","Chen Yunyu's smile froze, and he awkwardly withdrew his hand. \"Oh, the little one has quite the temper. I haven't even said anything, and you're already glaring at me?\"","Zong Jincheng couldn't be bothered to argue. In his eyes, none of the Xus in the room were good people, and this new son-in-law seemed even less trustworthy. He hadn't missed the lack of genuine joy in Chen Yunyu's eyes when they first met.","What a fake.","Chen Yunyu turned to Madam Liu and said, \"I heard that after Madam Xu married into Yangyuan Marquis Manor, she's been busy teaching this little one. If this is how he is after half a year, how unruly must he have been before?\"","Zong Jincheng, already on edge, exploded at the comment. \"Who are you calling unruly?\"","Chen Yunyu feigned surprise and quickly corrected himself, \"Oh, no, I just heard you were one of the four notorious young troublemakers in the capital. I was curious what you did to earn such a reputation.\"","Zong Jincheng couldn't tell if he was being mocked, but every word and gesture from this man made him deeply uncomfortable.","He was so irritated that he didn't even want to eat.","But leaving now would feel like running away, and Young Master Zong was no coward!"]},{"number":94,"title":"Chapter 94: Jincheng Frightens Chen Yunyu","paragraphs":["Seeing the tension between his younger brother and Chen Yunyu, Zong Wenxiu was afraid that his brother might lose his temper. He kept reminding him in his ear not to act impulsively and to avoid causing a scene.","The little troublemaker, Zong Jincheng, quickly wiped the cold expression off his face and replaced it with a sweet smile. \"Are you really curious about how I earned the title of the top troublemaker among the four young scoundrels?\"","Chen Yunyu was momentarily stunned by his sudden smile but quickly recovered and replied with a smile, \"Yes, I'd love to hear about your heroic deeds.\"","Zong Jincheng's smile grew even sweeter. \"Oh, it's nothing much. I just enjoy setting off firecrackers with friends. Once, a firecracker landed near a brothel and ended up burning the whole building down. It was quite a sight—people running out half-naked. Quite the spectacle!\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"......\"","Brother, you actually did something like that? That sounds terrifying.","Madam Liu and Xu Lian'er both twitched at the corners of their mouths, surprised that Xu Wan had taken on such a troublemaker as her stepson. He was truly a hot potato, and Xu Wan's seemingly glamorous life must not be as easy as it appeared.","Upon hearing this, Chen Yunyu's expression changed instantly, as if he had recalled something unpleasant. His face grew darker and darker.","He stared intently at Zong Jincheng and said, \"So, it was you who started that fire.\"","Damn it, that day was something he would never forget.","He had thought it was just an accidental fire, but it turned out to be the doing of this little rascal!","Zong Jincheng smiled sweetly. \"That's right! After the brothel caught fire, we even hung around the entrance for a while and saw quite a few familiar faces. Hmm, have I met you before? You look familiar.\"","\"No!\" Chen Yunyu immediately denied loudly.","Xu Lian'er was startled by the sudden outburst and quickly asked, \"Husband, what's wrong?\"","Chen Yunyu clenched his fists, trying to calm himself down, and then forced a smile. \"You must be mistaken. As the legitimate son of Duke Jin's Manor, how could I possibly have been to a brothel?\"","Zong Jincheng innocently replied, \"But I never forget a face. My memory has never failed me. I’m sure I’ve seen you before. Let me think where it was...\"","Chen Yunyu, who had just relaxed his fists, clenched them again and interrupted, \"Enough! Let’s not talk about such a filthy place. It’s almost time for dinner.\"","Seeing Chen Yunyu's agitation, Zong Jincheng felt much better.","Indeed, it’s much more satisfying to see someone else get worked up than to lose your own temper. Why had he always insisted on clashing head-on with others before?","Zong Jincheng, as if he had discovered a new world, felt increasingly pleased and even began to hum a tune.","Zong Wenxiu noticed that Chen Yunyu's expression was growing uglier, and the humming sounded more and more like a provocation.","Before coming here, his brother had said he was worried that Xu Wan might be bullied and that it would bring shame to the Marquis’s household. But before anyone could even think of bullying Xu Wan, his brother had already taken the initiative and managed to ruffle Chen Yunyu’s feathers. His skills were truly impressive, and Zong Wenxiu once again felt both ashamed of his own inadequacy and deeply impressed.","When Xu Wan arrived, she saw this scene: Madam Liu and Xu Lian'er were desperately trying to engage Chen Yunyu in conversation, while Chen Yunyu looked as if he had been hit by a truck. Zong Jincheng was humming a tune nearby, and Zong Wenxiu was nervously fidgeting.","Xu Wan smiled and asked, \"What’s going on here? Did I miss something?\"","Did Zong Jincheng actually manage to put Chen Yunyu in his place?","He had that kind of ability?","Zong Jincheng wagged his tail happily and threw her a triumphant look, as if to say, \"Why don’t you come over and thank me properly?\"","Upon hearing her voice, Chen Yunyu quickly stood up, his face a mix of red and black. He stammered nervously, \"Sister... Sister-in-law, you’re here. Please, take a seat. We were just waiting for you and father to start dinner.\"","Xu Wan found Chen Yunyu’s behavior a bit odd but didn’t dwell on it. She replied, \"Father isn’t feeling well, so he might be a bit late.\"","Madam Liu said, \"Then I’ll go check on him. Lian'er, Wan'er, you two take care of Yunyu and the children here.\"","\"Yes, Mother.\"","After Madam Liu left, Xu Wan asked, \"What were you all talking about just now?\"","Zong Jincheng said casually, \"He asked me how I became the top troublemaker in the capital, and I told him I set off firecrackers and burned down a brothel...\"","\"Jincheng!\" Chen Yunyu interrupted before he could finish. \"Let’s not talk about that anymore. In front of your mother, let’s discuss something else. How’s your studies going? Have you memorized the Thousand-Character Classic yet?\"","Zong Jincheng proudly raised his head. \"Child’s play! I memorized that ages ago!\"","The two of them began to chat back and forth. Chen Yunyu, after all, was a fourth-rank official who had risen through the ranks by passing the imperial examinations. He was well-educated and managed to keep up with Zong Jincheng, occasionally praising him for how quickly he was learning. Soon enough, Zong Jincheng was completely swept up in the compliments.","Xu Wan knew exactly what kind of person Zong Jincheng was. He didn’t have any real grudge against Chen Yunyu—it was just a minor clash. After a few compliments, he would forget all about the earlier incident.","However, what was strange was that while Chen Yunyu was talking to Zong Jincheng, he kept glancing in Xu Wan’s direction.","At first, she thought he was looking at Xu Lian'er, but when even Xu Lian'er started glaring at her, Xu Wan finally realized something was off.","...Could it really be that cliché?","The jealousy in Xu Lian'er’s eyes was almost palpable, and even Xu Wan felt a bit overwhelmed. She couldn’t help but shift closer to Zong Wenxiu.","She leaned on the table, resting her forehead in her hand, and muttered under her breath, \"This Chen Yunyu is really something.\"","No wonder he had stood up for her earlier and scolded Xu Lian'er. Now that she thought about it, his bringing over the pastries was just another way of trying to curry favor.","In her previous life, Xu Wan had been too busy climbing the social ladder to bother with romance. In this life, she had married early and hadn’t even met her husband, so she had never given much thought to matters of the heart. But now, she realized she was in trouble.","What a mess. What an absolute mess.","After mentally cursing, Xu Wan felt like leaving immediately. But remembering Minister Xu’s demeanor, she knew there was no way she could walk out of this door.","She felt like she was sitting on pins and needles.","Xu Lian'er, sitting beside her, gritted her teeth and asked, \"Sister, when do you plan to return home today?\"","Xu Wan replied with a sense of despair, \"You might not believe me, but the truth is, I want to leave right now.\"","Xu Lian'er: \"......?\"","Why wasn’t she following the script?","The anger in Xu Lian'er’s eyes softened slightly, and she pretended to be concerned. \"Sister, are you feeling unwell?\"","Xu Wan nodded repeatedly. \"Yes, I’m barely holding on.\"","If it weren’t for the fact that she couldn’t defy Minister Xu’s authority, she would have bolted before even entering the hall.","But even though her words didn’t carry much weight, if Xu Lian'er were to suggest letting her leave, Minister Xu might agree.","This place was so uncomfortable that she didn’t want to stay a second longer.","Xu Lian'er quickly said, \"Then I’ll speak to Father and let you return home to rest. You mustn’t overwork yourself and fall ill!\"","Xu Wan, almost tearful with gratitude, replied, \"Good sister, my health is in your hands!\""]},{"number":95,"title":"Chapter 95: Failed to Keep an Eye on the Little Rascal","paragraphs":["Xu Lian'er's mouth twitched, feeling that her sister was especially off today, but she couldn't care less. If Xu Wan, that seductive fox, stayed any longer, she would go mad.","So she stood up and hurried to find Minister Xu, but just as she was about to leave, Chen Yunyu immediately looked over.","Both sisters were startled.","Xu Lian'er quickly pulled Xu Wan up as well, saying, \"Sister, you should come with me.\"","Otherwise, leaving her alone here would just give them another chance to be together.","Xu Wan, as if seeing a savior, nodded repeatedly, \"Great idea, my dear sister!\"","Xu Lian'er: \"...\"","Had she been driven mad by that rebellious son in the Marquis's manor?","Otherwise, why was she suddenly so affectionate with her?","\"Hurry, sister, I'm in a bit of a rush,\" Xu Wan urged, dragging Xu Lian'er out.","Xu Lian'er: \"???\"","Who exactly was in a rush here!","But it was rare for these half-sisters to be on the same page, so they went together to ask Minister Xu to let Xu Wan leave.","Minister Xu, if not for the sake of face, didn't want to see Xu Wan's disobedient face any longer. But since Xu Lian'er had already come up with a reason, he quickly waved his hand and let Xu Wan go.","In the main hall, the food was already served.","The little devil, Zong Jincheng, hadn't even picked up his chopsticks when he was told they had to go home. He stood up with a start, feeling utterly absurd, and said to Chen Yunyu, \"You're not even letting us eat? You're really something.\"","Chen Yunyu: \"??\"","Who said you couldn't eat?","What does this have to do with me??","But he couldn't bother arguing with Zong Jincheng at the moment and quickly went out to ask what was going on. He heard that Xu Wan was feeling unwell and immediately became anxious, \"What's wrong? Sister-in-law was fine just now.\"","Xu Lian'er's face darkened further, feeling that her new husband's concern for Xu Wan was excessive.","But she forced herself to suppress her jealousy and softly explained, \"Sister caught a chill yesterday and came today just to support us. Now she's really feeling unwell, so I spoke to Father, and we'll invite her to the manor another day.\"","Chen Yunyu pondered, \"Sister-in-law has worked hard. Alright, we'll invite her to Duke Jin's Manor another day and make up for today's lack of hospitality.\"","Xu Lian'er's heart burned with anger. She wished she could never let Chen Yunyu see Xu Wan again, but her husband wanted to invite Xu Wan to Duke Jin's Manor. Why? That was her home, and she didn't want Xu Wan there!","Xu Lian'er outwardly complied but inwardly vowed to take control of Duke Jin's Manor as soon as possible and never let Xu Wan set foot in her home again!","Meanwhile, Zong Jincheng was still making a fuss, but Zong Wenxiu covered his mouth and dragged him out, muffling his protests, leaving only his arms flailing in the air.","Once stuffed into the carriage, Zong Jincheng finally regained his freedom and howled, \"This is outrageous! The food was on the table, and they wouldn't let us eat. How rude!\"","He had finally managed to annoy that pretentious Chen Yunyu, but he didn't even get to see him lose his appetite. It was so unsatisfying!","Zong Wenxiu quickly explained, \"These people are all strange. It's better not to eat with them. Our Marquis's manor has better food anyway.\"","Zong Jincheng then replied, \"True, our Marquis's manor's cooking is the best in the capital. The Xu family's food is just so-so.\"","Xu Wan sat in the carriage for a while before she felt safe again, only to realize she had been acting like she was fleeing for her life. When she turned her head, she heard Zong Jincheng's comment and instinctively replied, \"It really is just so-so, not tasty.\"","Zong Jincheng was a bit surprised. This woman actually agreed with him.","How unexpected.","Was the sun rising from the west today?","He lifted the carriage curtain to look outside...","Oh, never mind.","\"Gurgle...\" Someone's stomach suddenly growled.","The carriage fell silent for a moment before all three of them burst into laughter.","Xu Wan teased, \"Looks like we won't make it back to the Marquis's manor for lunch.\"","Zong Wenxiu scratched his head sheepishly. He thought it was his brother's stomach that had growled, no wonder he was so annoyed earlier.","Xu Wan instructed the outside, \"Cui Zhi, find a nearby restaurant. We'll eat there.\"","\"Yes, Madam.\"","Zuixiang House.","As they walked in, Zong Jincheng was still muttering, \"I’m warning you, a meal here costs at least dozens of taels. It's very expensive.\"","Since Xu Wan had cut off all his funds, he hadn't been to such a place in months.","And now he was very sensitive about money. Just thinking about how many copper coins it would convert into made it feel like an enormous expense.","Xu Wan smiled, \"Expensive or not, it's my treat. I don’t want to starve two delicate little children to death.\"","\"Haha...\" Zong Wenxiu laughed.","Zong Jincheng stuck his tongue out at her and bounced inside.","\"Ah, Young Master Zong is here! Please, come in!\"","Zong Jincheng, the infamous spendthrift of the capital, was recognized by the owners of every high-end restaurant. As soon as he entered, he was spotted, and the waiter hurried to serve him properly.","Xu Wan secretly clicked her tongue. This kid really could get by on his face anywhere. Fortunately, Steward Liu had already informed these establishments that they wouldn’t cover any debts, or else they really wouldn’t be able to stop that brat.","\"Young Master Zong, Madam Zong, I’ll take you to the best private room.\"","Xu Wan waved her hand, \"No need, just find us a table by the window.\"","\"Of course.\"","The three of them went up to the second floor, where the window seat offered a view of the street below. The weather in May was already slightly warm, and the breeze was comfortably cool.","\"Braised carp, roasted lamb, five-flavored goose, sliced perch, pickled winter melon...\"","Zong Jincheng didn’t even need to look at the menu, rattling off dish names one after another. The waiter's smile grew wider and wider, until his eyes were nearly shut.","Zong Wenxiu watched in awe, while Xu Wan idly observed the young master's performance.","When it came to food, no child could resist. Although the Marquis's manor's chef was also excellent, Zong Jincheng was clearly much happier eating out. His round little face beamed with joy, so heartwarming that it made one’s heart melt like a pool of spring water, wanting to give him the best things in the world.","Xu Wan had never been a mother before, and this was the first time she had felt this way. She silently sighed to herself, \"They say a doting mother spoils the child, but what mother wouldn’t want to lovingly pamper her child?\"","But her moment of maternal affection didn’t last long before Xu Wan couldn’t take it anymore and interrupted, \"Alright, that’s enough. We can’t possibly finish all that.\"","In the blink of an eye, the little rascal had already ordered ten dishes.","Xu Wan watched the waiter happily rush off to place the order, her mouth twitching. That little devil was really too good at charming people. She hadn’t kept an eye on him for just a moment, and he had already gone wild.","Xu Wan tried to salvage the situation, \"Ten dishes. Let’s try to finish them. If we can’t, we’ll take the leftovers back to the Marquis's manor and eat them tonight.\"","Zong Jincheng: \"!!!\"","Completely incomprehensible!","The little devil stood up from the table and protested loudly, \"Who takes leftovers home after eating out!\""]},{"number":96,"title":"Chapter 96: Standing Up for Qin Shi","paragraphs":["If others found out, how could Young Master Zong Jincheng keep his reputation intact? His friends would surely laugh him to scorn!","Xu Wan rolled her eyes at him and explained, \"Except for your household, everyone else does it.\"","Taking home leftovers is a traditional virtue of the Chinese nation. This kid, who seems to live in a world of his own, thinks everyone is as wasteful as he is.","Zong Jincheng immediately retorted, \"Impossible! I’ve never seen...\"","But before he could finish his sentence, he heard someone nearby shout, \"Waiter, pack this up.\"","\"Right away!\"","\"...\" Zong Jincheng immediately sat down.","Damn it, it’s true.","Had he just never noticed it before?","Zong Wenxiu chuckled softly and nudged his younger brother’s shoulder, saying, \"Jincheng, if you really don’t want to take the leftovers, we can just try to eat more and finish everything.\"","Zong Jincheng pouted and fake-cried in a whiny voice, \"But brother, we ordered too much. Even if we stuff ourselves, we can’t finish it all...\"","He had initially planned to make Xu Wan pay a hefty price to vent the frustration he’d built up over the past few months, but who knew she had a trick up her sleeve?","The little troublemaker’s rebellion had once again ended in failure.","Zong Wenxiu thought for a moment and suggested, \"How about we ask the waiter to cancel a few dishes? The kitchen hasn’t started cooking yet anyway.\"","The little troublemaker seemed a bit swayed.","Either take the leftovers and be laughed at, or cancel some dishes and be mocked by the owner.","Since both options would lead to embarrassment, he might as well grit his teeth and choose the former. After all, it would be Xu Wan who’d call for the leftovers, and the proud young master could pretend he had no idea.","Yes, that’s the way to go.","After weighing the pros and cons, Zong Jincheng declared with righteous determination, \"A gentleman’s word is unbreakable. We’re not canceling any dishes.\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","Is that really how you use \"a gentleman’s word\"...?","Xu Wan glanced at him, fully aware of the little troublemaker’s scheming. Did he really think he could shift the blame onto her? Not a chance.","The dishes arrived one after another, and the three of them, starving, began to eat. Zuixiang House’s food was expensive for a reason. Not only was it located in the best area, but the vegetables were fresh, the meat was tender, and the cooking techniques were exquisite. The taste was simply outstanding.","Xu Wan thought to herself that she might come here more often if she had the chance.","Although her monthly allowance of three hundred taels of silver might not be enough to sustain such luxury, there was still the ten-thousand-tael reward dangling in front of her. If she could get that, she could eat whatever she wanted whenever she wanted.","Ah, the allure of a big reward truly gives one hope.","After eating and drinking to their hearts’ content, there were still some leftovers on the table. The two boys, their bellies round, declared that even if they burst, they couldn’t finish it all.","Xu Wan couldn’t help but laugh.","The little troublemaker slumped in his chair, completely unwilling to move. Forget going home, he didn’t even want to speak right now. He needed to recover for a while.","As he lounged there, he idly glanced out the window and saw someone unexpected.","\"Qin Shi...\"","Zong Wenxiu also looked over and asked, \"Qin Shi? Is he Qin Ye’s older brother? How do you know him?\"","The little troublemaker pointed at the young man on the street who was being stopped by someone and said confidently, \"Yes, he’s Qin Ye’s brother. I saw him from a distance at Hanlin North Academy last time. Don’t you remember?\"","Zong Wenxiu shook his head and teased, \"I don’t have your photographic memory.\"","Zong Jincheng immediately puffed up with pride and said, \"Of course. Even if I only see someone from afar, I can remember exactly who they are. At the time, Qin Ye was talking to him, and he just kept nodding. He seemed really obedient.\"","\"Qin Shi must be a very mild-mannered person,\" Zong Wenxiu said, but then he noticed something was wrong. \"But right now, is he being harassed? Look, that guy is pushing Qin Shi.\"","\"Really?\" Zong Jincheng quickly leaned over to look and saw the young man in front of Qin Shi, poking his chest with his finger while muttering something, looking very aggressive.","\"Wow, he really is. Why is Qin Shi so easy to bully?\" The little troublemaker immediately stood up from his chair and rushed downstairs.","Zong Wenxiu was utterly amazed.","Hadn’t his brother just said he couldn’t move another inch?","Who was this kid running so fast now...?","But since his brother had already run down, he was worried something might happen, so he quickly got up and followed.","Cui Zhi asked beside them, \"Madam, should we go down and take a look?\"","Xu Wan looked at the scene below the window and smiled, \"No need. We can just watch the show from here. It’s better not to interfere too much in children’s matters. Besides, with Wenxiu there, I’m not worried.\"","Sometimes, children don’t listen to what adults say, but they’ll listen to their peers because they feel like they’re on the same side. Giving the brothers some space to handle things on their own is actually good for their growth.","Cui Zhi asked again, \"But from up here, we probably won’t be able to hear what they’re saying...\"","Xu Wan thought for a moment and said, \"People who practice martial arts have good hearing. Cui Liu, you’ll be our real-time commentator.\"","\"...?\" Cui Liu, who was suddenly called upon.","\"Yes, madam.\"","As soon as the little troublemaker stepped outside, he saw the troublemaker pushing Qin Shi and mocking him, \"You loser, why haven’t you passed the entrance exam for the children’s class yet? Looks like you’ve reached your limit and become a mediocrity. If you really can’t learn, why bother? Just get out of Hanlin North Academy and go join your talented brother at Qingbo Academy!\"","Qin Shi didn’t resist the pushing, as if he was used to it. His body retreated with the other’s movements, but he still held tightly to his books.","The troublemaker snatched the books from his hands, held them high, and shouted, \"Mediocrity, still reading books here? Do you think you can ever surpass your brother? Loser.\"","As he was about to throw the books in Qin Shi’s face, Zong Jincheng appeared out of nowhere and slapped the troublemaker’s shoulder, growling, \"Kid, you’re even more arrogant than me.\"","The troublemaker turned around and saw a kid two years younger than him. He immediately cursed, \"Brat, get lost, or Grandpa Feng Song will punch your head off.\"","\"Feng Song?\" The little troublemaker tilted his head and cracked his knuckles, replying coolly and arrogantly, \"Then have you heard of your ancestor, Zong Jincheng?\"","Feng Song’s heart nearly stopped.","Zong... Zong Jincheng...","The most favored grandson of Yangyuan Marquis Manor, the leader of the four little troublemakers in the capital, the little demon king who even ghosts feared?","\"You... you’re really Zong Jincheng?\"","Zong Jincheng raised his fist threateningly, \"Want your ancestor to punch you to see if it’s real or not?\"","Feng Song was terrified, but admitting defeat would be too humiliating. He struggled to say, \"Young Master Zong, you’ve misunderstood. I was just advising this mediocrity to give up studying so he doesn’t waste any more time on something useless.\"","The Feng family and the Qin family were distant relatives, so he knew Qin Shi couldn’t possibly know Zong Jincheng. He thought Zong Jincheng was just passing by and didn’t know the situation, so he dared to lie, \"I’m just doing him a favor.\""]},{"number":97,"title":"Chapter 97: Fight Violence with Violence","paragraphs":["Feng Song's expression was both ingratiating and sincere, so convincing that it seemed genuine. Fortunately, Zong Jincheng had just encountered the hypocritical Madam Liu and could instantly spot such lies.","\"How exactly is it for his own good?\" The little devil crossed his arms, looking down arrogantly as he waited for Feng Song to weave his tale.","Feng Song immediately began, \"His talent is just too poor. He’s been studying for six or seven years, but he’s still not as good as his eight-year-old brother. I don’t think he has any aptitude for academics, so it’s better for him to drop out of the academy early and make room for other students.\"","Zong Jincheng quickly grasped the key point, narrowing his eyes as he asked, \"Are you from Hanlin Southern Academy?\"","Feng Song hesitated for a moment before replying, \"Yes, I am. How did you know?\"","The little devil sneered, \"You want him to make room for you, which means you couldn’t even get into Hanlin North Academy, right?\"","If Hanlin North Academy was full of his defeated opponents, then Hanlin Southern Academy was just a group of even less capable rich kids who weren’t even qualified to be his sparring partners.","Zong Jincheng glanced at him and added, \"A rookie like you dares to look down on Qin Shi from Hanlin North Academy? Did you forget to look in the mirror before leaving the house?\"","\"You...\" Feng Song’s face immediately twisted in anger. He hated it when people said he was inferior to Qin Shi. His fists clenched tightly, but remembering the other’s status, he forced himself to loosen them.","The little devil continued to berate him, \"I just saw you pushing him and trying to smash his books. And you call it for his own good? Don’t dress up your bullying with such excuses. Even I, the so-called troublemaker, have never done something so shameless. How dare you twist the truth like this?\"","By the window on the second floor, Cui Liu was still acting as an emotionless messenger.","Xu Wan chuckled as she listened to her monotone voice, \"Cui Liu, can you put a bit more emotion into it? Such scolding needs some feeling to be truly satisfying.\"","Cui Liu: \"...\"","Your expectations are too high. She just wanted to switch places with Bu Yan.","Feng Song’s chest heaved, but he still tried to salvage the situation, \"I... I just went a bit too far, but my intentions were good. I was just trying to...\"","\"Good intentions my foot,\" the little devil said coldly, extending his hand. \"Give me the book.\"","Feng Song immediately handed it over with both hands, his palms sweaty and his body trembling slightly. He forced a smile and said, \"Here you go, here you go.\"","Though the little devil wasn’t as tall as him, he held his head high with an air of arrogance, like a tyrant bullying an ordinary person. Meanwhile, the original bully, Feng Song, had now become submissive and drenched in sweat.","Sometimes, even Zong Wenxiu had to admit:","Using force to counter force was highly effective.","Zong Jincheng took the book and glanced at it. It was *Meng Qiu*.","He had already mastered this book with his brother long ago. Why was Qin Shi still reading it?","Though puzzled, the little devil handed the book back to Qin Shi and said, \"Here, it’s yours.\"","Then he turned to Feng Song and ordered, \"Apologize to him.\"","Feng Song quickly turned around and said loudly, \"Qin Shi, I’m sorry! I shouldn’t have bullied you. Please forgive me!\"","Qin Shi had never expected this day to come. Feng Song, who had been bullying him for years, was now being forced to apologize to him.","It was unexpected, but also deeply moving.","Qin Shi replied, \"I accept your apology.\"","An eye for an eye would only lead to endless conflict. He just wanted to focus on his studies like his brother and avoid any further entanglement with Feng Song.","Zong Jincheng kicked him and said, \"If I see you bullying Qin Shi again, don’t blame me for using my fists.\"","\"Yes, yes, I won’t dare to do it again!\" Feng Song scurried away in an instant.","When Qin Shi took the book back, he was still in a daze. In the past, the books Feng Song had taken from him had never been returned intact. This was the first time.","All because of the child known as the leader of the troublemakers who had helped him.","But he didn’t seem bad at all, Qin Shi thought.","\"Thank you, Zong Jincheng,\" Qin Shi said with a smile, remembering the name Feng Song had called him.","The little devil snorted arrogantly, \"No need to thank me. Just remember my name, because it’s the one that will defeat you in the next joint exam!\"","\"Huh?\" Qin Shi was confused.","Was this kid here to challenge him?","But he looked about the same age as Xiao Ye.","Thinking of Xiao Ye, Qin Shi felt reassured. Perhaps this child was also exceptionally talented and highly knowledgeable, just like Xiao Ye.","Zong Wenxiu, worried that Qin Shi might misunderstand, quickly explained on his brother’s behalf, \"Qin Shi, don’t misunderstand. My brother means no harm. He just talks like that.\"","Zong Jincheng was full of questions and turned to ask, \"Brother, what did I say wrong?\"","Zong Wenxiu whispered, \"Your tone. It makes you sound like Feng Song, like you’re trying to intimidate him.\"","\"Then how should I phrase ‘defeating him’ in a nicer way?\" Zong Jincheng asked humbly.","\"Hmm...\" Zong Wenxiu thought for a moment and said, \"Surpass him?\"","\"Isn’t that the same thing?\"","\"It sounds more polite.\"","\"But it doesn’t sound as good. It doesn’t show my dominance.\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","Showing dominance...","Isn’t that exactly what intimidation is?!","The Zong brothers whispered back and forth for a while but couldn’t agree on the right wording, so they eventually gave up.","Qin Shi, watching them, smiled and said, \"It’s alright, I understand what he means. But are you also from Hanlin North Academy? I don’t think I’ve seen you before.\"","Zong Jincheng proudly replied, \"We study at home, but we take exams at Qingbo Academy every month.\"","Qin Shi nodded in understanding, \"My younger brother also studies at Qingbo Academy.\"","\"I know, your brother is Qin Ye,\" Zong Jincheng said through gritted teeth. \"That rude kid is nothing like you. I seriously doubt you share the same parents.\"","\"You know my brother?\" Qin Shi was amused and couldn’t help but say, \"You’re probably the first person to think that. Xiao Ye has always been more likable than me.\"","He was the one who had been doubted for not being as smart as his brother, not the other way around.","Zong Jincheng rolled his eyes and retorted, \"Not at all. I don’t like him. He always acts like he’s better than everyone, cold and arrogant, and his words are just begging for a punch.\"","Zong Wenxiu silently thought to himself, You’re not much better.","Qin Shi scratched his head, unsure how to respond. He earnestly explained, \"Xiao Ye might seem hard to get along with, but he’s actually a good person.\"","Zong Jincheng snorted, \"I don’t care if he’s good or not. I’ll never be friends with him. Never, ever.\"","Zong Wenxiu silently added in his mind: Qin Ye probably doesn’t want to be friends with you either...","But then he suddenly remembered something and asked Qin Shi, \"By the way, the results of the joint exam between Hanlin North Academy and Qingbo Academy just came out today. How did you do?\"","All fifty students from Hanlin North Academy had passed, and Qin Shi was surely among them. However, when Zong Wenxiu had checked the results that morning, he hadn’t known Qin Shi and hadn’t noticed his ranking.","Qin Shi nodded and replied, \"Not bad, second place.\"","Zong Wenxiu: \"...\"","Not bad...","Second place in the joint exam is \"not bad\"...","As someone who ranked nineteenth, he felt deeply wounded!"]},{"number":98,"title":"Chapter 98: Key Class Test","paragraphs":["Zong Jincheng was also astonished. He exclaimed, \"You did so well? You came in second place! How could Feng Song have the nerve to say you’re not suited for studying? Is he blind?\"","The little troublemaker instantly felt that he hadn’t scolded Feng Song enough earlier. That weakling from the southern academy was really asking for a beating. What level was he even at, to dare bully Qin Shi, who ranked second in the joint exam?","Qin Shi smiled lightly and said, \"It’s fine, I didn’t take it to heart.\"","His temper was truly too good.","Completely different from Qin Ye’s infuriating demeanor.","Zong Jincheng immediately decided to remove him from his grudge list and said earnestly, \"Alright, just wait. I’m definitely going to surpass you!\"","Zong Wenxiu turned his head in surprise. How had his brother suddenly learned to be tactful?","But he quickly added, \"And me too. My name is Zong Wenxiu.\"","Qin Shi smiled and said, \"Alright, I’ll be looking forward to it.\"","At the Qin household, Qin Shi had just walked in with a stack of books when he ran into Qin Ye, who had returned from the academy.","He looked the same as usual, without a trace of joy for having taken first place in the children’s division. Hanlin North Academy had prepared for this joint exam specifically to seek revenge against Qin Ye, but to their dismay, the entire children’s class of over a hundred students had been completely defeated, losing even more miserably than last month.","Qin Shi said, \"Qin Ye, congratulations on taking first place again. This time it’s first in the children’s division. When the children’s exam comes next spring, you’ll surely achieve an excellent result.\"","Qin Ye noticed the book in his hands and walked over, asking, \"Haven’t you already mastered 'Mengqiu'?\"","Qin Shi glanced down at the book and smiled again. \"I can recite it, but I’m not yet proficient in applying it. So I wanted to review it a few more times.\"","Qin Ye nodded and asked, \"Brother, did you bring back your exam paper? Let me take a look at where you went wrong.\"","Although Qin Shi was older than Qin Ye in age, Qin Ye was far more advanced in terms of knowledge. After persuading his brother not to sacrifice his own future for him, Qin Shi often took the initiative to ask Qin Ye for help, making his brother feel that he didn’t mind.","Over time, Qin Ye got used to helping him and began to proactively ask if there were any areas Qin Shi hadn’t fully grasped, just like now.","Qin Shi replied, \"Yes, I’ll come to the study later to find you.\"","Qin Ye nodded again, still speaking little.","In contrast, Qin Shi seemed more talkative. He casually mentioned, \"By the way, on my way back, I met two students from your academy and chatted with them for a while. They were really nice and even helped me get my book back from Feng Song.\"","\"Did Feng Song bully you again?\" Qin Ye frowned and was about to turn around. \"I’ll go tell Father and have him settle the score with the Feng family.\"","Qin Shi quickly stopped him, saying, \"No, no, we’re still relatives with the Feng family. It’s not good to have Father intervene and affect the adults’ relationship. Besides, Feng Song already apologized to me today and promised he’d never bully me again.\"","Qin Ye paused, slightly puzzled.","Qin Shi smiled and said, \"It was those two who helped me. One is named Zong Jincheng, the same age as you. He looks a bit fierce but is actually very kind. The other is probably his older brother, named Zong Wenxiu, the same age as me.\"","\"Those names sound familiar...\" Qin Ye searched his memory and recalled a time when Qingbo Academy was in chaos, and he couldn’t get out because of a reward notice posted by these two, offering five hundred taels to find something.","They didn’t seem very reliable.","Qin Shi smiled and said, \"They both said they’re going to surpass me. They’re quite confident, but they’re not like Feng Song. Honestly, I’m quite looking forward to it. Qin Ye, you should be careful too. I think Zong Jincheng might be as smart as you. He might even catch up to you.\"","To rank ninth in the joint exam after only four months of studying—even Qin Ye couldn’t have achieved such rapid progress.","Qin Ye said, \"Brother, you’re overthinking it.\"","\"No one can take my first place.\"","The young boy’s eyes were sharp and determined, his confidence intimidating.","At the Marquis Manor Elite Class, the two overachievers headed straight to the study as soon as they got home. It was the afternoon session after lunch, and the three private tutors had already sorted out the mistakes on their exam papers and prepared detailed explanations.","As soon as the two boys sat down, the tutors began explaining the errors. Each of them also had a scribe taking notes beside them. If they didn’t understand something, they could refer to the notes or ask the tutors to explain again.","To overtake others, it wasn’t just about having excellent tutors and high-quality exam questions. The students themselves had to put in a lot of time studying, memorizing, and practicing.","Listening, reading, and writing—none could be neglected.","After four months of studying in the study, the little troublemaker’s writing speed had already caught up to Zong Wenxiu’s. Although his handwriting was still atrocious, it was at least legible.","However, Xu Wan wasn’t in a hurry to correct his messy handwriting.","For one, the little troublemaker was still in the stage of enjoying the fun of using colorful ink to write ugly characters. It wasn’t the right time to crush his interest. Secondly, there was still more than half a year before the children’s exam, and there would be plenty of time to practice his handwriting before then.","Xu Wan understood the principle of not rushing things and knew how to balance things appropriately.","Meanwhile, the little troublemaker was still shouting, \"Tutor Zhao, I want to take the ten-year-old class exam with my brother. Teach me at his pace. I’m going to defeat Qin Shi!\"","Zhao Yin smiled and said, \"Young Master Jincheng, what an admirable goal. But let’s not rush. I’ve prepared two sets of exam papers for you. Try them both first.\"","\"Oh? What exam papers?\" Not only was the little troublemaker curious, but even Zong Wenxiu looked over.","Zhao Yin smiled and said, \"Our elite class has obtained the past exam papers from Qingbo Academy. These two are from the nine-year-old and ten-year-old classes. Young Master Jincheng can use them to test his current knowledge level.\"","Zong Jincheng’s eyes lit up. \"Great, give them to me!\"","The curriculum of the elite class was tailored to their learning speed. Since both children were highly talented, the lessons were faster and more detailed than those at the academy. However, it was also easy to lose track of their progress.","Now, with the academy’s exam papers for each age and month, they could clearly gauge their own progress.","Zong Wenxiu was also tempted.","Pan Hongzhi smiled and asked, \"Young Master Wenxiu, would you like to try the eleven-year-old exam paper?\"","Zong Wenxiu looked up, delighted. \"Eleven years old... Can I?\"","Pan Hongzhi smiled and said, \"You can give it a try.\"","\"Alright!\"","The three tutors handed out the exam papers to the two boys and lit the specially made exam incense that Xu Wan had ordered. They began preparing for the exam.","\"This incense burns for one hour, which is the duration of your exam. Please finish the exam before the incense burns out. You may submit your papers early, but once the time is up, you must stop writing immediately.\""]},{"number":99,"title":"Chapter 99: Help the Legitimate Sister","paragraphs":["During the mock exam, timing not only tests knowledge but also simulates the real exam environment, making the children feel the pressure of the actual test. This helps them manage their time more precisely in the future.","Both of them found it quite novel and were eager to get started.","\"I’m sure I’ll finish early!\" Contestant number one, Zong Jincheng, was as confident as ever.","Zong Wenxiu chuckled, \"My goal isn’t as high; I just hope to finish on time.\"","Cheng Zhidong kindly reminded them, \"Young masters, please don’t focus too much on speed. Make sure to read the questions carefully, think clearly, and write neatly to avoid careless mistakes.\"","Though he didn’t mention any names, it was clear who he was referring to.","The confident Zong Jincheng stuck out his tongue, picked up his brush, and began answering the questions.","The scent of burning incense inside the room gradually mingled with the fragrance of the blooming garden outside, creating a new, unique aroma.","Xu Wan sat in the pavilion, eating frozen pears while a maid fanned her. Despite the breeze, waves of heat still reached her, and she began to wonder how she would survive the coming summer, dressed in so many layers.","\"Madam, with the academy’s test papers, the young masters won’t need to go to the academy for exams anymore,\" Cui Zhi said.","Xu Wan, with her eyes closed, replied, \"They still have to go. Haven’t you seen how Jincheng is climbing the rankings?\"","Such a high-energy child was perfect for competitive events, which could bring out his potential.","\"Hmm... you’re right,\" Cui Zhi had to admit that every one of the madam’s strategies was effective.","Xu Wan opened her eyes and, through the window, saw the two children engrossed in their exams. She casually asked, \"Has the message been delivered to Auntie Hong? Why hasn’t she come out yet?\"","Auntie Hong’s presence in the manor was so faint that Xu Wan felt like it had been months since she last saw her. Even though the two households hadn’t separated and still lived under the same roof.","Cui Zhi replied, \"Auntie Hong said she’s very grateful for your guidance of Young Master Wenxiu. As a concubine, she feels it’s inappropriate to frequently accompany the main wife and doesn’t want to distract Young Master Wenxiu from his studies.\"","Xu Wan was surprised by Auntie Hong’s thoughtfulness. After a moment of surprise, she said, \"Well, let’s respect her choice. Make sure the second household is well taken care of and not mistreated.\"","\"Yes, madam.\"","Xu Wan then asked, \"Has the message been delivered to the Crown Princess in the palace?\"","\"It was delivered at noon. The Crown Princess said she would assist Consort Jing in thoroughly investigating the matter.\"","\"That’s good. With the Crown Princess involved, it’s bound to be more reliable than Consort Jing alone.\" Xu Wan had been slightly worried that Consort Jing might act hastily in her anxiety, but now she felt completely at ease.","\"Chen Shigeng... Chen Yunyu... truly, not a single one of them is reliable.\"","Xu Wan felt that people really needed to be compared. With these two scoundrels as a backdrop, she found Zong Jincheng’s mischievousness quite endearing.","Xu Wan ordered, \"Inform Steward Liu that all invitations from Duke Jin’s Manor or the Minister’s Mansion are to be declined.\"","\"Madam, are you afraid that Chen Yunyu might try to pursue you?\" Cui Zhi had sensed something amiss during the banquet when the two sisters were subtly competing.","Xu Wan looked up at her and asked, \"You noticed it too?\"","Cui Zhi, after all, was from the Marquis Manor. The thought of the madam of the Marquis Manor being pursued by her own brother-in-law was mortifying.","Cui Zhi nodded reluctantly, \"It was too obvious. If Minister Xu and Lady Liu had been there, they would have noticed too. I never expected Chen Yunyu to be so shameless and reckless, daring to set his sights on you. Madam, should we teach him a lesson? The team of experts the old marquis sent us hasn’t been used yet.\"","Xu Wan chuckled, \"What kind of lesson? Beat him up after covering his head?\"","Cui Zhi asked, \"Is that inappropriate?\"","Xu Wan shook her head, \"It’s not about appropriateness, but effectiveness. Beating him up might vent our anger, but if he doesn’t know who we are, he’ll continue to be a nuisance. If he finds out who we are, the trouble will only increase. Given the power of Duke Jin’s Manor, the latter is more likely.\"","\"Madam, don’t you feel wronged?\" Cui Zhi felt that the madam’s way of thinking was different from most people’s.","She seemed to focus on solving the problem first rather than getting caught up in the emotions of the situation, which was quite rare.","\"I’m not as fragile as you think,\" Xu Wan said. \"Speaking of which, I’m reminded of a story. Let me share it with you.\"","\"Please do, madam.\"","Xu Wan began, \"Once, there was a scholar about to enter the examination hall. At a restaurant where a meal should have cost 10 coins, the owner cheated him out of 100 coins. The examination hall’s gates were about to close, and if the scholar argued with the dishonest owner, he would have to wait three more years to take the exam. But if he paid the money, he would lose 90 coins. If it were you, what would you choose?\"","\"I...\" Cui Zhi’s first reaction was that the cheating owner was despicable. Even if she didn’t argue with him, she would report him to the authorities.","But for the scholar, who had only one chance every three years, missing the exam over 90 coins would be a huge mistake.","Cui Zhi sighed, \"I think I understand what you mean, madam, but I still feel uncomfortable about it.\"","\"You’re quite hot-headed,\" Xu Wan said with a smile. \"The current head of Duke Jin’s Manor’s inner court is still the Duchess. My younger sister Xu Lian'er will need a few years to wrestle control from her. But without her keeping him in check, Chen Yunyu will have more energy to stir up trouble. We need to find an opportunity to help my sister.\"","\"Huh?\" Cui Zhi asked, \"Help Xu Lian'er? Are you sure?\"","\"Of course,\" Xu Wan replied with a smile. \"Hasn’t Xu Lian'er discovered Chen Yunyu’s mistress yet? Let’s make sure she finds out.\"","Letting Xu Lian'er deal with the mistress first would be better than letting Chen Yunyu take the initiative. Even if Xu Lian'er couldn’t gain control of the household immediately, she could keep Chen Yunyu too busy to cause other trouble.","Cui Zhi praised, \"Madam, that’s a brilliant idea. I suggest we let Cui Liu handle it. She’ll make sure no one traces it back to us.\"","After all, they only knew about this because of Cui Liu’s discovery. Otherwise, they would have been fooled like everyone else in the capital.","Xu Wan nodded, \"Then let Cui Liu take care of it.\"","As they spoke, time flew by, and soon they heard the excited voice of the little troublemaker from inside the room, \"I’m done!\"","\"Shh... Young Master Wenxiu hasn’t finished yet. No loud noises.\"","\"Oh...\" The little troublemaker responded and quickly ran out of the room.","The private tutors were inside grading his exam. As soon as Zong Jincheng stepped out, he saw Xu Wan and rushed over, plopping down at the stone table in front of her. He grabbed a large peach and started munching on it.","The crisp sound of biting into the peach echoed in the air. The little troublemaker was in a good mood and casually asked, \"What were you talking about?\"","Xu Wan and Cui Zhi exchanged a glance and smiled, \"We were telling a story.\""]},{"number":100,"title":"Chapter 100: Violent Tricks","paragraphs":["“What story?” The Little Demon King’s curiosity was piqued.","Cui Zhi recounted the tale of the scholar who had been swindled during his exam preparations. Upon hearing it, the Little Demon King immediately flew into a rage, exclaiming, “He scammed me out of 90 coins! That unscrupulous shopkeeper might as well have robbed me!”","Cui Zhi secretly gave him a thumbs-up.","Earlier, she had thought she was more hot-tempered than Xu Wan, but with Zong Jincheng as a comparison, she now felt eerily calm.","Xu Wan raised an eyebrow and asked, “So, what would you do, Young Master, now that you’ve been swindled out of 90 coins?”","Without hesitation, the Little Demon King replied, “I’d smash his shop, of course. 90 coins is enough for Lin Yu to copy two or three books. I’m not giving it to him—I’m no fool.”","Xu Wan reminded him, “But if you take the time to smash his shop, you’ll miss your exam.”","The Little Demon King paused, then said, “Then I’ll have Buyan do it.”","Buyan: “...”","Day in and day out, he’s assigned these kinds of tasks, and none of them are good.","The Little Demon King added, “If Buyan’s busy, I’ll do it myself after the exam. The shopkeeper can’t run away—I’ll make sure he’s crying and begging for mercy, shouting ‘I’ll never do it again!’ at least three hundred times.”","Xu Wan fell silent for a moment, then also gave him a thumbs-up.","Truly, the Capital City’s number one troublemaker.","This little rascal’s approach was anything but conventional, relying on brute force to solve problems.","While outrageous, it was undeniably effective.","Xu Wan, for some reason, suddenly asked another question, “What if someone keeps bothering you, but if you hit them, they’ll only cling to you more? What would you do then?”","The Little Demon King took another bite of his crisp peach and decisively said, “Then I’d hit them in secret, making sure they don’t know it’s me. Buyan can handle that—he’s good at staying unnoticed.”","Buyan: “!”","Another one of these absurd tasks!","As a martial arts champion’s sparring partner, couldn’t he get some decent work to do??","Xu Wan pressed further, “But if the person doesn’t know it’s you, they might not learn their lesson and keep bothering you. What then?”","The Little Demon King replied, “Then Buyan can keep hitting them until they’re bedridden, too weak to go out, and in so much pain they can’t even think of causing trouble.”","Buyan: “...”","Young Master, I’m just a bodyguard, not a thug, and certainly not a torturer...","Xu Wan and Cui Zhi both fell silent.","Somehow, it sounded oddly tempting to try.","“Young Master Wenxiu has finished his exam,” the tutor’s voice came from inside the room.","The Little Demon King quickly got up to leave, but after a step, he turned back to grab a large peach, muttering, “This peach is delicious. I’ll take one for my brother too.”","With that, the little troublemaker was gone in a flash.","The pavilion fell silent for a few seconds before Cui Zhi suddenly burst into laughter.","Xu Wan joined in, chuckling as she said, “This kid’s thought process is much more thorough than before.”","“Though still a bit immature, it’s strangely satisfying to hear,” Cui Zhi remarked, feeling as if her frustration had been cleared.","Xu Wan laughed, “Haha, let’s go with that plan for now. If it doesn’t work out, we’ll just have to borrow Buyan.”","“Understood,” Cui Zhi replied with a smile, going off to arrange things with Cui Liu.","Inside the room, the incense had burned out. Zong Wenxiu had submitted his exam just in time, though he kept glancing at the collected papers, feeling he hadn’t done well.","Zong Jincheng ran in from outside, cheerfully handing him a large peach, “Brother, take a break. Have a peach—it’s really crisp.”","Zong Wenxiu accepted it, saying, “Thank you.”","But he wasn’t in the mood to eat.","Xu Wan entered shortly after, immediately noticing the dejected Zong Wenxiu, who looked like a pitiful little figure, clearly upset about his performance. In contrast, the Little Demon King was as carefree as ever.","Xu Wan spoke up, “This exam is just a test of your current knowledge. Even if you didn’t do well, it’s okay. There’s still a whole month before the academy’s monthly exam to improve. Besides, you’re learning material beyond your age group, so don’t put too much pressure on yourself. Stay calm.”","Hearing this, Zong Wenxiu snapped out of his self-doubt, realizing he had once again set impossibly high standards for himself.","“Thank you, Madam.”","The Little Demon King, however, couldn’t relate to his brother’s sensitive emotions or understand the significance of Xu Wan’s words. To him, it was just her usual nagging, which he didn’t need.","Zong Jincheng whispered slyly, “I just took the nine-year-old’s exam, and it was a breeze. Since there’s still time in the afternoon and the results aren’t out yet, maybe I’ll try the ten-year-old’s exam too?”","Perhaps if he aced this one, the tutors would be amazed, applauding him as the future prodigy and urging him to join the Child Prodigy Class to outshine Qin Ye. That would be... hahahahaha...","Zhao Yin was indeed impressed by the Little Demon King’s boundless energy. He turned to Xu Wan and asked, “Madam, what do you think?”","Xu Wan smiled, “Let him take it. Just don’t let him fail in silence.”","The Little Demon King placed his hands on his hips and declared, “Just wait. This prodigy is about to prove you wrong!”","A new exam paper was brought in, and the incense was lit once more.","Zong Wenxiu began silently reciting what he had learned the previous day, while Zong Jincheng picked up his brush to tackle the new exam.","However, things didn’t go smoothly.","The Little Demon King, who was already fidgety, became even more restless with this new exam. He scratched his head, kicked his legs, flipped through the pages, and beads of sweat formed on his forehead.","Damn it, I don’t know this one, or this one either.","I’ve memorized so many books—how can I be so far behind my brother?","Zong Jincheng glanced at Zong Wenxiu, who was sitting upright, silently writing things he hadn’t even learned yet.","Turning back, the Little Demon King continued to struggle.","Xu Wan’s words echoed in his mind: he wouldn’t even rank in the ten-year-old exam next month. Not ranking meant not even making it to the top tier. If he couldn’t do it in a month, how hard must it be for him now?","Zong Jincheng wanted to put down his brush, but Xu Wan was waiting outside. If he gave up after just fifteen minutes, she’d surely laugh at him.","But... damn it, I can’t do this! Why is this exam so hard? I know every word individually, but together they make no sense.","Zong Jincheng slammed his brush on the table, frustrated, and shouted, “Master Zhao, did you give me the wrong exam? Is this really for ten-year-olds?”"]}]);
